{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T09:48:56+08:00","record":{"name":"Xusheng Ai","current_title":"Research Assistant","current_company":"Clemson University · 全职","location":"美国 南卡罗莱纳 克莱姆森","headline":"Student at Clemson University, pursuing the implementing generative model in the field of biology. Specializing in Python and C","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/xusheng-ai-3b2a86196","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAC4TyrYBoCmmhoyJ1tXIoUFpIWvaq0L5Qu4","core_skills":["enrichment analysis","Python (Programming Language)","Transformers"],"positions":[{"title":"Research Assistant","company":"Clemson University · 全职","date_range":"2022年1月 - 现在","duration":"4 年 9 个月","location":"美国 南卡罗莱纳 克莱姆森","description":"PhD Candidate in Computer Engineering at Clemson University, advised by Prof. Melissa C. Smith. My research focuses on the intersection of Generative AI and Computational Biology, developing scalable deep learning frameworks to analyze high-dimensional genomic data. My work includes designing transformer-based diffusion models and Hierarchical VAEs to forecast gene expression dynamics and simulate tumor-to-normal tissue transitions for breast cancer research. I have published methodologies like \"Gemdiff\" in Briefings in Bioinformatics and optimized multi-GPU workflows to double training efficiency.\n\n• Latent Representation Learning and Trajectory Inference Aug 2023 – Present. \n• Developed a Hierarchical VAE Backend to extract interpretable latent features from noisy biological cancer stage data. \n• Modeled Latent Space Dynamics to infer biological progression (pseudotime), providing insights into the continuous progression of cell states. \n• GemDiff: Generative Foundation Model for Genomics Jan 2022 – Aug 2023. \n• Formulated a perturbation-aware generative process that simulates biological state transitions (e. \n• , normal-to-tumor), enabling in silico experimentation for therapeutic target discovery. \n• Utilized score-based generative modeling to approximate the gradient of the data log-density, ensuring high-fidelity distribution matching in complex biological spaces. \n• Engineered scalable training pipelines using PyTorch DDP on NVIDIA GPU clusters (Multi-Node). \n• Optimized data loading and memory usage to train foundation models on massive cell data. \n• Developed a benchmarking suite to assess generative quality using manifold topology (UMAP/PHATE) and statistical divergences (Maximum Mean Discrepancy), ensuring biological validity of generated samples.","skills":[]},{"title":"Graduate Student–Non-UTHSCH","company":"The University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center · 实习","date_range":"2025年5月 - 2025年11月","duration":"7 个月","location":"美国 德州 休斯顿","description":"Developed a comprehensive computational pipeline to analyze sparse multi-modal single-cell epigenomics data (H3K4me3, H3K27me3, and RNAPII) for CAR-T cell therapy research. \n \nMetacell Aggregation (SEACells): Addressed extreme data sparsity in single-cell histone modification data by implementing the SEACells algorithm. Successfully aggregated individual cells into \"metacells\" to enhance signal resolution, validated against k-means clustering baselines. \n \nMulti-Modal Integration: Engineered a workflow to integrate three distinct modalities (H3K4me3, H3K27me3, RNAPII). Utilized Seurat WNN (Weighted Nearest Neighbor) and sum-based integration strategies to merge tile matrices, enabling robust cross-modality analysis. \n \nData Preprocessing & QC: Built a hybrid R (ArchR) and Python (Scanpy) pipeline to generate bin-by-cell matrices, filter outliers via DBSCAN, and optimize fragment thresholds (minFrags). \n \nTrajectory & Pseudotime: Performed lineage trajectory inference and pseudotime analysis to model developmental paths. Visualized gene expression trends along pseudotime to identify lineage-specific regulatory patterns. \n \nDifferential Analysis: Implemented a regression-based differential gene expression model enhanced by MAGIC imputation and validated using Moran’s I spatial autocorrelation tests. Identified ~3,500 significant lineage-specific markers (e.g., in CM/EM lineages).\n\n• Modeling Biological Dynamics and Cross-Functional Collaboration. \n• Designed reasoning workflows to integrate heterogeneous omics data (H3K4me3/H3K27me3 and RNAPII), enabling the inference of dynamic cell lineage commitments from static snapshots. \n• Implemented Metacell Aggregation strategies to handle sparsity in high-dimensional single-cell data, ensuring robust downstream analysis. \n• Collaborated with cross-disciplinary teams to validate model predictions, achieving 96% cross-validation accuracy in identifying target genes, demonstrating the model’s ability to capture real-world biological signal.","skills":[]},{"title":"Backend Systems Researcher","company":"University of the Pacific","date_range":"2019年8月 - 2021年7月","duration":"2 年","location":"","description":"• Cloud Resource Optimization (A2Cloud-H). \n• Developed \"A2Cloud-H,\" a machine learning framework for cost-effective cloud resource selection, demonstrating strong fundamentals in system architecture and optimization, Achieving over 90% accuracy in matching cloud instances. \n• Conducted rigorous testing with 20+ cloud instances and 8+ applications.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Research Assistant at Clemson University · 2022年 - 现在 | Graduate Student–Non-UTHSCH at The University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center · 2025年 - 2025年 | Backend Systems Researcher at University of the Pacific · 2019年 - 2021年","education":[{"school":"Clemson University","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Computer Engineering","date_range":"2022年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"University of the Pacific","degree":"Master's degree","field_of_study":"Computer Engineering","date_range":"2019年 - 2021年","activities":"活动与社团: Research group, badminton, volunteer in the CCI","grade":"GPA: 3.94"},{"school":"长沙理工大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Automation Engineer Technology/Technician","date_range":"2014年 - 2018年","activities":"活动与社团: Project design, hiking club,","grade":"GPA 3.32"}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Clemson University，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2022年 | University of the Pacific，Master's degree · 2019年 - 2021年 | 长沙理工大学，Bachelor's degree · 2014年 - 2018年 | 档案分析行 | 最新动态 | 1 次浏览 | 保存到项目 | 将Xusheng保存到项目 | 发消息给Xusheng | Xusheng Ai的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
