d data, enhancing data collection and contributing to a 25% improvement in the accuracy and optimization of patient care strategies. \n• Facilitated cross-functional team communications, coordinated clinical research and data management, leading to a 15% increase in multidisciplinary project efficiency within established timelines. \n• Documented patient conditions, adverse events, and responses on Case Report Forms, driving timely reporting. \n• Assisted in training research personnel to stay updated on Good Clinical Practice (GCP) guidelines and meet protocol & regulatory standards, contributing to the development and improvement of clinical study processes.","skills":["Medical Review","Attention to Detail","Presentation Skills","Quality System","Oral Communication","Regulatory Compliance","Problem Solving","Communication"]},{"title":"Research Intern","company":"National Taiwan University School of Pharmacy - Regulatory Science Lab","date_range":"2020年3月 - 2020年9月","duration":"7 个月","location":"","description":"• Authored a research paper in Clinical Pharmacology & Therapeutics, presenting findings that contributed to advancements in the understanding of drug safety and efficacy. \n• Conducted literature review and data analysis for FDA-approved BLAs and authored an article published in Clinical Pharmacology & Therapeutics, contributing drug safety and regulatory insights. \n• Performed comprehensive analysis of 4000+ biosimilar adverse reaction reports, identifying critical safety signals and enhancing pharmacovigilance reporting efficiency by 20%. \n• Analyzed immunogenicity assessments from collected labeling and review data, summarized regulatory action, and generated statistical analyses of FDA-approved Biologics License Applications. \n• Utilized the Drugs@FDA database to establish project databases, synthesized regulatory actions from the Drugs@FDA database to establish project databases, conducted data analysis, and compiled findings for academic research 