{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T09:50:38+08:00","record":{"name":"Jian An","current_title":"Principal Scientist, Biological Sciences","current_company":"Entact Bio · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","headline":"Drug Discovery | Biologist | Project Lead | Oncology | Rare Diseases | Advancing Innovation into Life-Changing Therapies","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jiananbiology","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABYq5CYBb1olaYno7bfabF2C1PMmFJDt-TU","core_skills":["Rare Genetic & Oncology Diseases","In Vitro & In Vivo Pharmacology","antibody purification"],"positions":[{"title":"Principal Scientist, Biological Sciences","company":"Entact Bio · 全职","date_range":"2023年7月 - 2026年4月","duration":"2 年 10 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 沃特敦","description":"Oncology & Rare Genetic Disease Drug Discovery \n• Led biology strategy for pipeline program from target identification through Hit-to-Lead and Lead Optimization, delivering program transition into next stages ahead of timeline. \n• Regularly presented program updates and strategic recommendations to company-wide audiences, including the executive leadership team, driving alignment on program progress, risks, and key decisions. \n• Program Team Lead, Biology, driving integrated discovery strategy across biology, chemistry, DMPK, and structural biology. \n• Designed and implemented decision-driven assay funnels to support target validation, MOA differentiation, and biomarker-informed development. \n• Established and managed external collaborations with academic labs, CROs, and KOLs to accelerate in vivo and mechanistic studies. \n• Initiated and led strategic KOL engagement with renowned disease area expert, hosting company-wide discussions on a metabolic disease patient population, standards of care, and emerging therapeutic landscape to strengthen translational strategy and patient-centered program development. \n• Led an immunology and inflammation target proposal initiative, evaluating and prioritizing eight promising targets amenable to the company’s therapeutic modality and recommending two high-priority candidates for deep-dive assessment and strategic advancement. \n• Contributed to the development of a strategic oncology collaboration proposal for a pharmaceutical partnership, defining scientific rationale, target biology validation plans, timelines, and resource/budget estimates to support business development and portfolio evaluation.  \n• Mentored and developed a biology team, fostering scientific rigor, accountability, and career development.","skills":[]},{"title":"Principal Scientist, Rare Disease","company":"辉瑞","date_range":"5 年","duration":"9 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"Rare Diseases, Repeat Expansion Diseases, DNA Repair, Project management \n• Led the biology function and collaborated with the Research Project Leader to drive cross-functional alignment and advance the Huntington’s disease program from target validation into Lead Optimization stage. \n• Experienced in rare neurodegenerative, metabolic, and neuromuscular diseases, including Huntington’s disease, Friedreich’s Ataxia, ALS/FTD, Myotonic Dystrophy, and related genetically defined disorders. \n• Biology Lead on discovery programs managing the biology team and collaborating with external partners to identify key biological areas for novel target discovery and to advance pipeline programs.  \n• Designed and executed early-stage discovery experiments to establish disease relevance, mechanism, and screening strategy. \n• Developed an innovative cellular assay platform for quantifying DNA repeat expansion in repeat expansion disorders, leading to a 2023 bioRxiv publication and enabling mechanism-driven therapeutic discovery. \n• Proposed a novel therapeutic target for rare carcinomas that was selected for presentation to the internal Disease Area Working Group and review by Pfizer senior leadership team. \n• Mentor and manage junior scientists and co-op students, fostering scientific growth and team development. \n• Identify and engage with key opinion leaders (KOLs) in the field; establish 2 collaborations and implement 1 cutting-edge academic assay technologies in-house. \n• Evaluate external collaboration proposals and contribute to business development decisions on 1 strategic partnerships and 1 asset acquisition.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"辉瑞","date_range":"5 年","duration":"9 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"Rare Diseases, Repeat Expansion Diseases, DNA Repair, Project management \n• Led the biology function and collaborated with the Research Project Leader to drive cross-functional alignment and advance the Huntington’s disease program from target validation into Lead Optimization stage. \n• Experienced in rare neurodegenerative, metabolic, and neuromuscular diseases, including Huntington’s disease, Friedreich’s Ataxia, ALS/FTD, Myotonic Dystrophy, and related genetically defined disorders. \n• Biology Lead on discovery programs managing the biology team and collaborating with external partners to identify key biological areas for novel target discovery and to advance pipeline programs.  \n• Designed and executed early-stage discovery experiments to establish disease relevance, mechanism, and screening strategy. \n• Developed an innovative cellular assay platform for quantifying DNA repeat expansion in repeat expansion disorders, leading to a 2023 bioRxiv publication and enabling mechanism-driven therapeutic discovery. \n• Proposed a novel therapeutic target for rare carcinomas that was selected for presentation to the internal Disease Area Working Group and review by Pfizer senior leadership team. \n• Mentor and manage junior scientists and co-op students, fostering scientific growth and team development. \n• Identify and engage with key opinion leaders (KOLs) in the field; establish 2 collaborations and implement 1 cutting-edge academic assay technologies in-house. \n• Evaluate external collaboration proposals and contribute to business development decisions on 1 strategic partnerships and 1 asset acquisition.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow","company":"Harvard Medical School · 全职","date_range":"2016年1月 - 2018年8月","duration":"2 年 8 个月","location":"Great Boston Area","description":"Advisor: Dr. Eric S. Fischer; Department of Biological Chemistry and Molecular Pharmacology at Harvard Medical School; Department of Cancer Biology at Dana Farber Cancer Institute \n \n•   Investigated cancer-associated E3 ubiquitin ligase complexes using mechanistic, structural, genomic, and quantitative proteomic approaches to characterize target biology and support targeted protein-degradation strategies. \n•   Identified and characterized ZFP91 as a molecular glue-induced degradation target, defining target engagement and mechanism-of-action biology relevant to induced-proximity therapeutics (Nature Communications, 2016). \n•   Generated CRISPR knock-in cellular models with endogenous degron tagging to evaluate protein stability, target modulation, and pharmacological response.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow","company":"Mayo Clinic","date_range":"2012年7月 - 2015年12月","duration":"3 年 6 个月","location":"","description":"Advisor: Dr. Haojie Huang and Dr. Donald J. Tindall; Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology; Department of Urology \n \n•   Identified novel mechanisms of resistance to androgen receptor-targeted therapies in prostate cancer through discovery of SPOP mutation and AR splice variant-mediated degradation escape pathways (Cell Reports, 2014). \n•   Demonstrated that degradation resistance drives accumulation of oncogenic truncated ERG proteins in prostate cancer, revealing a previously unrecognized therapeutic vulnerability in SPOP-mutant tumors (Molecular Cell, 2015). \n•   Identified HDAC3 as a key activator of AKT–mTOR signaling and demonstrated that targeting HDAC3 simultaneously suppresses AKT–mTOR and androgen receptor signaling, revealing a therapeutic strategy for PTEN- or SPOP-mutant prostate cancer (EMBO Molecular Medicine, 2018).","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Principal Scientist, Biological Sciences at Entact Bio · 2023年 - 2026年 | Principal Scientist, Rare Disease at Pfizer · 2022年 - 2023年 | Senior Scientist at Pfizer · 2018年 - 2022年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow at Harvard Medical School · 2016年 - 2018年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow at Mayo Clinic · 2012年 - 2015年","education":[{"school":"复旦大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (PhD)","field_of_study":"Medical Genetics","date_range":"2006年 - 2012年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"D'Amore-McKim School of Business at Northeastern University","degree":"MBA candidate","field_of_study":"Business Strategy, AI-Enabled Decision Making, Innovation Management, Competitive Strategy","date_range":"2025年 - 2026年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"四川大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Biology/Biological Sciences, General","date_range":"2002年 - 2006年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 复旦大学，Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) · 2006年 - 2012年 | D'Amore-McKim School of Business at Northeastern University，MBA candidate · 2025年 - 2026年 | 四川大学，Bachelor's degree · 2002年 - 2006年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
