{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T09:50:50+08:00","record":{"name":"Fiona An, M.D.","current_title":"Global Clinical Development Lead","current_company":"Summit Therapeutics, Inc. · 全职","location":"美国","headline":"Global Oncology Clinical Development Lead | Summit Therapeutics","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/fionaan","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAGxBZYB_fIShG3cNswEKe9hHQcGv-nM4uc","core_skills":["Bispecifics","Early Phase Clinical Development","Late phase clinical development"],"positions":[{"title":"Global Clinical Development Lead","company":"Summit Therapeutics, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2025年6月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 4 个月","location":"美国","description":"Bringing Ivonescimab to patients globally","skills":["Regulatory Interactions","Bispecifics","Drug Development"]},{"title":"Executive Medical Director","company":"Bristol Myers Squibb · 全职","date_range":"2021年6月 - 2024年5月","duration":"3 年","location":"美国","description":"• Oversaw BMS Multiple Myeloma US Medical Affairs disease strategy and budgetary responsibilities. \n• Set priorities for disease area and established portfolio strategies; managed a substantial disease portfolio across various stages of life cycle and modalities, including CAR-T/Cellular Therapy myeloma assets ABECMA and GPRC5D CAR-T, IMids (REVLIMID, POMLYST, EMPLICITI), Cereblon E3 Ligase Modulatory Drugs (CELMoDs - Iberdomide, Mezigdomide), Bispecific Antibodies Alnuctamab, and Antibody Drug Conjugates (ADCs). \n• Supervised the medical launch of Abecma (ide-cel), the first-in-class CAR-T/cell therapy product in Relapsed and Refractory Multiple Myeloma. \n• Established the Medical Data Generation Strategy, encompassing 60+ Investigators Initiated Trials (IITs), real world data (RWD) generations, patient registries. \n• Collaborated very closely with Key Opinion Leaders (KOLs), study investigators and clinical site staff to strengthen BMS Sponsored Trials patients enrollment, ensure patient safety and quality data collection; extended crucial clinical support to ensure timely implementation/execution of Clinical Programs and data generations. \n• Interacted with FDA for Iberdomide regulatory submission and involved in redesigning of the registrational clinical programs based on key requirements of FDA Project Optimus. \n• Participated in BLAs (ide-cel) filings, including the preparation for ODAC discussions for ide-cel (ABECMA). \n• Conducted hands-on data cleaning tasks and final database lock for Phase 2 study of Pomalidomide in Relapsed Refractory Multiple Myeloma. \n• Served as the external spokesperson on behalf of BMS teams at meetings with clinical sites, hospitals, and academic institutions; in the forms of in-person visits, steering committees, advisory boards, or conferences engagements. \n• Managed team of 10 plus medical directors focusing on skillset building and career development.","skills":["Team Leadership","Cell Therapy","Oncology","Hematology","Clinical Trials","Strategy"]},{"title":"Franchise Lead of Oncology Clinical Development","company":"Ionis Pharmaceuticals, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2019年6月 - 2021年5月","duration":"2 年","location":"Greater San Diego Areua","description":"• Led Early Phase clinical development Oncology programs, including drafting asset clinical investigational plans, INDs filings, conducting first-in-human clinical study. \n• Played a critical role to bring preclinical Oncology assets of RNA targeting Antisense Oligonucleotides drug candidates into clinical space, making recommendations on tumor types and trial designs. \n• Designed and monitored early stage clinical studies across multiple tumor types including both solid and hematological malignancies (mainly Breast Cancer, Hepatic Carcinoma, Multiple Myeloma, Non-Hodgkin’s Lymphoma, Leukemia). \n• Headed regulatory interactions and successfully executed IND submission/approval of ION-251. \n• Led Oncology Franchise Clinical Development team, managed and mentored in-house Clinical team members and CRO teams. \n• Built Oncology Clinical Development team and processes from ground up, including establishing study teams, selecting CROs, drafting and reviewing study and safety monitoring plans, and implementing operational procedures. \n• Collaborated very closely with research and preclinical teams including Chemistry, Biology, Translational Sciences, CMC, Pharmacology, Pathology et al to identify additional Oncology target and expanding Oncology drug candidates and pipeline. \n• Spearheaded eternal alliances and collaborations, and eventually led to the out-licensing of entire Oncology portfolio to Private Equity firm (Flamingo) in 2021.","skills":["Regulatory Submissions","Early Phase Clinical Development","Oncology"]},{"title":"Executive Medical Director","company":"Seattle Genetics · 全职","date_range":"2018年5月 - 2019年6月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"西雅图地区","description":"• Led Antibody Drug Conjugates global programs in Breast Cancer, Cervical Cancer, and Ovarian Cancer. \n• Products focused on Ladiratuzumab Vedotin (Breast Cancer) and Tisotumab Vedotin (Cervical Cancer and Ovarian Cancer). \n• Engaged investigators and regulators globally (US, EU, Japan, China) to optimize regulatory path and strategy. \n• Worked very closely with collaboration partners to align clinical, medical and communication strategies. \n• Conducted in person visit to investigational sites to ensure proper interpretations and compliances of the clinical protocol and patient eligibility criteria. \n• Drafted and authored peer-reviewed publications for major Oncology conferences (ASCO, ESMO, AACR, San Antonio Breast Cancer Symposium).","skills":["Oncology","Therapeutic Areas","Biotechnology","Drug Development"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Global Clinical Development Lead at Summit Therapeutics, Inc. · 2025年 - 现在 | Executive Medical Director at Bristol Myers Squibb · 2021年 - 2024年 | Franchise Lead of Oncology Clinical Development at Ionis Pharmaceuticals, Inc. · 2019年 - 2021年 | Executive Medical Director at Seattle Genetics · 2018年 - 2019年 | Senior Director, US Oncology at Pfizer · 2015年 - 2018年 | Team Lead, Clinical Research and Development at Multiple Myeloma Research Foundation/Consortium (MMRF/C) · 2014年 - 2015年 | Senior Vice President, Head of Research and Clinical Development at Multiple Myeloma Research Foundation (MMRF) and Multiple Myeloma Research Consortium (MMRC) · 2014年 - 2015年 | Sr. Director/Director, Oncology Clinical Development at Pfizer · 2010年 - 2014年 | Oncology Global Strategy at Johnson & Johnson · 2009年 - 2010年 | Business Development at Forest Laboratories · 2008年 - 2009年 | The Scripps Research Institute, La Jolla at The Scripps Research Institute · 2005年 - 2007年 | Molelcular Oncology Laboratory at The University of Chicago Medical Center · 2000年 - 2005年","education":[{"school":"美国芝加哥大学","degree":"","field_of_study":"Cancer Biology","date_range":"2000年 - 2003年","activities":"活动与社团: • Fellow, Awarded full scholarship","grade":""},{"school":"美国纽约大学 - 斯特恩商学院","degree":"Master of Business Administration - MBA","field_of_study":"Finance and Marketing","date_range":"2007年 - 2009年","activities":"活动与社团: • Vice President, Stern Pharmaceutical and Healthcare Association http://people.stern.nyu.edu/spha/ • Member, Stern Women in Business","grade":""},{"school":"Beijing Medical University","degree":"M.D.","field_of_study":"Medicine","date_range":"1989年 - 1994年","activities":"活动与社团: • Received extensive training in basic science, clinical medicine and preventive medicine","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 美国芝加哥大学 · 2000年 - 2003年 | 美国纽约大学 - 斯特恩商学院，Master of Business Administration - MBA · 2007年 - 2009年 | Beijing Medical University，M.D. · 1989年 - 1994年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Independent Consultant Vice President Clinical Development Executive Medical Director 职位性质 合同制 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 北美洲 远程办公: 美国 亚洲 北美洲 欧洲 开始日期 我在随便看看，时间可灵活安排 工作场所类型 混合办公 远程办公"],"