{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T09:51:12+08:00","record":{"name":"Songzhu (Michael) An","current_title":"CEO","current_company":"BNB Bio · 全职","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 伯灵格姆","headline":"MD/PhD, drug developer, serial entrepreneur, US-China biotech R&D and BD","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/songzhu-michael-an-2b927ba","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAHRuu0BKuN2e3K4OQ8xCr4s_tzvD_jgXOk","core_skills":["Small molecule drugs","Recombiant proteins/antibodies","Independent academic research"],"positions":[{"title":"CEO","company":"BNB Bio · 全职","date_range":"2025年10月 - 现在","duration":"1 年","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Biotech Advisor/Consultant","company":"InScienceWeTrust BioAdvisory · 自由职业","date_range":"2025年1月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"• BD (senior advisor, InScienceWeTrust BioAdvisory group, specializing US-China biopharma business development deals): search and evaluation, competitive landscape analysis, due diligence, agreement, alliance management, clinical collaboration \n• R&D Strategy: Preclinical Research (target biology, pharmacology, biomarker, translational, IND enabling studies in cancer, fibrosis and degenerative diseases); Clinical Development (strategy, execution, and engagement of KOLs and clinical investigators in early-mid stage clinical trials in U.S. and China) \n• Regulatory Submission and Interactions: develop regulatory strategy and prepare for FDA submissions and interactions \n• R&D Management: preclinical, clinical, and drug manufacturing CROs in U.S. and China \n• Team Building: talent recruitment, team leadership, and site coordination across borders \n• Newco Formation: select legal structure and jurisdiction, file incorporation documents, ensure compliance with local labor and regulatory laws","skills":[]},{"title":"CEO","company":"Curegenix Corporation (Cayman); Curegenix, Inc. (US); Curegenix Guangzhou (CN) · 全职","date_range":"2010年 - 2025年","duration":"15 年 1 个月","location":"San Francisco Bay Area and China","description":"• Founded Curegenix, provided the business strategy and R&D direction, built the team, and led operations in U.S. and China \n• Led all R&D programs and advanced an innovative pipeline of the WNT pathway inhibitors to treat a range of major diseases of unmet needs \n• Developed a first-in-class WNT pathway inhibitors, from discovery, biomarker, pharmacological, translational research to clinical testing as monotherapy and combinations with aPD-1 and KRAS pathway inhibitors \n• Completed Ph1/1b/2a clinical trials of CGX1321 in GI cancers successfully at world-leading clinical centers (Dana-Farber, Johns Hopkins, Mass General, Duke, Georgetown, etc.)  \n• Selected to present CGX1321 safety and proof-of-concept efficacy results on the main oral discussion session on CRC at ASCO2023 \n• Obtained a partnership from Merck Sharp & Dohme with total value > $500M, and co-led clinical collaboration in Ph1b trial with Keytruda \n• Raised financing, including two rounds of equity investment from renowned VCs and Merck, with total proceeds > $30M \n• Established R&D operations in China, recruited a team of 20 FTEs for pre-clinical (conducted >500 in vivo experiments), Ph1 trial, and CRO management \n• Built a pipeline for treating WNT-driven diseases (fibrosis, degenerative diseases, age-related diseases) \n• Recruited an experienced clinical team, built development capabilities in U.S.\n\n• Founded Curegenix, provided the business strategy and R&D direction, built the team, and led operations in US and China Led all R&D programs and advanced an innovative pipeline of the WNT pathway inhibitors to treat a range of major diseases of unmet needs Completed successfully Ph1/1b/2a clinical trials of CGX1321, a first-in-class (FIC) WNT pathway inhibitor, in GI cancers at world-leading clinical centers (Dana-Farber, Johns Hopkins, Mass General, Duke, Georgetown, etc. \n• ) Selected to present CGX1321 safety and proof-of-concept efficacy results on the main GI cancer oral discussion session at ASCO2023 Obtained a partnership from Merck Sharp & Dohme with total value > $500M, and co-led clinical collaboration in Ph1b trial with Keytruda Raised financing, including two rounds of equity investment from renowned VCs and Merck, with total proceeds > $30M Established R&D operations in China, recruited a team of 20 FTEs for pre-clinical (conducted >500 in vivo experiments), Ph1 trial, and CRO management Built a pipeline for treating WNT-driven diseases (fibrosis, degenerative diseases, age-related diseases) Recruited an experienced clinical team, built development capabilities in US.","skills":["Cross-functional Team Leadership","Fundraising","Partnership with big pharma","Clinical Development","Executive Management"]},{"title":"Co-Founder","company":"StemRD","date_range":"2009年 - 2025年","duration":"16 年 1 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"• Co-founded StemRD, provided the strategy for business and R&D \n• Led R&D in the purification and production of some of the most important, yet the most challenging-to-produce, growth factors for stem cell research, such as WNTs, Hedgehogs, TGF-beta... \n• Designed serum-free, xeno-free, all-human and all-recombinant growth media for culturing human iPSC/ESC, MSC (OEM’d to Corning as StemGro), and differentiation kit for cardiomyocytes and chondrocytes \n• Successfully obtained small business research grants (SBIR) on novel approaches for MSC chondrogenesis with KOLs in MSC and cartilage repair","skills":["Stem Cell Research","Regenerative Medicine","Start-up Leadership"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | CEO at BNB Bio · 2025年 - 现在 | Biotech Advisor/Consultant at InScienceWeTrust BioAdvisory · 2025年 - 现在 | CEO at Curegenix Corporation (Cayman); Curegenix, Inc. (US); Curegenix Guangzhou (CN) · 2010年 - 2025年 | Co-Founder at StemRD · 2009年 - 2025年 | Principal Scientist and Project Leader