年6月","duration":"8 年 6 个月","location":"Cambridge, MA","description":"Provided project leadership for a large number of discovery projects in a multidisciplinary team environment under the NIH Molecular Library Probe Centers Network (MLPCN) and Broad Institute's internal discovery programs. Key responsibilities included design and implementation of discovery campaigns leveraging Broad’s fully and semi-automated high throughput screening platform. Go-to person for challenging and complex assays. Contributed to high quality publications including in journals of Cell, and ACS Chem Biol. Managed team. Partnered with medicinal chemistry, informatics, automation, compound management teams and external collaborators (academic collaborators and CROs) to ensure smooth and timely transition and implementation of workflows integral to project progression.","skills":["Target selection and program inception","Project leadership","Preclinical discovery","Oncology","Immuno-oncology","Immunological & inflammatory","High Throughput Screening","Assay Development","Molecular & Cellular Biology","Cell Biology","Molecular Biology","Biochemistry","Biotechnology","Drug Discovery","In Vitro","High Content Screening","Life Sciences","Laboratory","Cell Culture"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Vice President of Institute for Biologics, Biocytogen, US and China at Biocytogen · 2024年 - 现在 | Sr. Director of Antibody Therapeutics, Biocytogen Institute for Therapeutic Innovation at Biocytogen · 2020年 - 2024年 | Sr. Director of Immuno-oncology & in vitro Pharmacology, Sr. Study Director of Pharmacology at Biocytogen · 2019年 - 2020年 | Head of Immuno-oncology Assays & Laboratory Operations at Bicycle Therapeutics · 2017年 - 2019年 | Director of Immuno-oncology, Assay Platform Development & Cellular Pharmacology at Horizon Discovery (formerly Combinatorx) · 2014年 - 2016年 | Group Leader, Project Lead at The Broad Institute of Harvard and MIT · 2006年 - 2014年 | Senior Scientist III, Project Lead for immunological and inflammatory diseases at Bionaut Pharmaceuticals · 2003年 - 2005年 | Senior Scientist, Departments of Metabolic Diseases at Millennium Pharmaceuticals · 2000年 - 2003年 | Senior Scientist, Neurobiology at Millennium Pharmaceuticals · 1996年 - 2003年","education":[{"school":"Harvard Medical School","degree":"Post doctoral fellow (HMS, Dana Farber Cancer Institute)","field_of_study":"Immunology (T cell activation)","date_range":"","activities":"活动与社团: T cell biology","grade":""},{"school":"Brandeis University","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Molecular and Cellular Biology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"北京大学","degree":"Bachelor's of Science","field_of_study":"Biochemistry","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Harvard Medical School，Post doctoral fellow (HMS, Dana Farber Cancer Institute) | Brandeis University，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) | 北京大学，Bachelor's of Science | 档案分析行 | 最新动态 | 3 条消息 | 6 次浏览 | 保存到项目 | 将W. Frank保存到项目 | 发消息给W. Frank | W. Frank An的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":false,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T09:51:59+08:00","record":{"name":"Harry A.","current_title":"Director, Process Development","current_company":"Editas Medicine","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","headline":"Strategic technical leader solving complex manufacturing challenges and enabling reliable supply of innovative therapies","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/harryan","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAg7qgMBryDQ6Mdzy0w2zL1AYthQ-YhqmeY","core_skills":["Scale-up","Closed Cell Processing","Regulatory Filing"],"positions":[{"title":"Director, Process Development","company":"Editas Medicine","date_range":"4 年 9 个月","duration":"4 年 1 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"● Provided scientific, tactical, and strategic leadership to develop workflows suitable for clinical and commercial manufacturing for CRISPR-based engineered cell medicines within Editas’ ex vivo product portfolio \n \n● Supported GMP production and release of 300+ autologous, EDIT-301 drug substance intermediate, and 60+ drug product (DP) batches used in Ruby (Pivotal) and EdiThal (Phase 1) trials achieving >98% manufacturing success rate\n\n• Assumed leadership of the in vivo Drug Product Process Development function after strategic pivot, with end-to-end accountability for RNA–LNP formulation development, scale-up, and tech transfer supporting EDIT-401 and platform programs. \n• Defined and executed the DP development strategy aligned to program milestones, regulatory expectations, and long-term platform scalability. \n• Built, mentored, and retained a high-performing DP PD team (Sr Process Engineers and AD), establishing clear ownership across formulation development, process scale-up, and external manufacturing oversight. \n• Led the design, build-out, and operationalization of an internal LNP PAD/PD laboratory, enabling hands-on development, rapid iteration, and reduced dependency on external vendors. \n• Served as PIP for DP manufacturing at the CDMO, providing senior technical oversight to ensure IND-enabling non-GMP and GMP batches were delivered on schedule and met quality expectations. \n• Oversaw selection and implementation of critical DP equipment and analytical capabilities, aligning capital investments with pipeline needs. \n• Led DP process development input into the pre-IND briefing package, defined phase-appropriate specifications, in-use stability approaches, and control strategies for RNA–LNP DP.","skills":["技能: Collaborative Problem Solving • Coaching & Mentoring • Regulatory Filing • Team Building • Manufacturing Process Improvement • Project Planning • Communication • Vendor Management • Statistical Data Analysis • Team Leadership • Cell Therapy • cGMP manufacturing","Collaborative Problem Solving","Coaching & Mentoring","Regulatory Filing","Team Building","Manufacturing Process Improvement","Project Planning","Communication","Vendor Management","Statistical Data Analysis","Team Leadership","Cell Therapy","cGMP manufacturing","技能: Scale-up • Stem Cell Differentiation • Bioreactor • Team Management • Technical Data Analysis • Cell Processing • Process Development • Team Leadership • Aseptic Technique","Scale-up","Stem Cell Differentiation","Bioreactor","Team Management","Technical Data Analysis","Cell Processing","Process Development","Aseptic Technique"]},{"title":"Associate Director, Cellular Process Development","company":"Editas Medicine","date_range":"4 年 9 个月","duration":"4 年 1 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"● Provided scientific, tactical, and strategic leadership to develop workflows suitable for clinical and commercial manufacturing for CRISPR-based engineered cell medicines within Editas’ ex vivo product portfolio \n \n● Supported GMP production and release of 300+ autologous, EDIT-301 drug substance intermediate, and 60+ drug product (DP) batches used in Ruby (Pivotal) and EdiThal (Phase 1) trials achieving >98% manufacturing success rate\n\n• Assumed leadership of the in vivo Drug Product Process Development function after strategic pivot, with end-to-end accountability for RNA–LNP formulation development, scale-up, and tech transfer supporting EDIT-401 and platform programs. \n• Defined and executed the DP development strategy aligned to program milestones, regulatory expectations, and long-term platform scalability. \n• Built, mentored, and retained a high-performing DP PD team (Sr Process Engineers and AD), establishing clear ownership across formulation development, process scale-up, and external manufacturing oversight. \n• Led the design, build-out, and operationalization of an internal LNP PAD/PD laboratory, enabling hands-on development, rapid iteration, and reduced dependency on external vendors. \n• Served as PIP for DP manufacturing at the CDMO, providing senior technical oversight to ensure IND-enabling non-GMP and GMP batches were delivered on schedule and met quality expectations. \n• Oversaw selection and implementation of critical DP equipment and analytical capabilities, aligning capital investments with pipeline needs. \n• Led DP process development input into the pre-IND briefing package, defined phase-appropriate specifications, in-use stability approaches, and control strategies for RNA–LNP DP.","skills":["技能: Collaborative Problem Solving • Coaching & Mentoring • Regulatory Filing • Team Building • Manufacturing Process Improvement • Project Planning • Communication • Vendor Management • Statistical Data Analysis • Team Leadership • Cell Therapy • cGMP manufacturing","Collaborative Problem Solving","Coaching & Mentoring","Regulatory Filing","Team Building","Manufacturing Process Improvement","Project Planning","Communication","Vendor Management","Statistical Data Analysis","Team Leadership","Cell Therapy","cGMP manufacturing","技能: Scale-up • Stem Cell Differentiation • Bioreactor • Team Management • Technical Data Analysis • Cell Processing • Process Development • Team Leadership • Aseptic Technique","Scale-up","Stem Cell Differentiation","Bioreactor","Team Management","Technical Data Analysis","Cell Processing","Process Development","Aseptic Technique"]},{"title":"Principal Scientist, Process Development","company":"TScan Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2021年4月 - 2022年1月","duration":"10 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 沃尔瑟姆","description":"• Lead a team of scientists, responsible for the design, execution, and interpretation of experimental studies \n• Develop, optimize, and scale up a robust cell manufacturing process for autologous and allogeneic TCR-T drug products support IND enabling studies and GMP manufacturing \n• Act as primary SME for all internal and external process development and process instrumentation engineering activities including, but not limited to, target cell isolation platforms, automated cell washing, electroporation systems, controlled rate freezing systems, culture expansion, and cryopreservation systems \n• Author and review of technical documentation to support early-stage activities (development reports and supporting documentation for regulatory filings) as well as draft manufacturing documentation to support tech transfer \n• Collaborate closely with manufacturing to tech transfer the developed process to a GMP facility and act as SME during training / process shake-down runs\n\n• Developed functionally closed manufacturing process for TScan’s lead T cells-based development candidates (TSC-100, TSC-101), currently in Phase 1/2 trials. \n• Successfully generated multiple DP batches under time pressure to support IND-enabling toxicology studies, while tech transferring to internal manufacturing team. \n• Authored CMC focused IND sections to accelerate first-in-human studies. \n• Managed 3 FTEs scientists (RA to Principal RA).","skills":["Biotechnology","Product Development","Closed Cell Processing","Cell Culture","Electroporation","Technical Data Analysis"]},{"title":"Senior Scientist II and Team Lead, Cell Process Development","company":"Editas Medicine","date_range":"1 年 9 个月","duration":"7 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"• Lead the design and implementation of a closed and automated clinical-scale manufacturing process for HSC-based autologous gene-edited drug product \n• Draft and review equipment standard operating procedures (SOPs), master batch records (MBRs), bill of materials (BOM), study/qualification protocols, internal memos and technical reports to enable GMP manufacturing and technology transfer \n• Author and review CMC sessions for regulatory submissions \n• Mentor and manage the day-to-day activities of three junior scientists \n• Communicate to functional line management and cross-functional teams regarding progress against technical objectives/milestones  \n• Evaluate, optimize and troubleshoot systems and processes for cell isolation, washing, transfection, and freeze/thaw \n• Plan and execute manufacturing campaigns at CMO to generate materials for critical IND-enabling studies \n• Establish tracking and trending analyses of process development, pilot and cGMP production runs \n• Evaluate new technologies and drive scientific innovation in process development \n• Work independently and closely with cross functional colleagues in pre-clinical, analytical development and quality to advance program and corporate goals \n• Work with suppliers to ensure timely delivery of critical off- the-shelf and custom consumables and reagents \n• Source and implement new capital equipment to support process development and optimization\n\n• Managed and executed, if required, campaigns to generate materials to support IND submissions, including not limited to toxicology, engineering, reference standards, assay qualification, lead stability, forced degradation. \n• Supported Quality with required data, technical assessments, and expertise including contributing to change controls, CAPAs, deviations, stability plans, specifications, OOT/OOS investigations, management reviews and vendor notifications. \n• Established tracking and trending analyses of process development and GMP batches. \n• Ensured compliance with electronic lab notebook (eLN) use to properly document experimental data in a timely manner. \n• Created inventories of process representative cells (HSC, iNK, CD4/CD8 T cells) to support needs from cross functional teams. \n• Sourced and implemented new capital equipment to support process development and drive innovation.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist I and Team Lead, Cell Process Development","company":"Editas Medicine","date_range":"1 年 9 个月","duration":"7 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"• Lead the design and implementation of a closed and automated clinical-scale manufacturing process for HSC-based autologous gene-edited drug product \n• Draft and review equipment standard operating procedures (SOPs), master batch records (MBRs), bill of materials (BOM), study/qualification protocols, internal memos and technical reports to enable GMP manufacturing and technology transfer \n• Author and review CMC sessions for regulatory submissions \n• Mentor and manage the day-to-day activities of three junior scientists \n• Communicate to functional line management and cross-functional teams regarding progress against technical objectives/milestones  \n• Evaluate, optimize and troubleshoot systems and processes for cell isolation, washing, transfection, and freeze/thaw \n• Plan and execute manufacturing campaigns at CMO to generate materials for critical IND-enabling studies \n• Establish tracking and trending analyses of process development, pilot and cGMP production runs \n• Evaluate new technologies and drive scientific innovation in process development \n• Work independently and closely with cross functional colleagues in pre-clinical, analytical development and quality to advance program and corporate goals \n• Work with suppliers to ensure timely delivery of critical off- the-shelf and custom consumables and reagents \n• Source and implement new capital equipment to support process development and optimization\n\n• Managed and executed, if required, campaigns to generate materials to support IND submissions, including not limited to toxicology, engineering, reference standards, assay qualification, lead stability, forced degradation. \n• Supported Quality with required data, technical assessments, and expertise including contributing to change controls, CAPAs, deviations, stability plans, specifications, OOT/OOS investigations, management reviews and vendor notifications. \n• Established tracking and trending analyses of process development and GMP batches. \n• Ensured compliance with electronic lab notebook (eLN) use to properly document experimental data in a timely manner. \n• Created inventories of process representative cells (HSC, iNK, CD4/CD8 T cells) to support needs from cross functional teams. \n• Sourced and implemented new capital equipment to support process development and drive innovation.","skills":[]},{"title":"Process Development Scientist and Team Lead","company":"Editas Medicine","date_range":"1 年 9 个月","duration":"7 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"• Lead the design and implementation of a closed and automated clinical-scale manufacturing process for HSC-based autologous gene-edited drug product \n• Draft and review equipment standard operating procedures (SOPs), master batch records (MBRs), bill of materials (BOM), study/qualification protocols, internal memos and technical reports to enable GMP manufacturing and technology transfer \n• Author and review CMC sessions for regulatory submissions \n• Mentor and manage the day-to-day activities of three junior scientists \n• Communicate to functional line management and cross-functional teams regarding progress against technical objectives/milestones  \n• Evaluate, optimize and troubleshoot systems and processes for cell isolation, washing, transfection, and freeze/thaw \n• Plan and execute manufacturing campaigns at CMO to generate materials for critical IND-enabling studies \n• Establish tracking and trending analyses of process development, pilot and cGMP production runs \n• Evaluate new technologies and drive scientific innovation in process development \n• Work independently and closely with cross functional colleagues in pre-clinical, analytical development and quality to advance program and corporate goals \n• Work with suppliers to ensure timely delivery of critical off- the-shelf and custom consumables and reagents \n• Source and implement new capital equipment to support process development and optimization\n\n• Managed and executed, if required, campaigns to generate materials to support IND submissions, including not limited to toxicology, engineering, reference standards, assay qualification, lead stability, forced degradation. \n• Supported Quality with required data, technical assessments, and expertise including contributing to change controls, CAPAs, deviations, stability plans, specifications, OOT/OOS investigations, management reviews and vendor notifications. \n• Established tracking and trending analyses of process development and GMP batches. \n• Ensured compliance with electronic lab notebook (eLN) use to properly document experimental data in a timely manner. \n• Created inventories of process representative cells (HSC, iNK, CD4/CD8 T cells) to support needs from cross functional teams. \n• Sourced and implemented new capital equipment to support process development and drive innovation.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist, Process Development and Manufacturing","company":"SQZ Biotechnologies","date_range":"4 年 6 个月","duration":"1 年 7 个月","location":"Watertown, MA","description":"• Lead development and scale-up of SQZ process suitable for phase 1 clinical manufacturing of SQZ APCs for oncology \n• Design and execute process scale-up and process improvement activities, including cell isolation, SQZ, and cryo-preparation \n• Develop custom, completely closed, GMP-ready single-use disposable assemblies for manufacturing process \n• Support day-to-day activities at CMO to drive completion of tech transfer \n• Manage interactions with external vendors to ensure material readiness  \n• Develop and implement analytical methods (e.g., cell counting, immunophenotyping) to support process development \n• Supervise and mentor direct reports\n\n• Led numerous PD studies to develop manufacturing process for SQZ’s first autologous, immuno-oncology PBMC based DP. \n• Designed and implemented high-throughput “CellSqueeze” chip to support production of SQZ’s first GMP clinical materials. \n• Led development of custom equipment and single-use disposables to enable DP manufacturing and aseptic media fill at CMO. \n• Responsible for defining critical chip specifications to ensure reproducible clinical-scale process performance. \n• Developed timelines to coordinate activities and project deliverables across multiple vendors to meet program objectives. \n• Managed 1 FTE and 4 intern/coops, trained, mentored junior engineers within the PD team.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist","company":"SQZ Biotechnologies","date_range":"4 年 6 个月","duration":"1 年 7 个月","location":"Watertown, MA","description":"• Lead development and scale-up of SQZ process suitable for phase 1 clinical manufacturing of SQZ APCs for oncology \n• Design and execute process scale-up and process improvement activities, including cell isolation, SQZ, and cryo-preparation \n• Develop custom, completely closed, GMP-ready single-use disposable assemblies for manufacturing process \n• Support day-to-day activities at CMO to drive completion of tech transfer \n• Manage interactions with external vendors to ensure material readiness  \n• Develop and implement analytical methods (e.g., cell counting, immunophenotyping) to support process development \n• Supervise and mentor direct reports\n\n• Led numerous PD studies to develop manufacturing process for SQZ’s first autologous, immuno-oncology PBMC based DP. \n• Designed and implemented high-throughput “CellSqueeze” chip to support production of SQZ’s first GMP clinical materials. \n• Led development of custom equipment and single-use disposables to enable DP manufacturing and aseptic media fill at CMO. \n• Responsible for defining critical chip specifications to ensure reproducible clinical-scale process performance. \n• Developed timelines to coordinate activities and project deliverables across multiple vendors to meet program objectives. \n• Managed 1 FTE and 4 intern/coops, trained, mentored junior engineers within the PD team.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Director, Process Development at Editas Medicine · 2022年 - 现在 | Associate Director, Cellular Process Development at Editas Medicine · 2022年 - 2022年 | Principal Scientist, Process Development at TScan Therapeutics · 2021年 - 2022年 | Senior Scientist II and Team Lead, Cell Process Development at Editas Medicine · 2020年 - 2021年 | Senior Scientist I and Team Lead, Cell Process Development at Editas Medicine · 2020年 - 2020年 | Process Development Scientist and Team Lead at Editas Medicine · 2019年 - 2020年 | Senior Scientist, Process Development and Manufacturing at SQZ Biotechnologies · 2018年 - 2019年 | Scientist at SQZ Biotechnologies · 2015年 - 2018年 | Research Scientist at Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) · 2014年 - 2015年 | Engineering Consultant at General Mills · 2009年 - 2009年 | Engineering Consultant at Morgan Stanley · 2009年 - 2009年 | Graduate Student at MIT · 2008年 - 2014年 | Peer Tutor at Carnegie Mellon University, Office of Academic Development · 2005年 - 2008年","education":[{"school":"美国麻省理工学院","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (PhD)","field_of_study":"Chemical Engineering","date_range":"2008年 - 2014年","activities":"活动与社团: Ashdown House Council","grade":""},{"school":"美国卡内基梅隆大学","degree":"Bachelor of Science (B.S.)","field_of_study":"Chemical Engineering","date_range":"2004年 - 2008年","activities":"活动与社团: Tau Beta Pi Honor Society, Modern Languages Student Advisory Council, American Institute of Chemical Engineers (CMU Chapter)","grade":"3.95/4.0"},{"school":"River Dell High School","degree":"","field_of_study":"","date_range":"2000年 - 2004年","activities":"活动与社团: • National Honor Roll Scholarship For Academic Achievement • New Jersey Governor’s School in the Sciences (NJGSS) at Drew University • National Honor Society","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 美国麻省理工学院，Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) · 2008年 - 2014年 | 美国卡内基梅隆大学，Bachelor of Science (B.S.) · 2004年 - 2008年 | River Dell High School · 2000年 - 2004年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Director Process Development Director of Manufacturing Senior Director Director 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥 美国 纽约 美国 新泽西州 远程办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[{"name":"Mandarin Chinese","proficiency":"中级 (日常会话)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T09:52:10+08:00","record":{"name":"Kyongman An","current_title":"Assistant Professor","current_company":"Hoseo University · 全职","location":"韩国 忠清南道 牙山市","headline":"Assistant Professor of MOT at Hoseo University | AB2EL (Advanced Bio-Brain Engineering Lab) | Neurobiology Ph.D | Antiviral/ Anticancer Peptide | LNP drug delivery | Exosome |","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/kyongman-an","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAA71SQgBi8u3reDPwPmWvy_6bmhfE3M79ZE","core_skills":["Novel Target Development","Iv Vivo drug efficacy test","Therapeutic target development/validation"],"positions":[{"title":"Assistant Professor","company":"Hoseo University · 全职","date_range":"2025年3月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 7 个月","location":"韩国 忠清南道 牙山市","description":"As a dedicated professional in Hoseo University's Graduate School of Management of Technology (MOT), I am committed to advancing the technical development of biotechnology companies while fostering global open innovation among MOT-related collaborators. By leveraging the program's interdisciplinary approach, specialized curriculum, research-driven focus, and global vision, I aim to bridge the gap between technological innovation and strategic business management. My role emphasizes creating synergies between cutting-edge biotechnology advancements and collaborative innovation, driving sustainable growth and impactful solutions in the field.","skills":[]},{"title":"Associate Director of R&D Center","company":"LUCA AICell, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2022年11月 - 2025年2月","duration":"2 年 4 个月","location":"韩国 京畿道","description":"LUCA AICell, Inc. is a lipid-based bio-platform corporation developing application techniques of LUCA's proprietary lipid bilayer technologies in the bio-industry. (https://www.lucaaicell.com/) \nThereof, we made 1) highly controllable/safe/ and efficient lipid nanoparticles (LNPs) for nucleic acid API delivery, cosmetic ingredient, or nutrients delivery; 2) in-vitro diagnostic devices including COVID-19; 3) anti-microbial products such as nasal spray; and 4) anti-viral drug discovery platform, which contributed developing world's recognized broad-spectrum anti-viral drug candidate of LUCA (Elie Dolgin, Nature, 2021; Jackman, Nat Material, 2018).","skills":["Novel Target Development","Strategic Planning","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Drug Delivery","Targeted Drug Delivery","Drug Development","Business Development","Project Management"]},{"title":"Senior Researcher (Team Leader in Drug Discovery)","company":"CTX, INC. · 全职","date_range":"2022年3月 - 2022年10月","duration":"8 个月","location":"韩国 大田广域市","description":"CTX, inc. is a company developing cell therapeutics for multiple disease, primarily focusing on neurodegenerative disease.","skills":["Competitor Analysis","Project Management"]},{"title":"Chief Manager in Business Development","company":"BIORCHESTRA Co., Ltd. · 全职","date_range":"2021年9月 - 2022年2月","duration":"6 个月","location":"韩国 大田广域市","description":"BIORCHESTRA Co., Ltd. is a company developing RNA-drug for the neurodegenerative diseases.  \nI served as a chief manager in Business Development division to support introducing the company's proprietary technology on drug delivery system and the company's drug product.","skills":["Business Development","Project Management","Scientific Communications"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Assistant Professor at Hoseo University · 2025年 - 现在 | Associate Director of R&D Center at LUCA AICell, Inc. · 2022年 - 2025年 | Senior Researcher (Team Leader in Drug Discovery) at CTX, INC. · 2022年 - 2022年 | Chief Manager in Business Development at BIORCHESTRA Co., Ltd. · 2021年 - 2022年 | Faculty Scientist at The Johns Hopkins University · 2020年 - 2021年 | Postdoctoral Fellow at The Johns Hopkins University · 2014年 - 2020年 | Visiting Research Scientist at Harvard Medical School · 2013年 - 2013年 | Visiting Research Scientist at Trinity College Dublin · 