{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T09:55:30+08:00","record":{"name":"Dongyi Zhao-Seehus, BA, MS.Pharm, Ph.D.","current_title":"Business Development & Licensing Manager","current_company":"Biocytogen · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","headline":"Business Development & Licensing | Corporate Strategy | Sourcing Innovation & Therapeutic Targets from Academia","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/dongyi-zhao","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACpThckBmxH8rBc0hX0LUHi_RCIndgduku4","core_skills":["Venture Deals Modeling","Strategic Corporation","Cell signaling pathway"],"positions":[{"title":"Business Development & Licensing Manager","company":"Biocytogen · 全职","date_range":"2025年7月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 3 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"• Spearheaded out-licensing for antibody assets, engaging partnerships with global biotech and pharma companies.  \n• Evaluated therapeutic candidates across various modalities, driving scientific and commercial potential assessments.  \n• Collaborated with cross-functional teams to align deal execution with development goals, ensuring strategic alignment\n\n• Conducted structured market and technology intelligence across biologics platforms, synthesizing scientific, competitive, and market signals to inform Out/In-licensing strategy and asset positioning (Biologics assets out-licensing including BBB shuttle and in vivo CAR delivery vehicle, site-specific conjugation, linker, payload in-licensing). \n• Developed hypothesis-driven landscape analyses and opportunity assessments, translating incomplete data into decision-relevant strategic insights for senior leadership. \n• Built executive-ready intelligence outputs including market landscapes, competitive maps, and risk-adjusted scenarios. \n• Collaborated with R&D, strategy, and external partners to align scientific direction with innovation strategy. \n• Strong hands-on experience in developing master decks, external and internal presentation decks, and organizing data rooms, including market analysis, MOA, unmet medical need, partner strategic fit, and NPV projections. \n• Supported preliminary evaluation of external companies, technologies, and partnerships within the global biotech ecosystem, financial modeling includes rNPV, DCF, and cost approach.","skills":["Strategic Partnerships","Due Diligence","Business Development"]},{"title":"The \"Pulse\" Podcast","company":"GSAS Harvard Biotech Club","date_range":"1 年 9 个月","duration":"1 年 4 个月","location":"Boston, Massachusetts, United States","description":"•Co-led strategic planning and execution of international career series, engaging 15+ global biotech leaders and startup founders to support PhDs’ transition from academia to business through mentorship, insights, and real-world exposure. \n•Launched and scaled the ‘Build Your Path’ program across US-Asia networks, driving outreach, event logistics, and cross-border partnerships to expand access for 500+ scientific trainees. \n•17th Harvard/MIT Case Competition led a cross-functional team to the semi-finals, delivering actionable biotech strategy and a robust go-to-market plan recognized for analytical rigor, stakeholder relevance, and execution feasibility. \n•1st Harvard Biotech Club/ Business Club BioVenture Pitch Deck Competition led in developing an investor-ready biotech pitch deck, driving strategy, market analysis, and financial modeling; recognized for innovation, commercial viability, and presentation strength.","skills":[]},{"title":"Co-Director of International Initiative","company":"GSAS Harvard Biotech Club","date_range":"1 年 9 个月","duration":"1 年 4 个月","location":"Boston, Massachusetts, United States","description":"•Co-led strategic planning and execution of international career series, engaging 15+ global biotech leaders and startup founders to support PhDs’ transition from academia to business through mentorship, insights, and real-world exposure. \n•Launched and scaled the ‘Build Your Path’ program across US-Asia networks, driving outreach, event logistics, and cross-border partnerships to expand access for 500+ scientific trainees. \n•17th Harvard/MIT Case Competition led a cross-functional team to the semi-finals, delivering actionable biotech strategy and a robust go-to-market plan recognized for analytical rigor, stakeholder relevance, and execution feasibility. \n•1st Harvard Biotech Club/ Business Club BioVenture Pitch Deck Competition led in developing an investor-ready biotech pitch deck, driving strategy, market analysis, and financial modeling; recognized for innovation, commercial viability, and presentation strength.","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Fellow","company":"Brigham and Women's Hospital · 全职","date_range":"2023年7月 - 2025年6月","duration":"2 年","location":"美国 麻塞诸塞州 波士顿","description":"• Orchestrated the design and execution of translational in vivo studies (mouse) investigating the role of innate immune signaling in regulating tumor-initiating cells across breast, prostate cancer.  \n• Project 1: Investigated accumulation of DNA damage in BRCA1-deficient luminal MECs induces cell fate plasticity by reactivating developmental pathways like Wnt and FGF using advanced CRISPR/Cas9 genome-editing approaches, including nucleofection and/or lentiviral transductions. \n Established multiple preclinical cancer models, including viral-induced and tamoxifen-inducible systems, and managed xenograft studies with immune cell engraftment. \n Engineered 3D organoid models from mammary gland, prostate, and fallopian tube tissues, and delivered immune co-culture assays to evaluate cell–cell interactions. \n• Project 2: Led the investigation of the key immune regulator TMPRSS2 in prostate cancer progression and immuno-profiling (B cells, T cells, Macrophage, etc.) of the TME. \n Developed multi-color flow cytometry panels to comprehensively profile immune cell populations B cells, T cells, macrophages and neutrophils in tumor microenvironments, enabling high-dimensional immunophenotyping \n Deciphered complex biological processes through RNA-seq and single-cell transcriptomic data analysis, identifying three novel gene expression patterns correlated with specific immune cell phenotypes, furthering understanding of disease mechanisms. \n Worked with another postdoc in the lab and with another lab at HMS to examine the importance of Tmprss2 using the nanoparticle deliver system \n• Mentored two undergraduate students and one visiting scholar, providing hands-on training and supervising independent research projects.","skills":["RNA-seq","In Vivo","Multi-color Flow Cytometry","Organoids","Oncology","Immunology"]},{"title":"Research Fellow","company":"Harvard Medical School · 全职","date_range":"2023年7月 - 2025年6月","duration":"2 年","location":"美国 麻塞诸塞州 波士顿","description":"• Led translational research programs under scientific uncertainty, generating insights relevant to therapeutic and innovation strategy. \n• Synthesized complex biological data into structured hypotheses and strategic insights. \n• Translated advanced scientific concepts into clear narratives to support cross-disciplinary collaboration. \n• Orchestrated the design and execution of translational in vivo studies (mouse) investigating the role of innate immune signaling in regulating tumor-initiating cells across breast, prostate cancer.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Business Development & Licensing Manager at Biocytogen · 2025年 - 现在 | The \"Pulse\" Podcast at GSAS Harvard Biotech Club · 2025年 - 现在 | Co-Director of International Initiative at GSAS Harvard Biotech Club · 2025年 - 2025年 | Research Fellow at Harvard Medical School · 2023年 - 2025年 | Research Fellow at Brigham and Women's Hospital · 2023年 - 2025年 | Ph.D. graduate and Postdoctoral Research Fellow at The University of Tokyo · 2019年 - 2023年 | Graduate Student Intern at Harvard Medical School · 2018年 - 2019年","education":[{"school":"日本东京大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Pharmaceutical Sciences","date_range":"2019年 - 2023年","activities":"活动与社团: I mentored undergraduate researchers in experimental planning, data interpretation, and scientific presentation. Out of the lab, I led molecular biology instruction for over 100 students, including undergraduates and high school students, by designing and delivering hands-on training sessions and conceptual lectures in molecular and cellular biology.","grade":"4.0"},{"school":"中国医科大学","degree":"Master's degree","field_of_study":"Pharmacy","date_range":"2016年 - 2019年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"沈阳药科大学","degree":"Bachelor of Arts - BA","field_of_study":"International trade and economic","date_range":"2012年 - 2016年","activities":"活动与社团: President of Student Union of Shenyang Pharmaceutical University • Led the largest student unions on campus with 200+ members, and cross-border partnerships to expand access for 1000+ campus students. • Organized 3 competitions, 5 social events and 1 career fair event","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 日本东京大学，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2019年 - 2023年 | 中国医科大学，Master's degree · 2016年 - 2019年 | 沈阳药科大学，Bachelor of Arts - BA · 2012年 - 2016年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Business Development Manager Business Analyst Business Development Specialist Scientist Senior Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿 远程办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿 开始日期 我在随便看看，时间可灵活安排 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
