{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T09:58:43+08:00","record":{"name":"Yulong Bai","current_title":"Principal Scientist","current_company":"Johnson & Johnson Innovative Medicine · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","headline":"Computational Biologist | Applied Machine Learning Scientist","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/yulong-bai-06b39a14b","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACQvsNMBdfVzRfOQ_uyvDUWFs67rAdiGYg0","core_skills":["R Programming","Prognostic Analysis","Spatial Transcriptomics"],"positions":[{"title":"Principal Scientist","company":"Johnson & Johnson Innovative Medicine · 全职","date_range":"2026年7月 - 现在","duration":"3 个月","location":"Cambridge, MA","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist, Applied Machine Learning","company":"百时美施贵宝","date_range":"3 年 6 个月","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"- Evaluated CNN- and transformer-based image encoders and built an end-to-end pipeline to predict tile-level features from H&E images using training targets derived from matched spatial transcriptomics (ST) data. Enabled population-scale translational analyses and ROI selection for spatial profiling studies using routinely available H&E images. Selected for presentation at BMS Frontier Science Symposium. \n- Built a multimodal machine learning pipeline integrating ST and imaging data to infer spatially resolved transcription factor activity. Deployed across multiple oncology indications to support therapeutic target prioritization, biomarker development, and translational hypothesis generation. Selected for an oral presentation at BMS Cambridge Science Day. \n- Built analytical workflows for subcellular-resolution spatial profiling platforms and implemented semi-automated, human-in-the-loop processes to improve analysis efficiency, reproducibility, and quality control. \n- Provided consulting in machine learning and spatial analysis, including benchmarking computational methods and 