{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T09:59:17+08:00","record":{"name":"Nan Bai","current_title":"Principal Scientist","current_company":"安进","location":"洛杉矶地区","headline":"Principal Scientist","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/nan-bai-3a948543","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAkli_EBe11xXU-0Xrupnsg3cFDhGSSkIyM","core_skills":["PROTAC activity & selectivity prediction","Rosetta","Biochemistry assay development"],"positions":[{"title":"Principal Scientist","company":"安进","date_range":"6 年 5 个月","duration":"3 年","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist","company":"安进","date_range":"6 年 5 个月","duration":"3 年","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Researcher","company":"安进","date_range":"6 年 5 个月","duration":"3 年","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Associate","company":"Fox Chase Cancer Center","date_range":"3 年 10 个月","duration":"5 个月","location":"美国 宾夕法尼亚州 费城","description":"• Predicting PROTAC activity and selectivity using Rosetta  \n¬ Develop novel computational method: Linker Prediction Approach, to predict activity and selectivity of PROTAC molecules by generating protein of interesting (POI) / PROTAC / E3 ligase ternary structure models using Rosetta. \n¬ Predict activity of PROTAC molecules designed for Brd4-CRBN system with “Linker Prediction Approach” and validate the results by using cell data from published literatures. \n¬ Predict selectivity of PROTAC molecules designed for kinases-CRBN/VHL and CDK4/CDK6-CRBN systems and validate the results by using cell data from published literatures. \n \n• Designing inhibitors of RNA-Binding Proteins by RNA mimicry  \n¬ Rationally design inhibitors of Musashi1 and SRSF2 (both are RNA-binding proteins, RBPs) with RNA mimicry approach. \n¬ Apply multiple biochemistry identification assays to validate ligands from RNA mimicry approach: including FP assay, DSF, detergent titration, and NMR. \n¬ Optimize ligands based on SAR study.  \n¬ Study selectivity of top ligands between Msi1 and other RNA-binding proteins with FP assay. \n \n• Isothermal analysis of ThermoFluor data can readily provide quantitative binding affinities  \n¬ Develop novel isothermal analysis approach to calculate binding affinities with ThermoFluor data. \n¬ Test the accuracy and robustness of isothermal approach with simulation. \n¬ Validate isothermal approach with MBP/maltose system and calculate binding affinity of maltose at melting temperature. \n¬ Explore the application of isothermal approach at low temperature by combining denaturant. \n¬ Apply isothermal approach to other systems like carbonic anhydrases and their four ligands.","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Volunteer","company":"Fox Chase Cancer Center","date_range":"3 年 10 个月","duration":"5 个月","location":"美国 宾夕法尼亚州 费城","description":"• Predicting PROTAC activity and selectivity using Rosetta  \n¬ Develop novel computational method: Linker Prediction Approach, to predict activity and selectivity of PROTAC molecules by generating protein of interesting (POI) / PROTAC / E3 ligase ternary structure models using Rosetta. \n¬ Predict activity of PROTAC molecules designed for Brd4-CRBN system with “Linker Prediction Approach” and validate the results by using cell data from published literatures. \n¬ Predict selectivity of PROTAC molecules designed for kinases-CRBN/VHL and CDK4/CDK6-CRBN systems and validate the results by using cell data from published literatures. \n \n• Designing inhibitors of RNA-Binding Proteins by RNA mimicry  \n¬ Rationally design inhibitors of Musashi1 and SRSF2 (both are RNA-binding proteins, RBPs) with RNA mimicry approach. \n¬ Apply multiple biochemistry identification assays to validate ligands from RNA mimicry approach: including FP assay, DSF, detergent titration, and NMR. \n¬ Optimize ligands based on SAR study.  \n¬ Study selectivity of top ligands between Msi1 and other RNA-binding proteins with FP assay. \n \n• Isothermal analysis of ThermoFluor data can readily provide quantitative binding affinities  \n¬ Develop novel isothermal analysis approach to calculate binding affinities with ThermoFluor data. \n¬ Test the accuracy and robustness of isothermal approach with simulation. \n¬ Validate isothermal approach with MBP/maltose system and calculate binding affinity of maltose at melting temperature. \n¬ Explore the application of isothermal approach at low temperature by combining denaturant. \n¬ Apply isothermal approach to other systems like carbonic anhydrases and their four ligands.","skills":[]},{"title":"PHD Candidate","company":"Univerisity of Kansas","date_range":"2014年9月 - 2019年12月","duration":"5 年 4 个月","location":"美国 堪萨斯州 劳伦斯","description":"","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Principal Scientist at Amgen · 2023年 - 现在 | Scientist at Amgen · 2021年 - 2023年 | Postdoctoral Researcher at Amgen · 2020年 - 2021年 | Postdoctoral Associate at Fox Chase Cancer Center · 2020年 - 2020年 | Research Volunteer at Fox Chase Cancer Center · 2016年 - 2019年 | PHD Candidate at Univerisity of Kansas · 2014年 - 2019年","education":[{"school":"Fox Chase Cancer Center","degree":"","field_of_study":"Cancer Drug Design","date_range":"2016年 - 2019年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"The University of Kansas","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (PhD)","field_of_study":"Biochemistry","date_range":"2014年 - 2019年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"美国伊利诺伊理工大学","degree":"Master's degree","field_of_study":"Biology, General","date_range":"2012年 - 2014年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Fox Chase Cancer Center · 2016年 - 2019年 | The University of Kansas，Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) · 2014年 - 2019年 | 美国伊利诺伊理工大学，Master's degree · 2012年 - 2014年 | 北京大学，Bachelor's degree · 2008年 - 2012年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
