{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T09:59:36+08:00","record":{"name":"Shelley Yang Bai, PhD","current_title":"Postdoctoral Researcher","current_company":"Weill Cornell Medicine · 全职","location":"纽约地区","headline":"Postdoctoral Associate at Weill Cornell Medicine","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/shelley-yang-bai-phd-3a1a0085","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABIfyikB-lp5hz5X9RK6ar-Tn8F3HonF9dE","core_skills":["Cell Lines","Protein Purification","Data Analysis"],"positions":[{"title":"Postdoctoral Researcher","company":"Weill Cornell Medicine · 全职","date_range":"2024年4月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 6 个月","location":"","description":"","skills":["Animal Models","Molecular Biology","Teamwork","Cell Culture"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Associate","company":"NewYork-Presbyterian Hospital","date_range":"2024年6月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 4 个月","location":"","description":"• Investigated epigenetic regulation of chromosomal instability (CIN) in triple-negative breast cancer (TNBC) metastasis, generating mechanistic insights with translational relevance to biologics and cell therapy development; published as first-author in Cancer Discovery. \n• Designed and implemented preclinical in vivo studies (orthotopic and metastatic) to assess anti-tumor activity and therapeutic response, incorporating tumor growth measurements, immune phenotyping, and biomarker analyses. \n• Evaluated tumor–immune interactions within the tumor microenvironment to understand mechanisms of therapeutic sensitivity, resistance, and immune evasion. \n• Collaborated with interdisciplinary teams integrating genomics, imaging, and computational analysis to prioritize candidate targets and guide iterative optimization strategies. \n• Experienced in flow cytometry–based immune profiling and cytokine assays to assess pharmacodynamic responses and therapeutic mechanism of action. \n• Developed and optimized cell-based assays (migration, viability, microscopy, flow cytometry) and RNA-based activity assays (RT-qPCR, RISC loading) to evaluate drug performance. \n• Maintained, cultured, and engineered mammalian cell lines and primary cells, including generation of stable cell lines using lentiviral, retroviral, and AAV vectors. \n• Conducted molecular biology and biochemical analyses, including PCR, Western blot, ELISA, luciferase, and fluorescence assays, to validate target engagement and functional outcomes. \n• Published findings in peer-reviewed journals and presented research at national and international conferences. \n• Mentored junior scientists, providing guidance on experimental design, data interpretation, and troubleshooting strategies.","skills":[]},{"title":"PhD Candidate","company":"Cornell University Weill Cornell Medical Center","date_range":"2017年8月 - 2024年6月","duration":"6 年 11 个月","location":"","description":"• Designed and executed single-cell RNA-seq and multi-omics experiments to dissect tumor heterogeneity and immune microenvironment interactions. \n• Designed and optimized immune cell-based functional assays, including T cell activation, cytokine profiling, and co-culture systems, to evaluate tumor–immune interactions.","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Technician","company":"Weill Cornell Medical College · 全职","date_range":"2015年1月 - 2017年7月","duration":"2 年 7 个月","location":"1300 York Ave, NY, NY","description":"• Conducted biomarker discovery and validation studies in prostate cancer, integrating genomic, transcriptomic, and proteomic data to identify molecular signatures linked to disease progression and therapeutic response. \n• Performed molecular and cellular biology experiments related to the project. \n• Developed and maintained mouse models for in vivo studies. \n• Acquired and analyzed confocal microscopy-based images to assess cellular and molecular changes. \n• Managed lab operations, including ordering and maintaining lab supplies for a lab of 10-12 people.","skills":["Animal Models","Mouse Models","Flow Cytometry","DNA Extraction","Genetics","Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR)","Molecular Biology","Teamwork","Cell Culture"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Postdoctoral Researcher at Weill Cornell Medicine · 2024年 - 现在 | Postdoctoral Associate at NewYork-Presbyterian Hospital · 2024年 - 现在 | PhD Candidate at Cornell University Weill Cornell Medical Center · 2017年 - 2024年 | Research Technician at Weill Cornell Medical College · 2015年 - 2017年 | Research Assistant at Tsinghua University · 2014年 - 2014年 | Student Intern at Columbia University Medical Center · 2014年 - 2014年 | Student Intern at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology · 2013年 - 2013年","education":[{"school":"Weill Cornell Graduate School of Medical Sciences","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Oncology and Cancer Biology, Epigenetics","date_range":"2017年 - 2024年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"吉林大学","degree":"Bachelor of Science (B.S.)","field_of_study":"Biological and Biomedical Sciences","date_range":"2009年 - 2014年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Weill Cornell Graduate School of Medical Sciences，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2017年 - 2024年 | 吉林大学，Bachelor of Science (B.S.) · 2009年 - 2014年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 纽约地区 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":true,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T09:59:46+08:00","record":{"name":"Xiaoyun (Grace) Bai","current_title":"Senior Scientist","current_company":"Novavax","location":"美国 马里兰州 盖瑟斯堡","headline":"Scientist at Novavax Inc","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/xiaoyun-grace-bai-22a0969a","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABUDYsIBqQydQXnLGxx32XzoT0fHGovDawk","core_skills":["Protein Folding","Research","Structural Biology"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"Novavax","date_range":"4 年 8 个月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"","description":"Vaccine characterization, formulation and stability, analytical assay development, structure based vaccine design","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist II","company":"Novavax","date_range":"4 年 8 个月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"","description":"Vaccine characterization, formulation and stability, analytical assay development, structure based vaccine design","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Fellow","company":"The National Institutes of Health","date_range":"6 年 1 个月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"美国 马里兰州 贝塞斯达","description":"Project 1: Structural and functional mechanism of membrane protein mediated drug resistance in cancers. \n• Identified a novel membrane protein mediated cancer drug export system via extracellular vesicles, providing new drug targets for reversing drug resistance. \n• Unveiled 3D structures of disease-causing human membrane proteins at atomic resolution using x-ray crystallography.  \n• Analyzed drug binding within the protein and set up drug binding test using various biochemical, cellular, and molecular biology assays.  \n• Developed engineered cells: modified mammalian cell and yeast cells to stably express target protein for downstream cellular functional assays and structural studies. \n• Collected and analyzed extracellular vesicle released from cancer cells using ultracentrifugation method, nanoparticle tracking analysis (NTA) with Nanosights, and ICP-MS assays.  \n \nProject 2: Microbic drug screening in treatment of fugus infection. \n• Tested the toxicity and efficacy of a microbic drug specifically targeting human fugus infection. \n• Analyzed drug binding within the 3D structure of target protein. \n \nProject 3: Cryo-EM study of SARS-CoV2 spike protein with a diagnostic aptamer. \n• Prepared Cryo-EM samples of spike protein purified from mammalian cells. \n• Collected, processed, and analyzed Cryo-EM data using Titan Krios, cisTEM, Chimera, and COOT. \n• Tested the binding of diagnostic aptamer with spike protein using various drug binding assays. \n \nOther projects:  \n• Monoclonal antibody development in collaboration with pharmaceutical companies. \n• Various cancer cell line culture: melanoma and breast cancer cell lines, 293T, KB cells and drug resistance cell lines. \n• Protein expression, purification and crystallization, small molecule-protein co-crystallization. \n• Development and optimization of protein expression in yeast cells Pichia pastoris. \n• Single channel recording analysis of membrane protein channel activities. \n• Lipid cubic phase study of transmembrane protein.","skills":[]},{"title":"Visiting Fellow","company":"The National Institutes of Health","date_range":"6 年 1 个月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"美国 马里兰州 贝塞斯达","description":"Project 1: Structural and functional mechanism of membrane protein mediated drug resistance in cancers. \n• Identified a novel membrane protein mediated cancer drug export system via extracellular vesicles, providing new drug targets for reversing drug resistance. \n• Unveiled 3D structures of disease-causing human membrane proteins at atomic resolution using x-ray crystallography.  \n• Analyzed drug binding within the protein and set up drug binding test using various biochemical, cellular, and molecular biology assays.  \n• Developed engineered cells: modified mammalian cell and yeast cells to stably express target protein for downstream cellular functional assays and structural studies. \n• Collected and analyzed extracellular vesicle released from cancer cells using ultracentrifugation method, nanoparticle tracking analysis (NTA) with Nanosights, and ICP-MS assays.  \n \nProject 2: Microbic drug screening in treatment of fugus infection. \n• Tested the toxicity and efficacy of a microbic drug specifically targeting human fugus infection. \n• Analyzed drug binding within the 3D structure of target protein. \n \nProject 3: Cryo-EM study of SARS-CoV2 spike protein with a diagnostic aptamer. \n• Prepared Cryo-EM samples of spike protein purified from mammalian cells. \n• Collected, processed, and analyzed Cryo-EM data using Titan Krios, cisTEM, Chimera, and COOT. \n• Tested the binding of diagnostic aptamer with spike protein using various drug binding assays. \n \nOther projects:  \n• Monoclonal antibody development in collaboration with pharmaceutical companies. \n• Various cancer cell line culture: melanoma and breast cancer cell lines, 293T, KB cells and drug resistance cell lines. \n• Protein expression, purification and crystallization, small molecule-protein co-crystallization. \n• Development and optimization of protein expression in yeast cells Pichia pastoris. \n• Single channel recording analysis of membrane protein channel activities. \n• Lipid cubic phase study of transmembrane protein.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Fellow","company":"University of Toronto","date_range":"2013年8月 - 2015年7月","duration":"2 年","location":"加拿大多伦多地区","description":"• Structural and functional studies of Solute Carrier family membrane proteins. \n• Investigated the mechanism of multiple human diseases induced by SLC mutations/defects using various biochemical and structural assays.  \n• Assessed links of SLCs to clinical therapeutics and human diseases.","skills":[]},{"title":"PHD Student","company":"北京大学","date_range":"4 年 11 个月","duration":"4 年 11 个月","location":"中国 北京市","description":"• Structural and biochemical characterization of LPS with Stabilin-1 interacting chitinase-like protein (SI-CLP), a human secreted protein that is abundantly in patients with chronic inflammatory disorders of the respiratory tract, human peripheral blood leukocytes, and patients undergoing glucocorticoid therapy.  \n• Lead role in structural and functional studies of PACSIN proteins which are involved in membrane deformations. Identify drug targets within the family in treatment of Huntington disease. \n• Provided consulting service for 23 PKU undergraduate students for four years.","skills":[]},{"title":"Teaching Assistant","company":"北京大学","date_range":"4 年 11 个月","duration":"4 年 11 个月","location":"中国 北京市","description":"• Structural and biochemical characterization of LPS with Stabilin-1 interacting chitinase-like protein (SI-CLP), a human secreted protein that is abundantly in patients with chronic inflammatory disorders of the respiratory tract, human peripheral blood leukocytes, and patients undergoing glucocorticoid therapy.  \n• Lead role in structural and functional studies of PACSIN proteins which are involved in membrane deformations. Identify drug targets within the family in treatment of Huntington disease. \n• Provided consulting service for 23 PKU undergraduate students for four years.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Senior Scientist at Novavax · 2023年 - 现在 | Scientist II at NOVAVAX INC · 2022年 - 2023年 | Research Fellow at The National Institutes of Health · 2021年 - 2022年 | Visiting Fellow at The National Institutes of Health · 2016年 - 2021年 | Postdoctoral Fellow at University of Toronto · 2013年 - 2015年 | Teaching Assistant at Peking University · 2009年 - 2010年 | PHD Student at Peking University · 2008年 - 2013年","education":[{"school":"北京大学","degree":"PhD","field_of_study":"Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 北京大学，PhD | 档案分析行 | 最新动态 | 1 次浏览 | 保存到项目 | 将Xiaoyun (Grace)保存到项目 | 发消息给Xiaoyun (Grace) | Xiaoyun (Grace) Bai的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"中高级 (商务会话)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T09:59:57+08:00","record":{"name":"Hanwen (Evan) Bai","current_title":"Director, Computational Genomics","current_company":"Vertex Pharmaceuticals","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","headline":"Vertex Computational Genomics Director | Interior Decorating Entrepreneur","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/evan-bai","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAShrsgBSOEk-2c3TwZB0iuxoB3SPz5NFzg","core_skills":["Cancer Research","Perl","Sequencing"],"positions":[{"title":"Director, Computational Genomics","company":"Vertex Pharmaceuticals","date_range":"10 年 4 个月","duration":"2 年 6 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"• [Leadership] Serving as the accountable person for the computational genomics portfolio for 2 clinical stage and 5 pre-clinical small molecule disease programs, ranging from early target discovery to currently in late-stage clinical trials. Responsible for computational genomic deliverables across the drug discovery pipeline, ranging from target discovery, disease model characterization, biomarker discovery, to defining treatable patient population. \n \n• [People management] Managing 3 PhD-level, full-time, computational biologists. Mentoring and empowering them to identify knowledge gaps in our drug discovery programs, design and implement cutting-edge genomic studies (e.g. spatial transcriptomics, SomaLogic proteomics, and SLAM-seq) to address them, and conduct best practice computational analysis to gain novel insights. \n \n• [External collaboration] Proposed and currently managing Vertex’s joint research collaborations with 4 external academic research labs, conducting joint genomic studies to advance 2 late-stage disease programs. \n \n• [Clinical trial sample analysis] Proposed, implemented, and conducting transcriptomic and serum proteomic analysis of patient tissue samples for 2 clinical trial studies to discover and validate response biomarkers.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Principal Research Scientist, Computational Genomics","company":"Vertex Pharmaceuticals","date_range":"10 年 4 个月","duration":"2 年 6 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"• [Leadership] Serving as the accountable person for the computational genomics portfolio for 2 clinical stage and 5 pre-clinical small molecule disease programs, ranging from early target discovery to currently in late-stage clinical trials. Responsible for computational genomic deliverables across the drug discovery pipeline, ranging from target discovery, disease model characterization, biomarker discovery, to defining treatable patient population. \n \n• [People management] Managing 3 PhD-level, full-time, computational biologists. Mentoring and empowering them to identify knowledge gaps in our drug discovery programs, design and implement cutting-edge genomic studies (e.g. spatial transcriptomics, SomaLogic proteomics, and SLAM-seq) to address them, and conduct best practice computational analysis to gain novel insights. \n \n• [External collaboration] Proposed and currently managing Vertex’s joint research collaborations with 4 external academic research labs, conducting joint genomic studies to advance 2 late-stage disease programs. \n \n• [Clinical trial sample analysis] Proposed, implemented, and conducting transcriptomic and serum proteomic analysis of patient tissue samples for 2 clinical trial studies to discover and validate response biomarkers.","skills":[]},{"title":"Principal Research Scientist, Computational Genomics","company":"Vertex Pharmaceuticals","date_range":"10 年 4 个月","duration":"2 年 6 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"• [Leadership] Serving as the accountable person for the computational genomics portfolio for 2 clinical stage and 5 pre-clinical small molecule disease programs, ranging from early target discovery to currently in late-stage clinical trials. Responsible for computational genomic deliverables across the drug discovery pipeline, ranging from target discovery, disease model characterization, biomarker discovery, to defining treatable patient population. \n \n• [People management] Managing 3 PhD-level, full-time, computational biologists. Mentoring and empowering them to identify knowledge gaps in our drug discovery programs, design and implement cutting-edge genomic studies (e.g. spatial transcriptomics, SomaLogic proteomics, and SLAM-seq) to address them, and conduct best practice computational analysis to gain novel insights. \n \n• [External collaboration] Proposed and currently managing Vertex’s joint research collaborations with 4 external academic research labs, conducting joint genomic studies to advance 2 late-stage disease programs. \n \n• [Clinical trial sample analysis] Proposed, implemented, and conducting transcriptomic and serum proteomic analysis of patient tissue samples for 2 clinical trial studies to discover and validate response biomarkers.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Research Scientist, Computational Genomics","company":"Vertex Pharmaceuticals","date_range":"10 年 4 个月","duration":"2 年 6 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"• [Leadership] Serving as the accountable person for the computational genomics portfolio for 2 clinical stage and 5 pre-clinical small molecule disease programs, ranging from early target discovery to currently in late-stage clinical trials. Responsible for computational genomic deliverables across the drug discovery pipeline, ranging from target discovery, disease model characterization, biomarker discovery, to defining treatable patient population. \n \n• [People management] Managing 3 PhD-level, full-time, computational biologists. Mentoring and empowering them to identify knowledge gaps in our drug discovery programs, design and implement cutting-edge genomic studies (e.g. spatial transcriptomics, SomaLogic proteomics, and SLAM-seq) to address them, and conduct best practice computational analysis to gain novel insights. \n \n• [External collaboration] Proposed and currently managing Vertex’s joint research collaborations with 4 external academic research labs, conducting joint genomic studies to advance 2 late-stage disease programs. \n \n• [Clinical trial sample analysis] Proposed, implemented, and conducting transcriptomic and serum proteomic analysis of patient tissue samples for 2 clinical trial studies to discover and validate response biomarkers.","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Scientist, Computational Genomics","company":"Vertex Pharmaceuticals","date_range":"10 年 4 个月","duration":"2 年 6 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"• [Leadership] Serving as the accountable person for the computational genomics portfolio for 2 clinical stage and 5 pre-clinical small molecule disease programs, ranging from early target discovery to currently in late-stage clinical trials. Responsible for computational genomic deliverables across the drug discovery pipeline, ranging from target discovery, disease model characterization, biomarker discovery, to defining treatable patient population. \n \n• [People management] Managing 3 PhD-level, full-time, computational biologists. Mentoring and empowering them to identify knowledge gaps in our drug discovery programs, design and implement cutting-edge genomic studies (e.g. spatial transcriptomics, SomaLogic proteomics, and SLAM-seq) to address them, and conduct best practice computational analysis to gain novel insights. \n \n• [External collaboration] Proposed and currently managing Vertex’s joint research collaborations with 4 external academic research labs, conducting joint genomic studies to advance 2 late-stage disease programs. \n \n• [Clinical trial sample analysis] Proposed, implemented, and conducting transcriptomic and serum proteomic analysis of patient tissue samples for 2 clinical trial studies to discover and validate response biomarkers.","skills":[]},{"title":"Founder & Interior Decorator","company":"Hanwen Interiors · 自雇","date_range":"2022年1月 - 现在","duration":"4 年 9 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"Hanwen Interiors (hanwen-interiors.com) is a Boston-based interior decorating firm, specializing in modern, Asian-inspired homes. I help homeowners find peace and retreat by creating functional and beautiful designs. \n \nMy work has been featured in: \n- Boston Globe Magazine (Sep 2022 issue cover story), \n- Boston Spirit Magazine (Jan/Feb 2023), \n- OWU Magazine (Fall 2022), \n- Celtics & VistaPrint Banner Business Spotlight (2023). \n \nHanwen Interiors is a proud member of the Massachusetts LGBT Chamber of Commerce. To help support the LGBTQ+ community, I pledge to donate 10% of our design fees to local LGBTQ+ non-profit organizations.","skills":[]},{"title":"Bioinformatics Intern","company":"Gilead Sciences","date_range":"2015年6月 - 2015年8月","duration":"3 个月","location":"Foster City, CA","description":"• [Tool development] Created a web tool for Gilead researchers to identify cancer cells based on their genomic backgrounds and an R software package to explore the functional relationships between genes, drugs, and diseases.","skills":[]},{"title":"PhD Candidate","company":"耶鲁大学","date_range":"4 年 9 个月","duration":"4 年 9 个月","location":"New Haven, CT","description":"Carolyn Slayman Prize for Outstanding PhD Thesis awardee. \n \nPrecision medicine in oncology: (2016) \n• Performed clinical genomics diagnostics, including whole-exome sequencing analysis, of brain tumors from patients at the Yale-New Haven Hospital, in order to determine personalized treatment regimen. \n \nGenomic analysis of brain glial tumor progression (in collaboration with Gilead Sciences): (2013 – 2016) \n• Used genomics tools including whole-exome sequencing, SNP genotyping, RNA expression, and DNA methylation profiling, and computational analyses to characterize the genetic cause of benign-to-malignant brain tumor transformation. \n• Identified bromodomain and extra-terminal (BET) family inhibition as a potential therapeutic approach. \n• Publication: Bai et al., Nature Genetics, 2016. \n \nGenomic analysis of brain meningeal tumors: (2011 – 2016) \n• Conducted whole-exome sequencing, RNA expression, and computational analyses to characterize the genetic cause of common brain tumors.  \n• Identified novel gene mutations that cause over 90% of meningimas, as well as gene expression profiles that classify meningiomas into distinct subgroups. \n• Publications: Clark et al., Science, 2012. Clark et al., Nature Genetics, 2016. Harmancı et al., Nature Communications, 2017. \n \nComputational prediction of gene essentiality during neuro-development: (2011 – 2013) \n• Applied support vector machine algorithm to model the gene essentiality for human brain development, incorporating features such as common genetic variations. \n \nCharacterization of limb development using ChIP-seq: (2011) \n• Performed and analyzed ChIP-seq experiments to identify the roles of cohesin in regulating gene transcription during mouse limb development.","skills":[]},{"title":"Journal Editor","company":"耶鲁大学","date_range":"4 年 9 个月","duration":"4 年 9 个月","location":"New Haven, CT","description":"Carolyn Slayman Prize for Outstanding PhD Thesis awardee. \n \nPrecision medicine in oncology: (2016) \n• Performed clinical genomics diagnostics, including whole-exome sequencing analysis, of brain tumors from patients at the Yale-New Haven Hospital, in order to determine personalized treatment regimen. \n \nGenomic analysis of brain glial tumor progression (in collaboration with Gilead Sciences): (2013 – 2016) \n• Used genomics tools including whole-exome sequencing, SNP genotyping, RNA expression, and DNA methylation profiling, and computational analyses to characterize the genetic cause of benign-to-malignant brain tumor transformation. \n• Identified bromodomain and extra-terminal (BET) family inhibition as a potential therapeutic approach. \n• Publication: Bai et al., Nature Genetics, 2016. \n \nGenomic analysis of brain meningeal tumors: (2011 – 2016) \n• Conducted whole-exome sequencing, RNA expression, and computational analyses to characterize the genetic cause of common brain tumors.  \n• Identified novel gene mutations that cause over 90% of meningimas, as well as gene expression profiles that classify meningiomas into distinct subgroups. \n• Publications: Clark et al., Science, 2012. Clark et al., Nature Genetics, 2016. Harmancı et al., Nature Communications, 2017. \n \nComputational prediction of gene essentiality during neuro-development: (2011 – 2013) \n• Applied support vector machine algorithm to model the gene essentiality for human brain development, incorporating features such as common genetic variations. \n \nCharacterization of limb development using ChIP-seq: (2011) \n• Performed and analyzed ChIP-seq experiments to identify the roles of cohesin in regulating gene transcription during mouse limb development.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Director, Computational Genomics at Vertex Pharmaceuticals · 2024年 - 现在 | Founder & Interior Decorator at Hanwen Interiors · 2022年 - 现在 | Senior Principal Research Scientist, Computational Genomics at Vertex Pharmaceuticals · 2022年 - 2024年 | Principal Research Scientist, Computational Genomics at Vertex Pharmaceuticals · 2019年 - 2022年 | Senior Research Scientist, Computational Genomics at Vertex Pharmaceuticals · 2018年 - 2019年 | Research Scientist, Computational Genomics at Vertex Pharmaceuticals · 2016年 - 2018年 | Bioinformatics Intern at Gilead Sciences · 2015年 - 2015年 | Journal Editor at Yale Journal of Biology and Medicine · 2012年 - 2015年 | PhD Candidate at Yale University · 2011年 - 2016年 | Research Fellow at Ohio State University · 2010年 - 2010年 | Research Fellow at Ohio Wesleyan University · 2008年 - 2011年","education":[{"school":"耶鲁大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Genetics","date_range":"2011年 - 2016年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"耶鲁大学","degree":"Master of Philo