{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:00:28+08:00","record":{"name":"Yunpeng Bai","current_title":"Research Scientist","current_company":"美国普渡大学","location":"美国 印第安纳 Indianapolis","headline":"Assistant Research Scientist at Purdue University","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/yunpeng-bai-84220226","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAVeijIBBvy7PF_03qkoqWA04UO60Wb4OBc","core_skills":["biochemistry and molecular biology","Molecular & Cellular Biology","Cancer Research"],"positions":[{"title":"Research Scientist","company":"美国普渡大学","date_range":"10 年 9 个月","duration":"3 年 7 个月","location":"美国 印第安纳 西拉斐叶","description":"My research focus is to better understand protein tyrosine phosphatases (PTPs) and develop novel therapeutics for human diseases including cancer, diabetes, neurodegenerative and autoimmune diseases. The goal is to fully characterize disease-associated PTP family members, (including PRLs, SHP1/2, LYP, TCPTP, PTP1B, etc.), and understand how PTP is involved in different cellular signaling and how PTP malfunction causes diseases by using different molecular, cellular and mouse genetic techniques (e.g. CRISPR gene editing, proteomics and gene knockout mouse, etc.). Determine the potency and selectivity of newly generated chemical probes (orthosteric and allosteric inhibitors, covalent inhibitors, and PROTAC-based small molecule degraders) for different PTP targets by developing suitable bioassays, cellular assays and mouse models for target validation and therapeutic evaluation.","skills":["技能: Bioinformatics • Mouse Models • Cancer Immunotherapy • Molecular & Cellular Biology • Pharmacology","Bioinformatics","Mouse Models","Cancer Immunotherapy","Molecular & Cellular Biology","Pharmacology","技能: biochemistry and molecular biology • Mouse Models • Cancer Immunotherapy • Molecular & Cellular Biology • Pharmacology • Signal Transduction","biochemistry and molecular biology","Signal Transduction"]},{"title":"As