{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:02:17+08:00","record":{"name":"Xun Bao","current_title":"Postdoctoral Research Associate","current_company":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","headline":"Postdoctoral Research Associate at Massachusetts Institute of Technology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/xun-bao-912544234","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAADp04B4B269n1h1q040biKIfxQ87uXvKsfI","core_skills":["Bacterial Transformation","UV/Vis Spectroscopy","Assay Development"],"positions":[{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Associate","company":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology · 全职","date_range":"2019年4月 - 现在","duration":"7 年 6 个月","location":"","description":"• Determined the structure of TorsinA-Lull1[R449A]-nanobody complex by X-ray crystallography. \n• Generated stable mammalian cell lines and developed a high-throughput cell-based assay for restoration of TorsinA[∆E]-Lull1 interactions in a neuromuscular disorder named Primary Dystonia. \n• Created a novel split luciferase assay to identify compounds that enhance the interaction of TorsinA[∆E] with the Lull1 protein. \n• Discovered small molecules that function as activators of the TorsinA[∆E]-Lull1 complex or inhibitors of the TorsinA-Lull1 complex. \n• Served as the project leader of broad collaboration. \n• Supervised the research of graduate students. \n• Served as EHS representative in the lab. \n• Provided annual lab safety training to all the lab members.","skills":["Bacterial Transformation","UV/Vis Spectroscopy","Protein Chemistry","Microsoft Word","Molecular & Cellular Biology","Tissue Culture","Biotechnology","Life Sciences","Protein Expression","Data Analysis","Mammalian Cell Culture","Microsoft Excel","Protein Purification","Gel Electrophoresis","Microsoft PowerPoint","High-Performance Liquid Chromatography (HPLC)","Microsoft Office","Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR)","Electroporation","Pharmacology","Interpersonal S