{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:02:26+08:00","record":{"name":"Xingfeng Bao","current_title":"VP of Biology","current_company":"GV20 Therapeutics · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","headline":"VP, Head of Biology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/xingfeng-bao-4982a026","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAVhpLQBpMk1gF2c6W2BiaYDVu5bNsK6dws","core_skills":["Pharmaceutical Industry","Translational Biomarkers","Translational pharmacology"],"positions":[{"title":"VP of Biology","company":"GV20 Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2023年 - 现在","duration":"3 年 9 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Exe. Director, Discovery Biology and Pharmacology","company":"H3biomedicine Inc · 全职","date_range":"2019年1月 - 现在","duration":"7 年 9 个月","location":"Cambridge, Massachusetts","description":"Joined H3biomedicine in Jan 2019 to establish an immuno-oncology discovery biology engine and manage an in vivo pharmacology platform. Major contributions include:  \n1) Built a differentiated immuno-oncology pipelines focusing on innate immune modulation and tumor immunogenicity reprogramming from target validation to phase 1 clinical trials with modalities of small molecule, antibody and antibody drug conjugates (ADC) \n2) Filed two INDs, achieved one clinical proof-of-principle for STING agonist E7766, one candidate selection on multiple myeloma targeting ADC, two lead identification with in vivo POC for novel immunotherapy ADC projects, and initiated multiple initiatives via collaboration \n3) Led strategic collaboration program with Bristol-Myers-Squib to discover RNA splice modulation-based novel IO therapies by reprogramming tumor neoantigens. Newslink:https://www.h3biomedicine.com/2018/12/17/bristol-myers-squibb-and-h3-biomedicine-announce-research-collaboration-to-advance-novel-neoantigen-inducing-therapeutics-leveraging-h3s-rna-splicing-platform/ \n4) Supervised and managed a group of > 15 biologists and pharmacologists including a AAALAC accredited vivarium  \n5) Core research leadership team member","skills":[]},{"title":"Sr. Director, Cancer Immunotherapy Discovery","company":"Eisai US","date_range":"2011年5月 - 2018年12月","duration":"7 年 8 个月","location":"Andover, MA","description":"● Held increasing responsibility in the R&D of cancer immunotherapies and in the team building and management: discovery project lead (2011), global project leader (2014), group leader (2015), Director (2017) and Sr. Director (2018) for discovery and translational research of cancer immunotherapies.  \n \n● Led multidisciplinary project teams to advance preclinical oncology programs into early clinical development with the most advanced one currently in Phase Ib trial, including first-in-class EP4 antagonist E7046 for CRC and first-in-class potential STING agonist E77766 for non-muscle invasive bladder cancer, in addition to multiple discovery stage projects.  \n \n \n● Responsible for in vitro and in vivo translational pharmacology for target validation, Hit ID, Lead optimization, and translational biomarker discovery  \n \n● Establish and manage external collaborations with academy KOLs and CROs for target ID, efficacy, biomarker, drug mechanism, and drug re-purposing studies  \n \n● Manage internal pharmacologists and immunologists for biological data generation, interpretation and reporting, regulatory IND Modules preparation, and their career advancement  \n \n● Strategize and oversee discovery to early development stage oncology programs in the organization","skills":[]},{"title":"Staff Scientist","company":"Sanford|Burnham Medical Research Institute","date_range":"2005年7月 - 2011年4月","duration":"5 年 10 个月","location":"San Diego, CA","description":"Investigation of the molecular mechanism and biosynthesis pathway of complex cell surface carbohydrates in lymphocyte trafficking and immune response generation: \n \n● Identified a novel class of L-selectin carbohydrate ligands and heparan sulfate as chemokine co-receptors that cooperatively guide the lymphocyte trafficking for immune response generation and tumor growth in animals through genetic approach \n \n● Demonstrated a novel tumor suppressor function of dystroglycan-mediated cancer cell-extracellular matrix interaction in prostate cancer using a combined approach of genetics and orthotopic animal tumor modeling \n \n● Discovered a compound that inhibits inflammatory response in a mouse model by blocking heparan sulfate-CCL20 interaction  \n \n● Prepared research grants and publications in Immunity, Nature Immunology, Nature Chemical Biology, PNAS and etc.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | VP of Biology at GV20 Therapeutics · 2023年 - 现在 | Exe. Director, Discovery Biology and Pharmacology at H3biomedicine Inc · 2019年 - 现在 | Sr. Director, Cancer Immunotherapy Discovery at Eisai US · 2011年 - 2018年 | Staff Scientist at Sanford|Burnham Medical Research Institute · 2005年 - 2011年 | JSPS postdoctoral fellow at Kobe Pharmaceutical University · 2002年 - 2005年","education":[{"school":"Graduate School of Chinese Academy of Sciences","degree":"Ph.D.","field_of_study":"Chemistry and Pharmacology","date_range":"1997年 - 2002年","activities":"","grade":"President Award recipient"}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Graduate School of Chinese Academy of Sciences，Ph.D. · 1997年 - 2002年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese and English","proficiency":""}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
