{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:03:32+08:00","record":{"name":"Riyue \"Sunny\" Bao Ph.D.","current_title":"Principal Investigator | Director of Translational Immuno-Informatics Lab (TIILab)","current_company":"UPMC Hillman Cancer Center · 全职","location":"美国 宾夕法尼亚州 匹兹堡","headline":"Scientific Leader | Translational Medicine | Omics & AI | Associate Professor of University of Pittsburgh","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/riyuebao","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAR8OswB_mkqBx7gHng-TAi333yZXRKMzPk","core_skills":["Early discovery","Correlative analysis and validation","Multiomics"],"positions":[{"title":"Principal Investigator | Director of Translational Immuno-Informatics Lab (TIILab)","company":"UPMC Hillman Cancer Center · 全职","date_range":"2019年9月 - 现在","duration":"7 年 1 个月","location":"美国 宾夕法尼亚州 匹兹堡","description":"• Lead a multidisciplinary research team focused on translational oncology, immunotherapy resistance mechanisms, and AI-driven pathology, with direct oversight of strategy, operations, personnel management, and funding. \n \n• Drive end-to-end development of novel preclinical models (e.g., patient-derived organoids, 3D co-culture, spatial omics) and integrate multi-omic, imaging, and computational platforms to accelerate therapeutic discovery. \n \n• Serve as PI or Co-PI on multiple NIH, DoD, and foundation-funded grants, responsible for scientific vision and execution. \n \n• Spearhead cross-functional collaborations with clinicians, pathologists, bioengineers, and industry partners to bridge discovery and clinical application, supporting biomarker discovery and translational development in early-phase trials. \n \n• Build and mentor high-performing teams (scientists, analysts, trainees), and drive the integration of computational analytics across clinical and research programs. \n \n• Co-lead institutional big data science and oncology initiatives and contribute to strategic planning, faculty recruitment, and programmatic growth.","skills":[]},{"title":"Associate Professor of Medicine","company":"University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine · 全职","date_range":"2019年9月 - 现在","duration":"7 年 1 个月","location":"美国 宾夕法尼亚州 匹兹堡","description":"Selected Publications \n \nA full list of 85+ peer-reviewed publications is available on Google Scholar (Link: https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=_KmrkZ0AAAAJ&hl=en ).  \n \n1. Luke JJ, Dadey RE, Augustin RC, ..., Bao R. Pan-cancer tumor cell p38 inhibition to overcome immunotherapy resistance. In Revision. \n2. Dadey R, …, Luke J, Bao R. Multi-omics Identifies Tumor-Intrinsic SREBP1 Driving Immune Exclusion in Hepatocellular Carcinoma. Journal for ImmunoTherapy of Cancer. 2025. \n***IMPACT: Opens new interventions for PD1 refractory tumors.  \n \n3. Matson V†, Fessler J†, Bao R†, ..., Gajewski TF. The commensal microbiome is associated with anti-PD-1 efficacy in metastatic melanoma patients. Science. 2018. (†Co-first author). \n4. Feehley T†, Plunkett CH†, Bao R†, ..., Nagler CR. Healthy infants harbor intestinal bacteria that protect against food allergy. Nature Medicine. 2019. (†Co-first author). \n***IMPACT: Enables scientific translation for microbiome therapeutics + IND filing.  \n \n5. Bao R, Stapor D, Luke JJ. Molecular correlates and therapeutic targets in T cell-inflamed versus non-T cell-inflamed tumors across cancer types. Genome Med. 2020. \n***IMPACT: Establishes an atlas of therapeutic targets for immunotherapy translation. \n \n6. Tompkins AG, Gray ZN, …, Luke JJ, Bao R. Radiomic analysis of patient and interorgan heterogeneity in response to immunotherapies and BRAF-targeted therapy in metastatic melanoma. J Immunother Cancer. 2025. \n***IMPACT: Establishes radiomics as new biomarkers to predict immunotherapy response.  \n \n7. Doerfler R, …, Bao R. Integrating Artificial Intelligence-Driven Digital Pathology and Genomics to Establish Patient-Derived Organoids as a Novel Alternative Model for Drug Response in Head and Neck Cancer. bioRxiv 2025:2025.06.24.660824. doi: 10.1101/2025.06.24.6608245. \n***IMPACT: Establishes TransferNet-PDO as new digital pathology AI to predict PDO identity.","skills":["Early discovery","Correlative analysis and validation","Multiomics","Team Leadership","Strategic Vision","Ex Vivo","In Vitro","Grantsmanship","In Vivo","Immunotherapy","Organoids","Translational Medicine"]},{"title":"Co-Director of Cancer Bioinformatics","company":"UPMC · 全职","date_range":"2019年9月 - 现在","duration":"7 年 1 个月","location":"Pittsburgh, PA","description":"• Provide strategic leadership and scientific direction for the Cancer Bioinformatics Program as part of the NCI-designated comprehensive cancer center, supporting translational research and data-driven discovery across >$100M in funded projects, including the NCI Cancer Center Support Grant (CCSG) and three SPORE grants (Skin, Head & Neck, Ovarian). \n \n• Drive integration of genomics, spatial transcriptomics, radiomics, and AI/ML into translational oncology pipelines, collaborating with 100+ PIs across 7 disease programs and therapeutic areas. \n \n• Mentor and oversee bioinformatics teams in supporting 230+ research projects including investigator-initiated clinical trials, preclinical studies, and institutional research priorities; implemented scalable data workflows and analytics platforms to enhance research productivity and reproducibility. \n \n• Actively shape institutional and national research strategies through leadership roles, including NIH R01 and U24 scientific review panels, faculty recruitment efforts, and chairing the Cancer Data Science and Analytics Committee (CDSAC). Enhance national visibility through invited talks, panel leadership, and session chairing at major international conferences (e.g., SITC, ESMO). \n \n• Recognized for leadership in multidisciplinary collaboration across major schools (Medicine, Public Health, Engineering, Arts & Sciences), scientific innovation, and elevating institutional competitiveness in national cancer research initiatives.","skills":["Strategic Partnerships","Grantsmanship","Radiomics","Digital Pathology","Deep Learning","Single Cell Sequencing","Spatial Data","Computational Biology and Artificial Intelligence","Strategic & Scientific Leadership"]},{"title":"Associate Director of Cancer Immunology","company":"美国芝加哥大学","date_range":"7 年 5 个月","duration":"10 个月","location":"芝加哥地区","description":"• Led/Co-led landmark studies reporting WNT/beta-catenin driving immune exclusion (Nature 2015), linking gut microbiome to anti-PD-1 response in melanoma (Science 2018), and pediatric food allergies (Nature Medicine 2018; JCI 2019), resulting in three IP filings. \n• Directed 100+ bioinformatics research projects supporting 90+ research labs across 17 departments. \n• Created ExScalibur: a scalable WES analysis suite adopted across multiple academic centers. \nMentored 4 trainees & 7 junior scientists through internships, lab research, and institutional capstone projects.","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Assistant Professor (Bioinformatics)","company":"美国芝加哥大学","date_range":"7 年 5 个月","duration":"10 个月","location":"芝加哥地区","description":"• Led/Co-led landmark studies reporting WNT/beta-catenin driving immune exclusion (Nature 2015), linking gut microbiome to anti-PD-1 response in melanoma (Science 2018), and pediatric food allergies (Nature Medicine 2018; JCI 2019), resulting in three IP filings. \n• Directed 100+ bioinformatics research projects supporting 90+ research labs across 17 departments. \n• Created ExScalibur: a scalable WES analysis suite adopted across multiple academic centers. \nMentored 4 trainees & 7 junior scientists through internships, lab research, and institutional capstone projects.","skills":[]},{"title":"Manager of Bioinformatics","company":"美国芝加哥大学","date_range":"7 年 5 个月","duration":"10 个月","location":"芝加哥地区","description":"• Led/Co-led landmark studies reporting WNT/beta-catenin driving immune exclusion (Nature 2015), linking gut microbiome to anti-PD-1 response in melanoma (Science 2018), and pediatric food allergies (Nature Medicine 2018; JCI 2019), resulting in three IP filings. \n• Directed 100+ bioinformatics research projects supporting 90+ research labs across 17 departments. \n• Created ExScalibur: a scalable WES analysis suite adopted across multiple academic centers. \nMentored 4 trainees & 7 junior scientists through internships, lab research, and institutional capstone projects.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Bioinformatician","company":"美国芝加哥大学","date_range":"7 年 5 个月","duration":"10 个月","location":"芝加哥地区","description":"• Led/Co-led landmark studies reporting WNT/beta-catenin driving immune exclusion (Nature 2015), linking gut microbiome to anti-PD-1 response in melanoma (Science 2018), and pediatric food allergies (Nature Medicine 2018; JCI 2019), resulting in three IP filings. \n• Directed 100+ bioinformatics research projects supporting 90+ research labs across 17 departments. \n• Created ExScalibur: a scalable WES analysis suite adopted across multiple academic centers. \nMentored 4 trainees & 7 junior scientists through internships, lab research, and institutional capstone projects.","skills":[]},{"title":"Bioinformatician","company":"美国芝加哥大学","date_range":"7 年 5 个月","duration":"10 个月","location":"芝加哥地区","description":"• Led/Co-led landmark studies reporting WNT/beta-catenin driving immune exclusion (Nature 2015), linking gut microbiome to anti-PD-1 response in melanoma (Science 2018), and pediatric food allergies (Nature Medicine 2018; JCI 2019), resulting in three IP filings. \n• Directed 100+ bioinformatics research projects supporting 90+ research labs across 17 departments. \n• Created ExScalibur: a scalable WES analysis suite adopted across multiple academic centers. \nMentored 4 trainees & 7 junior scientists through internships, lab research, and institutional capstone projects.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Principal Investigator | Director of Translational Immuno-Informatics Lab (TIILab) at UPMC Hillman Cancer Center · 2019年 - 现在 | Associate Professor of Medicine at University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine · 2019年 - 现在 | Co-Director of Cancer Bioinformatics at UPMC · 2019年 - 现在 | Associate Director of Cancer Immunology at University of Chicago · 2018年 - 2019年 | Manager of Bioinformatics at University of Chicago · 2017年 - 2018年 | Research Assistant Professor (Bioinformatics) at The University of Chicago · 2017年 - 2019年 | Senior Bioinformatician at The University of Chicago · 2015年 - 2017年 | Bioinformatician at The University of Chicago · 2012年 - 2015年 | Research Assistant at Department of Biological Sciences, Wayne State University · 2006年 - 2012年 | Laboratory instructor for Microbiology at College of Arts and Sciences, Wayne State University · 2006年 - 2008年 | Research Assistant at School of Life Sciences, University of Science and Technology of China · 2004年 - 2005年 | Undergraduate Student Researcher at School of Life Sciences, University of Science and Technology of China · 2003年 - 2004年","education":[{"school":"美国韦恩州立大学","degree":"Ph.D.","field_of_study":"Biology (Concentration: Bioinformatics)","date_range":"2005年 - 2012年","activities":"","grade":"4.0/4.0"},{"school":"NESCent","degree":"","field_of_study":"Evolutionary biology and population genetics","date_range":"2009年 - 2009年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"中国科学技术大学","degree":"B.S.","field_of_study":"Biological Sciences (Concentration: Biochemistry)","date_range":"2000年 - 2004年","activities":"","grade":"3.7/4.0"}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 美国韦恩州立大学，Ph.D. · 2005年 - 2012年 | NESCent · 2009年 | 中国科学技术大学，B.S. · 2000年 - 2004年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Senior Director Senior Vice President SVP 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 宾夕法尼亚州 匹兹堡 远程办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿 美国 纽约 纽约 美国 华盛顿州 西雅图 美国 加利福尼亚 美国 伊利诺伊州 芝加哥 开始日期 我在随便看看，时间可灵活安排 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":"母语"}],"