{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:06:34+08:00","record":{"name":"Minjuan, Emma, Bian","current_title":"Resaerch scientist","current_company":"Stanford University · 全职","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 帕罗奥图","headline":"M.D., Ph.D.. Neuroscientist & Translational Project Leader | Gene & Cell Therapy | Driving CNS Therapeutics from Discovery to IND | Tennis Enthusiast","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/minjuan-emma-bian-1b59b031","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAa7eBkBhCF7WlHZTZtPgG6xJibSH1MFHiw","core_skills":["Receptor Pharmacology","Photo Imaging","Luciferase Assay"],"positions":[{"title":"Resaerch scientist","company":"Stanford University · 全职","date_range":"2018年6月 - 现在","duration":"8 年 4 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 帕罗奥图","description":"• Lead independent research in gene therapy for retinal ganglion cell survival and regeneration, \ndevelopment of lipid magnetic nanoparticle based cellular delivery systems, and microelectrode \narray (MEA)-based functional screening of therapeutic potentials for vision loss, such as \nantibody treatment, gene therapy. \n• Designed and executed translational studies integrating AAV vector design, in vivo validation \nin disease models, and uncovering critical mechanisms underlying vision loss and rescue, and \nlaying the groundwork for clinical therapeutic potentials. \n• Fostered cross-functional collaborations across departments and biotech partners, optimizing \nassay pipelines and validating therapeutic candidates, ultimately accelerating project timelines. \n• Mentored junior scientists and coordinated project milestones, ensuring adherence to \nregulatory and quality standards, and co-authored multiple peer-reviewed publications, \nenhancing the team’s impact in the field.","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Associate","company":"Yueyang Hospital","date_range":"2014年7月 - 2018年6月","duration":"4 年","location":"中国 上海市","description":"• Directed innovative research projects focused on molecular and cellular mechanisms of \nphotoreceptor degeneration, leading to the identification of natural compounds for therapeutic \nefficacy. \n• Developed light-induced photoreceptor degeneration mouse models and streamlined \nmitochondrial analysis workflows, enhancing the ability to investigate degeneration mechanisms \nand potential treatments. \n• Collaborated on groundbreaking discovery projects focused on non-coding RNA and oncology, \ncontributing valuable insights to the intersection of these critical areas. \n• Mentored junior researcher and students, and co-authored multiple publications and patents.","skills":[]},{"title":"Technical Sales Specialist","company":"Life Technologies · 全职","date_range":"2011年11月 - 2014年6月","duration":"2 年 8 个月","location":"中国 上海市","description":"• Managed client engagement across academic, pharma and biotech sectors, providing project \ndesign, proposal support, and technical consultation. \n• Analyzed market trends, coordinated CRO partnerships, and supported integration post- \nacquisition to expand service capabilities.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Associate","company":"Yale University School of Medicine · 全职","date_range":"2010年3月 - 2011年8月","duration":"1 年 6 个月","location":"美国 康乃狄克州 纽黑文","description":"• Investigated molecular mechanisms in ALS progression using advanced histology and gene \nexpression profiling. \n• Supported collaborative projects identifying biomarkers of ALS and co-authored peer- \nreviewed publications.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Resaerch scientist at Stanford University · 2018年 - 现在 | Research Associate at Yueyang Hospital · 2014年 - 2018年 | Technical Sales Specialist at Life Technologies · 2011年 - 2014年 | Postdoctoral Research Associate at Howard Hughes Medical Institute (HHMI) · 2010年 - 2011年 | Postdoctoral Research Associate at Yale University School of Medicine · 2010年 - 2011年","education":[{"school":"复旦大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy",