","date_range":"2022年 - 2025年","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"美国 印第安纳 印第安纳波利斯","description":"Spearheaded advancements in preclinical space to enhance drug discovery.  \nHelped to automate and find new approaches to accelerate discovery, reagents production and deliverables for the therapeutic areas.  \nCollaborated cross-functionally to drive breakthroughs that accelerate development \nCultivated a culture of innovation by mentoring high-performing teams in immunology, neuroscience, metabolic, and RNA-targeted therapeutics.\n\n• Role: Scientific leader in structural biology–driven discovery, uniting protein science, biophysics, structural biology, and structure-based design to advance preclinical assets. \n• Guided cross-functional programs across immunology, metabolic disease, genetic medicine, neuroscience, while beginning to leverage AI and computational approaches to boost translational impact. \n• Studied previously unannotated human hormone peptides through optimized extraction and chromatographic purification from clinical specimens, coupled with de novo crystallization for high-resolution structural elucidation. \n• Drove cross-platform collaboration between SB and NMR, HDX, PeptiDream to uncover peptide hits and elucidate MOA for emerging immunology targets, fueling design of next-generation peptidomimetic and macrocyclic peptide therapeutics. \n• Served as a scientific advisor to cross-functional discovery teams, translating biochemical, structural and biophysical data into actionable design insights in collaboration with medicinal chemistry, computational modeling, and biology groups. \n• Developed nanobody-based and fusion protein engineering strategies to enhance molecular stability and enable crystallization, supporting high-resolution structural characterization of key peptidomimetic immunology targets. \n• Directed development of a novel RNAi research platform, combining X-ray and Cryo-EM methods to design siRNA/mRNA therapeutics. \n• Solved structures, built models, and developed computational and experimental approaches for structural modeling of complex protein–RNA assemblies. \n• Built and led core laboratory and external research capabilities, including strategic CRO partnerships, streamlining program execution and enabling rapid validation of high-priority and pre-portfolio concepts. \n• Directed cross-functional adoption of novel tools, ensuring teams could interpret complex datasets and accelerate project milestones with higher confidence. \n• Provided portfolio-level scientific guidance, presenting data-driven recommendations to internal and external stakeholders to report progress and decisions. \n• Mentored cross-functional teams and cultivated a culture of innovation and execution excellence.","skills":["automation systems","Continuous Improvement","Team Collaboration in Improvement Projects","Executive Management","Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP)","Director level","Project Planning","Business Strategy","Analytical Skills","Decision-Making","Relationship Building","Leadership Development","Strategic Thinking","Communication","Public Speaking","Program Management","Creativity and Innovation","Stakeholder Management","Cross-Functional Team Building","Teaching","Scientific Communications","Problem Solving","Project Leadership","Group Leadership","X-ray crystallography","Biochemistry","Protein Purification","Structural Biology","Crystallography","Crystallization","Bioinformatics","Life Sciences","recombinant DNA technology","Biophysics","Protein Engineering","Science"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Venture Institute Fellow (Cohort 7) at VC Lab · 2026年 - 现在 | Mentor @ VC accelerator at PharmStars · 2026年 - 现在 | Independent Scientific & Biopharma Consultant at Self-Employed · 2026年 - 现在 | Senior Director at Eli Lilly and Company · 2022年 - 2025年 | Board member AbbVie representative at IMCA-CAT · 2018年 - 2022年 | Principal Scientist at AbbVie · 2017年 - 2022年 | Assistant Scientist at Argonne National Laboratory · 2008年 - 2012年 | Scientist at Center for Structural Genomics of Infectious Diseases | Argonne National Laboratory · 2008年 - 2017年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow at Argonne National Laboratory · 2004年 - 2008年 | Postdoc at Montana State University · 2003年 - 2004年 | Biochemist/X-ray Crystallography at Utah State University · 1999年 - 2003年 | Quality Assurance Consultant at Baltic Marine Surveyors Ltd , · 1996年 - 1998年 | Chemical Engineering and Process Optimization grad student at Silesian technical University · 1995年 - 1999年","education":[{"school":"Utah State University","degree":"Ph.D.","field_of_study":"Biochemistry","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":"Advisor John W. Peters"},{"school":"Politechnika Śląska","degree":"M.Sc.","field_of_study":"Chemical Engineering","date_range":"1994年 - 1999年","activities":"","grade":"with honors, as the top student in the program,one of 55 in the class"},{"school":"Medical Vocational College, Gliwice, Poland","degree":"Medical Laboratory Technician","field_of_study":"Analytical medicine, hematology, histology, phlebotomy, microbiology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Utah State University，Ph.D. | Politechnika Śląska，M.Sc. · 1994年 - 1999年 | Medical Vocational College, Gliwice, Poland ，Medical Laboratory Technician | VC Lab · 2026年 - 2026年 | VC Lab · 2026年 - 2026年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Director Senior Director Executive Director Associate VP Vice President 职位性质 全职 兼职 合同制 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 芝加哥地区 纽约地区 美国 加利福尼亚 波士顿地区 远程办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿 美国 San Diego Metropolitan Area 芝加哥地区 纽约地区 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
