{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:11:29+08:00","record":{"name":"邓彩云","current_title":"Vice President & Head of Pharmacology and Preclinical Development","current_company":"BioMed Linkage Tech Co., Limited · 合同","location":"香港特别行政区 香港","headline":"Vice President & Head of Pharmacology and Preclinical Development at BioMed Linkage | One-Stop Access to All CRO and CDMO Services in China","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/biomedlinkage-ellen-deng","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABa9yfEBIwe8Kuppt4nZ3dsFreftFMGLgm4","core_skills":["GLP Audit","GMP Audit","Gene Therapy"],"positions":[{"title":"Vice President & Head of Pharmacology and Preclinical Development","company":"BioMed Linkage Tech Co., Limited · 合同","date_range":"2024年2月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 8 个月","location":"香港特别行政区","description":"","skills":["GLP Audit","GMP Audit","Antibodies","Gene Therapy","Small Molecules","Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP)","Research and Development (R&D)","Good Laboratory Practice (GLP)","Oligonucleotides","ADME","Project Management","Drug Development","Toxicology","Pharmacology","Pre-clinical Studies"]},{"title":"Director, Department of Preclinical Development","company":"Lerna Biopharma · 合同","date_range":"2022年4月 - 2024年1月","duration":"1 年 10 个月","location":"新加坡","description":"※ Directed comprehensive non-clinical IND-enabling studies for siRNA drug development, including pharmacology, ADME, and toxicology, with a strategic focus on liver diseases. \n \n※ Spearheaded the design and execution of pharmacology, ADME, and toxicology studies for pre-clinical candidate (PCC) screening, advancing the pipeline of siRNA therapeutics. \n \n※ Managed collaborations with CDMOs and CROs for modality synthesis, in vivo animal efficacy studies, ADME profiling, and toxicology assessments to support R&D and preclinical projects. \n \n※ Led the scale-up of GalNAc monomer production to kilogram levels and siRNA synthesis to gram levels, working closely with CMC teams across multiple CDMOs to optimize manufacturing processes. \n \n※ Collaborated with the CMC Vice President in conducting GMP audits of CDMOs, playing a pivotal role in efficiently screening and selecting a suitable CDMO for GMP batch production of siRNA drugs.","skills":["Gene Therapy","Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP)","Research and Development (R&D)","Good Laboratory Practice (GLP)","Oligonucleotides","ADME","Project Management","Drug Development","Toxicology","Pharmacology","Pre-clinical Studies"]},{"title":"Senior Project Manager, Department of Preclinical Development,","company":"Hengrui Pharma Co.,Ltd · 合同","date_range":"2019年9月 - 2022年3月","duration":"2 年 7 个月","location":"中国","description":"※ Led the overall non-clinical IND-enabling studies, including pharmacology, ADME, and toxicology, with a primary focus on neurodegenerative diseases, pain, bone metastasis, and androgenetic alopecia. \n \n※ Managed disease model selection and animal species selection, study design, CRO selection, data analysis and interpretation, and study report reviews. \n \n※ Prepared IND documents based on eCTD standards for submission, including M2.4, M2.6, M4, IB, and related documentation. \n \n※ Interacted with regulatory authorities, leading two pre-IND meetings and two Type III meetings with the NMPA. \n \n※ Led the entire preclinical work for seven projects, covering small molecules, monoclonal antibodies, and bispecific antibodies. Four applications were approved, including two multinational approvals, and supported four clinical-stage projects. \n \n※ Drafted over 20 project proposals and feasibility reports, as well as more than 60 drug news reports, successfully facilitating the initiation and drug development of multiple targets. \n \n※ Successfully completed evaluations for two license-in projects and conducted due diligence for one license-out project.","skills":["Antibodies","Gene Therapy","Small Molecules","Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP)","Research and Development (R&D)","Good Laboratory Practice (GLP)","Neuroscience","Oligonucleotides","ADME","Project Management","Drug Development","Toxicology","Pharmacology","Pre-clinical Studies"]},{"title":"Assistant Investigator/Postdoctoral Fellow","company":"Institute of Neuroscience (ION), Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai · 合同","date_range":"2014年8月 - 2019年8月","duration":"5 年 1 个月","location":"中国 上海市","description":"※ Designed and conducted experiments, collecting and analyzing data while ensuring data quality, reproducibility, and thorough documentation. \n \n※ Skilled in electrophysiology and surgical techniques, proficient in multiple whole-cell patch-clamp recordings, in utero electroporation, and stereotaxic injections. \n \n※ Elucidated the molecular mechanism of synaptic specificity among excitatory neurons in the neocortex. Published in eLife on March 12, 2024, titled \"Combinatorial expression of γ-protocadherins regulates synaptic connectivity in the mouse neocortex\". \n \n※ Secured three postdoctoral fellowships and received a grant from China's National Natural Science Foundation. \n \n※ Managed grants by strategizing budget allocations, setting milestones, and efficiently managing resources; fostered local and international collaborations with grant managers and researchers. \n \n※ Reviewed manuscripts for journal publications, presented at conferences, and supervised graduate students and research assistants.","skills":["Electrophysiology","Cell Culture","Molecular Biology","Neuroscience"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Vice President & Head of Pharmacology and Preclinical Development at BioMed Linkage Tech Co., Limited · 2024年 - 现在 | Director, Department of Preclinical Development at Lerna Biopharma · 2022年 - 2024年 | Senior Project Manager, Department of Preclinical Development, at Hengrui Pharma Co.,Ltd · 2019年 - 2022年 | Assistant Investigator/Postdoctoral Fellow at Institute of Neuroscience (ION), Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai · 2014年 - 2019年","education":[{"school":"中国科学院","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Neuroscience","date_range":"2008年 - 2014年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"武汉大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Biotechnology","date_range":"2004年 - 2008年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 中国科学院，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 2008年 - 2014年 | 武汉大学，Bachelor's degree · 2004年 - 2008年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:11:41+08:00","record":{"name":"蔡逸超","current_title":"Bioinformatics Scientist","current_company":"Experimental Drug Development Centre (EDDC) · 全职","location":"新加坡 新加坡","headline":"生物信息 | 深度学习 | 数据科学 | 基因组 | 癌症基因组 | 表观遗传学 | 下一代测序","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/yichao-cai-0a5791112","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABw8VD0ByIkv78gUz8W3twW-wYSndHkDJQQ","core_skills":["Next-generation sequencing data analysis (ChIP-seq","RNA-seq","4C-seq)","Chromatin interaction","Nextflow"],"positions":[{"title":"Bioinformatics Scientist","company":"Experimental Drug Development Centre (EDDC) · 全职","date_range":"2023年12月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 10 个月","location":"新加坡","description":"Drug Discovery | Computational Biology","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Bioinformatics Scientist","company":"Illumina","date_range":"1 年 3 个月","duration":"1 年 3 个月","location":"新加坡 新加坡","description":"Developed and implemented cutting-edge deep learning algorithms to gain insights into RNA splicing biology, aiming to shed light on human genome interpretation.\n\n• Sourced next-generation sequencing data from cancer databases and established robust data analysis pipelines to ensure consistent and clean input data for downstream analysis. \n• Utilized state-of-the-art machine learning frameworks to train models using the processed input data, enabling the exploration of complex patterns and biological differences. \n• Designed and executed in sillico experiments to study model interpretability, facilitating a deeper understanding of the underlying mechanisms. \n• Provided mentoring and knowledge sharing for graduate students in the subjects of bioinformatics, data science and machine learning.","skills":["技能: Bioinformatics • Machine Learning • Deep Learning • Python • PyTorch • R • Cancer Biology • Git • GNU/Linux • BASH • Jupyter • RStudio • Interdisciplinary Collaboration • Nextflow • SGE • High Performance Computing (HPC) • pandas • NumPy • RNA-seq","Bioinformatics","Machine Learning","Deep Learning","Python","PyTorch","R","Cancer Biology","Git","GNU/Linux","BASH","Jupyter","RStudio","Interdisciplinary Collaboration","Nextflow","SGE","High Performance Computing (HPC)","pandas","NumPy","RNA-seq","技能: Bioinformatics • Deep Learning • Python • PyTorch • R • Cancer Biology • GNU/Linux • BASH • Interdisciplinary Collaboration • Nextflow"]},{"title":"Bioinformatics Scientist 2","company":"Illumina","date_range":"1 年 3 个月","duration":"1 年 3 个月","location":"新加坡 新加坡","description":"Developed and implemented cutting-edge deep learning algorithms to gain insights into RNA splicing biology, aiming to shed light on human genome interpretation.\n\n• Sourced next-generation sequencing data from cancer databases and established robust data analysis pipelines to ensure consistent and clean input data for downstream analysis. \n• Utilized state-of-the-art machine learning frameworks to train models using the processed input data, enabling the exploration of complex patterns and biological differences. \n• Designed and executed in sillico experiments to study model interpretability, facilitating a deeper understanding of the underlying mechanisms. \n• Provided mentoring and knowledge sharing for graduate students in the subjects of bioinformatics, data science and machine learning.","skills":["技能: Bioinformatics • Machine Learning • Deep Learning • Python • PyTorch • R • Cancer Biology • Git • GNU/Linux • BASH • Jupyter • RStudio • Interdisciplinary Collaboration • Nextflow • SGE • High Performance Computing (HPC) • pandas • NumPy • RNA-seq","Bioinformatics","Machine Learning","Deep Learning","Python","PyTorch","R","Cancer Biology","Git","GNU/Linux","BASH","Jupyter","RStudio","Interdisciplinary Collaboration","Nextflow","SGE","High Performance Computing (HPC)","pandas","NumPy","RNA-seq","技能: Bioinformatics • Deep Learning • Python • PyTorch • R • Cancer Biology • GNU/Linux • BASH • Interdisciplinary Collaboration • Nextflow"]},{"title":"Bioinformatics Scientist","company":"Vela Diagnostics · 全职","date_range":"2021年4月 - 2022年4月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"新加坡 新加坡","description":"- Managed and maintained in vitro cancer diagnostic products based on next-generation sequencing data.  \n- Spearheaded the development of new product features, expanding upon existing offerings to deliver innovative medical insights that positively impact patient care. \n- Acted as a go-to resource for addressing bioinformatics pipeline queries, providing support to both the internal business development department and external customers.","skills":["Python","R","Cancer Biology","Next-generation sequencing data analysis (ChIP-seq, RNA-seq, 4C-seq)","Git","GNU/Linux","BASH","Project Planning","Customer Service","Project Management","Technical Support","Interdisciplinary Collaboration","Airflow","Databases"]},{"title":"Research Fellow","company":"Cancer Science Institute of Singapore · 全职","date_range":"2019年9月 - 2021年4月","duration":"1 年 8 个月","location":"新加坡","description":"- Formulated research questions for a range of diverse research projects. Engaged in active communication and collaboration within multidisciplinary teams from various universities and backgrounds. \n- Orchestrated the design and construction of robust analytic pipelines for processing and analyzing next-generation sequencing (NGS) data including RNA-seq, ChIP-seq, Hi-C, 4C-seq, etc. \nPerformed data visualization using R and python to present research results in a clear, concise, and visually appealing manner. \n- Maintained and managed high-performance Linux server and data storage in the lab.","skills":["Bioinformatics","Python","R","Epigenetics","Cancer Biology","Next-generation sequencing data analysis (ChIP-seq, RNA-seq, 4C-seq)","Git","GNU/Linux","BASH","Snakemake","Project Management","Chromatin interaction","Interdisciplinary Collaboration","Cancer Genomics","RNA-seq","ChIP-seq"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Bioinformatics Scientist at Experimental Drug Development Centre (EDDC) · 2023年 - 现在 | Senior Bioinformatics Scientist at Illumina · 2022年 - 2023年 | Bioinformatics Scientist 2 at Illumina · 2022年 - 2022年 | Bioinformatics Scientist at Vela Diagnostics · 2021年 - 2022年 | Research Fellow at Cancer Science Institute of Singapore · 2019年 - 2021年","education":[{"school":"新加坡国立大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Bioinformatics in Department of Biological Science","date_range":"2015年 - 2019年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"华中科技大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Bioinformatics","date_range":"2011年 - 2015年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 新加坡国立大学，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2015年 - 2019年 | 华中科技大学，Bachelor's degree · 2011年 - 2015年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Research Fellow Data Scientist Bioinformatics Scientist Computational Biologist Machine Learning Engineer 职位性质 全职 合同制 所在地点 现场办公: 新加坡 中国 上海市 远程办公: 新加坡 新加坡 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:11:53+08:00","record":{"name":"Winson Cai, PhD","current_title":"Scientist II - Immunology (Novel CAR Design)","current_company":"Legend Biotech · 全职","location":"美国 纽约 纽约","headline":"Research Scientist | Cell & Gene Therapy | Immunotherapy","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/winsoncai","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAC5XxJIBj3UdUL3lfskScs030pHaEi0c9hY","core_skills":["Animal Husbandry","Transduction","Assay Development"],"positions":[{"title":"Scientist II - Immunology (Novel CAR Design)","company":"Legend Biotech · 全职","date_range":"2024年11月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 11 个月","location":"","description":"• Develop In Vivo CAR Platforms: Investigate non-viral/viral vector platforms and envelope engineering approaches to achieve targeted CAR transgene delivery into immune effector cells, with a focus on transient expression systems to enhance safety. Establish robust in vivo models and biodistribution analytics to assess efficacy, specificity, and safety. Collaborate across teams to apply synthetic biology, gene editing, and tissue-targeting approaches in the development of off-the-shelf immunotherapies. \n \n•Develop Anti-HvG Candidates: Lead the development of anti-host-versus-graft (HvG) candidates for allogeneic cell-based therapies, focusing on NK cells and gamma-delta (γδ) T cells. Establish efficient evaluation platforms and design next-generation modalities to overcome HvG responses. \n \n•Innovate Cytokine Arming Strategies: Design, screen, and evaluate novel cytokine arming strategies to mitigate toxicity while enhancing the therapeutic efficacy of CAR-engineered NK and γδ T cells.\n\n• Evaluate In vivo CAR-T and γδ T-cell platforms with a focus on scalability, safety, and competitive positioning within the allogeneic cell therapy market.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow","company":"纪念斯隆-凯特琳癌症中心","date_range":"6 年 3 个月","duration":"7 个月","location":"美国","description":"•Preclinical to Clinical Translation: Led the development of a novel, universally applicable armored CAR for solid tumors, advancing towards IND-enabling studies by optimizing antibody binders, linker lengths, and affinity maturation. \n•Toxicity and Expression Profiling: Conducted toxicity assessments and expression profiling using tissue microarray analysis and Retrogenix screening, ensuring safety and precision in CAR-T cell therapies for clinical trials. \n•Master Cell Bank Development: Developed a GMP-compliant master cell bank for scalable CAR-T cell production, crucial for consistent clinical manufacturing. \n•Immunogenicity Assessment: Spearheaded a project on CAR-T cell immunogenicity, utilizing immunological assays and prediction algorithms like NetMHCPan to identify and mitigate immune responses. Contributed to the REFUEL trial (NCT05460533) on second infusion CAR-T therapy in B-ALL, gaining insights into regulatory and manufacturing processes. \n•Research Coordination: Coordinated between preclinical and clinical teams, aligning biospecimen collection with clinical biomarker identification, and ensuring research adherence to HSP, GCP, GLP, and GxP standards.","skills":["技能: Clinical Research • Biomedical Research • Pharmacology • Immunology • Cancer Immunotherapy","Clinical Research","Biomedical Research","Pharmacology","Immunology","Cancer Immunotherapy","技能: Cell Culture • Analytical Skills • Easily Adaptable • Data Analytics • Cellular Assays • Teamwork • ADME • Assay Development • Research Skills • Oncology • Cell Biology • Pharmacology • Immunology • DNA Extraction • Cancer Immunotherapy • Synthetic Biology • Confocal Microscopy • Single Cell Sequencing • Mouse Models • Transduction • Fluorescence Microscopy • Fluorescence • FACS analysis • Cell Lines • Antibodies • Flow Cytometry • Immunohistochemistry • Molecular Cloning • Crispr • Cell Therapy","Cell Culture","Analytical Skills","Easily Adaptable","Data Analytics","Cellular Assays","Teamwork","ADME","Assay Development","Research Skills","Oncology","Cell Biology","DNA Extraction","Synthetic Biology","Confocal Microscopy","Single Cell Sequencing","Mouse Models","Transduction","Fluorescence Microscopy","Fluorescence","FACS analysis","Cell Lines","Antibodies","Flow Cytometry","Immunohistochemistry","Molecular Cloning","Crispr","Cell Therapy"]},{"title":"Ph.D Candidate","company":"纪念斯隆-凯特琳癌症中心","date_range":"6 年 3 个月","duration":"7 个月","location":"美国","description":"•Preclinical to Clinical Translation: Led the development of a novel, universally applicable armored CAR for solid tumors, advancing towards IND-enabling studies by optimizing antibody binders, linker lengths, and affinity maturation. \n•Toxicity and Expression Profiling: Conducted toxicity assessments and expression profiling using tissue microarray analysis and Retrogenix screening, ensuring safety and precision in CAR-T cell therapies for clinical trials. \n•Master Cell Bank Development: Developed a GMP-compliant master cell bank for scalable CAR-T cell production, crucial for consistent clinical manufacturing. \n•Immunogenicity Assessment: Spearheaded a project on CAR-T cell immunogenicity, utilizing immunological assays and prediction algorithms like NetMHCPan to identify and mitigate immune responses. Contributed to the REFUEL trial (NCT05460533) on second infusion CAR-T therapy in B-ALL, gaining insights into regulatory and manufacturing processes. \n•Research Coordination: Coordinated between preclinical and clinical teams, aligning biospecimen collection with clinical biomarker identification, and ensuring research adherence to HSP, GCP, GLP, and GxP standards.","skills":["技能: Clinical Research • Biomedical Research • Pharmacology • Immunology • Cancer Immunotherapy","Clinical Research","Biomedical Research","Pharmacology","Immunology","Cancer Immunotherapy","技能: Cell Culture • Analytical Skills • Easily Adaptable • Data Analytics • Cellular Assays • Teamwork • ADME • Assay Development • Research Skills • Oncology • Cell Biology • Pharmacology • Immunology • DNA Extraction • Cancer Immunotherapy • Synthetic Biology • Confocal Microscopy • Single Cell Sequencing • Mouse Models • Transduction • Fluorescence Microscopy • Fluorescence • FACS analysis • Cell Lines • Antibodies • Flow Cytometry • Immunohistochemistry • Molecular Cloning • Crispr • Cell Therapy","Cell Culture","Analytical Skills","Easily Adaptable","Data Analytics","Cellular Assays","Teamwork","ADME","Assay Development","Research Skills","Oncology","Cell Biology","DNA Extraction","Synthetic Biology","Confocal Microscopy","Single Cell Sequencing","Mouse Models","Transduction","Fluorescence Microscopy","Fluorescence","FACS analysis","Cell Lines","Antibodies","Flow Cytometry","Immunohistochemistry","Molecular Cloning","Crispr","Cell Therapy"]},{"title":"Ph.D Candidate","company":"Weill Cornell Graduate School of Medical Sciences · 全职","date_range":"2018年9月 - 2024年5月","duration":"5 年 9 个月","location":"","description":"","skills":["Cell Culture","Analytical Skills","Easily Adaptable","Data Analytics","Cellular Assays","Teamwork","Assay Development","Research Skills","Oncology","Cell Biology","Immunology","DNA Extraction","Transduction","Fluorescence Microscopy","Fluorescence","FACS analysis","Cell Lines","Antibodies"]},{"title":"Research Technician","company":"Joan & Sanford I. Weill Medical College of Cornell University · 全职","date_range":"2016年7月 - 2018年6月","duration":"2 年","location":"纽约地区","description":"Stem Cell Research: Spearheaded and discovered 12 novel de novo gain-of-function mutations in the FGF-Ras-MAPK signaling pathway, using next-generation sequencing and in vivo. These mutations were found to be associated with advanced paternal age and linked to an increased risk of cancer and autism spectrum disorder (ASD) in offspring. Identified key pathogenic mutations associated with advanced paternal age and linked to 3-4x increased risk of cancer and autism spectrum disorder (ASD). Collaborated with clinical teams in the surgery department to establish a biobank of patient samples for further research on germline mutations. \n-Responsible for animal husbandry, genotyping, surgeries, post-operative care, behavioral testing, sectioning and histology. \n-Perform genomic editting technology such as CRISPR-Cas9 and CRISPR-PITCh system as well as constitutive/inducible knock down system such as Cre-LoxP, shRNA. \n-Perform routine molecular biology laboratory procedures such as, PCR, protein and DNA electrophoresis, cloning, and DNA/RNA extraction. \n-Culturing mammalian cell lines as well as production of Lenti-virus. \n-Perform biochemistry assays such as proliferation/cytotoxicity assay, western blotting, qRT-PCR, FACS/flow cytometry, immunohistochemistry(IHC)/Immunocytochemistry(ICC). \n-Duties in ordering laboratory stocks and management of laboratory supplies including maintaining proper cleanliness and autoclaving appropriate lab equipment.\n\n• Stem Cell Research: Discovered 12 novel de novo gain-of-function mutations in the FGF-Ras-MAPK signaling pathway associated with the paternal age effect, which contributed to a 3-4x increased risk of cancer and autism.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Scientist II - Immunology (Novel CAR Design) at Legend Biotech · 2024年 - 现在 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow at Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center · 2024年 - 2024年 | Ph.D Candidate at Weill Cornell Graduate School of Medical Sciences · 2018年 - 2024年 | Ph.D Candidate at Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center · 2018年 - 2024年 | Research Technician at Joan & Sanford I. Weill Medical College of Cornell University · 2016年 - 2018年 | Research Assistant at Stony Brook University, Pharmacological Science · 2014年 - 2016年 | Laboratory Technician at Stony Brook University · 2013年 - 2016年","education":[{"school":"Weill Cornell Graduate School of Medical Sciences","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Pharmacology","date_range":"2018年 - 2024年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Stony Brook University","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Pharmacology","date_range":"","activities":"活动与社团: Honorary Member of Sigma Beta Honor Society, Recipient of Presidential Scholarship Award, Participant of URECA Summer Research Program, Member of the Stony Brook Undergraduate Pharmacology Society, Recipient of Deans List and Degree with Distinction.","grade":""},{"school":"Bronx High School of Science","degree":"","field_of_study":"","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Weill Cornell Graduate School of Medical Sciences，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2018年 - 2024年 | Stony Brook University，Bachelor's degree | Bronx High School of Science | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Senior Scientist Equity Analyst 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 纽约 纽约 开始日期 我在随便看看，时间可灵活安排 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":false,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:12:04+08:00","record":{"name":"Xiaofeng (Stephen) Cai, MD, PhD","current_title":"Director, Business Development & Partnerships","current_company":"Sanyou Biopharmaceuticals · 全职","location":"波士顿地区","headline":"Scientific Business Development | Advancing Antibody & Peptide Therapeutics | Biologics Discovery & Development | Strategic Partnerships & Licensing","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/xiaofeng-stephen-cai-md-phd-25662328","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAXJf6IBYDJO_kO_o7DafyQgL_hVlFmKXJo","core_skills":["Bispecific Antibodies","Nanobodies","VEGF/VEGFR Signaling"],"positions":[{"title":"Director, Business Development & Partnerships","company":"Sanyou Biopharmaceuticals · 全职","date_range":"2025年4月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 6 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"Lead business development and strategic partnerships across the U.S., working with biotechnology, pharmaceutical, and academic partners to advance biologic therapeutic programs from discovery through preclinical development. \n \nKey areas of collaboration include: \n▪ Antibody Discovery — Fully human antibodies, VHH/nanobodies, immune and synthetic library screening, antibody engineering, humanization and affinity maturation  \n▪ Next-Generation Modalities — Bispecific/multispecific antibodies, cyclic peptides, and discovery support for ADC/AOC and other emerging biologic modalities  \n▪ Protein & Antibody Production — Recombinant antibody/protein expression, CHO/HEK293 production, and stable cell line development  \n▪ Characterization & Optimization — ELISA, SPR/BLI, epitope binning, developability assessment, functional characterization and lead optimization  \n▪ Preclinical Development — Integrated in-vitro and in-vivo evaluation and development support  \n▪ Strategic Partnerships — CRO collaborations, therapeutic asset licensing, co-development and customized partnership models \n \nI work directly with scientists, R&D leaders and biotech executives to understand the scientific and development challenges behind each program and translate them into practical, customized development strategies.","skills":["Bispecific Antibodies","Antibody Engineering","Protein Expression","Licensing","Nanobodies","Pre-clinical Development","Protein Engineering","Peptide Therapeutics","Biologics","Strategic Partnerships","Business Development","Antibody Discovery","Drug Discovery"]},{"title":"Sr. Technical Account Manager","company":"GenScript · 全职","date_range":"2022年5月 - 2025年3月","duration":"2 年 11 个月","location":"","description":"Managed and developed biotech, pharmaceutical, academic, and research accounts by providing customized life-science solutions across gene synthesis, peptides, oligonucleotides, mRNA, proteins, antibodies, viral vectors, and cell-line services. \n \n• Developed new business opportunities and strategic customer relationships across a broad portfolio of research and development services. \n• Translated scientific project requirements into customized technical solutions, proposals, and project strategies. \n• Managed complex projects and coordinated cross-functional teams to support successful project execution and long-term customer partnerships. \n• Identified emerging customer needs and cross-platform opportunities across biologics and advanced therapeutic modalities.\n\n• Identify/develop opportunities and provide services to customers from US Central area (23 states), with primary focus on these territories (OH, MI, WI, WV) to ensure completion of defined task/activities for sales goal achievement. \n• Represent the company at conferences, trade shows, and networking events by giving presentations to promote services, enhance brand visibility, and expand the market reach. \n• Generate customized project proposals and price quotes, identify cross-sell/upsell opportunities, and close sales successfully by employing excellence, efficiency, and value. \n• Provide regular reports on key projects, territory development activities, performance metrics, and market insights into senior management in Central team and Company meetings. \n• Work closely with other commercial teams (inside sales manager, FAS or market team) to Prospect / visit / follow up with customers, address questions, and secure contracts to achieve sustainable growth in sales and business development. \n• Collaborate closely with internal teams (e. \n• , production / logistic / financial teams) to ensure seamless project execution and client satisfaction. \n• Provide training for junior team members and help new members to adapt efficiently.","skills":["Account Management","Life Sciences","Technical Sales","Business Development","Antibody Expression","Project Management","Biotechnology"]},{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"Oklahoma Medical Research Foundation · 全职","date_range":"2017年 - 2022年","duration":"5 年 1 个月","location":"Oklahoma City, Oklahoma","description":"Led translational research in cancer biology, inflammation, endocytosis, and cell signaling, with a particular focus on epsin/LUBAC/NF-κB signaling and breast cancer development. \n \nConducted mechanistic and preclinical studies using cellular, transgenic, and patient-derived xenograft models, contributing to peer-reviewed publications and therapeutic target validation.\n\n• Identified a target molecule whose expression is upregulated in cancers and associated with poor relapse-free survival in cancer patients, then further demonstrate that this molecule is essential for cancer development and metastasis by coordinately regulating tumor intrinsic and microenvironmental signaling. \n• In addition, demonstrate how activated protein C (APC), as a serine protease, inhibits inflammation by acting in endothelial and immune cells; Isolate PBMCs and PMNs from whole blood of patients with autoimmune diseases; Culture and differentiate induced pluripotent stem cells (iPSCs) towards hematopoietic progenitor cells (HPCs) and neutrophils, evaluate the differentiation by Flow cytometry (BD LSR II or Aurora), and check surface markers, cytokines in supernatants by Luminex assays. \n• Establish some experimental assay protocols; Supervise junior scientists and technicians.","skills":["Cell Signaling","Pre-clinical Studies","Drug Target Identification","Translational Research","Cancer Biology","Inflammation","Immunology"]},{"title":"Senior Research Fellow","company":"University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center · 全职","date_range":"2016年 - 2017年","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"Oklahoma City, Oklahoma","description":"Identify an immunoregulatory molecule regulating bone remodeling by coordinately modulating osteoclastogenesis and osteoblastogenesis; Establish some experimental assay protocols; Supervise technicians and rotating students","skills":["Research Supervision","Experimental Design","Bone Biology","Translational Research","Cell Biology","Immunology"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Director, Business Development & Partnerships at Sanyou Biopharmaceuticals · 2025年 - 现在 | Sr. Technical Account Manager at GenScript · 2022年 - 2025年 | Senior Scientist at Oklahoma Medical Research Foundation · 2017年 - 2022年 | Senior Research Fellow at University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center · 2016年 - 2017年 | Research Fellow at Harvard Medical School · 2015年 - 2016年 | Postdoctoral Fellow at Oklahoma Medical Research Foundation · 2009年 - 2015年","education":[{"school":"中山大学","degree":"Ph.D.","field_of_study":"Pharmacology","date_range":"2004年 - 2009年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Hubei School of Medicine","degree":"Bachelor of Clinical Medicine","field_of_study":"Clinical Medicine","date_range":"1999年 - 2004年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 中山大学，Ph.D. · 2004年 - 2009年 | Hubei School of Medicine，Bachelor of Clinical Medicine · 1999年 - 2004年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"