{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:12:15+08:00","record":{"name":"Zheng C.","current_title":"SELECTED INDEPENDENT RESEARCH PROJECTS","current_company":"University of California ‑ San Francisco","location":"旧金山湾区","headline":"AI scientist | Drug Discovery & Development","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhengcai","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAARqTWQBD4SY_7KeQQihDC_bu4KPjZzs1OY","core_skills":["PharmaKB - The Pharmaceutical KnowledgeBase","Genetic Epidemiology","Host-pathogen Interactions"],"positions":[{"title":"SELECTED INDEPENDENT RESEARCH PROJECTS","company":"University of California ‑ San Francisco","date_range":"2025年 - 现在","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"","description":"• Drug Discovery & Translational Development: Completed graduate‑level training spanning the drug discovery and development pipeline, including target identification, hit discovery, lead optimization, preclinical evaluation, and clinical development strategies. \n• Pharmacometrics &Model‑InformedDrugDevelopment: Applied computational pharmacology approaches to evaluate pharmacokinetics (PK), pharmacodynamics (PD), ADMETproperties, pharmacogenomics, and candidate selection using quantitativemodeling to supportmodel‑informed drug development and dose optimization. \n• AI‑Enabled Computational Toxicology: Developed an agentic system for computational toxicology prediction by implementing a data extrac‑tion pipeline and applying structure–activity relationship (SAR) and quantitative structure–activity relationship (QSAR) models. \n• Evaluatedmachine learning algorithms for toxicity prediction and interpreted model performance. \n• RWD/RWE Mining: Applied natural language processing, large language models, and multimodal clinical data integration approaches to analyze real‑world evidence fromdiverse clinical data sources (integrating biomedical literature, electronic health records, and clinical trial data, claims data and registries) for target identification and drug repurposing. \n• Systems Pharmacology & Multi‑Omics: Applied systems biology and multi‑omics integration approaches to identify potential safety liabilities (avoidome) and support target prioritization in translational drug discovery. \n• Clinical Development&Regulatory Science: Prepared regulatory‑style documentation and experimental development plans encompassing first‑in‑human study design, dose selection, proof‑of‑concept studies, pivotal trial design, and benefit–risk assessment. \n• Digital Pathology & Medical Imaging: Gained hands‑on experience in multimodal study design and machine learning approaches for digital pathology and neuroimaging analysis through graduate coursework and ongoing research. \n• Computational Immunology: Gained hands‑on experience applying established R and Python workflows to analyze single‑cell, spatial transcrip‑tomic, and multi‑modal datasets, including scRNA‑seq, CITE‑seq, ATAC‑seq, TCR/BCR repertoire sequencing, Xenium, and MERFISH, as well as CyTOF and flow cytometry, with emphasis on quality control, integration, visualization, and biological interpretation. \n• Built reproducible R/Python workflows for single‑cell immune profiling across scRNA‑seq, CITE‑seq, ATAC‑seq, and spatial transcriptomic datasets, identifying immune cell pop‑ulations and disease‑associated transcriptional programs.","skills":[]},{"title":"Staff Scientist","company":"Thermo Fisher Scientific · 全职","date_range":"2016年 - 2024年","duration":"8 年 1 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"• Led multi‑modal genomic data analyses across 3+ platforms (CRISPR experiments, Perturb‑seq, NGS, microarray, and PCR) over eight years, sup‑porting translational research pipelines that informed data‑driven decision‑making across multiple clinical and translational research programs. \n• Developed andmaintained scalable, reproducible bioinformatics pipelines in a Linux‑based environment, integrating large‑scale genomic datasets and analytical tools into production‑quality research workflows, supporting multiple translational biobank programs. \n• Supported the development of variant discovery and functional annotation workflows that enabled interpretation of clinically and biologically relevant genomic alterations for translational research applications. \n• Recognized with Thermo Fisher appreciation awards for technical leadership and collaborative contributions to multidisciplinary genomics and bioinformatics initiatives. \n• Explored applications of generative AI and large language models (LLMs) for scientific analysis, workflow automation, and biomedical knowledge extraction through participation in the GenAI Ambassadors Program. \n• Leveraged GitHub Copilot and LLM‑based agentic system to accelerate pipeline development, code refactoring, documentation, and exploratory analysis. \n• Applied machine learning and statistical methods to large‑scale clinico‑genomic datasets, generating insights relevant to biomarker discovery and translational research.","skills":["Large Language Models (LLM)","Computational Biology","Bioinformatics","R","Machine Learning","Python","Cloud Computing"]},{"title":"BiOiNFORMATiCS PROGRAMMER ANALYST III","company":"Affymetrix Biotech Shanghai Ltd.","date_range":"2014年 - 2015年","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"","description":"• Authored and contributed to internal scientific reports and 4+ posters on ethnicity inference, population‑scale somatic mutation screening, and development of multi‑ethnic genomic variant reference resources. \n• Performed large‑scale genomic analyses across microarray and multiplex sequencing platforms, supporting research applications in biobanking, immuno‑oncology, microbiome science, and agricultural biotechnology. \n• Advised technical support teams on genomic and transcriptomic assay design strategies for translational research and agricultural biotechnology applications. \n• Contributed to technical documentation andworkflow standardization efforts for genomic data analysis pipelines supporting translational research and genomics product workflows. \n• Partnered with 10+ academic collaborators to optimize genomic data processing pipelines and resolve technical bottlenecks in translational and clinical genomics projects.","skills":[]},{"title":"SENiOR POSTDOCTORAL FELLOW","company":"University of Washington","date_range":"2012年 - 2013年","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"","description":"• Applied survival analysis and multi‑modal clinical–molecular integration methods to investigate prognostic biomarkers and candidate molecular drivers relevant to disease progression. \n• Designed and implemented a virtual population control framework leveraging local ancestry inference to enable population‑scale genomic analy‑ses, improving power and precision in disease‑associated gene mapping. \n• Strengthened quantitative research expertise through graduate‑level training in biostatistics, machine learning, and clinical research methods. \n• Presented research findings at scientific conferences and prepared an NIH K99/R00 grant application focused on translational genomics and com‑putational disease modeling.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | SELECTED INDEPENDENT RESEARCH PROJECTS at University of California ‑ San Francisco · 2025年 - 现在 | Staff Scientist at Thermo Fisher Scientific · 2016年 - 2024年 | BiOiNFORMATiCS PROGRAMMER ANALYST III at Affymetrix Biotech Shanghai Ltd. · 2014年 - 2015年 | SENiOR POSTDOCTORAL FELLOW at University of Washington · 2012年 - 2013年 | GRADUATE RESEARCH ASSiSTANT at University of Utah & University of Washington · 2007年 - 2011年","education":[{"school":"University of California, San Francisco","degree":"","field_of_study":"AIDD","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"美国华盛顿大学","degree":"Postdoctoal","field_of_study":"Biostatistics","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"University of Utah","degree":"PhD","field_of_study":"Biomedical Informatics","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | University of California, San Francisco | 美国华盛顿大学，Postdoctoal | University of Utah，PhD | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Research Scientist Computational Scientist Data Scientist Machine Learning Researcher Artificial Intelligence Researcher 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 旧金山湾区 远程办公: 旧金山湾区 开始日期 我在随便看看，时间可灵活安排 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:12:27+08:00","record":{"name":"Xinming Cai","current_title":"Senior Director, Immunology","current_company":"Kymera Therapeutics · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 贝尔蒙","headline":"Drug Hunter Specializing in Immune Diseases","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/xinming-cai-2174686","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAEirTMB7VCB0deVqLWgTFZjoscLSZDr0VM","core_skills":["Pharmaceutical Industry","antibody drug discovery","Anti-inflammatory"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Director, Immunology","company":"Kymera Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2024年5月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 5 个月","location":"","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Director","company":"Viridian Therapeutics, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2022年5月 - 2024年5月","duration":"2 年 1 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 沃尔瑟姆","description":"• Reporting to the CSO, leading B cell targeting cellular and in vivo pharmacology studies. \n• Project leader for an autoimmune biologics project, from discovery to candidate nomination within 12 months. \n• Partnering with and overseeing studies conducted by CROs.","skills":[]},{"title":"Distinguished Scientist","company":"Sanofi","date_range":"5 年","duration":"2 年 4 个月","location":"波士顿地区","description":"• Headed an autoimmunity research group. \n• Managed a team of 3 Ph. \n• D and 2 BA/MS scientists. \n• Led pre-clinical efforts for SAR441344 (Anti-CD40L mAb) from pre-clinical to phase 2. \n• Contributed as a pre-clinical team member for SAR444336 (Non-beta IL2 synthorin for inflammatory indications). \n• Successfully led a co-stimulatory receptor antagonist Ab project from target nomination to pre-clinical candidate. \n• Managed the small molecular weight nucleic acid sensor modulator discovery platform, including two pipeline projects and exploratory studies. \n• Acted as the research representative for Sanofi's lupus strategic initiative and drafted the research section of the company-wide 'win in lupus' proposal. \n• Founded the Sanofi novel targeted-degradation biologics initiative and drafted the immunology target ID strategy. \n• Led the lupus target triaging initiative and compiled the target list for Business Development. \n• Represented the research department in evaluating and performing due diligence on multiple external assets, such as Kymera IRAK4 PROTAC. \n• Championed Sanofi/Harvard collaboration projects in chemical biology (with Dr. \n• Sun Hur) and functional genomics (with Dr. \n• Alex Marson). \n• Served as a representative on the Sanofi/Imagine Institute collaboration joint steering committee for phenotypical screening and biomarker discovery. \n• Represented Sanofi in the collaboration with ImmuNext for clinical biomarker discovery.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Principal Scientist","company":"Sanofi","date_range":"5 年","duration":"2 年 4 个月","location":"波士顿地区","description":"• Headed an autoimmunity research group. \n• Managed a team of 3 Ph. \n• D and 2 BA/MS scientists. \n• Led pre-clinical efforts for SAR441344 (Anti-CD40L mAb) from pre-clinical to phase 2. \n• Contributed as a pre-clinical team member for SAR444336 (Non-beta IL2 synthorin for inflammatory indications). \n• Successfully led a co-stimulatory receptor antagonist Ab project from target nomination to pre-clinical candidate. \n• Managed the small molecular weight nucleic acid sensor modulator discovery platform, including two pipeline projects and exploratory studies. \n• Acted as the research representative for Sanofi's lupus strategic initiative and drafted the research section of the company-wide 'win in lupus' proposal. \n• Founded the Sanofi novel targeted-degradation biologics initiative and drafted the immunology target ID strategy. \n• Led the lupus target triaging initiative and compiled the target list for Business Development. \n• Represented the research department in evaluating and performing due diligence on multiple external assets, such as Kymera IRAK4 PROTAC. \n• Championed Sanofi/Harvard collaboration projects in chemical biology (with Dr. \n• Sun Hur) and functional genomics (with Dr. \n• Alex Marson). \n• Served as a representative on the Sanofi/Imagine Institute collaboration joint steering committee for phenotypical screening and biomarker discovery. \n• Represented Sanofi in the collaboration with ImmuNext for clinical biomarker discovery.","skills":[]},{"title":"Investigator III","company":"诺华","date_range":"9 年 6 个月","duration":"1 年","location":"波士顿地区","description":"• Headed an innate immunity target discovery lab. \n• Managed a team of 3 BA/MS scientists. \n• Led a project to develop innate immune antagonists for treating autoimmune diseases and cancer. \n• Led a project to identify novel innate immune pathway drug targets using functional genomics and phenotypic screening, and validated their potential disease indications. \n• Led microbiome research to investigate the interplay between the microbiome and innate immunity. \n• Directed a GPCR project aimed at treating IBD. \n• Co-led a project to develop drugs protecting islet beta cells under stress conditions for diabetes treatment. \n• Led the identification of the first small molecular weight Pyrin inflammasome activator. \n• Made primary contributions to identifying the target and mechanism of action of apilimod, a clinically evaluated IL12/23 antagonist. \n• Contributed to a team working on low molecule immune potentiators for cancer immunotherapy and vaccine adjuvant development.","skills":[]},{"title":"Investigator II","company":"诺华","date_range":"9 年 6 个月","duration":"1 年","location":"波士顿地区","description":"• Headed an innate immunity target discovery lab. \n• Managed a team of 3 BA/MS scientists. \n• Led a project to develop innate immune antagonists for treating autoimmune diseases and cancer. \n• Led a project to identify novel innate immune pathway drug targets using functional genomics and phenotypic screening, and validated their potential disease indications. \n• Led microbiome research to investigate the interplay between the microbiome and innate immunity. \n• Directed a GPCR project aimed at treating IBD. \n• Co-led a project to develop drugs protecting islet beta cells under stress conditions for diabetes treatment. \n• Led the identification of the first small molecular weight Pyrin inflammasome activator. \n• Made primary contributions to identifying the target and mechanism of action of apilimod, a clinically evaluated IL12/23 antagonist. \n• Contributed to a team working on low molecule immune potentiators for cancer immunotherapy and vaccine adjuvant development.","skills":[]},{"title":"Investigator I","company":"诺华","date_range":"9 年 6 个月","duration":"1 年","location":"波士顿地区","description":"• Headed an innate immunity target discovery lab. \n• Managed a team of 3 BA/MS scientists. \n• Led a project to develop innate immune antagonists for treating autoimmune diseases and cancer. \n• Led a project to identify novel innate immune pathway drug targets using functional genomics and phenotypic screening, and validated their potential disease indications. \n• Led microbiome research to investigate the interplay between the microbiome and innate immunity. \n• Directed a GPCR project aimed at treating IBD. \n• Co-led a project to develop drugs protecting islet beta cells under stress conditions for diabetes treatment. \n• Led the identification of the first small molecular weight Pyrin inflammasome activator. \n• Made primary contributions to identifying the target and mechanism of action of apilimod, a clinically evaluated IL12/23 antagonist. \n• Contributed to a team working on low molecule immune potentiators for cancer immunotherapy and vaccine adjuvant development.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Associate","company":"诺华","date_range":"9 年 6 个月","duration":"1 年","location":"波士顿地区","description":"• Headed an innate immunity target discovery lab. \n• Managed a team of 3 BA/MS scientists. \n• Led a project to develop innate immune antagonists for treating autoimmune diseases and cancer. \n• Led a project to identify novel innate immune pathway drug targets using functional genomics and phenotypic screening, and validated their potential disease indications. \n• Led microbiome research to investigate the interplay between the microbiome and innate immunity. \n• Directed a GPCR project aimed at treating IBD. \n• Co-led a project to develop drugs protecting islet beta cells under stress conditions for diabetes treatment. \n• Led the identification of the first small molecular weight Pyrin inflammasome activator. \n• Made primary contributions to identifying the target and mechanism of action of apilimod, a clinically evaluated IL12/23 antagonist. \n• Contributed to a team working on low molecule immune potentiators for cancer immunotherapy and vaccine adjuvant development.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Senior Director, Immunology at Kymera Therapeutics · 2024年 - 现在 | Senior Director at Viridian Therapeutics, Inc. · 2022年 - 2024年 | Distinguished Scientist at Sanofi · 2020年 - 2022年 | Senior Principal Scientist at Sanofi · 2017年 - 2020年 | Investigator III at Novartis Institutes for BioMedical Research (NIBR) · 2016年 - 2017年 | Investigator II at Novartis Institutes for BioMedical Research (NIBR) · 2012年 - 2016年 | Investigator I at Novartis Institutes for BioMedical Research (NIBR) · 2010年 - 2012年 | Postdoctoral Associate at Novartis Institutes for BioMedical Research (NIBR) · 2007年 - 2009年 | University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill - Ph.D. Student · 2003年 - 2007年","education":[{"school":"美国北卡罗来纳大学教堂山分校","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Dept. of Cell and Developmental Biology","date_range":"2003年 - 2007年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"华东理工大学","degree":"Master of Science (M.S.)","field_of_study":"Dept. of Applied Biology Science","date_range":"2000年 - 2003年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"华东理