{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:12:39+08:00","record":{"name":"Zheng (David) Cai","current_title":"Principal Scientist","current_company":"勃林格殷格翰","location":"美国 康乃狄克州 里奇菲尔德","headline":"Principal Scientist Biotherapeutics Discovery","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/cloneren","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAADbCewBl-g5MVAzgMiHmMrvZywQJ7i1yj4","core_skills":["Biotherapeutics Discovery","soft agar assay","UV-Vis"],"positions":[{"title":"Principal Scientist","company":"勃林格殷格翰","date_range":"7 年 5 个月","duration":"3 年 5 个月","location":"美国 康乃狄克州 里奇菲尔德","description":"Team Lead and Project Lead in Biotherapeutics Discovery  \n \nExploratory-> Lead Identification -> Lead Optimization -> SoCG -> SOD","skills":["技能: Team Motivation • Lead Generation • Project Management • Biologics • Biotherapeutics Discovery • Team Management • Antibodies • Protein Engineering • Biophysics","Team Motivation","Lead Generation","Project Management","Biologics","Biotherapeutics Discovery","Team Management","Antibodies","Protein Engineering","Biophysics","技能: Lead Generation • Project Management • Biologics"]},{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"勃林格殷格翰","date_range":"7 年 5 个月","duration":"3 年 5 个月","location":"美国 康乃狄克州 里奇菲尔德","description":"Team Lead and Project Lead in Biotherapeutics Discovery  \n \nExploratory-> Lead Identification -> Lead Optimization -> SoCG -> SOD","skills":["技能: Team Motivation • Lead Generation • Project Management • Biologics • Biotherapeutics Discovery • Team Management • Antibodies • Protein Engineering • Biophysics","Team Motivation","Lead Generation","Project Management","Biologics","Biotherapeutics Discovery","Team Management","Antibodies","Protein Engineering","Biophysics","技能: Lead Generation • Project Management • Biologics"]},{"title":"Co-founder","company":"SternGreene Pharmaceuticals","date_range":"2013年 - 2019年5月","duration":"6 年 5 个月","location":"Narberth, PA","description":">>>Leading in-depth research and development collaboration with an international pharmaceutical company; Developed the 4th generation EGFR kinase inhibitors which targets the drug-resistant EGFR mutation. \n>>>Managed FTEs of a chemistry CRO; reviewed weekly reports, attended monthly meeting and provided scientific guidance  \n>>>Spin off virtual biotech startups from academia setting; Prepared slides and presented to angel and venture investors; Negotiated the research collaboration and licence agreement with pharma companies.","skills":["Project Management","Biologics"]},{"title":"Research Assistant Professor","company":"美国宾夕法尼亚大学","date_range":"14 年 2 个月","duration":"3 年 7 个月","location":"Philadelphia","description":">>>Leading a team of junior postdocs, research scientist and research technicians. \n>>>Humanized a mouse monoclonal antibody in preparation for human therapeutic applications; optimized antibody production in CHO-S cells; verified the binding of humanzied antibody to antigen. This project is now partially supported by SANOFI. \n>>>Engineered a mutant of platelet factor 4 and developed a new diagnostc kit for Heparin-Induced Thrombocytopenia (HIT) which improved specificity of the current FDA-approved HIT kit.  \n>>>Co-developed small molecule TNF inhibitors to to treat inflammatory conditions such as rheumatoid arthritis \n>>>Co-developed a small molecule PCSK9 inhibitor for treatment of Hyperlipidemia","skills":["技能: Team Motivation • Project Management • Biologics","Team Motivation","Project Management","Biologics","技能: Project Management • Biologics"]},{"title":"Senior Research Investigator/Research Associate","company":"美国宾夕法尼亚大学","date_range":"14 年 2 个月","duration":"3 年 7 个月","location":"Philadelphia","description":">>>Leading a team of junior postdocs, research scientist and research technicians. \n>>>Humanized a mouse monoclonal antibody in preparation for human therapeutic applications; optimized antibody production in CHO-S cells; verified the binding of humanzied antibody to antigen. This project is now partially supported by SANOFI. \n>>>Engineered a mutant of platelet factor 4 and developed a new diagnostc kit for Heparin-Induced Thrombocytopenia (HIT) which improved specificity of the current FDA-approved HIT kit.  \n>>>Co-developed small molecule TNF inhibitors to to treat inflammatory conditions such as rheumatoid arthritis \n>>>Co-developed a small molecule PCSK9 inhibitor for treatment of Hyperlipidemia","skills":["技能: Team Motivation • Project Management • Biologics","Team Motivation","Project Management","Biologics","技能: Project Management • Biologics"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Researcher","company":"美国宾夕法尼亚大学","date_range":"14 年 2 个月","duration":"3 年 7 个月","location":"Philadelphia","description":">>>Leading a team of junior postdocs, research scientist and research technicians. \n>>>Humanized a mouse monoclonal antibody in preparation for human therapeutic applications; optimized antibody production in CHO-S cells; verified the binding of humanzied antibody to antigen. This project is now partially supported by SANOFI. \n>>>Engineered a mutant of platelet factor 4 and developed a new diagnostc kit for Heparin-Induced Thrombocytopenia (HIT) which improved specificity of the current FDA-approved HIT kit.  \n>>>Co-developed small molecule TNF inhibitors to to treat inflammatory conditions such as rheumatoid arthritis \n>>>Co-developed a small molecule PCSK9 inhibitor for treatment of Hyperlipidemia","skills":["技能: Team Motivation • Project Management • Biologics","Team Motivation","Project Management","Biologics","技能: Project Management • Biologics"]},{"title":"Graduate Research Assistant","company":"University of Science and Technology of China","date_range":"1998年9月 - 2004年12月","duration":"6 年 4 个月","location":"","description":">>>Expertise in molecular cloning, protein expression, protein purification  \n>>>Expression, purification and stability study of ADR6 protein via Spectroscopic methods(CD, FTIR); investigated ADR6 protein folding by deuterium exchange experiment  \n>>>Expressed, purified, 15N/13C-labelled Homo sapiens glia maturation factor beta and determined its solution structure using hetero-nuclear NMR spectroscopy \n>>>Determined the solution structures of BmBKTx1, BmKX and BmK38— three new BKCa channel blockers by homo-nuclear NMR. Used protein-toxin docking simulation to study the recognition of the scorpion Toxin BmKX with the potassium ion channels.","skills":["Biologics"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Principal Scientist at Boehringer Ingelheim · 2023年 - 现在 | Senior Scientist at Boehringer Ingelheim · 2019年 - 2023年 | Research Assistant Professor at University of Pennsylvania · 2015年 - 2019年 | Co-founder at SternGreene Pharmaceuticals · 2013年 - 2019年 | Senior Research Investigator/Research Associate at University of Pennsylvania · 2010年 - 2015年 | Postdoctoral Researcher at University of Pennsylvania · 2005年 - 2010年 | Graduate Research Assistant at University of Science and Technology of China · 1998年 - 2004年","education":[{"school":"University of Pennsylvania School of Medicine","degree":"Postdoctoral Training","field_of_study":"Structure-based drug discovery","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"中国科学技术大学","degree":"Ph.D.","field_of_study":"Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"中国科学技术大学","degree":"B.S.","field_of_study":"Biology, Special Class for the Gifted Young(SCGY)","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | University of Pennsylvania School of Medicine，Postdoctoral Training | 中国科学技术大学，Ph.D. | 中国科学技术大学，B.S. | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Principal Scientist Associate Director Director Senior Principal Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿 波士顿地区 美国 宾夕法尼亚州 美国 新泽西州 费城地区 远程办公: 美国 开始日期 我在随便看看，时间可灵活安排 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:12:49+08:00","record":{"name":"Hongliang Cai","current_title":"Senior Director, Clinical Pharmacology and Drug Metabolism","current_company":"Sumitomo Pharma America, Inc. · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","headline":"Senior Director, Clinical Pharmacology at Boston Biomedical, Inc.","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hongliang-cai-7235203","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAACcUgsBZigYO5dODKCe9aZOadky9UAR0zs","core_skills":["Peptides","Biomarkers","Assay Development"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Director, Clinical Pharmacology and Drug Metabolism","company":"Sumitomo Pharma America, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2023年7月 - 现在","duration":"3 年 3 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 马波罗","description":"Support Phase I/II oncology programs TP-3654 for MF and DSP-5336 for AML \no Develop and execute measurable strategies to push the developmental programs from Phase 1 to POC and establish clin pharm strategies to support NDA via traditional and accelerated approval pathways. \no Prepare clin pharm documentations for regulatory submission of IND, NDA, and/or MMA, and respond queries related to clin pharm and drug metabolism. \no Plan and execute on-going PK sample analysis and characterization, cold metabolite profiling, PK formulation comparability, food effect, DDI studies in patients and NHV. \no Work with vendors/CROs to deliver Pop PK modeling and PK/PD M&S in support of regulatory submission and therapeutic dose justification. \nLead the transition programs from preclin to clin as the Clin Pharm/DMPK rep \no Collaborate with the DSP and DCI to ensure sufficient non-clinical studies conducted and data collected for successful IND and clinical program. \no Identify suitable CROs to develop and validate human PK assays and put in place the contracts for the work. \no Develop SIMCYP models and utilize them to project human PK for the DSP compounds, model FIH doses, and assess any DDI liabilities using probe substrates and inhibitors. \nMentor junior Ph.D. clinical pharmacology scientists and supervise consultants.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director-Senior Director, Clinical Pharmacology and Drug Metabolism","company":"Boston Biomedical, Inc. (Sumitomo Pharma subsidiary) · 全职","date_range":"2018年10月 - 2023年6月","duration":"4 年 9 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"Support Napabucasin NDA \no Contribute to the gap analysis of Napa clin pharm package \no Lead the risk assessment of napa ADME (AKR/CR, OAT2, and potential interaction with paclitaxel via CYP2C8). \no Contribute to clinical PK/ADME reports/CSRs and reporting of human mass balance study \no Utilize SIMCYP to model potential DDI liabilities involving CYPs and drug transporters to anticipate regulatory questions \nSupport Phase I/II oncology programs TP-3654 for MF and DSP-5336 for AML \no Develop and execute measurable strategies to push the developmental programs from Phase 1 to POC and establish clin pharm strategies to support NDA via traditional and accelerated approval pathways. \no Prepare clin pharm documentations for regulatory submission of IND, NDA, and/or MMA, and respond queries related to clin pharm and drug metabolism. \no Plan and execute on-going PK sample analysis and characterization, cold metabolite profiling, PK formulation comparability, food effect, DDI studies in patients and NHV. \no Work with vendors/CROs to deliver Pop PK modeling and PK/PD M&S in support of regulatory submission and therapeutic dose justification. \n• Lead the transition programs from preclin to clin as the Clin Pharm/DMPK rep \no Collaborate with the DSP and DCI to ensure sufficient non-clinical studies conducted and data collected for successful IND and clinical program. \no Identify suitable CROs to develop and validate human PK assays and put in place the contracts for the work. \no Develop SIMCYP models and utilize them to project human PK for the DSP compounds, model FIH doses, and assess any DDI liabilities using probe substrates and inhibitors. \nLead the three Tolero clinical programs as the Clin Pharm/DMPK rep \no Conduct gap analysis on the DMPK package of IND for the three clinical programs and implement the strategies to conduct the necessary DMPK studies to ensure the success of the programs moving forward. \n• Mentor junior Ph.D. clinical pharmacology scientists and supervise consultants.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director, nonclinical & clinical pharmacology","company":"Ziopharm Oncology · 全职","date_range":"2013年10月 - 2018年10月","duration":"5 年 1 个月","location":"1 1st Ave, Parris Building 34, Boston, MA 02129","description":"• • Participate on multidisciplinary drug development teams, plan, design, analyze, interpret and report in vitro and in vivo non-clinical and clinical ADME/pharmacology studies of IL-12 program (Ad-RTS-IL-12 + veledimex) gene therapy.  \no Lead all Clinical Pharmacology/ADME studies to support BLA for glioma and breast cancer and annual IB update. \n Design, analyze, interpret and report clinical pharmacology data, including SAD, MAD, food effect, drug interaction studies from Phase I of veledimex in healthy subjects. \n Analyze and interpret dose exposure-response relationship across three Phase I/II clinical trials of Ad-RTS-IL-12 + veledimex in melanoma, breast cancer and GBM subjects. Prepare and finalize clinical study reports summarizing all the exposure-response relationship (PK/PD) data as the leading author \n Author PK and clinical pharmacology sections of BLA and perform gap analysis on the data package and identify critical clinical pharmacology studies to be completed for successfully BLA filing \n Oversee assay development and establish validated PK/PD assays for preclinical and clinical use, including transferring, monitoring and managing assays with CROs \no Support non-clinical pharmacology studies in 4T1 breast cancer murine model and GL261 orthotopic murine glioma model to establish efficacy, define dose and schedule of Ad-RTS-mIL-12 + veledimex in clinic, and guide clinical study design. \no Interact with FDA reviewers by answering questions relating to PK/ADME and clinical pharmacology. \n• Support drug development programs of CAR-T cell therapy using Sleeping Beauty transposon system. Plan, design, analyze, interpret and report clinical pharmacology data (propagation and persistence of CAR-T, PD biomarkers, and efficacy) from Phase I/II studies in cancer patients \n• Lead clinical PK/ADME studies supporting darinaparsin NDA, in collaboration with Solasia. \n• Mentor a senior BS/MS scientist","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Principle Scientist","company":"Aileron Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2011年10月 - 2013年","duration":"1 年 4 个月","location":"Cambridge, MA","description":"• • Support in vitro and in vivo ADME/TK and PK and PK/PD studies. \n• Represent PK discipline to support Aileron’s development candidates (ALRN-6924 (P53) & ALRN-5281) by projecting human PK, modeling PK/PD data to derive human efficacious concentration, and establishing human doses in FIH. Contribute to clinical study protocols, implement bioanalytical strategies for PK and PD measurements, review, analyze and model Phase I human PK/clinical pharmacology data, review and comment on clinical study reports, simulate human dose regimens and contribute to the overall design of Phase Ib/II studies. \n• Lead the interactions with CRO’s to execute all in vitro and in vivo ADME/TK/PK and PK/PD studies required for regulatory filing. \n• Represent DMPK on all Aileron’s platform discovery teams. \n• Mentor a Ph.D. senior scientist","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Senior Director, Clinical Pharmacology and Drug Metabolism at Sumitomo Pharma America, Inc. · 2023年 - 现在 | Director-Senior Director, Clinical Pharmacology and Drug Metabolism at Boston Biomedical, Inc. (Sumitomo Pharma subsidiary) · 2018年 - 2023年 | Director, nonclinical & clinical pharmacology at Ziopharm Oncology · 2013年 - 2018年 | Senior Principle Scientist at Aileron Therapeutics · 2011年 - 2013年 | Group Lead at Alnylam Pharmaceuticals · 2010年 - 2011年 | Principle Scientist - Senior Principle Scientist at Pfizer Inc · 2000年 - 2010年 | Research Fellow at Vanderbilt University Medical Center · 1998年 - 2000年","education":[{"school":"Wake Forest University","degree":"Ph.D.","field_of_study":"Physical Organic Chemistry","date_range":"1994年 - 1998年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Wake Forest University，Ph.D. · 1994年 - 1998年 | 保存到项目 | 将Hongliang保存到项目 | 发消息给Hongliang | Hongliang Cai的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
