{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:16:02+08:00","record":{"name":"Na Cai","current_title":"Executive Director Biostatistics","current_company":"4D Molecular Therapeutics","location":"芝加哥地区","headline":"Executive Director Biostatistics","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/na-cai-88911924","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAUAHqkBLac_IHidB1YgKFlpHjCL8RuKJSI","core_skills":["Pharmaceutical Industry","SAS Programming","Perl"],"positions":[{"title":"Executive Director Biostatistics","company":"4D Molecular Therapeutics","date_range":"2026年1月 - 现在","duration":"9 个月","location":"","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Director Biostatistics","company":"Sarepta Therapeutics","date_range":"2023年2月 - 2026年1月","duration":"3 年","location":"","description":"• Biometrics program lead for the siRNA targeted therapy program for Idiopathic Pulmonary Fibrosis (IPF), Gene therapy programs for Non-Sarc Limb Girdle Muscular Dystrophy (LGMD), RNA targeted therapy programs (PMO and PPMO) for Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy (DMD); ELEVIDYS Gene Therapy program for DMD. \n• Represents biostatistics, statistical programming, and data management for multiple programs, leading and overseeing biometrics team for study and program level deliverables. \n• Represented biometrics function for various regulatory interactions, e. \n• g. \n• , FDA late-cycle meeting for ELEVIDYS, advisory committee meeting for ELEVIDYS Accelerated Approval BLA, type C meeting on PPMO, numerous FDA requests for information for ELEVIDYS and PPMO programs, pre-IND interaction for non-sarc LGMD program, etc. Successfully led the biometrics team in supporting the accelerated approval of ELEVIDYS BLA, achieving several milestone readouts for the PPMO and PMO programs, preparing for the PPMO pre-NDA, PMO pre-sNDA/sNDA and executing studies from Phase I to Phase III across multiple programs, etc. Represented biometrics function for multiple external asset evaluations and represents biometrics function for the internalization and development of the IPF program. \n• Led several initiatives on biometrics related SOPs and processes, etc. People manager with experience in hiring and overseeing direct reports. \n• Successfully hired and onboarded new biostatisticians. \n• Overseeing projects and performance of direct reports.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director Biostatistics","company":"Astellas Pharma","date_range":"7 年 2 个月","duration":"1 年 5 个月","location":"芝加哥地区","description":"• Global statistical lead for compounds in multiple areas, including rare genetic disease, pain, vaccine, and imaging agent. \n• Represented biostatistician, statistical programming, and data management in core team. \n• Provided statistical and strategic inputs for global development plans, study designs, regulatory submissions and interactions, etc. Led the biostatistics and statistical programming team for statistical deliverables at study and program level. \n• People manager with direct reports. \n• Experienced in hiring and onboarding new biostatisticians. \n• Oversaw projects and performance of direct reports. \n• Lead for statistical work groups. \n• Led and collaborated with Go/No Go work group members to provide guidance and support for quantitative decision making (QDM) within Biostatistics. \n• Provided example programs (in R and SAS) and user guide documents for QDM, and developed an interactive user interface (R shiny app) for QDM. \n• Supported the development of QDM processes for multiple programs. \n• Led and worked with rare disease work group members to share knowledge on drug development in rare disease within Biostatistics. \n• Other selected activities. \n• Experienced in due diligence for in-licensing and out-licensing compounds. \n• Proposed initiatives for intern projects and provided supervision and mentorship for interns. \n• Provided statistical support as a study statistician for late phase clinical trials in pain.","skills":[]},{"