{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:16:58+08:00","record":{"name":"Zhen Cai","current_title":"Senior Scientist","current_company":"Pfizer · 全职","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","headline":"Senior Scientist","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhen-cai-6b431633","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAb80WgBQGZa-muQO-W_xakdEOThjmQvwfo","core_skills":["Kinase study","Ubiquitination study","Protein Post-modification"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"Pfizer · 全职","date_range":"2024年5月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 5 个月","location":"La Jolla","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"Zentalis Pharmaceuticals · 全职","date_range":"2021年4月 - 2024年5月","duration":"3 年 2 个月","location":"San Diego Metropolitan Area","description":"I have joined Zentalis Pharmaceuticals since April 2021 after my ten years` academic research experience. I always have a strong desire to use my knowledge and expertise to improve the public health of the whole society. Zentalis provided my a great platform to understand the process of drug development, from assay design, target validation, compound optimization to clinical trial design. I am taking care of two projects related to DNA damage responses and DNA repair signals. My efforts will be focusing on the exploration of any potential synthetic lethality strategy and the development of small molecules, PROTAC degraders or Molecular glues for cancer treatment.\n\n• Industrial Research Experience 1. \n• Pro-apoptotic strategy for cancer therapy --- PROTAC based degraders As biology lead, I have contributed to the SAR process, MOA study as well as the preclinical toxicity evaluation of Bcl-xL degrader program. \n• The lead candidates have been nominated in 2022. \n• A) Developed in vitro ternary complex assay to evaluate the ability of compounds to incorporate the E3 ligases and substrates. \n• B) Established the cellular assay to assess the protein degradation including WB, JESS, Elisa. \n• C) Investigated the cellular efficacy and platelet toxicity. \n• D) Explored potential synergistic strategy by the combination of existing therapeutic regimens in various cancer models. \n• E) Designed and conducted MOA study to understand the kinetics of the degraders and evaluate the cellular apoptosis. \n• F) Independently managed CRO scientists in the design, development, and implementation of in vitro assays for the advancement of the program. \n• G) Co-ordinated with CRO to investigate the in vivo efficacy as well as PK/PD studies. \n• Develop small molecules and degraders to target Ras-driven cancers by limiting MAPK signal Institution: Department of Discovery Biology, Zentalis Pharmaceuticals As biology lead, I have initiated the target validation efforts, and built several tiers of in vitro assessments from biochemical assays to cellular efficacy assays to advance the candidate selection. \n• A) Incorporated multiple genetic tools including SiRNAs and CRISPR to proceed target validation efforts. \n• B) Advanced SAR process by independently managing CRO scientists to develop in vitro assays including SPR, HTRF to assess the interactions between the targets and small molecules as well as pERK alphaLISA to monitor the perturbations of MAPK signal. \n• C) Developed 3D culture model to evaluate the cellular efficacy of the candidates. \n• D) Established platform to assess protein degradation upon degraders. \n• E) Explored any potential synergistic interactions within MAPK signal as well as between MAPK signal and other signals including DNA damage response, metabolic adaptation etc. F) Co-ordinated with CRO to investigate the in vivo efficacy for both single treatment as well as combo treatment. \n• 3. \n• Synthetic lethal strategy for cancer therapy by potentiating DNA Damage --- Small molecule and degrader based DNA repair modulators As the key biologist, I have introduced both genetic and pharmacological tools to identify the novel synthetic lethal factors and developed small molecules or degraders to tackle HR defect tumors. \n• A) Developed novel Nanoluc based reporter platforms to individually investigate the efficiency of HR, NHEJ and TMEJ repair pathways. \n• B) Explored potential synthetic lethal factors with HR deficiency by Crispr tools. \n• C) Validated any synthetic lethal relationships with most state of art techniques to support the early stage of drug development. \n• D) Established both cellular and biochemical models to evaluate the efficacy of small molecule inhibitors and degraders. \n• E) Advanced the MOA study and biomarker identification, explored combination strategy for Zentalis Wee1 inhibitor-Azenosertib.","skills":[]},{"title":"Assistant Professor","company":"Wake Forest Baptist Cancer Center · 全职","date_range":"2018年8月 - 2021年4月","duration":"2 年 9 个月","location":"美国 北卡罗来纳州 温斯顿塞勒姆","description":"From Aug 2018, I am promoted as an assistant professor due to the outstanding performance for last three years. Currently, my research interests mainly focus on signal transduction, posttranslational modification especially phosphorylation and ubiquitination pathway, epigentic regulation as well as metabolic modulation during cancer development with particular emphasis on tumor metastasis and drug resistance. So far, I have published 17 papers mostly on high impact journals including Cell, Nature Cell biology, Molecular Cell, Nature Communication, Journal of Experimental Medicine, Cancer Research, Molecular and Cellular Proteomics, Seminars in Cancer Biology and etc.","skills":[]},{"title":"Instructor","company":"Wake health Baptist medical Center · 全职","date_range":"2015年8月 - 2018年8月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"美国 北卡罗来纳州 温斯顿塞勒姆","description":"I was recruited as an instructor from Aug 2015 to Aug 2018 at Wake Forest Baptist Cancer Center after my four years postdoctor training at MD Anderson Cancer Center. During this period, I mainly worked on how cell metabolism rewiring affects cancer initiation, progression and metastasis. In the meanwhile I also help regulate the whole lab and in charge of training fresh people.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Senior Scientist at Pfizer · 2024年 - 现在 | Senior Scientist at Zentalis Pharmaceuticals · 2021年 - 2024年 | Assistant Professor at Wake Forest Baptist Cancer Center · 2018年 - 2021年 | Instructor at Wake health Baptist medical Center · 2015年 - 2018年 | Postdoctoral Fellow at MD Anderson Cancer Center · 2011年 - 2015年","education":[{"school":"Institution of Nutritional Science, Shanghai institutes for biological science, Chinese Academy of S","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (PhD)","field_of_study":"Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Cancer biology","date_range":"2005年 - 2011年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"复旦大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree of biology science","field_of_study":"Biology/Biological Sciences, General","date_range":"2001年 - 2005年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Shanghai High School","degree":"","field_of_study":"","date_range":"1994年 - 2001年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Institution of Nutritional Science, Shanghai institutes for biological science, Chinese Academy of S，Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) · 2005年 - 2011年 | 复旦大学，Bachelor's degree of biology science · 2001年 - 2005年 | Shanghai High School · 1994年 - 2001年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Senior Scientist Principal Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 中国 上海市 美国 San Diego Metropolitan Area 美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":""}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
