{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:22:09+08:00","record":{"name":"Yu Cao","current_title":"Managing Director","current_company":"CADA Biosciences · 自雇","location":"波士顿地区","headline":"Immunologist / In Vivo CGT / Preclinical Development / Program Management","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/clay-yu-cao","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACqtmrABrhFBftvioV0l0u-VBNKMlrBJMpA","core_skills":["biotech strategy","IND-enabling","cell adoptive transfer"],"positions":[{"title":"Managing Director","company":"CADA Biosciences · 自雇","date_range":"2025年9月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"波士顿地区","description":"Preclinical development & Regulatory strategy  \nChina CRO/CDMO collaboration and IIT strategy \nBiotech strategy; Competitive landscape intelligence \nTechnology evaluation and due diligence","skills":["biotech strategy","Program Evaluation","Leadership"]},{"title":"Editorial Advisory Board Member","company":"BioInsights","date_range":"2023年7月 - 现在","duration":"3 年 3 个月","location":"","description":"Editorial Advisor for Cell & Gene Therapy Insights (https://www.insights.bio/cell-and-gene-therapy-insights), an online, open-access, peer-reviewed journal with an interdisciplinary, translational focus on all aspects of the cell and gene therapy field.","skills":["Immunology"]},{"title":"Head of Drug Discovery","company":"GenEditBio Limited · 全职","date_range":"2025年4月 - 2026年6月","duration":"1 年 3 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"Head of Drug Discovery at GEB: Led Drug Discovery and Pharmacology/Toxicology Departments. Provide strategic leadership for portfolio establishment, project management and therapeutic DP development. \nExecutive Manager at Zingen Therapeutics (U.S. site): support regulatory affairs, clinical development, and global BD activities. \nLed IND-enabling activities for multiple early- and late-stage programs (in vivo CAR-T, in vivo gene editing projects in multiple systems), overseeing IND preparation, submission, and regulatory interactions. Led lead optimization and early stage strategy definition. Successfully secured FDA clearance and initiated global Phase 1/2 clinical trials.\n\n• Lead and manage Drug Discovery and Pharmacology/Toxicology departments, overseeing organizational strategy, portfolio prioritization and cross-functional pipeline programs. \n• Serve as key decision maker for candidate selection, resource allocation, external partnerships, development prioritization, and preclinical investment strategy. \n• Direct multidisciplinary scientific teams and external CRO/CDMO partners across discovery, translational research, GLP toxicology, IND-enabling studies, and early clinical planning. \n• Oversee operational management of the US site, including organizational coordination, team development, milestone management, budgeting discussions, and strategic planning. \n• Lead development of in vivo CAR-T and other non-viral delivery platform programs. \n• Manage cross-border collaborations with Chinese and US-based stakeholders. \n• Co-lead business development initiatives including technology evaluation, partnership discussions, external scientific presentations, and strategic collaboration opportunities. \n• Coordinate preparation for regulatory interactions including pre-IND and IND submissions while aligning internal teams and external vendors to achieve development milestones.","skills":["Program Evaluation","IND-enabling","Investigational New Drug Application (IND)","Clinical Study Design","Drug Discovery","Team Management","Project Management","Pre-clinical Studies","Team leadership","Immunology","Leadership"]},{"title":"Associate Director, Pharmacology, Preclinical Development","company":"Tessera Therapeutics","date_range":"2022年3月 - 2025年4月","duration":"3 年 2 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"Preclinical Development Unit Head and In Vivo Pharmacology Principal Investigator. Leading pre-clinical in vivo projects for the POCs of Tessera's Gene writing and re-writing modalities, and delivery systems (LNP) in developing novel Gene and Cell therapies.\n\n• Built and led an in vivo pharmacology and translational science teams to support preclinical development for gene writing platform and in vivo cell and gene therapy projects. \n• During company reorganization, make pipeline and resource allocation prioritization and execute “change management” strategies to keep processes meet expectation. \n• Designed and interpreted in vivo studies integrating efficacy, PK/PD and toxicity endpoints in rodent (naïve and humanized) and NHP models. \n• Partnered with CMC, regulatory and clinical teams to support IND-enabling development and regulatory readiness. \n• Contributed to pre-IND/INTERACT documentation. \n• Managed CROs and external collaborators to execute pharmacology and safety studies. \n• Support business team and act as key technology representatives in business activities.","skills":["IND-enabling","Investigational New Drug Application (IND)","Drug Discovery","Team Management","Project Management","Pre-clinical Studies","Drug development","Team leadership","Immunology","Leadership","Gene Therapy"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Managing Director at CADA Biosciences · 2025年 - 现在 | Editorial Advisory Board Member at BioInsights · 2023年 - 现在 | Head of Drug Discovery at GenEditBio Limited · 2025年 - 2026年 | Associate Director, Pharmacology, Preclinical Development at Tessera Therapeutics · 2022年 - 2025年 | Scientist, Immunology at Agios Pharmaceuticals · 2020年 - 2022年 | Research Scientist, Immunology at Moffitt Cancer Center · 2017年 - 2019年 | Postdoctoral Researcher, Immunology, Neurology at Augusta University · 2014年 - 2017年","education":[{"school":"Harvard Business School Online","degree":"","field_of_study":"Team Management and Leadership","date_range":"2023年 - 2024年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"The Academy of Military Science","degree":"Doctor of Philosoph