{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:22:22+08:00","record":{"name":"peirang cao","current_title":"Scientist II","current_company":"Perceptive Inc. · 全职","location":"美国","headline":"Translational Oncology Scientist | Preclinical Strategy | Targeted Radiopharmaceutical & Translational Pharmacology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/peirangcao-boston789","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABCq098Btfz5a0joyU5Hl-9sxxh_5zCznCs","core_skills":["xenograft modeling","Oncology research","Radioligand Binding","cell internalization"],"positions":[{"title":"Scientist II","company":"Perceptive Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2024年10月 - 2025年11月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 尼德姆","description":"Continued scientific leadership across sponsor-driven oncology and targeted radiopharmaceutical programs following organizational transition from Invicro to Perceptive. Focus areas included translational biology, radioligand pharmacology, PK/PD, biodistribution, and study interpretation supporting preclinical decision making. \nLed oncology and supported targeted radiopharmaceutical studies across PK/PD, efficacy, and biodistribution. \nParticipated in study design discussions and translational recommendations. \nContributed scientific leadership across assay execution and cross-functional study delivery.","skills":["Oncology research","Radioligand Binding, cell internalization","in vitro pharmacology","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Pre-clinical Studies","Radioligand Binding","Multi-color Flow Cytometry"]},{"title":"Scientist II","company":"Invicro","date_range":"3 年 9 个月","duration":"1 年 10 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 尼德姆","description":"Contributed to sponsor-driven oncology and targeted radiopharmaceutical programs through translational biology, radioligand pharmacology, and preclinical study execution. Applied integrated in vitro and in vivo approaches to evaluate target biology, pharmacologic activity, biodistribution, and translational relevance across candidate evaluation and program decision making. \nEstablished and optimized oncology pharmacology platforms including CDX and syngeneic tumor models to support efficacy, PK/PD, biodistribution, and translational assessment across radiopharmaceutical programs. \n• Designed and executed radioligand biology workflows including receptor binding, competitive displacement, internalization kinetics, target engagement, and ligand characterization to support biological evaluation of radiolabeled therapeutics. \n• Conducted preclinical characterization across targeted radiopharmaceutical modalities including antibody radioconjugates, peptide ligands, and small-molecule targeting platforms. \n• Supported studies utilizing multiple radionuclide platforms including Ac-225 and Lu-177 with integration of biological assays, imaging-supported endpoints, biodistribution analysis, and translational interpretation. \n• Developed and optimized immunoreactive fraction (IRF), radioligand qualification, and assay workflows to assess biological integrity and target-specific performance of radiolabeled test articles. \n• Applied flow cytometry, ex vivo tissue analysis, cellular labeling, and mechanistic biology approaches to support pharmacodynamic evaluation and study interpretation. \n• Participated in sponsor and internal scientific discussions supporting study design, experimental prioritization, data review, and translational recommendations across oncology programs. \n• Mentored junior scientists and coordinated activities across in vitro and in vivo workflows to improve study quality, reproducibility, and delivery.","skills":["技能: xenograft modeling • Oncology research • Radioligand Binding, cell internalization • in vitro pharmacology • In vivo pharmacology • Cross-functional Team Leadership • Pre-clinical Studies • Radiolabeling of CAR-T cells and immune cells • Radioligand Binding • Cell cultures • Multi-color Flow Cytometry • Immunology","xenograft modeling","Oncology research","Radioligand Binding, cell internalization","in vitro pharmacology","In vivo pharmacology","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Pre-clinical Studies","Radiolabeling of CAR-T cells and immune cells","Radioligand Binding","Cell cultures","Multi-color Flow Cytometry","Immunology","技能: xenograft modeling • Oncology research • Molecular Biology • Radioligand Binding, cell internalization • in vitro pharmacology • In vivo pharmacology • Pre-clinical Studies • Radiolabeling of CAR-T cells and immune cells • Radioligand Binding • Cell cultures","Molecular Biology"]},{"title":"Scientist I","company":"Invicro","date_range":"3 年 9 个月","duration":"1 年 10 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 尼德姆","description":"Contributed to sponsor-driven oncology and targeted radiopharmaceutical programs through translational biology, radioligand pharmacology, and preclinical study execution. Applied integrated in vitro and in vivo approaches to evaluate target biology, pharmacologic activity, biodistribution, and translational relevance across candidate evaluation and program decision making. \nEstablished and optimized oncology pharmacology platforms including CDX and syngeneic tumor models to support efficacy, PK/PD, biodistribution, and translational assessment across radiopharmaceutical programs. \n• Designed and executed radioligand biology workflows including receptor binding, competitive displacement, internalization kinetics, target engagement, and ligand characterization to support biological evaluation of radiolabeled therapeutics. \n• Conducted preclinical characterization across targeted radiopharmaceutical modalities including antibody radioconjugates, peptide ligands, and small-molecule targeting platforms. \n• Supported studies utilizing multiple radionuclide platforms including Ac-225 and Lu-177 with integration of biological assays, imaging-supported endpoints, biodistribution analysis, and translational interpretation. \n• Developed and optimized immunoreactive fraction (IRF), radioligand qualification, and assay workflows to assess biological integrity and target-specific performance of radiolabeled test articles. \n• Applied flow cytometry, ex vivo tissue analysis, cellular labeling, and mechanistic biology approaches to support pharmacodynamic evaluation and study interpretation. \n• Participated in sponsor and internal scientific discussions supporting study design, experimental prioritization, data review, and translational recommendations across oncology programs. \n• Mentored junior scientists and coordinated activities across in vitro and in vivo workflows to improve study quality, reproducibility, and delivery.","skills":["技能: xenograft modeling • Oncology research • Radioligand Binding, cell internalization • in vitro pharmacology • In vivo pharmacology • Cross-functional Team Leadership • Pre-clinical Studies • Radiolabeling of CAR-T cells and immune cells • Radioligand Binding • Cell cultures • Multi-color Flow Cytometry • Immunology","xenograft modeling","Oncology research","Radioligand Binding, cell internalization","in vitro pharmacology","In vivo pharmacology","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Pre-clinical Studies","Radiolabeling of CAR-T cells and immune cells","Radioligand Binding","Cell cultures","Multi-color Flow Cytometry","Immunology","技能: xenograft modeling • Oncology research • Molecular Biology • Radioligand Binding, cell internalization • in vitro pharmacology • In vivo pharmacology • Pre-clinical Studies • Radiolabeling of CAR-T cells and immune cells • Radioligand Binding • Cell cultures","Molecular Biology"]},{"title":"Senior Research Associate","company":"Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center","date_range":"2018年2月 - 2021年2月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"Boston, MA","description":"Conducted interdisciplinary translational research integrating disease models, biomarker evaluation, imaging technologies, and ex vivo pharmacology to investigate inflammatory and early disease mechanisms and support translational research initiatives. \nSelected Contributions \n• Designed and established translational research platforms including ex vivo human biopsy culture, 3D organoid systems, and disease-relevant animal studies to strengthen preclinical–clinical alignment. \n• Supported development and application of advanced optical and confocal imaging approaches for noninvasive detection and characterization of early disease states in Barrett’s esophagus and translational clinical studies. \n• Investigated mechanisms of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) and therapeutic response using animal and ex vivo tissue systems, including evaluation of cytokine signaling and immune-associated pathways. \n• Conducted translational pharmacology and biomarker studies investigating melanin-concentrating hormone (MCH) signaling in gastrointestinal inflammation and fibrosis. \n• Performed molecular and cellular characterization using qPCR, multiplex cytokine profiling, multi-parameter flow cytometry, protein analysis, and integrated biological interpretation across tissue and biopsy-derived samples. \n• Applied ex vivo tissue pharmacology approaches to evaluate biological activity and mechanism of action across patient-derived and preclinical systems. \n• Collaborated across clinical, engineering, and external research teams supporting translational studies, grant activities, and clinical research execution. \nRepresentative Platforms \nEx Vivo Human Tissue | Barrett’s Esophagus | IBD | Translational Imaging | Biomarker Discovery | Organoid Models | Flow Cytometry | Multiplex Analysis | Translational Pharmacology","skills":["Oncology research","Molecular Biology","in vitro pharmacology","In vivo pharmacology","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Pre-clinical Studies","3D Cell Culture","Multiplex cytokine analysis","CRISPR","Cell cultures","Project Management","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)","Multi-color Flow Cytometry","Immunology","Immunofluorescence","Clinical Trials","Expression vector construction","Biochemistry","Energy metabolism","Cell Biology","Protein degradation, UPP","liposome preparation"]},{"title":"Principal Investigator / Professor","company":"Jiangnan University · 全职","date_range":"2013年10月 - 2017年12月","duration":"4 年 3 个月","location":"常州-无锡-苏州地区","description":"Established and led an independent academic research program focused on nutritional biology, metabolic regulation, and physiological responses to nutrition and food-processing interventions through integrated in vivo and molecular approaches. \nSelected Contributions \n• Founded and developed an interdisciplinary laboratory investigating nutritional science, metabolism, and translational physiology. \n• Designed and led preclinical research programs evaluating biological effects of dietary lipids, oxidized oils, and food-processing technologies on obesity, metabolic function, inflammation, and tissue physiology. \n• Established rodent disease and nutrition models integrating physiological phenotyping, molecular biology, and biomarker-driven assessment. \n• Applied integrated biological approaches including gene expression analysis, immune characterization, histology, and molecular profiling to investigate mechanisms underlying nutritional and metabolic responses. \n• Directed research strategy across grant development, experimental design, publication planning, trainee development, and collaborative initiatives. \n• Supervised undergraduate, Master’s, and doctoral trainees and developed collaborations across academic and industry partners. \nSelected Outcomes \n• Generated peer-reviewed publications and intellectual property supporting advances in nutritional biology and food-related translational research. \nRepresentative Platforms \nTranslational Physiology | Nutritional Biology | Metabolic Disease | Biomarker Discovery | Gene Regulation | Preclinical Research | Scientific Leadership","skills":["Molecular Biology","In vivo pharmacology","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Cell cultures","Project Management","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)","Immunofluorescence","Biochemistry","Energy metabolism","Cell Biology","Nutrition","Lipid Metabolism","liposome preparation"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Scientist II at Perceptive Inc. · 2024年 - 2025年 | Scientist II at Invicro · 2023年 - 2024年 | Scientist I at Invicro, A Konica Minolta Company · 2021年 - 2023年 | Senior Research Associate at Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center · 2018年 - 2021年 | Principal Investigator / Professor at Jiangnan University · 2013年 - 2017年 | Research Fellow / Associate at Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center · 2003年 - 2013年 | Research Affiliate at Roswell Park Comprehensive Cancer Center · 1999年 - 2003年","education":[{"school":"Universität des Saarlandes","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","date_range":"1996年 - 1999年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"山东大学","degree":"Master's degree","field_of_study":"Microbiology","date_range":"1985年 - 1987年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"山东师范大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Biology","date_range":"1980年 - 1984年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Universität des Saarlandes，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 1996年 - 1999年 | 山东大学，Master's degree · 1985年 - 1987年 | 山东师范大学，Bachelor's degree · 1980年 - 1984年 | Harvard Catalyst, Certificate Clinical and Translational Research training · 2019年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Senior Scientist Principal Scientist 职位性质 全职 合同制 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English and Chinese","proficiency":""}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:22:33+08:00","record":{"name":"Minghui Cao","current_title":"Scientist, II","current_company":"Regulus Therapeutics · 全职","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","headline":"Researcher in Translational Biology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/minghui-cao-348498109","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABtNUOgBLCCW5eRr_n5pE4ZZRv5i5Ya4BeU","core_skills":["Transduction","Immunoprecipitation","Flow Cytometry"],"positions":[{"title":"Scientist, II","company":"Regulus Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2024年6月 - 2026年7月","duration":"2 年 2 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","description":"●     Generated translational biomarker data supporting clinical advancement of Farabursen (anti-miR-17) in ADPKD, contributing to the program value that supported acquisition of Regulus by Novartis.  \n \n●     Authored and critically reviewed clinical biomarker report to support documentation preparation for company-agency meetings.  \n \n●     Led the development of version II PC1/PC2 urine biomarker assay by cooperating within the internal team and managing the external CROs to enable the assessment of target engagement and pharmacodynamics (PD) of Farabursen in future clinical trials.  \n \n●     Expanded the translational biomarker strategy with the implementation of exploratory studies on various platform technologies: serum proteomics, plasma metabolomics and urine exosomal miRNAs profiling and transcriptomics.\n\n• Advanced the development of version II PC1/PC2 urine biomarker assay to support key translational aspects of farabursen in future clinical trials. \n• Expanded the translational biomarker strategy with the implementation of exploratory studies on various platform technologies.","skills":[]},{"title":"Assistant Project Scientist","company":"UC San Diego School of Medicine","date_range":"7 年 11 个月","duration":"4 年 8 个月","location":"La Jolla, California, United States","description":"●       Implemented comprehensive translational research with in vitro functional genomic models, xenograft and PDX breast cancer mouse models, exploring and validating the function of breast-cancer-EVs-capsulated miR-122 in regulating insulin secretion. Gathered and interpreted solid data enabling the publication of first-authored article in journal Nature Cell Biology 2022.  \n \n●       Plentiful experiences of drug administration routes and formulation selection with in vivo models to explore therapeutic potentials of validated targets by 1, intravenous administration of large particles through tail vein injection; 2, orally administrating small molecules; 3, subcutaneously implanting sustained-release pellet; 4, applying oligonucleotides inhibitor or siRNAs through IP injection.  \n \n●       Profound experiences of ex vivo models setup and assay development, covering the isolation and culture of primary pancreatic islets to develop ex vivo glucose stimulated insulin secretion (GSIS) assay, isolating and culturing mouse primary lung fibroblast cells to develop intracellular Ca2+ response assay, and the culture of mouse primary liver cells to conduct glucose uptake assay. \n \n●       Deeply profiled the microRNA contents in exosome that were isolated from breast cancer patients serum. Validated CD24 as the protein biomarker of breast cancer derived exosome.  \n \n●       Considerable experience in endocrinology with the focus on HPA axis (hypothalamus, pituitary gland and adrenal gland). Deeply participated in dissecting the factors of regulating CRH transcription and glucocorticoid receptor signaling.","skills":["技能: Bioreactor • Mechanism Of Action Studies • Flow Cytometry • Protein Expression • Crispr • Transduction • Mouse Models • Molecular Biology • Molecular Cloning • Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR) • Immunohistochemistry","Bioreactor","Mechanism Of Action Studies","Flow Cytometry","Protein Expression","Crispr","Transduction","Mouse Models","Molecular Biology","Molecular Cloning","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)","Immunohistochemistry","技能: High Throughput Screening • Mouse Handling • Endocrinology • Obesity Research • Diabetes • Tissue Culture • Reverse Transcription Polymerase Chain Reaction (RT-PCR) • Biology • Molecular Biology","High Throughput Screening","Mouse Handling","Endocrinology","Obesity Research","Diabetes","Tissue Culture","Reverse Transcription Polymerase Chain Reaction (RT-PCR)","Biology"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Researcher","company":"UC San Diego School of Medicine","date_range":"7 年 11 个月","duration":"4 年 8 个月","location":"La Jolla, California, United States","description":"●       Implemented comprehensive translational research with in vitro functional genomic models, xenograft and PDX breast cancer mouse models, exploring and validating the function of breast-cancer-EVs-capsulated miR-122 in regulating insulin secretion. Gathered and interpreted solid data enabling the publication of first-authored article in journal Nature Cell Biology 2022.  \n \n●       Plentiful experiences of drug administration routes and formulation selection with in vivo models to explore therapeutic potentials of validated targets by 1, intravenous administration of large particles through tail vein injection; 2, orally administrating small molecules; 3, subcutaneously implanting sustained-release pellet; 4, applying oligonucleotides inhibitor or siRNAs through IP injection.  \n \n●       Profound experiences of ex vivo models setup and assay development, covering the isolation and culture of primary pancreatic islets to develop ex vivo glucose stimulated insulin secretion (GSIS) assay, isolating and culturing mouse primary lung fibroblast cells to develop intracellular Ca2+ response assay, and the culture of mouse primary liver cells to conduct glucose uptake assay. \n \n●       Deeply profiled the microRNA contents in exosome that were isolated from breast cancer patients serum. Validated CD24 as the protein biomarker of breast cancer derived exosome.  \n \n●       Considerable experience in endocrinology with the focus on HPA axis (hypothalamus, pituitary gland and adrenal gland). Deeply participated in dissecting the factors of regulating CRH transcription and glucocorticoid receptor signaling.","skills":["技能: Bioreactor • Mechanism Of Action Studies • Flow Cytometry • Protein Expression • Crispr • Transduction • Mouse Models • Molecular Biology • Molecular Cloning • Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR) • Immunohistochemistry","Bioreactor","Mechanism Of Action Studies","Flow Cytometry","Protein Expression","Crispr","Transduction","Mouse Models","Molecular Biology","Molecular Cloning","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)","Immunohistochemistry","技能: High Throughput Screening • Mouse Handling • Endocrinology • Obesity Research • Diabetes • Tissue Culture • Reverse Transcription Polymerase Chain Reaction (RT-PCR) • Biology • Molecular Biology","High Throughput Screening","Mouse Handling","Endocrinology","Obesity Research","Diabetes","Tissue Culture","Reverse Transcription Polymerase Chain Reaction (RT-PCR)","Biology"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Fellow","company":"City of Hope","date_range":"2014年10月 - 2016年6月","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 杜阿尔特","description":"Led in dissecting and processing mouse liver, adrenal glands, WAT, BAT and skeletal muscle tissues within several internal collaborative projects. Gained profound experiences with RNA extraction from animal tissues, RT-qPCR, WB and IHC to validate target protein expression in tissue samples. \n \nHands-on experiences of analyzing Metabolomics data of serum samples derived from exosome injected mice.","skills":["Tissue Processing","Immunofluorescence","Immunoprecipitation","Bioinformatics","Molecular Biology","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)","Western Blotting","Immunohistochemistry"]},{"title":"PHD Student","company":"Nanjing University · 全职","date_range":"2008年9月 - 2014年9月","duration":"6 年 1 个月","location":"中国 江苏省 南京市","description":"Successfully demonstrated that small interfering RNAs (siRNAs) could be incorporated into cell-derived nanoparticles, which was proved to be effective in inhibiting HIV infection with in vitro HIV pseudotype virus model. \n \nFirstly explored the function of plant microRNA MIR156a from vegetable consumption in regulating human monocyte recruitment on inflamed human endothelial cells and proved this mechanism might be underlying the protective role of veggies diet in preventing cardiovascular diseases. \n \nSystematically explained the roles of dysregulated microRNAs in regulating tumor progression by proving the interactions between miR-150 and target SRCIN1 in lung cancer cells, or miR-495 and target JAM-A in breast cancer cells.","skills":["Cell Biology","Reporter Gene Assays","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Scientist, II at Regulus Therapeutics · 2024年 - 2026年 | School of Medicine - Assistant Project Scientist at University of California, San Diego · 2019年 - 2024年 | Postdoctoral Researcher at UC San Diego School of Medicine · 2016年 - 2019年 | Postdoctoral Fellow at City of Hope · 2014年 - 2016年 | PHD Student at Nanjing University · 2008年 - 2014年","education":[{"school":"南京大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Biochemistry","date_range":"2008年 - 2014年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 南京大学，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 2008年 - 2014年 | 保存到项目 | 将Minghui保存到项目 | 发消息给Minghui | Minghui Cao的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":true,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:22:45+08:00","record":{"name":"Juxiang Cao","current_title":"Principle scientist","current_company":"Candel Therapeutics · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 沃本","headline":"Principle scientist at Candel Therapeutics","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/juxiang-cao-bb706722","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAASiu_sB1HqdpjCPn53qHeJYkj9ybC6eoc8","core_skills":["lentivial production","mouse xenograft","recombinant DNA techniques"],"positions":[{"title":"Principle scientist","company":"Candel Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2026年4月 - 现在","duration":"6 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 尼德姆","description":"Analytical development, Bioassay, Cell based potency","skills":[]},{"title":"Volunteer","company":"Flatley Discovery Lab","date_range":"2017年6月 - 现在","duration":"9 年 4 个月","location":"Charles town, MA","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Consultant","company":"enGene Therapeutics · 合同","date_range":"2025年7月 - 2026年3月","duration":"9 个月","location":"Boston","description":"CMC Analytical Development, Bioassay, Cell Based Potency methods, Gene Therapy  \nManage external lab method development, optimization, qualification/validation, transfer, comparability study and GMP testing to support in process, release and stability testing of late stage clinical trial DS and DP\n\n• CMC Analytical development, Bioassay Potency methods.","skills":[]},{"title":"Group leader, Analytical development and QC","company":"Resilience/Cell and Gene Therapy, Biologicals manufacturing · 全职","date_range":"2025年4月 - 2025年6月","duration":"3 个月","location":"Allston, MA","description":"Lead Bioassay and Molecular biology assay development team for Cell and Gene therapy (AAV, LVV) and biologicals (protein, mAb mRNA and conjugates). \nMange direct reports \nManage analytical lab (instruments qualification and maintenance, environmental safety, documentation) \nLead assay development, qualification, validation, transfer and lifecy