{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:22:55+08:00","record":{"name":"Jingsong Cao","current_title":"Sr. Fellow","current_company":"Innorna Co., Ltd. · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 列克星敦","headline":"Molecular and Cellular Biologist/Biochemist/Pharmacologist","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jingsong-cao-84598611","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAJ1MTUBJvf1FmesLAdShbs6aOALFgrsPxk","core_skills":["bile acid transporting","GI physiology","lipid metablism"],"positions":[{"title":"Sr. Fellow","company":"Innorna Co., Ltd. · 全职","date_range":"2024年9月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 1 个月","location":"美国","description":"Directing the research and development of mRNA-based therapies for metabolic and immunological diseases. Leading the IND-enabling studies and authoring preclinical pharmacology and toxicology sessions for preIND and IND submission of mRNA/LNP based therapeutic programs in treating chronic diseases. Received the IND clearance from FDA for a program aimed at treating chronic gout.\n\n• Leading the IND-enabling studies and IND filing for a lead mRNA/LNP program treating chronic gout. \n• Received IND clearance from FDA for this program.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director of Pharmacology and Bioassays","company":"Frontera Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2023年9月 - 2024年8月","duration":"1 年","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 Bedford","description":"Oversaw the preclinical pharmacology bioassays to advance the development of AAV-based therapies for cardiovascular, ocular, and rare metabolic diseases. Led the preclinical pharmacology studies for developing AAV-based therapies for genetic cardiomyopathies caused by deficiency of MyBPC3 or PKP2. Prepared and authored preclinical pharmacology and toxicology documents for IND submission for an AAV-based therapy treating wet age-related macular degeneration (AMD). Received IND clearance from FDA for this program. Managed a team of 5-6 scientists.","skills":[]},{"title":"Associate Scientific Director","company":"Moderna","date_range":"8 年 2 个月","duration":"4 年 7 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"Directing, designing, and executing the in vitro and in vivo preclinical studies for mRNA-based therapeutic targets for monogenetic liver and cardiovascular metabolic diseases \n• Led the in vitro and in vivo preclinical biology studies for Gsd1a program, including all IND-enabling pharmacology studies. Took the program from concept inception to phase I clinical development with promising early efficacy in patients.  \n• Established biochemical, cell-based, ex vivo, and in vivo assays/tools in support of discovery and development of mRNA-based therapies to treat a variety of metabolic liver and cardiovascular diseases related to dysregulations in glucose, lipid, or amino acid homeostatis. Achieved preclinical proof of in vivo efficacy for treating these diseases in clinically relevant animal models.  \n• Applied bioinformatics-aided protein and nucleotide engineering approach in identifying mRNA-based therapies with enhanced pharmacology. \n• Directed and oversaw collaborations with external academic labs and CROs.\n\n• Directed and executed the in vitro and in vivo preclinical studies of several mRNA-based therapeutic targets for monogenetic liver and cardiovascular metabolic diseases, including Glycogen storage disease 1a (Gsd1a), Progressive Familial Intrahepatic Cholestasis 3 (PFIC3), and Citrullinemia type 2 (CTLN2), Ornithine Transcarbamoylase Deficiency (OTCD), and Lipoprotein lipase deficiency (LPL). \n• Applied computer-aided and knowledge-based approaches for protein engineering in developing superior molecules with improved pharmacology and therapeutic potentials.","skills":["技能: Rare Diseases • ELISA • Western Blotting • Mammalian Cell Culture • RNA Biology • Assay Development • Metabolic Diseases • Liver Disease • Drug Development • mRNA-based drug discovery research and development","Rare Diseases","ELISA","Western Blotting","Mammalian Cell Culture","RNA Biology","Assay Development","Metabolic Diseases","Liver Disease","Drug Development","mRNA-based drug discovery research and development","技能: RNA Biology • Assay Development • Metabolic Diseases • Liver Disease • mRNA-based drug discovery research and development • Drug Discovery","Drug Discovery"]},{"title":"Principal Scientist","company":"Moderna","date_range":"8 年 2 个月","duration":"4 年 7 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"Directing, designing, and executing the in vitro and in vivo preclinical studies for mRNA-based therapeutic targets for monogenetic liver and cardiovascular metabolic diseases \n• Led the in vitro and in vivo preclinical biology studies for Gsd1a program, including all IND-enabling pharmacology studies. Took the program from concept inception to phase I clinical development with promising early efficacy in patients.  \n• Established biochemical, cell-based, ex vivo, and in vivo assays/tools in support of discovery and development of mRNA-based therapies to treat a variety of metabolic liver and cardiovascular diseases related to dysregulations in glucose, lipid, or amino acid homeostatis. Achieved preclinical proof of in vivo efficacy for treating these diseases in clinically relevant animal models.  \n• Applied bioinformatics-aided protein and nucleotide engineering approach in identifying mRNA-based therapies with enhanced pharmacology. \n• Directed and oversaw collaborations with external academic labs and CROs.\n\n• Directed and executed the in vitro and in vivo preclinical studies of several mRNA-based therapeutic targets for monogenetic liver and cardiovascular metabolic diseases, including Glycogen storage disease 1a (Gsd1a), Progressive Familial Intrahepatic Cholestasis 3 (PFIC3), and Citrullinemia type 2 (CTLN2), Ornithine Transcarbamoylase Deficiency (OTCD), and Lipoprotein lipase deficiency (LPL). \n• Applied computer-aided and knowledge-based approaches for protein engineering in developing superior molecules with improved pharmacology and therapeutic potentials.","skills":["技能: Rare Diseases • ELISA • Western Blotting • Mammalian Cell Culture • RNA Biology • Assay Development • Metabolic Diseases • Liver Disease • Drug Development • mRNA-based drug discovery research and development","Rare Diseases","ELISA","Western Blotting","Mammalian Cell Culture","RNA Biology","Assay Development","Metabolic Diseases","Liver Disease","Drug Development","mRNA-based drug discovery research and development","技能: RNA Biology • Assay Development • Metabolic Diseases • Liver Disease • mRNA-based drug discovery research and development • Drug Discovery","Drug Discovery"]},{"title":"Director of Biology","company":"Eternity Bioscience, Inc · 全职","date_range":"2012年6月 - 2015年5月","duration":"3 年","location":"美国 新泽西州 Cranbury","description":"• Directed biological and pharmacological efforts in Eternity Bioscience Inc, which is dedicated in discovering novel therapies for human diseases including cancer, inflammation, and metabolic diseases. \n• Discovered novel, potent, and selective small molecule compounds targeting MAPK and BTK pathways, and Ezh2 epigenetic regulators. Advanced 3 candidate compounds into clinical development for treatment of cancer and autoimmune diseases. \n \nRelated publication at Eternity Biosciences - \n \n5. Lu B, Shen X, Zhang L, Liu D, Zhang C, Cao J, Shen R, Zhang J, Wang D, Wan H, Xu Z, Ho MH, Zhang M, Zhang L, He F, Tao W. Discovery of EBI-2511: A Highly Potent and Orally Active EZH2 Inhibitor for the Treatment of Non-Hodgkin's Lymphoma.ACS Med Chem Lett. 2018 Jan 29;9(2):98-102.  \n \n6. Lu B, Huang S, Cao J, Hu Q, Shen R, Wan H, Wang D, Yuan J, Zhang L, Zhang J, Zhang M, Tao W, Zhang L. Discovery of EBI-1051: A novel and orally efficacious MEK inhibitor with benzofuran scaffold. Bioorg Med Chem. 2018 Feb 1;26(3):581-589.  \n \n7. Liu W, Guo W, Hang N, Yang Y, Wu X, Shen Y, Cao J, Sun Y, Xu Q. MALT1 inhibitors prevent the development of DSS-induced experimental colitis in mice via inhibiting NF-κB and NLRP3 inflammasome activation. Oncotarget. 2016 May 24;7(21):30536-49. \n \n8. Zhang J, Lu B, Liu D, Shen R, Yan Y, Yang L, Zhang M, Zhang L, Cao G, Cao H, Fu B, Gong A, Sun Q, Wan H, Zhang L, Tao W, Cao J. EBI-907, a novel BRAF(V600E) inhibitor, has potent oral anti-tumor activity and a broad kinase selectivity profile. Cancer Biol Ther. 2016;17(2):199-207. \n \n9. Lu B, Cao H, Cao J, Huang S, Hu Q, Liu D, Shen R, Shen X, Tao W, Wan H, Wang D, Yan Y, Yang L, Zhang J, Zhang L, Zhang L, Zhang M. Discovery of EBI-907: A highly potent and orally active B-Raf(V600E) inhibitor for the treatment of melanoma and associated cancers. Bioorg Med Chem Lett. 2016 Feb 1;26(3):819-823.","skills":["Oncology","Metabolic Diseases","in vivo pharmacology","Drug Discovery","Cell Based Assays"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Sr. Fellow at Innorna Co., Ltd. · 2024年 - 现在 | Director of Pharmacology and Bioassays at Frontera Therapeutics · 2023年 - 2024年 | Associate Scientific Director at Moderna · 2019年 - 2023年 | Principal Scientist at Moderna · 2015年 - 2019年 | Director of Biology at Eternity Bioscience, Inc · 2012年 - 2015年 | Lab Head, Investigator III at Novartis Institute for Biomedical Research Inc. · 2010年 - 2012年 | Sr. Research Scientist II at Pfizer · 2009年 - 2010年 | Senior Research Scientist at Wyeth/Pfizer, Cardiovascular and Metabolic Disease · 2005年 - 2010年 | Sr. Research Scientist I/II at Wyeth Research · 2005年 - 2009年 | Postdoctoral Fellow at Lilly Research labs · 2002年 - 2004年 | Postdoctoral Researcher at Eli Lilly and Company, Endocrine Research · 2002年 - 2004年 | Postdoctoral fellow at University of Kentucky · 1999年 - 2002年","education":[{"school":"美国麻省理工学院","degree":"Advanced Study Program (Certificate awarded)","field_of_study":"Biology","date_range":"2007年 - 2008年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"中国药科大学","degree":"Ph.D","field_of_study":"Pharmacology","date_range":"1994年 - 1999年","activities":"活动与社团: Character