{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:23:16+08:00","record":{"name":"Ying Cao","current_title":"Biomarker Operations Lead (Contractor)","current_company":"Servier · 合同","location":"法国 法兰西岛 巴黎","headline":"Biomarker, Pharmacology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ying-cao-79471338","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAfvvaABZ0mlD6tRkTQfz_DIIczl1xH-xlQ","core_skills":["HGR","Clinical Biomarker","Biomarkers"],"positions":[{"title":"Biomarker Operations Lead (Contractor)","company":"Servier · 合同","date_range":"2025年7月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 3 个月","location":"法国 法兰西岛 萨克雷","description":"Clinical Trial Management Department\n\n• Responsible for clinical biomarker activities during clinical studies. \n• Key member of clinical biomarker subteam to design biomarker scientific and operational strategy. \n• Responsible for the clinical biomarker activities outsourcing, including vendor identification, contracting, monitoring assay validation and sample analysis, data internalization. \n• Biomarker representative in several clinical study teams.","skills":["HGR","Assay Development","ICH","Good Clinical Practice (GCP)","Contract Management","Timeline Management","Vendor Management","Clinical Trials","Project Management","Clinical Biomarker"]},{"title":"Senior Scientist in vitro Pharmacology/Biomarker/Translational Sciences","company":"NovAliX · 正式","date_range":"2023年 - 2025年","duration":"2 年 1 个月","location":"法国 法兰西岛 罗曼维尔","description":"• Serve as Translational Sciences (TS) leads multiple client projects (small molecules, antibody, ADC). \n• Lead development of in vitro, in vivo, and ex vivo models; conduct PK/PD studies; identify and validate pharmacodynamic biomarkers; and develop relevant assays. \n• Design, development and validation of companion diagnostic assays. \n• Drive the creation of novel models to support client programs and expand internal platform capabilities. \n• Author study protocols, reports, and project documentation.","skills":["Problem Solving","Outsourcing Management","Project Management","Clinical Research","Biomarkers","Clinical Biomarker","Biotechnology","Precision Medicine","Pre-clinical Studies","Drug Development","PK/PD"]},{"title":"Senior Scientist Translational Research Biomarker","company":"Galapagos · 正式","date_range":"2020年 - 2023年","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"法国 法兰西岛 罗曼维尔","description":"● Responsible for the biomarker activities in several projects in the oncology and fibrosis therapeutic areas. These include the identification of in vitro and in vivo target engagement biomarkers, pathway biomarkers, disease prognostic and prediction biomarkers. \n● Work as the lead contact in collaboration with CROs and monitor the progression and the quality of the projects. \n● Documentation of project reports, SOPs and clinical biomarker plan.\n\n• Led biomarker strategies for several preclinical and clinical programs, including identification of target engagement, prognostic, predictive, and patient stratification biomarkers. \n• Translational research biomarker representative in the cross functional team from target discovery to PCC nomination. \n• Acted as primary contact for collaborations with CROs; monitored project progress and quality. \n• Prepared project reports, SOPs, and clinical biomarker plans. \n• Contributed to clinical trial laboratory selection and biomarker assay transfer. \n• Participated in back-translational research using clinical samples.","skills":["Problem Solving","Outsourcing Management","Project Management","Clinical Research","Biomarkers","Clinical Biomarker","Biotechnology","Precision Medicine","Pre-clinical Studies","Drug Development","PK/PD"]},{"title":"Chargé de recherche, Chargé de recherche expert","company":"Institut Pasteur · 全职","date_range":"2012年 - 2019年","duration":"7 年 1 个月","location":"巴黎地区","description":"Nuclear Organization and Oncogenesis Unit, under the supervision of Professor Anne Dejean. \n● Investigated how small ubiquitin like modifier (SUMO) regulates gene transcription in cell cycle. Specifically, I discovered the molecular mechanism of the canonical histone genes transcription regulated by SUMOylation.  \n● Investigated the crosstalk of proteins in SUMOylation and autophagy cell signaling pathway, and their roles in oncogenesis. \n● Established a method to identify new nuclear body protein composition by proximity labeling followed by Mass-Spec analysis.\n\n• Studied the role of protein SUMOylation in regulating gene transcription during the cell cycle. \n• Uncovered mechanisms linking histone gene transcription to crosstalk between SUMOylation and phosphorylation. \n• Investigated how protein SUMOylation affects autophagy signaling and its implications in oncogenesis. \n• Developed a proximity labeling method followed by mass spectrometry to identify protein components of PML nuclear bodies.","skills":["Problem Solving","Biotechnology"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Biomarker Operations Lead (Contractor) at Servier · 2025年 - 现在 | Senior Scientist in vitro Pharmacology/Biomarker/Translational Sciences at NovAliX · 2023年 - 2025年 | Senior Scientist Translational Research Biomarker at Galapagos · 2020年 - 2023年 | Chargé de recherche, Chargé de recherche expert at Institut Pasteur · 2012年 - 2019年 | Research Fellow, Research Associate, Research Assistant Professor at Mayo Clinic · 2006年 - 2012年","education":[{"school":"北京协和医学院","degree":"Ph.D.","field_of_study":"Cell Biology & Stem Cell","date_range":"2001年 - 2006年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"吉林大学","degree":"Bachelor of Science (B.S.)","field_of_study":"Biochemistry","date_range":"1997年 - 2001年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 北京协和医学院，Ph.D. · 2001年 - 2006年 | 吉林大学，Bachelor of Science (B.S.) · 1997年 - 2001年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Biomedical Scientist Account Manager Clinical Research Molecular Biologist Project Manager 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 法国 远程办公: 法国 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":true,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:23:27+08:00","record":{"name":"Yu Joshua Cao","current_title":"Principal Investigator","current_company":"Peking University Shenzhen Graduate School","location":"中国 广东省 深圳","headline":"Principal Investigator in Translational Immuno-Oncology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/joshuacao","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAYg2s0B0DBylEJi973DC6M4972q36K2jvQ","core_skills":["Bispecific Antibodies","Antibody Drug Conjugates","CAR-T"],"positions":[{"title":"Principal Investigator","company":"Peking University Shenzhen Graduate School","date_range":"2017年10月 - 现在","duration":"9 年","location":"中国 广东省 深圳","description":"During the past decades, anticancer immunotherapy has evolved from a promising therapeutic option to a robust clinical reality. Many immunotherapeutic regimens are now approved by the US Food and Drug Administration and the European Medicines Agency for cancer patients, and many others are being investigated as standalone therapeutic interventions or combined with conventional treatments to improve the clinical efficacy. By critical thinking the distinct cell killing efficacy and potential unwanted toxicity of different targeted strategies, our lab is building versatile platforms and finding optimal strategies to develop novel immunotherapeutic agents for cancer treatment. Our goal is to design the precision medicine approach for individual cancer patient groups for fully realizing the potential benefits of immunotherapy.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist/Senior Scientist","company":"Sorrento Therapeutics, Inc.","date_range":"2016年4月 - 2017年8月","duration":"1 年 5 个月","location":"Greater San Diego Area","description":"The major responsibility is to develop different generations of CAR-T cells targeting different antigen expression blood malignances and solid tumors. The other focuses included the novel design of universal CARs so that the allograft CAR-T cells can be applied to cancer patients without graft versus host disease effects, and the novel CAR-T strategy by gene editing to knockdown and knockout the immune checkpoint antigen or immunosuppressive targets to enhance the CAR-T efficacy and durability, but reduced exhaustion and anergy.","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Associate","company":"The Scripps Research Institute","date_range":"2013年2月 - 2016年4月","duration":"3 年 3 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","description":"The central theme of my research is to develop novel cancer targeted therapeutics. One of the major components in the program is aimed at the engineering and use of a differentiated, switchable, CAR-T in adoptive immune therapy targeting tumor associated antigens. The novel sCAR-T approach is superior to conventional CAR-T method to prevent “on-target/off tumor” toxicity and cytokine release syndrome. This also provides a broad platform of the potential use of different specific molecules targeting distinct antigens and various cancers. \nAnother focus of my research is to develop multi-formats of T- cell redirected bispecific antibodies using site-specifically conjugated IgG or Fab, as well as the side-by-side characterization and comparison with antibody-drug conjugates in cancers with different antigen density. The study is critical to identify the different formats of bispecific antibodies in relationship with the antitumor efficacy and antigen-independent T cell activity, as well as the potential prospect of bispecific antibodies and antibody drug conjugates on specific cancer patient population.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoc Fellow","company":"MD Anderson Cancer Center","date_range":"2007年10月 - 2013年2月","duration":"5 年 5 个月","location":"休斯敦地区","description":"My research included the development of antibody drug fusions and antibody drug conjugates, and characterized how different antibodies, antibody formats, linker choices and construct orientation impact the affinity, avidity, specificity, cytotoxicity, antitumor efficiency and off-target toxicity. These optimizing strategies have significant impacts on the rational design of antibody-based fusions or conjugates, and provide efficient support on the R&D of immuno-drugs targeting a variety of tumor associated antigens expressing on blood and solid malignancies.  \nI also developed the active immunoprotease containing human serine protease Granzyme B. This immunoprotease could efficiently induce cell death under apoptosis in vitro and in vivo. The further study was based on the different cancer cells showing resistant to Her2 targeted agents (Herceptin, Lapatinib or both), and the resistance to chemotherapy by expressing multi-drug resistance protein 1. By using these cells, I investigated the potential efficacy of immunoprotease against them, and the associated signaling mechanism counteracting the cross-resistance.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Principal Investigator at Peking University Shenzhen Graduate School · 2017年 - 现在 | Scientist/Senior Scientist at Sorrento Therapeutics, Inc. · 2016年 - 2017年 | Research Associate at The Scripps Research Institute · 2013年 - 2016年 | Postdoc Fellow at MD Anderson Cancer Center · 2007年 - 2013年","education":[{"school":"南开大学","degree":"Ph.D","field_of_study":"Microbiology and Immunology","date_range":"2001年 - 2007年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 南开大学，Ph.D · 2001年 - 2007年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":""}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
