{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:23:49+08:00","record":{"name":"Sherry Cao","current_title":"SVP, Computational Science","current_company":"Affinia Therapeutics","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 弗雷明翰","headline":"SVP, Computational Science","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/sherry-cao-b399071","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAABP8Z0BL-IKl7if5sHsqT8rIIhgEcpTLjQ","core_skills":["Pharmaceutical Industry","Biomarkers","Assay Development"],"positions":[{"title":"SVP, Computational Science","company":"Affinia Therapeutics","date_range":"5 年 1 个月","duration":"2 年 9 个月","location":"","description":"• Report to the CSO and am responsible for the overall R&D scientific data and analysis strategy formulation and execution, supporting R&D, competitive intelligence and business development initiatives. \n• Implemented an integrated ML/AI, cloud-based NGS data analysis infrastructure and pipeline. \n• Drive Affinia’s AAV capsid engineering platform evolution, transitioning from ancestral library based to peptide insertion library and receptor based capsid screening. \n• Applied generative AI, protein modeling and systems bioinformatics techniques for efficient capsid library designs and capsid prioritization. \n• Collaborated with the vector biology group and reduced the design, screen, analysis cycle time by three months. \n• Discovered best in class skeletal and cardiac muscle tropic capsids that resulted in multiple IP filings and earned $30 million research collaboration milestones. \n• Lead cardiac muscle capsid was used for Affinia’s first BAG3 dilated cardiomyopathy program, which is the basis for Series C fund raise. \n• Discovered best in class CNS penetrating AAV capsids via a receptor based capsid experimental screening paradigm for both internal program development and out-licensing business development.","skills":["技能: Data-driven Decision Making • Data Science • Strategy • Drug Delivery • Computer Science • CRO Manageme