{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:28:07+08:00","record":{"name":"Jing Cao","current_title":"VP Program Management","current_company":"Zai Lab · 全职","location":"费城地区","headline":"VP Program Management","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jing-cao-6b249815","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAMY0uYBsYTOcXjpHsQuP6f0WHPgq0caQ5M","core_skills":["Languages: English","Chinese","Japanese","Pharmaceutical Industry","Biomarkers"],"positions":[{"title":"VP Program Management","company":"Zai Lab · 全职","date_range":"2022年1月 - 2024年12月","duration":"3 年","location":"","description":"• Led program management and development cross-functional teams and provided leadership roles in alliance partner teams ensuring global integration. \n• Provided oversight to CRO/CDMO and vendors. \n• Achieved approvals and commercialization of Nuzyra® (omadacycline), Vyvgart® (efgartigimod IV & SC), & Xacduro® (Sul-Dur) in China. \n• Led the team for Cobenfy® (KarXT, xanomeline-trospium chloride) China development registration programs in schizophrenia and Alzheimer’s disease psychosis from initial license-in to Ph3 program planning/execution resulting in a positive pivotal Ph3 schizophrenia trial and NDA in China. \n• Led key CMC & commercial supply planning teams including China manufacturing localization work streams. \n• Coached China based colleagues and functional teams.","skills":[]},{"title":"Chief Operating Officer","company":"US Green Valley Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","date_range":"2021年4月 - 2022年1月","duration":"10 个月","location":"","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Director","company":"Incyte","date_range":"2017年9月 - 2021年4月","duration":"3 年 8 个月","location":"费城地区","description":"• Led Immuno-Oncology multiple asset strategy and program teams with responsibilities in program strategy, operations and budgets for assets ranging from IND to phase 3. \n• Primary program leadership for integrating preclinical, translational and clinical development & regulatory strategy, and executing operational work-streams, including alliance partnerships (US & China based), a global CDx partnership for a registration confirmatory trial, and global regulatory interactions (US, EU, Japan & China) leading to execution of global phase 3 trials. \n• Managed immune-oncology program teams in successful completing four IND submissions (3 novel small molecule compounds and 1 new monoclonal antibody); 4 FDA end-of-phase 2 meetings & 4 EMA scientific advice procedures in 4 cancer indications; and 1 Japan PMDA consultation; 1 FDA pre-BLA meeting and 1 EMA pre-submission/co-rapporteur meeting. \n• Supported China alliance partnership for taking a phase 3 clinical asset to China including IND dossier, NMPA meetings, CTAs and global CRO operational management of multiple registration-directed phase 2-3 studies. \n• Led the submission dossier team planning, preparation and BLA/MAA submissions, and an FDA ODAC operational preparation, all in remote settings under Covid-19 environment. \n• Led program budget planning, monthly finance tracking, and quarterly executive management budget reviews for the responsible assets with 12 ongoing clinical trials ranging from phase 1 to phase 3.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director","company":"Director","date_range":"2006年3月 - 2009年3月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"","description":"• Managed prasugrel (Effient® - US, Efient® - EU) alliance teams and development in alliance territories by working with Eli Lilly project managers and colleagues. \n• ▪ Served as a member of the alliance Joint Product Development Committee (JPDC) that provides oversight to global development strategy development, operation planning, and effective execution of global brand plan. \n• ▪ Led Daiichi Sankyo internal effort for cross-functional alignment including Senior Management reviews & approvals for all major deliverables and decisions. \n• Provided support to Japan development effort. \n• ▪ Provided operational leadership in achieving major milestones of Phase 3 TRITON study (n=13,000) resulting in AHA & NEJM simultaneous data publications and NDA/MAA approvals. \n• ▪ Managed FDA Advisory Committee meeting preparation and mock rehearsals that resulted in a successful FDA Advisory Committee meeting with unanimous approval recommendation. \n• Began building Oncology TA PM group and managed priority oncology Project Teams ▪ Provided project management and operational leadership to the oncology teams. \n• Coordinated with Japan based functional departments and stakeholders supporting oncology projects.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | VP Program Management at Zai Lab · 2022年 - 2024年 | Chief Operating Officer at US Green Valley Pharmaceuticals, Inc. · 2021年 - 2022年 | Senior Director at Incyte · 2017年 - 2021年 | Director at Director · 2006年 - 2009年 | Senior Director - Global Project Management & Leadership Oncology at Daiichi Sankyo Co., Ltd. · 2006年 - 2017年 | Associate Director at Bristol-Myers Squibb · 2002年 - 2006年 | Project Manager at Pfizer · 1998年 - 2002年","education":[{"school":"美国罗格斯新泽西州立大学新布朗斯维克分校","degree":"Ph.D.","field_of_study":"Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Cornell Johnson Graduate School of Management","degree":"MBA","field_of_study":"","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"南开大学","degree":"B.S.","field_of_study":"Biochemistry","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 美国罗格斯新泽西州立大学新布朗斯维克分校，Ph.D. | Cornell Johnson Graduate School of Management，MBA | 南开大学，B.S. | 美国波士顿大学，Project Management Certificate · 2002年 | 北里大学 / Kitasato University | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:28:18+08:00","record":{"name":"Roberto Cao-Milán","current_title":"Sr. Development Scientist","current_company":"Malvern Panalytical","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 奇科皮","headline":"Sr. Development Scientist | Black Belt in Lean Six Sigma | Expert in Biophysical Characterization Products | Driving Innovation at Malvern-Panalytical","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/roberto-cao-mil%C3%A1n-6220a241","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAi7yvoBkcxoEilLC_rdhPUug6MS0jBGsOE","core_skills":["Protective Coatings","Surface Chemistry","Collaborative Problem Solving"],"positions":[{"title":"Sr. Development Scientist","company":"Malvern Panalytical","date_range":"6 年 11 个月","duration":"3 年 2 个月","location":"Northampton, Massachusetts, United States","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Development Scientist","company":"Malvern Panalytical","date_range":"6 年 11 个月","duration":"3 年 2 个月","location":"Northampton, Massachusetts, United States","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Sr. Development Scientist","company":"MicroCal from Malvern-Panalytical","date_range":"2019年 - 现在","duration":"7 年 9 个月","location":"","description":"• Product Manager (interim, 50% time) August 2023-Present. \n• Responsible for validating and updating value propositions on next generation of calorimeters. \n• Conceived strategies to avoid market saturation. \n• Design for Six Sigma and Lean Six Sigma Champion at regional level (North America). \n• Facilitator of the process of translating the voice of customers (VoCs) into new product requirements and engineering directions in the next generation of calorimeters. \n• Defined the Critical to Qualities parameters to be optimized and control. \n• Responsible for developing and validating measurement systems for evaluating the Key Performance Parameters like surface finish of critical electro machined parts, doping degree and stability of thermoelectrical parts, and precision 