{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:29:09+08:00","record":{"name":"Liang Cao","current_title":"Head, Molecular Targets Core Lab","current_company":"National Cancer Institute","location":"美国 马里兰州 贝塞斯达","headline":"Retired","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/liang-cao-32720b10","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAIqpA8Bi_Izs-et1jGZIb9C6O9UWN4704Q","core_skills":["Clinical Development","Biomarkers","Cancer Research"],"positions":[{"title":"Head, Molecular Targets Core Lab","company":"National Cancer Institute","date_range":"2005年 - 2023年7月","duration":"18 年 7 个月","location":"Bethesda, MD","description":"Experiences \n• Directed clinical laboratory studies of over 50 US FDA-registered oncology drug trials at NCI, covering various critical drug development objectives, including pharmacokinetics, pharmacodynamics, mechanism of action, dose response relation, proof of concept, and drug safety.  \n• Productive experiences in collaborating with clinicians and pharma companies during early drug development of novel anti-cancer agents. Strong ability to plan and execute laboratory studies to deliver vital data in time for drug development decisions. Highly experienced for project management with multiple concurrent clinical trials.  \n• Effective communicator across a wide range of stakeholders. Skilled in presenting the work in writing and in oral  \n• Served as an NCI expert on biomarkers in early clinical development. Extensive publications on biomarkers for clinical trials in leading oncology journals, including Lancet Oncol, JCO, JCO Prec Med, Clin Cancer Res, and Cancer Res.  \n• Comprehensive knowledge and experience in oncology drug R&D, including the concept, agent generation, preclinical, and early clinical development. In-depth knowledge of US FDA regulations, and strong ability for implementation.  \n• An innovator in developing novel biomarkers and assays to support the widest range of immunotherapeutic drug development.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director Of Research Development","company":"OriGene Technologies","date_range":"2004年 - 2005年","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"Rockville, MD","description":"• Directly reporting to CEO and accountable for product development initiatives  \n• Responsible for new product development in the company \n• In charge of the manufacturing of genomic products and their quality control. Experienced with all issues relating to QC/QA","skills":[]},{"title":"Vice President Research And Development","company":"Aptus Pharmaceuticals","date_range":"2000年 - 2004年","duration":"4 年 1 个月","location":"Rockville, MD","description":"• Serving as the most senior person in research and development. Responsible for establishing the R&D teams and programs. Directed the R&D efforts on drug discovery technologies and drug discovery. \n• Managed R&D strategies and pipeline development. In charge of patent strategy and applications, government grant applications, and regulatory issues. Responsible for partnerships with pharma companies on technologies and drug development. \n• Presentations to VC investors in all fund-raise activities. Presentations on technology, products, and drug agents to pharmaceutical companies for product sales and licensing.","skills":[]},{"title":"Associate Professor, Medical School","company":"The University of Hong Kong","date_range":"1994年 - 2000年","duration":"6 年 1 个月","location":"香港特别行政区","description":"• Research activities on cancer and infectious disease with extensive publications \n• Had various leadership roles, including Department Chair for Graduate Studies, Chief Examiner and Chief Coordinator for Preclinical Program","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Head, Molecular Targets Core Lab at National Cancer Institute · 2005年 - 2023年 | Director Of Research Development at OriGene Technologies · 2004年 - 2005年 | Vice President Research And Development at Aptus Pharmaceuticals · 2000年 - 2004年 | Associate Professor, Medical School at The University of Hong Kong · 1994年 - 2000年 | Scientist and Project Leader at Human Genome Sciences · 1993年 - 1994年 | Damon Runyon Cancer Research Fellow at Mass General Hospital, Cancer Center; Harvard Medical School · 1991年 - 1993年","education":[{"school":"美国哈佛大学","degree":"PhD","field_of_study":"Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","date_range":"1984年 - 1991年","activities":"活动与社团: • Serve as Vice President, Association for Graduate School of Arts and Sciences (GSAS); and Standing Committee Member, Committee on Graduate Education for GSAS • Authored two Cell papers, and pioneered an original method for gene alteration via recombination","grade":""},{"school":"北京大学","degree":"BS","field_of_study":"Biology","date_range":"1979年 - 1983年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 美国哈佛大学，PhD · 1984年 - 1991年 | 北京大学，BS · 1979年 - 1983年 | 档案分析行 | 最新动态 | 1 条消息 | 1 次浏览 | 保存到项目 | 将Liang保存到项目 | 发消息给Liang | Liang Cao的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:29:19+08:00","record":{"name":"Xufeng Cao","current_title":"Scientist III, Medicinal Chemistry","current_company":"Olema Oncology · 全职","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 旧金山","headline":"Scientist III, Medicinal Chemistry at Olema Oncology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/xufeng-cao-a918661aa","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAADDklI0BoODs4qu98XCjz2_5Rea9s7sLgpQ","core_skills":["Drug Discovery and Development","Fragment-Based Screening","Structure-Activity Relationship Studys"],"positions":[{"title":"Scientist III, Medicinal Chemistry","company":"Olema Oncology · 全职","date_range":"2021年6月 - 现在","duration":"5 年 4 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 旧金山","description":"1. Discover novel and potent Complete Estrogen Receptor Antagonist (CERAN), inhibitors of PI3Kα and CDK2 that conform to anti-breast cancer Target Candidate Profile. \n2. Performing lead optimization through the design and synthesis of proprietary small novel anti-breast cancer molecules with improved properties.  \n3. Elucidating instructive SAR by interpreting complex data sets derived from biological and physicochemical assays.  \n4. Engaging in the scale-up of selected target molecules and high-value intermediates.  \n5. Providing clear presentations of research progress to the chemistry group, cross-functional project teams, and executive leadership. \n6. Directly managing internal associate scientists and engaging in the management of CRO Chemistry. Generate for synthetic targets, communicate the ideas. Identify synthetic problems and propose the solution. Track the progress of project and make sure the timeline is met. \n7. Supporting the drafting of patent applications, scientific publications, and external presentations.","skills":[]},{"title":"Chemical Biology Specialist III","company":"MOFFITT CANCER CENTER & RESEARCH INSTITUTE · 全职","date_range":"2020年12月 - 2021年6月","duration":"7 个月","location":"美国 佛罗里达 坦帕","description":"1. Design and synthesis of hits, lead compounds, and chemical probes to elucidate molecular mechanism of proteins involved in cancer cell signaling. \n2. Discovery and development of highly potent and selective Antibody-Drug Conjugates with novel Aurora Kinase Inhibitors. \n3. Design and synthesis of novel small molecules as anticancer agents via synthesis of focused libraries.","skills":[]},{"title":"Post-doctoral Research Associate","company":"Purdue University College of Pharmacy · 全职","date_range":"2018年9月 - 2020年12月","duration":"2 年 4 个月","location":"美国 印第安纳 西拉斐叶","description":"1. Designed and synthesized of novel highly active inhibitors of Staphylococcus aureus RnpA (A protein subunit of Ribonuclease P) using computational modeling, traditional and fragment-based screening approaches.  \n \n2. Discovery and development of novel potent therapeutic agents against Vancomycin-Resistant Enterococcus (VRE) and Neisseria gonorrhoeae using both traditional and computational modeling techniques. \n \n3. Designed and synthesized of methamphetamine like haptens to generate the antibodies by active immunization, which could theoretically bind the drug, thereby preventing methamphetamine from reaching its multiple sites of action within the central nervous system. This approach became a promising treatment for methamphetamine addiction. \n \n4. Design, synthesis and structure‐activity relationship studies of novel Adaptive Efflux Inhibitors, which can be used in combination with new and existing antibiotics to treat Acinetobacter baumannii bacterial infections.","skills":[]},{"title":"Post-Doctoral Research Associate","company":"University of Wisconsin-Madison School of Pharmacy · 全职","date_range":"2015年8月 - 2018年8月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"美国 威斯康辛 麦迪逊","description":"1. Designed and synthesized over 200 novel potent, broad spectrum inhibitors of encephalitis virus by targeting viral RNA polymerase in a couple of new scaffold series requiring different synthetic development \n \n2. Evaluated structure-activity and structure-property relationships to prepare antiviral analogs with improved Drug-like Properties and in vivo efficacy \n \n3. Developed novel methodologies to enable synthesis of unrepresented scaffolds and key analogs with bioactivities \n \n4. Reliably prepared and delivered pure compounds on scale for multiple time-critical in vitro and in vivo studies \n \n5. The contributions have advanced project into preclinical lead development for a novel antiviral platform","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Scientist III, Medicinal Chemistry at Olema Oncology · 2021年 - 现在 | Chemical Biology Specialist III at MOFFITT CANCER CENTER & RESEARCH INSTITUTE · 2020年 - 2021年 | Post-doctoral Research Associate at Purdue University College of Pharmacy · 2018年 - 2020年 | Post-Doctoral Research Associate at University of Wisconsin-Madison School of Pharmacy · 2015年 - 2018年 | Assistant Professor at Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences · 2012年 - 2014年","education":[{"school":"Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (PhD)","field_of_study":"Medicinal Chemistry","date_range":"2009年 - 2012年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences，Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) · 2009年 - 2012年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Senior Scientist Research Chemist Scientist Organic Chemist Chemistry Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 中国 开始日期 我在随便看看，时间可灵活安排 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese, English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
