{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:30:11+08:00","record":{"name":"Zhisong Cao","current_title":"Chief Chemist","current_company":"Stehlin Foundation for Cancer Research","location":"美国 德州 弗伦兹伍德","headline":"Research Professional","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhisong-cao-7003238b","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABMXTjAB-ZvKKb8d-7s7pKllkNmgfVBhQi4","core_skills":["Lifesciences","Analytical Chemistry","Spectroscopy"],"positions":[{"title":"Chief Chemist","company":"Stehlin Foundation for Cancer Research","date_range":"1994年 - 现在","duration":"32 年 9 个月","location":"","description":"• Directed the institutional program of anticancer drug discovery and development, successfully submitted 3 INDs (Investigational New Drug) to the FDA, conducted the subsequent management of human clinical trials.  \n• Applied and developed cutting edge synthetic and medicinal chemistry methodologies for the design and synthesis of new chemical entities to enable advancement of Foundation's drug discovery projects. \n• Designed and executed biological experiments including in vitro and in vivo evaluations, ADME (absorption, distribution, metabolism, and excretion) and PK studies with new molecules. \n• Analyzed data generated on lead compounds and leveraged results for the design of future compounds with superior overall efficacy and toxicity profiles. \n• Generated hypotheses for the design and synthesis of new target molecules with improved overall profile. \n• Applied the latest synthetic approaches, and parallel medicinal chemistry and modern purification methods to prepare any potential drug candidates for further testing and evaluation. \n• Collaborated with other scientists, e.g., computational chemist, pharmacologist and biologist, and other team members in compound design. \n• Supervised the contractual studies including GLP toxicity study and GMP manufacturing of APIs and drug products. \n• Assisted in managing regulatory affairs including interaction with the FDA (new IND applications and human clinical trials) and using animal models for experiments.  \n• Wrote study summaries and published research articles. \n• Prepared patent applications.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Fellow","company":"UTMB","date_range":"1992年6月 - 1994年4月","duration":"1 年 11 个月","location":"","description":"1. Studied the possible mechanism of breast cancer caused by 4-hydroxylation of estrogens. \n2. Synthesized 6-oxeestrogens (by total synthesis) to inhibit the 4-hydroxylation reaction of estrogens. \n3. Published 5 articles in various journals.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Chief Chemist at Stehlin Foundation for Cancer Research · 1994年 - 现在 | Postdoctoral Fellow at UTMB · 1992年 - 1994年","education":[{"school":"University of Delaware","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Organic Chemistry","date_range":"1988年 - 1992年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"华中师范大学","degree":"Master's degree","field_of_study":"Organic Chemistry","date_range":"1984年 - 1987年","activities":"活动与社团: MS thesis entitled \"The Chemistry of Tricyclic Triazophospholine\". From this work, 8 articles published in various scientific journals and also more ten research projects derived for subsequent graduate students.","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | University of Delaware，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 1988年 - 1992年 | 华中师范大学，Master's degree · 1984年 - 1987年 | 保存到项目 | 将Zhisong保存到项目 | 发消息给Zhisong | Zhisong Cao的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
