{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:33:39+08:00","record":{"name":"Connie Chai, PhD","current_title":"Scientist III","current_company":"Omniose · 全职","location":"圣路易斯地区","headline":"Drug Discovery","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/connie-chai-phd-14688131","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAa2v4YBIBJybF3DF_6AN--pgns_Y8jOtD0","core_skills":["Scrum","Project Management","In Vivo"],"positions":[{"title":"Scientist III","company":"Omniose · 全职","date_range":"2024年1月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 9 个月","location":"St.Louis, MO","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist I","company":"Vir Biotechnology, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2020年1月 - 2023年12月","duration":"4 年","location":"美国 密苏里州 圣路易斯","description":"•Served as in vivo lead across nine preclinical programs spanning infectious disease and immuno-oncology; generated the in vivo efficacy and PK/PD data package. \n•Designed Fc variant panels for checkpoint inhibitor candidates and ranked them on effector function to improve anti-tumor efficacy. \n•Defined the dosing regimen and target engagement criteria that advanced a small-molecule ENPP1 inhibitor into solid tumor efficacy studies, building the in vivo PK/PD strategy around a mechanism-based cGAMP biomarker and directing cross-functional execution with bioanalytical and chemistry. \n•Built and led a 20-person team for validation and immune phenotyping of hFcγR mouse lines, deploying fit-for-purpose models across infectious disease and oncology pipelines. \n•Partnered across discovery functions to enable in vivo evaluation: co-developed cross-species flow cytometry panels with Immune Targeting for mouse and human FcγR phenotyping, worked with Medicinal Chemistry on compound design and dosing formulation, and managed CRO relationships for animal sourcing and outsourced bioanalytical work. \n•Chaired program meetings to align stakeholders on status, risk, and go/no-go decisions, surfacing risks with mitigation plans ahead of impact; trained and mentored junior scientists in in vivo study design and data interpretation.","skills":["Monoclonal Antibodies","Small Molecules","Oncology","In Vivo"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Researcher","company":"Northwestern University - The Feinberg School of Medicine","date_range":"2014年9月 - 2019年7月","duration":"4 年 11 个月","location":"Chicago IL","description":"•Identified amyloid precursor protein as an innate anti-HIV-1 restriction factor in macrophages and microglia, blocking virion production via Gag sequestration in lipid rafts.","skills":["Immunology","Flow Cytometry"]},{"title":"Project Manager","company":"The State Key Laboratory of Agricultural Microbiology","date_range":"1 年 8 个月","duration":"1 年 8 个月","location":"中国 湖北省 武汉","description":"• Performed job specific tasks in compliance with applicable regulations, Wuhan Keqian Biological Co.,Ltd. policies, and SOPs \n• Ensured that all project work was completed in accordance with SOPs and applicable regulations, policies and practices.","skills":["技能: Communication • Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)","Communication","Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)","技能: Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)"]},{"title":"Clinical Research Associate","company":"The State Key Laboratory of Agricultural Microbiology","date_range":"1 年 8 个月","duration":"1 年 8 个月","location":"中国 湖北省 武汉","description":"• Performed job specific tasks in compliance with applicable regulations, Wuhan Keqian Biological Co.,Ltd. policies, and SOPs \n• Ensured that all project work was completed in accordance with SOPs and applicable regulations, policies and practices.","skills":["技能: Communication • Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)","Communication","Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)","技能: Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Scientist III at Omniose · 2024年 - 现在 | Scientist I at Vir Biotechnology, Inc. · 2020年 - 2023年 | The Feinberg School of Medicine - Postdoctoral Researcher at Northweste