{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:33:49+08:00","record":{"name":"Annie Wai Yeeng Chai","current_title":"Head of Translational Cancer Biology Unit","current_company":"Cancer Research Malaysia","location":"马来西亚 吉隆坡 WP. Kuala Lumpur","headline":"Head of Translational Cancer Biology Unit, Cancer Research Malaysia","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/anniewaiyeengchai","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAB18mkgBrMS8E0RPi5ju_nZPye1GgAK-BIA","core_skills":["CRISPR gene editing","Target discovery","Basic R programming"],"positions":[{"title":"Head of Translational Cancer Biology Unit","company":"Cancer Research Malaysia","date_range":"8 年 11 个月","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"马来西亚","description":"Leading the Translational Cancer Biology (TCB) Unit, I drive research efforts to uncover novel treatment strategies for cancers prevalent in Asian populations. My role involves overseeing multidisciplinary projects that bridge fundamental cancer biology with translational applications, ensuring that our discoveries move from the lab to clinical impact. \n \nKey responsibilities include: \n🔬 Spearheading research on targeted therapies, drug discovery, and biomarker development. \n🤝 Fostering collaborations with academic, clinical, and industry partners to accelerate innovation. \n📊 Securing funding and managing resources to sustain high-impact cancer research. \n👩‍🔬 Mentoring scientists and fostering a culture of scientific excellence within the team. \n💡 Engaging in strategic planning to align research priorities with CRMY’s mission of saving Asian lives. \n \nPassionate about bridging the gap between scientific discoveries and real-world applications, I am committed to making a meaningful difference in cancer treatment and outcomes. \n \nCurrently, I lead a team of postdoctoral scientists and research associates and co-supervise master and PhD students with our university collaborators. On-going projects include the TeD1-funded project in drug discovery for oral cancers, characterization of host-EBV interactions for therapeutic intervention for NPC, as well as studies on the immunomodulatory roles of essential genes in oral cancers and NPC.","skills":["技能: Functional Genomics • CRISPR gene editing • Target discovery • Cancer Biology • Drug Repositioning","Functional Genomics","CRISPR gene editing","Target discovery","Cancer Biology","Drug Repositioning"]},{"title":"Deputy Head of Translational Cancer Biology Unit","company":"Cancer Research Malaysia","date_range":"8 年 11 个月","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"马来西亚","description":"Leading the Translational Cancer Biology (TCB) Unit, I drive research efforts to uncover novel treatment strategies for cancers prevalent in Asian populations. My role involves overseeing multidisciplinary projects that bridge fundamental cancer biology with translational applications, ensuring that our discoveries move from the lab to clinical impact. \n \nKey responsibilities include: \n🔬 Spearheading research on targeted therapies, drug discovery, and biomarker development. \n🤝 Fostering collaborations with academic, clinical, and industry partners to accelerate innovation. \n📊 Securing funding and managing resources to sustain high-impact cancer research. \n👩‍🔬 Mentoring scientists and fostering a culture of scientific excellence within the team. \n💡 Engaging in strategic planning to align research priorities with CRMY’s mission of saving Asian lives. \n \nPassionate about bridging the gap between scientific discoveries and real-world applications, I am committed to making a meaningful difference in cancer treatment and outcomes. \n \nCurrently, I lead a team of postdoctoral scientists and research associates and co-supervise master and PhD students with our university collaborators. On-going projects include the TeD1-funded project in drug discovery for oral cancers, characterization of host-EBV interactions for therapeutic intervention for NPC, as well as studies on the immunomodulatory roles of essential genes in oral cancers and NPC.","skills":["技能: Functional Genomics • CRISPR gene editing • Target discovery • Cancer Biology • Drug Repositioning","Functional Genomics","CRISPR gene editing","Target discovery","Cancer Biology","Drug Repositioning"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Fellow","company":"Cancer Research Malaysia","date_range":"8 年 11 个月","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"马来西亚","description":"Leading the Translational Cancer Biology (TCB) Unit, I drive research efforts to uncover novel treatment strategies for cancers prevalent in Asian populations. My role involves overseeing multidisciplinary projects that bridge fundamental cancer biology with translational applications, ensuring that our discoveries move from the lab to clinical impact. \n \nKey responsibilities include: \n🔬 Spearheading research on targeted therapies, drug discovery, and biomarker development. \n🤝 Fostering collaborations with academic, clinical, and industry partners to accelerate innovation. \n📊 Securing funding and managing resources to sustain high-impact cancer research. \n👩‍🔬 Mentoring scientists and fostering a culture of scientific excellence within the team. \n💡 Engaging in strategic planning to align research priorities with CRMY’s mission of saving Asian lives. \n \nPassionate about bridging the gap between scientific discoveries and real-world applications, I am committed to making a meaningful difference in cancer treatment and outcomes. \n \nCurrently, I lead a team of postdoctoral scientists and research associates and co-supervise master and PhD students with our university collaborators. On-going projects include the TeD1-funded project in drug discovery for oral cancers, characterization of host-EBV interactions for therapeutic intervention for NPC, as well as studies on the immunomodulatory roles of essential genes in oral cancers and NPC.","skills":["技能: Functional Genomics • CRISPR gene editing • Target discovery • Cancer Biology • Drug Repositioning","Functional Genomics","CRISPR gene editing","Target discovery","Cancer Biology","Drug Repositioning"]},{"title":"Chair","company":"AACR-Global Scholars Alumni Committee","date_range":"2023年8月 - 现在","duration":"3 年 2 个月","location":"","description":"The AACR Global Scholar Alumni Committee (GSAC) supports the AACR’s mission to prevent and cure cancer by promoting the professional development of early- and mid-career Global Scholar-in-Training Awardee (GSITA) alumni who currently represent more than 80 talented scholars from countries with emerging economies.","skills":[]},{"title":"Student Research Assistant","company":"Academic Liaison Section, The University of Hong Kong","date_range":"2012年1月 - 2012年5月","duration":"5 个月","location":"Global Lounge, The University of Hong Kong","description":"Assisted in international and exchange students’ admission affairs","skills":[]},{"title":"Assistant Chemist","company":"Tender Products Malaysia","date_range":"2010年5月 - 2010年6月","duration":"2 个月","location":"","description":"Assisted the chief chemist in the quality control of the company’s products, regular equipment maintenance and calibration in the laboratory.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Head of Translational Cancer Biology Unit at Cancer Research Malaysia · 2025年 - 现在 | Chair at AACR-Global Scholars Alumni Committee · 2023年 - 现在 | Deputy Head of Translational Cancer Biology Unit at Cancer Research Malaysia · 2021年 - 2024年 | Postdoctoral Fellow at Cancer Research Malaysia · 2017年 - 2020年 | Student Research Assistant at Academic Liaison Section, The University of Hong Kong · 2012年 - 2012年 | Assistant Chemist at Tender Products Malaysia · 2010年 - 2010年","education":[{"school":"香港大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (PhD)","field_of_study":"Cellular and Molecular Biology of Cancer","date_range":"2013年 - 2017年","activities":"活动与社团: Student Ambassador","grade":""},{"school":"香港大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_stud