{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:35:52+08:00","record":{"name":"Man (Manna) C.","current_title":"Principal Biostatistician","current_company":"Regeneron / Proclinical · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 South Weymouth","headline":"Principal Biostatistician","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/mchang99","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAACa_RoB-G43MosNHBGJc2T475gxa17OnsU","core_skills":["Pharmaceutical Industry","Study Reports","Medical Affairs"],"positions":[{"title":"Principal Biostatistician","company":"Regeneron / Proclinical · 全职","date_range":"2025年11月 - 现在","duration":"11 个月","location":"美国","description":"• Serve as project/study lead statistician for Phase II and Phase III oncology clinical studies, providing statistical leadership across study development and regulatory activities. \n• Collaborate with the team to develop responses to regulatory queries related to the study protocols and make amendments to the protocols as requested. \n• Partner with cross-functional teams to author major Phase II protocol amendments, including sample size justification and statistical boundaries for accepting new regimens. \n• Lead supplementary resubmission activities across multiple studies within a clinical program, including mock-shell amendments, data review, and coordination with Data Management, Clinical Science, and Statistical Programming. \n• Provide statistical review and issue resolution for CSR, ISS/ISE, PSUR, and DSUR deliverables supporting regulatory submissions. \n• Support clinical decision-making through predictive probability, statistical modeling, simulation, time-to-event analysis, and estimation of median PFS, OS, DOCR, and DOR.","skills":[]},{"title":"Principal Biostatistician FSP","company":"Cytel / AstraZeneca · 全职","date_range":"2024年9月 - 2025年10月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"波士顿地区","description":"Serve as study lead statistician supporting study design of early and late phase clinical studies; conducted analysis including but not limited to sample size calculation, consistency analysis, phase III adaptive design and time to event analysis; authoring SAP, SIP and TLF shells and review; provide input to protocol deviation plan and eCRF design.","skills":[]},{"title":"Principal Data Scientist and Biostatistician","company":"Lumicell · 全职","date_range":"2019年4月 - 2024年9月","duration":"5 年 6 个月","location":"Newton, MA","description":"• Serve as study lead biostatistician for early- and late-phase clinical studies in breast cancer and other oncology indications.  \n• Led the statistical function for the clinical development of LUMISIGHT, including Phase II feasibility and Phase III pivotal INSIGHT studies evaluating safety, efficacy, and real-time residual tumor detection. \n• Supported the NDA/PMA regulatory submission and successful FDA approval, including CSR and ISE development, regulatory document review, ADRG preparation, responses to regulatory authorities, and preparation for FDA BIMO inspection. \n• Participated in preparation for and execution of the FDA Advisory Committee meeting supporting the product approval process. \n• Led development of ISS and ISE SAPs and statistical deliverables and oversaw/quality-controlled CRO-generated ISS and other regulatory deliverables. \n• Authored statistical sections of clinical study protocols and SAPs; developed and reviewed CSRs and supported scientific publications. \n• Conducted analyses using GEE, GLM, MMRM, parametric and non-parametric methods, patient-reported outcomes, quality analyses, and subgroup/subset analyses, providing statistical interpretation for clinical teams. \n• Developed and implemented a biometrics SOP to support consistent statistical practices. \n• Applied Bayesian study-design approaches and historical-data borrowing to support clinical development decisions. \n• Managed and mentored junior statisticians and interns and coordinated work with external statistical consultants.","skills":["Manuscript","Regulatory Filings","New Drug Application (NDA)","Statistics","Scientific Communications","Regulatory Submissions","Medical Affairs","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Biotechnology Industry","Statistical Programming","Statistical Analysis Plans","Randomization","Communication","CDISC Standards","Contract Research Organization (CRO)","Query Writing","Study Reports","Statistical Analysis","CRFs","SAS","Clinical Development"]},{"title":"Senior Data Scientist","company":"UnitedHealth Group · 全职","date_range":"2017年9月 - 2019年4月","duration":"1 年 8 个月","location":"波士顿地区","description":"Analyzed large-scale real-world healthcare and claims data to generate insights and support significant business and healthcare decisions. \nDeveloped and applied machine-learning methods, including artificial neural networks and transformer-based deep learning, to identify rapidly progressing CKD patients, improve targeting of personalized healthcare, detect data anomalies, and classify sentiment in application reviews. \nApplied Explainable DeepLIFT to interpret neural-network feature contributions and support hypothesis generation. \nConsulted with stakeholders to define machine-learning project requirements, recommend analytical methodologies, and negotiate deliverables. \nLed and mentored junior data scientists in delivery of agile analytical projects.","skills":["Statistics","Scientific Communications","Observational Studies","Randomization","Communication","Statistical Analysis"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Principal Biostatistician at Regeneron / Proclinical · 2025年 - 现在 | Principal Biostatistician FSP at Cytel / AstraZeneca · 2024年 - 2025年 | Principal Data Scientist and Biostatistician at Lumicell · 2019年 - 2024年 | Senior Data Scientist at UnitedHealth Group · 2017年 - 2019年 | Senior Analytics Scientist at Foundation Medicine · 2015年 - 2017年 | Application Specialist at Linguamatics · 2009年 - 2015年 | Principal Scientist at Pfizer · 2000年 - 2009年 | Research Fellow at University of Michigan · 1996年 - 1999年 | Postdoc at University of North Carolina · 1995年 - 1995年","education":[{"school":"美国德克萨斯A&M大学","degree":"Master's degree","field_of_study":"Statistics","date_range":"2015年","activities":"活动与社团: ASA","grade":"3.63"},{"school":"北京协和医学院","degree":"","field_of_study":"Medicine","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"美国韦恩州立大学","degree":"Ph.D.","field_of_study":"Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 美国德克萨斯A&M大学，Master's degree · 2015年 | 北京协和医学院 | 美国韦恩州立大学，Ph.D. | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:36:06+08:00","record":{"name":"Jen-Kuan C.","current_title":"Associate Director","current_company":"Henlius USA Inc.","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 弗里蒙特","headline":"Associate Director | Biologics Discovery & Translational Strategy | Oncology & Immunology | Discovery to IND","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jen-kuan-c","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABNkZfIBu7tyMJuO3Oax0LYTAEw8Wb5H5Y8","core_skills":["Transduction","Immunoprecipitation","Assay Development"],"positions":[{"title":"Associate Director","company":"Henlius USA Inc.","date_range":"8 年 9 个月","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"Milpitas, California, United States","description":"• Lead scientific strategy, translational research, and external innovation across oncology, immunology, and next-generation therapeutic platforms. \n• Serve in a scientific leadership role in the E-688/HLX316 co-development program, a first-in-class B7-H3-targeted sialidase biologic, spanning translational strategy, pharmacology, partner collaboration, and cross-functional program development. \n• Designed and drove key in vivo studies that supported E-688/HLX316 through IND clearance in Dec 2025 and entry into clinical development in May 2026. \n• Supported scientific and translational activities for E-602/HLX79, a clinical-stage human sialidase therapeutic being developed for autoimmune disease. \n• Generated and led new therapeutic concepts by integrating disease biology, asset repurposing, functional screening, candidate prioritization, and early development planning as Project Team Leader (PTL). \n• Led preclinical and translational strategy for HLX109 (anti-IL-1R3), including in vitro and in vivo validation, benchmark assessment, indication strategy, and evaluation of additional therapeutic applications. \n• Evaluate external assets and platforms across biologics, multispecific antibodies, T-cell engagers, immunocytokines, targeted delivery, AI-enabled discovery, and other emerging modalities. \n• Conduct scientific due diligence and provide go/no-go recommendations based on mechanism, differentiation, translational rationale, preclinical evidence, competitive landscape, development feasibility, and strategic fit; coordinate across R&D, CMC, toxicology, clinical development, IP, and external collaborators.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist to Principal Scientist","company":"Henlius USA Inc.","date_range":"8 年 9 个月","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"Milpitas, California, United States","description":"• Lead scientific strategy, translational research, and external innovation across oncology, immunology, and next-generation therapeutic platforms. \n• Serve in a scientific leadership role in the E-688/HLX316 co-development program, a first-in-class B7-H3-targeted sialidase biologic, spanning translational strategy, pharmacology, partner collaboration, and cross-functional program development. \n• Designed and drove key in vivo studies that supported E-688/HLX316 through IND clearance in Dec 2025 and entry into clinical development in May 2026. \n• Supported scientific and translational activities for E-602/HLX79, a clinical-stage human sialidase therapeutic being developed for autoimmune disease. \n• Generated and led new therapeutic concepts by integrating disease biology, asset repurposing, functional screening, candidate prioritization, and early development planning as Project Team Leader (PTL). \n• Led preclinical and translational strategy for HLX109 (anti-IL-1R3), including in vitro and in vivo validation, benchmark assessment, indication strategy, and evaluation of additional therapeutic applications. \n• Evaluate external assets and platforms across biologics, multispecific antibodies, T-cell engagers, immunocytokines, targeted delivery, AI-enabled discovery, and other emerging modalities. \n• Conduct scientific due diligence and provide go/no-go recommendations based on mechanism, differentiation, translational rationale, preclinical evidence, competitive landscape, development feasibility, and strategic fit; coordinate across R&D, CMC, toxicology, clinical development, IP, and external collaborators.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior ScientistPrincipal scientist/Project leader","company":"Henlix/Hengenix Biotech/Henlius USA, Inc.","date_range":"2018年1月 - 现在","duration":"8 年 9 个月","location":"","description":"• Hands-on in vitro assay design and development (protein phosphorylation, proliferation, phenotyping, cytotoxicity, phagocytosis, cytokine release, MLR, ELISA, Multi-channel extra/intracellular FACS) for antibody screening and MoA studies. \n• Design, analyze in vivo studies and do ex vivo studies for therapeutic antibody screening and validation. \n• Propose and lead novel tumor-killing and immune checkpoint-related bi-specific antibody/cytokine/enzyme fusion protein projects. \n• Participate in poster presentation/patent/BD/IND and move the project to the clinical stage as project leader (HLX35). \n• Participate in llama VHH antibody humanization/cloning, to support biomolecular binding kinetic assay and protein stability test.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Scholar","company":"University of California, Los Angeles","date_range":"2016年4月 - 2017年11月","duration":"1 年 8 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 洛杉矶","description":"• Conducted mechanistic studies of Protein Kinase D (PKD) signaling in intestinal epithelial and cancer models in the laboratory of Dr. Enrique Rozengurt. \n• Investigated regulation of PKD1 localization and signaling by p21-activated kinases (PAKs), including downstream effects on HDAC phosphorylation, transcriptional regulation, and ERK signaling. \n• Studied the effects of statins on PKD and YAP/TAZ signaling in intestinal and pancreatic cancer models. \n• Applied cell and molecular biology approaches including signal-transduction analysis, protein phosphorylation, gene-expression studies, cell culture, and biochemical assays. \n• Contributed to peer-reviewed publications resulting from this research.\n\n• To study type I p21-activated kinase (PAK) mediated PKD1 phosphorylation, localization, and downstream signaling. \n• PKD-induced extracellular signal-regulated kinase (ERK) relocation and downstream signaling in intestinal epithelial cell.","skills":[]},{"title":"Graduate Research Assistant","company":"Temple University","date_range":"2011年9月 - 2015年11月","duration":"4 年 3 个月","location":"美国 宾夕法尼亚州 费城","description":"• Conducted doctoral research in Dr. Thomas Rogers’ laboratory investigating μ-opioid receptor signaling, Protein Kinase D (PKD), microRNA regulation, and inflammatory responses in human monocytes and immune-cell models. \n• Studied opioid-induced signaling and gene-regulatory responses using primary human monocytes, macrophages, and established cell models. \n• Identified and characterized miRNA-mediated regulation of inflammatory signaling, including the relationship between opioid exposure, miR-21, and PKD/MAPK-associated pathways. \n• Performed primary-cell isolation and differentiation, mammalian cell culture, RNA/protein analysis, signal-transduction studies, and gene-expression profiling. \n• Conducted additional research on environmental toxicant-induced microRNA responses in lung tissue and lung cancer models. \n• Authored/co-authored peer-reviewed publications arising from doctoral research.\n\n• To study µ-opioid receptor (MOR) mediated Protein Kinase D (PKD) phosphorylation and downstream miRNA expression. \n• Isolate, culture, and treat PBMCs, BALs, bone marrow cells and splenocytes for HIV-, COPD- and drug abuse-related research.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Associate Director at Henlius USA Inc. · 2025年 - 现在 | Senior ScientistPrincipal scientist/Project leader at Henlix/Hengenix Biotech/Henlius USA, Inc. · 2018年 - 现在 | Scientist to Principal Scientist at Henlius USA Inc. · 2018年 - 2024年 | Postdoctoral Scholar at University of California, Los Angeles · 2016年 - 2017年 | Graduate Research Assistant at Temple University · 2011年 - 2015年 | Research Assistant at Fu Jen Catholic University · 2008年 - 2009年 | Second Lieutenant at ROC Army · 2005年 - 2006年 | Graduate Research Assistant at National Taiwan University · 2003年 - 2005年 | Trainee Student at National Sun Yat-sen University · 2002年 - 2003年","education":[{"school":"Temple University","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Molecular Biology and Genetics","date_range":"2010年 - 2015年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Master’s Degree","field_of_study":"Oral Biology","date_range":"2003年 - 2005年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"中山大学","degree":"Bachelor’s Degree","field_of_study":"Biological Science","date_range":"1999年 - 2003年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Temple University，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 2010年 - 2015年 | 台湾大学，Master’s Degree · 2003年 - 2005年 | 中山大学，Bachelor’s Degree · 1999年 - 2003年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 洛杉矶地区 旧金山湾区 开始日期 我在随便看看，时间可灵活安排 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
