{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:37:12+08:00","record":{"name":"Katarina Chang","current_title":"Scientist I","current_company":"UCB","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","headline":"Scientist I at UCB | Molecular Medicine PhD | Drug Discovery and Disease Modeling | AI Image Analysis | Biomedical Researcher","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/katarina-chang-189193133","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACCYqjkBvjlIA1xG8SMtLufNtDgmsBJuW_g","core_skills":["Target Identification and Validation","Bacterial Transformation","Molecular & Cellular Biology"],"positions":[{"title":"Scientist I","company":"UCB","date_range":"2023年7月 - 现在","duration":"3 年 3 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"Cross-functional role within the Translational Biology and Functional Genomics teams \nLeveraging high-content imaging and AI/machine learning image analysis in complex cellular systems to identify and validate novel targets\n\n• Spearheaded target discovery efforts by developing and implementing complex disease relevant iPSC based cellular models (iPSC-derived striatal medium spiny neuronal cultures). \n• Designed and implemented complex iPSC based cellular models for high-content imaging assays and image analysis. \n• Spearheaded novel platform acquisition for target discovery efforts by assessing platform performance in complex disease relevant iPSC-based cellular models (iPSC-derived myoblasts) for arrayed CRISPR screens. \n• Supported the validation of targets gleaned from functional genomics and human genetics screens for the neuromuscular focus area. \n• Contributed to the development of strategy for new target discovery for neuroscience and neuromuscular disorders for the neuromuscular and rare diseases for the UCB US Research organization.","skills":["Target Identification and Validation","Assay Development","High Content Screening","Spotfire"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Researcher","company":"University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB)","date_range":"5 年","duration":"3 个月","location":"","description":"Under the direction of Dr. Stuart Martin, I am elucidating the role of acute calcium signaling and its impact on the cytoskeleton in breast epithelial and tumor cell models.\n\n• Completed doctoral dissertation in the lab of Stuart S Martin, PhD. \n• Designed and executed molecular biology assays to assess the effects of transient calcium signaling on rapid cytoskeletal rearrangement in a nonadherent breast epithelial and cancer cell culture model. \n• Presented novel scientific findings in an oral presentation at the 12th Annual Cancer Biology Research Retreat at the University of Maryland, Baltimore. \n• Repurposed high throughput screening with liquid handling capability instrumentation to examine calcium signaling in breast epithelial and breast tumor cells stimulated by fluid stress. \n• Collaborated on the interdisciplinary project optimizing TetherChip technology for single cell tracking of mammosphere formation in 3D anchorage independent formation. \n• Mentored and trained undergraduate, graduate, and rotation students.","skills":["技能: Cancer Research","Cancer Research"]},{"title":"Doctoral Student","company":"University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB)","date_range":"5 年","duration":"3 个月","location":"","description":"Under the direction of Dr. Stuart Martin, I am elucidating the role of acute calcium signaling and its impact on the cytoskeleton in breast epithelial and tumor cell models.\n\n• Completed doctoral dissertation in the lab of Stuart S Martin, PhD. \n• Designed and executed molecular biology assays to assess the effects of transient calcium signaling on rapid cytoskeletal rearrangement in a nonadherent breast epithelial and cancer cell culture model. \n• Presented novel scientific findings in an oral presentation at the 12th Annual Cancer Biology Research Retreat at the University of Maryland, Baltimore. \n• Repurposed high throughput screening with liquid handling capability instrumentation to examine calcium signaling in breast epithelial and breast tumor cells stimulated by fluid stress. \n• Collaborated on the interdisciplinary project optimizing TetherChip technology for single cell tracking of mammosphere formation in 3D anchorage independent formation. \n• Mentored and trained undergraduate, graduate, and rotation students.","skills":["技能: Cancer Research","Cancer Research"]},{"title":"Research Technician","company":"Binghamton University School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences","date_range":"2017年7月 - 2018年6月","duration":"1 年","location":"美国","description":"Under the direction of Dr. Tracy A Brooks, we investigated the functions, characteristics and expression of quadruplexes which promote cancer. Specifically, I worked on developing a novel therapeutic to target downregulation of MYC through the G-quadruplex for breast cancer and lymphoma.\n\n• Mentored by Principal Investigator: Tracy A Brooks, PhD. \n• Investigated and presented the therapeutic potential of manipulating the MYC g-quadruplex utilizing nucleic acid clamps for breast cancer and lymphoma. \n• Assessed and validated the therapeutic target potential of the kRASmid g-quadruplex. \n• Assisted in the coordination, setup and management of laboratory space and daily affairs. \n• Mentored and guided the project of an undergraduate research student.","skills":["Cancer Research"]},{"title":"Undergraduate Summer Research Intern","company":"Taipei Medical University","date_range":"2016年5月 - 2016年8月","duration":"4 个月","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","description":"• Performed real-time PCR and statistical analysis to verify microarray data gathered to study the interaction between lncRNA and mRNA and its role in the glioma microenvironment. \n• Taught wet lab technical and analytical skills to interns and graduate students, including pipetting, RNA isolation, RNA concentration calculations, protein concentration determination (using standard curve and calculations), and real-time PCR.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Scientist I at UCB · 2023年 - 现在 | Postdoctoral Researcher at University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB) · 2023年 - 2023年 | Doctoral Student at University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB) · 2018年 - 2023年 | Research Technician at Binghamton University School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences · 2017年 - 2018年 | Undergraduate Summer Research Intern at Taipei Medical University · 2016年 - 2016年 | Undergraduate Research Intern at National Chen Kung University · 2015年 - 2016年 | University at Buffalo's School of Public Health and Health Professions - Undergraduate Research Assistant · 2015年 - 2017年 | University at Buffalo - Undergraduate Research Assistant · 2014年 - 2015年","education":[{"school":"University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB)","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Molecular Medicine","date_range":"2018年 - 2023年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"美国纽约州立大学布法罗分校","degree":"Bachelor's of Science Pharmacology and Toxicology","field_of_study":"","date_range":"2013年 - 2017年","activities":"活动与社团: University at Buffalo Honors College, University at Buffalo Women's Swimming and Diving Team (2013-2015)","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB)，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2018年 - 2023年 | 美国纽约州立大学布法罗分校， Bachelor's of Science Pharmacology and Toxicology · 2013年 - 2017年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Scientist Senior Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":false,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:37:23+08:00","record":{"name":"Renxu Chang","current_title":"Senior Researcher investigator","current_company":"Synnovation Therapeutics · 全职","location":"费城地区","headline":"drug discovery scientist","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/renxu-chang-5b25b7142","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACKdyZYBW_BuRZyUW0_e_b7g450XBCIS2sc","core_skills":["2D and 3D culture","Organoids culture","xenograft model"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Researcher investigator","company":"Synnovation Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2024年8月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 2 个月","location":"美国 德拉瓦 威尔明顿","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Researcher","company":"University of Pennsylvania · 全职","date_range":"2018年8月 - 2024年8月","duration":"6 年 1 个月","location":"","description":"understanding the function and cellular mechanism of E3 ligases in diffuse large B-cell Lymphoma, the cellular mechanism of drug resistance in cancer.\n\n• Function and mechanism of E3 ligases in Leukemia 1. \n• CRISPR screening coupled with proteomics to reveal DCAF15 as a cell autonomous acute myeloid leukemia dependency sustaining DNA replication through control of cohesin recycling and acetylation dynamics. \n• 2. \n• Identified the Runt-related transcription factor 1 and 3 (RUNX1 and RUNX3) as interactors of IKZF1 and IKZF3. \n• Interaction with RUNX1 and RUNX3 inhibits CRBN-dependent binding, ubiquitylation, and degradation of IKZF1 and IKZF3 upon lenalidomide treatment. \n• Inhibition of RUNXs results in sensitization of myeloma cell lines and primary tumors to lenalidomide.","skills":["Tissue Culture","Immunofluorescence","Immunoprecipitation","Mouse Models","Western Blotting","RNAseq Analysis","Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR)","Molecular Cloning","Mutagenesis","Cell Culture"]},{"title":"Ph.D. graduate researcher","company":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences · 全职","date_range":"2011年9月 - 2018年1月","duration":"6 年 5 个月","location":"中国 上海市","description":"1. Mechanisms of metastasis and chemotherapeutic sensitivity in solid tumors. \nMy graduating works uncovered the functions and mechanisms of a couple of polarity proteins or polarity-relevant proteins polarity protein in cancer development, particularly in metastasis and chemotherapeutic sensitivity. Specifically, my works revealed that loss of Scribble-induced HuR translocation mediates the accumulation of Snail via activation of the p38 MAPK pathway to elevate chemical drug sensitivity of NSCLC and revealed that loss of Wwox promotes breast cancer metastasis by JAK/STAT3 pathway. \n2. The crosstalk between lesion and microenvironment in inflammatory blow disease. \nIdentified miR-494-3p-mediated cross-talk mechanism by which inflamed colonic lamina propria macrophages integrate signals from differentiated IECs to regulate colonic stemness and colonic epithelial repair/homeostasis.\n\n• The crosstalk between lesion and microenvironment in inflammatory blow disease, Mechanisms of metastasis and chemotherapeutic sensitivity in solid tumors.","skills":["Tissue Culture","2D and 3D culture","Organoids culture","ELISA","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)","xenograft model","Western Blotting","Molecular & Cellular Biology","Cell Based Assays"]},{"title":"Bachelor of Science: Clinical Laboratory Science","company":"Shanghai Jiaotong University","date_range":"2007年9月 - 2011年5月","duration":"3 年 9 个月","location":"","description":"","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Senior Researcher investigator at Synnovation Therapeutics · 2024年 - 现在 | Postdoctoral Researcher at University of Pennsylvania · 2018年 - 2024年 | Ph.D. graduate researcher at University of Chinese Academy of Sciences · 2011年 - 2018年 | Bachelor of Science: Clinical Laboratory Science at Shanghai Jiaotong University · 2007年 - 2011年","education":[{"school":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD",