{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:37:35+08:00","record":{"name":"Chou-Wei Chang, PhD","current_title":"Molecular Biology Scientist","current_company":"AB Biosciences · 全职","location":"波士顿地区","headline":"Molecular biology scientist, Vector Design | Extracellular Vesicle/Delivery vehicle Engineering | CRISPR-Cas technology | Gene editing | Cell line development","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/chou-wei-chang-phd-a67867a7","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABa66y8B31mA53klrIvA-EmtUohbxEZuX6o","core_skills":["Prime editing","Base editing","primary cell isolation and culture"],"positions":[{"title":"Molecular Biology Scientist","company":"AB Biosciences · 全职","date_range":"2026年9月 - 现在","duration":"1 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 康科特","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"Vesigen Therapeutics, Inc.","date_range":"2 年 3 个月","duration":"9 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"• Led platform development initiatives, including novel gene editor development, payload enhancement, non-viral delivery engineering, gRNA optimization, and re-targeting (cell tropism) initiatives. \n• Designed and optimized RNA, peptide payload, and CRISPR/Cas-based genome-editing strategies for both in vivo (mice, mini-pig, rabbit, NHP, human) and in vitro applications, with a focus on ocular diseases and immunomodulation. \n• Designed and executed complex molecular cloning workflows (Gibson assembly, Golden Gate, restriction enzyme-based methods) for RNA, peptide, and protein delivery studies. \n• Established and optimized cell-based assays to assess therapeutic candidates and streamline preclinical workflows. \n• Collaborated with bioinformatics and in vivo teams to refine experimental workflows and enhance gene modulation efficiency. \n• Managed and trained research associates and associate scientists. \n• Maintained detailed documentation of scientific work in an electronic notebook (ELN) to ensure data integrity.\n\n• Led mammalian cell engineering studies supporting development of extracellular vesicle-based biologic therapeutics. \n• Designed and optimized cell-based functional assays to evaluate therapeutic payload delivery and biological activity. \n• Applied CRISPR genome editing approaches to investigate cellular pathways and improve platform performance. \n• Developed scalable multi-well screening workflows supporting parallel evaluation of engineered therapeutic constructs. \n• Collaborated with discovery, molecular biology, protein engineering, and in vivo teams to advance therapeutic programs. \n• Troubleshot complex experimental workflows and presented scientific findings to project teams.","skills":["技能: Flow Cytometry • Droplet Digital PCR (ddPCR) • Prime editing • Base editing • CRISPR/Cas • Crispr • Cell Based Assays • RNA Biology • primary cell isolation and culture • Development Strategy","Flow Cytometry","Droplet Digital PCR (ddPCR)","Prime editing","Base editing","CRISPR/Cas","Crispr","Cell Based Assays","RNA Biology","primary cell isolation and culture","Development Strategy"]},{"title":"Scientist II","company":"Vesigen Therapeutics, Inc.","date_range":"2 年 3 个月","duration":"9 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"• Led platform development initiatives, including novel gene editor development, payload enhancement, non-viral delivery engineering, gRNA optimization, and re-targeting (cell tropism) initiatives. \n• Designed and optimized RNA, peptide payload, and CRISPR/Cas-based genome-editing strategies for both in vivo (mice, mini-pig, rabbit, NHP, human) and in vitro applications, with a focus on ocular diseases and immunomodulation. \n• Designed and executed complex molecular cloning workflows (Gibson assembly, Golden Gate, restriction enzyme-based methods) for RNA, peptide, and protein delivery studies. \n• Established and optimized cell-based assays to assess therapeutic candidates and streamline preclinical workflows. \n• Collaborated with bioinformatics and in vivo teams to refine experimental workflows and enhance gene modulation efficiency. \n• Managed and trained research associates and associate scientists. \n• Maintained detailed documentation of scientific work in an electronic notebook (ELN) to ensure data integrity.\n\n• Led mammalian cell engineering studies supporting development of extracellular vesicle-based biologic therapeutics. \n• Designed and optimized cell-based functional assays to evaluate therapeutic payload delivery and biological activity. \n• Applied CRISPR genome editing approaches to investigate cellular pathways and improve platform performance. \n• Developed scalable multi-well screening workflows supporting parallel evaluation of engineered therapeutic constructs. \n• Collaborated with discovery, molecular biology, protein engineering, and in vivo teams to advance therapeutic programs. \n• Troubleshot complex experimental workflows and presented scientific findings to project teams.","skills":["技能: Flow Cytometry • Droplet Digital PCR (ddPCR) • Prime editing • Base editing • CRISPR/Cas • Crispr • Cell Based Assays • RNA Biology • primary cell isolation and culture • Development Strategy","Flow Cytometry","Droplet Digital PCR (ddPCR)","Prime editing","Base editing","CRISPR/Cas","Crispr","Cell Based Assays","RNA Biology","primary cell isolation and culture","Development Strategy"]},{"title":"Staff Scientist","company":"City of Hope","date_range":"5 年 9 个月","duration":"11 个月","location":"California Duarte","description":"•Dissect the role of BRCA1 in ribosomal R-loop repression and rRNA processing. --A novel biochemical property of BRCA1 BRCT in binding to single-stranded RNA and promoting double-stranded RNA formation within ribosomal RNA, and this property is disrupted by a pathogenic mutation within the BRCT motif. \n•Investigate how RECQ4 dysfunction leads to developmental abnormalities and cancer. --Engineer and purify clinical mutations of RECQ proteins to compare similarities and differences to understand what aspects of genome maintenance and DNA metabolism are required for normal development and cancer prevention \n•Managed research associates and mentored new postdoctoral researchers.\n\n• Designed and optimized mammalian cell-based functional assays investigating innate immune signaling and mitochondrial stress responses. \n• Engineered mammalian expression constructs using molecular cloning and CRISPR technologies. \n• Performed mammalian cell culture, transient transfection, reporter assays, and functional validation experiments. \n• Mentored junior researchers and coordinated experimental planning across multiple research projects. \n• Communicated experimental findings through presentations and scientific reports.","skills":["技能: CRISPR/Cas • Crispr • Cell Based Assays • RNA Biology • Development Strategy","CRISPR/Cas","Crispr","Cell Based Assays","RNA Biology","Development Strategy","技能: CRISPR/Cas • Cell Based Assays • RNA Biology • Development Strategy"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Fellow","company":"City of Hope","date_range":"5 年 9 个月","duration":"11 个月","location":"California Duarte","description":"•Dissect the role of BRCA1 in ribosomal R-loop repression and rRNA processing. --A novel biochemical property of BRCA1 BRCT in binding to single-stranded RNA and promoting double-stranded RNA formation within ribosomal RNA, and this property is disrupted by a pathogenic mutation within the BRCT motif. \n•Investigate how RECQ4 dysfunction leads to developmental abnormalities and cancer. --Engineer and purify clinical mutations of RECQ proteins to compare similarities and differences to understand what aspects of genome maintenance and DNA metabolism are required for normal development and cancer prevention \n•Managed research associates and mentored new postdoctoral researchers.\n\n• Designed and optimized mammalian cell-based functional assays investigating innate immune signaling and mitochondrial stress responses. \n• 