ling (Tox) studies. \n• ​ Authored and reviewed CMC documents including Test methods, Development report, Assay qualification protocols/reports, Study reports, Data summary and a pending patent application. \n• ​ Helped with resource arrangement and FTE/contractor hiring. \n• ​ Responsible for managing 5 staff (Scientists to Senior Associate).","skills":["技能: Chemistry, Manufacturing, and Controls (CMC) • Biologics • CRO Management • Gene Therapy","Chemistry, Manufacturing, and Controls (CMC)","Biologics","CRO Management","Gene Therapy"]},{"title":"Senior Scientist, Analytical Development","company":"Locanabio, Inc.","date_range":"2 年 6 个月","duration":"5 个月","location":"","description":"-Supervision of bioassay selection, development, optimization, qualification and test method transfer to both CDMO/CRO and internal partners. \n-Study lead for In-use compatibility and stability, formulation, biological assay bridging studies.  \n-Subject matter expert (SME) for titer assay in support of non-GLP toxicology study. \n-Technical SME for leading cross functional team collaboration with Process Development, Vector Development, Quality Assurance, and Research.\n\n• ​ Directed and managed bioanalytical team for assay selection, development, optimization, qualification/validation for batch release and stability testing of DS/DP and in-process samples. \n• With a focus on cell-based potency assays. \n• ​ Transferred 7 assays to CDMO/CRO and internal partners. \n• Designed transfer procedures and feasibility studies. \n• Reviewed CDMO/CRO data packages and conducted troubleshooting and OOS investigation. \n• ​ Spearheaded in-use compatibility and stability, formulation, critical reagent bridging studies. \n• ​ Managed analytical testing to support GLP toxicology studies and non-GMP manufacturing. \n• ​ Collaboration with cross functional teams including Process Development, Vector Development, Quality Assurance, and Research to support IND enabling (Tox) studies. \n• ​ Authored and reviewed CMC documents including Test methods, Development report, Assay qualification protocols/reports, Study reports, Data summary and a pending patent application. \n• ​ Helped with resource arrangement and FTE/contractor hiring. \n• ​ Responsible for managing 5 staff (Scientists to Senior Associate).","skills":["技能: Chemistry, Manufacturing, and Controls (CMC) • Biologics • CRO Management • Gene Therapy","Chemistry, Manufacturing, and Controls (CMC)","Biologics","CRO Management","Gene Therapy"]},{"title":"Senior Scientist - Analytical Development","company":"诺华","date_range":"3 年 1 个月","duration":"2 年","location":"Greater San Diego Area","description":"Image-based assay optimization and qualification. \nMOA-reflecting enzymatic assay development.\n\n• ​ Project lead for undisclosed preclinical pipeline projects. \n• ​ Initiated 15+ AAV plasmid construction. \n• Developed cell-based in vitro potency assays for 6 pipeline projects. \n• ​ Steered the development, optimization and qualification of image-, ELISA-, RT-qPCR-based and MOA-reflecting cell-based potency assay. \n• ​ Developed AAV identity (ID) assays: ELISA-based (in house) and lateral flow-base (with external CRO). \n• ​ Worked under agency guidelines and in GxP environment, drafted SOPs, method development reports and other supporting documents, provided technical support to Quality. \n• ​ Established in vitro AAV9 neutralization assay and AAV9 and AAV2 binding assay with Octet platform. \n• ​ Designed and executed in vivo safety and efficacy studies. \n• ​ Managed 1 scientist and 1 intern student.","skills":["技能: Biologics • Gene Therapy","Biologics","Gene Therapy"]},{"title":"Senior Scientist - Research and Development","company":"诺华","date_range":"3 年 1 个月","duration":"2 年","location":"Greater San Diego Area","description":"Image-based assay optimization and qualification. \nMOA-reflecting enzymatic assay development.\n\n• ​ Project lead for undisclosed preclinical pipeline projects. \n• ​ Initiated 15+ AAV plasmid construction. \n• Developed cell-based in vitro potency assays for 6 pipeline projects. \n• ​ Steered the development, optimization and qualification of image-, ELISA-, RT-qPCR-based and MOA-reflecting cell-based potency assay. \n• ​ Developed AAV identity (ID) assays: ELISA-based (in house) and lateral flow-base (with external CRO). \n• ​ Worked under agency guidelines and in GxP environment, drafted SOPs, method development reports and other supporting documents, provided technical support to Quality. \n• ​ Established in vitro AAV9 neutralization assay and AAV9 and AAV2 binding assay with Octet platform. \n• ​ Designed and executed in vivo safety and efficacy studies. \n• ​ Managed 1 scientist and 1 intern student.","skills":["技能: Biologics • Gene Therapy","Biologics","Gene Therapy"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Associate Director, Analytical Development at Abzena · 2025年 - 现在 | Senior Principal Scientist, CMC Analytical Development at Neurocrine Biosciences · 2024年 - 2025年 | Associate Director, Analytical and Formulation Development at Locanabio, Inc. · 2023年 - 2023年 | Senior Scientist, Analytical Development at Locanabio, Inc. · 2021年 - 2023年 | Senior Scientist - Analytical Development at Novartis · 2019年 - 2021年 | Senior Scientist - Research and Development at Novartis · 2018年 - 2019年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow at Genentech · 2013年 - 2018年 | PhD Student at University of Massachusetts Medical School · 2008年 - 2013年 | Teaching Assistant at National Taiwan University · 2006年 - 2006年 | Research Assistant at National Yang Ming University · 2005年 - 2008年","education":[{"school":"UMass Chan Medical School","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (PhD)","field_of_study":"Autophagy and Cancer Biology","date_range":"2008年 - 2013年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"阳明大学","degree":"Master of Science - MS","field_of_study":"Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"台湾大学","degree"