ew technologies to further improve quality and efficiency of clinical biomarker analyses. \nReviewing and uploading study related documentations in Trial Master File (TMF). \nDemonstrating exceptional teamwork skills to achieve study goals and drive successful project outcomes.","skills":["技能: Presentations • Good Clinical Practice (GCP) • Oncology • Clinical Trials • Clinical Development • Clinical Research • Research and Development (R&D) • Data Analytics • Drug Development • Clinical Data Management • Oncology Clinical Research • Project Management • Clinical Operations","Presentations","Good Clinical Practice (GCP)","Oncology","Clinical Trials","Clinical Development","Clinical Research","Research and Development (R&D)","Data Analytics","Drug Development","Clinical Data Management","Oncology Clinical Research","Project Management","Clinical Operations"]},{"title":"Manager, Biomarker Clinical Assay Lead","company":"辉瑞","date_range":"3 年 9 个月","duration":"2 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","description":"A key stakeholder is responsible for scientific oversight, vendor management, data integrity and quality of biomarker analyses in support of the development strategy for phase I-III oncology programs. \n \nSupporting study setup, study protocol development and design, review of informed consent documents and CRF, finalization on biomarker strategy and sample collection plan. \nInvolving in central lab selection and management, and site initiation and training activities. \nSupporting data operations and management to establish data collection and data transfer specifications with analytical labs. \nReviewing and querying biomarker analysis plan, clinical data and reports in support of critical snapshot and submission and contributes to development and review of CSR. \nParticipating in vendor selection, qualification, and periodic audits of CROs. \nResponsible for review and approval of vendor contracts, budget, bioanalytical plans and reports, assay validation and overall data quality. \nEvaluating and implementing new technologies to further improve quality and efficiency of clinical biomarker analyses. \nReviewing and uploading study related documentations in Trial Master File (TMF). \nDemonstrating exceptional teamwork skills to achieve study goals and drive successful project outcomes.","skills":["技能: Presentations • Good Clinical Practice (GCP) • Oncology • Clinical Trials • Clinical Development • Clinical Research • Research and Development (R&D) • Data Analytics • Drug Development • Clinical Data Management • Oncology Clinical Research • Project Management • Clinical Operations","Presentations","Good Clinical Practice (GCP)","Oncology","Clinical Trials","Clinical Development","Clinical Research","Research and Development (R&D)","Data Analytics","Drug Development","Clinical Data Management","Oncology Clinical Research","Project Management","Clinical Operations"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Fellow","company":"Ivy Brain Tumor Center · 全职","date_range":"2019年6月 - 2021年11月","duration":"2 年 6 个月","location":"凤凰城地区","description":"Supporting sample analysis at a CAP CLIA lab by performing Immunohistochemistry, Next-Generation Sequencing and ELISA assay for 7 Phase 0/2 clinical studies. \nAnalyzing and managing clinical data with experience in Electronic Data Capture (EDC). \n \nServing as the clinical project lead for Pamiparib in newly diagnosed and recurrent glioblastoma (NCT04614909). \n \nLeading a preclinical study with an external pharmaceutical company to evaluate a novel inhibitor in glioblastoma and meningioma. Participating in establishing suitable PDX model, treatment regimen, study design and PK/PD analysis. \nContributing scientific background to understand MOA of testing drugs and targeted signaling pathways for protocol and IND submission. \n \nExperienced in in vivo, in vitro and ex vivo models combined with radiation treatment. \nBeing proficient at wet lab techniques such as DNA/RNA extraction, western blotting, ELISA, qPCR, cell cycle analysis by flow cytometry, histopathological image analysis.","skills":["Presentations","Oncology","Research and Development (R&D)","Data Analytics"]},{"title":"Graduate Research Assistant","company":"Texas Tech University","date_range":"2015年8月 - 2019年5月","duration":"3 年 10 个月","location":"Lubbock, Texas","description":"Handling two major research projects during this position. Research projects: 1. the mechanism of estrogen-induced chemotherapeutic sensitivity in human breast cancer cells. 2. The mechanisms of environmental chemical-induced the progression of chronic kidney disease and kidney cancer. \nMajor research techniques used in those projects are including in vitro cell culture, DNA/RNA extraction, gene expression analysis and western blotting.","skills":["Presentations","Data Analytics"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Principal Scientist, Translational Medicine Lead at RayzeBio · 2025年 - 现在 | Associate Director, Biomarker Clinical Assay at Pfizer · 2025年 - 2025年 | Manager, Biomarker Clinical Assay Lead at Pfizer · 2021年 - 2025年 | Postdoctoral Fellow at Ivy Brain Tumor Center · 2019年 - 2021年 | Graduate Research Assistant at Texas Tech University · 2015年 - 2019年","education":[{"school":"Texas Tech University","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Environmental Toxicology","date_range":"2015年 - 2019年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Master’s Degree","field_of_study":"Toxicology","date_range":"2012年 - 2014年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"中兴大学","degree":"Bachelor’s Degree","field_of_study":"Biotechnology","date_range":"2008年 - 2012年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Texas Tech University，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 2015年 - 2019年 | 台湾大学，Master’s Degree · 2012年 - 2014年 | 中兴大学，Bachelor’s Degree · 2008年 - 2012年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":true,"detail_error":""}}
