, PGxHealth LLC, Clinical Data · 2007年 - 2010年 | Research Scientist and Project Manager at United Biomedical, Inc. · 2000年 - 2007年 | Associate Research Scientist at United Biomedical, Inc., Asia · 1999年 - 2000年","education":[{"school":"National Defense Medical Center, Taiwan","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Graduate Institute of Life Sciences","date_range":"1992年 - 1997年","activities":"","grade":"4.0"},{"school":"National Chung-Hsing University, Taiwan","degree":"Master of Science (MS)","field_of_study":"Graduate Institute of Veterinary Medicine","date_range":"1990年 - 1992年","activities":"","grade":"3.89"},{"school":"National Chung-Hsing University, Taiwan","degree":"Bachelor of Science (B.S.)","field_of_study":"Veterinary Medicine","date_range":"1985年 - 1990年","activities":"","grade":"3.60"}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | National Defense Medical Center, Taiwan，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 1992年 - 1997年 | National Chung-Hsing University, Taiwan，Master of Science (MS) · 1990年 - 1992年 | National Chung-Hsing University, Taiwan，Bachelor of Science (B.S.) · 1985年 - 1990年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":""}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:39:10+08:00","record":{"name":"Ray C.","current_title":"Executive Director, US CMC Lead","current_company":"AsymBio · 全职","location":"洛杉矶地区","headline":"Biologics CMC & Process Development Leader | mAb, TCE, ADC, Bispecific & Multispecific | Developability, IND-to-BLA | CDMO Oversight, Tech Transfer, Manufacturing & Clinical Supply | Global Regulatory (FDA/EMA/NMPA)","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/raychuang","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAAFOfwB4bvSDJNrhSD0bbvJxI3h_XyKKKU","core_skills":["CMC Strategy","Developability Assessment","Upstream Process Development"],"positions":[{"title":"Executive Director, US CMC Lead","company":"AsymBio · 全职","date_range":"2026年5月 - 现在","duration":"5 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚","description":"Lead US West Coast technical governance and client CMC strategy across AsymBio's integrated biologics and bioconjugate (ADC/XDC) CDMO platforms. \n• ​End-to-End CMC Leadership. \n​• Cross-Functional Project Execution. \n​• Client Alignment & Business Development.\n\n• Provide executive-level technical oversight for contracted biologic and ADC development portfolios across all clinical phases.","skills":["Antibody-Drug Conjugates (ADC)","ICH Guidelines","Complex Biologics","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Biologics Manufacturing"]},{"title":"Strategic CMC Consultant","company":"AskGene Pharma, Inc.","date_range":"2026年1月 - 2026年5月","duration":"5 个月","location":"","description":"• Strategic Advisory: Reviewed CMC sections of pre-BLA and BLA documents, ensuring alignment with global regulatory requirements for a late-stage Phase 3 program. \n• Technical Guidance: Provided high-level guidance on CLD and Upstream PD strategies for discovery and clinical-stage projects.","skills":[]},{"title":"VP, CLD & Upstream PD / CMC","company":"ASKGENE PHARMA, INC. · 全职","date_range":"2018年9月 - 2025年12月","duration":"7 年 4 个月","location":"Camarillo, CA","description":"Built and led the US Technical Operations organization to transform discovery-stage biologics into IND-ready clinical assets across monoclonal antibodies (mAbs), complex bispecifics, and cytokine prodrug fusion proteins. \n• ​Accelerated IND Submissions: Advanced 4 complex pipeline programs to IND by embedding front-loaded Developability Assessments, QTPP definition, and stage-gate CMC risk management, eliminating late-stage redesigns and candidate attrition. \n• ​Engineered Next-Gen CLD Platform: Reduced cell line development timelines by 25% and boosted specific productivity (qP) by 50–100% by pioneering a transposase-mediated integration platform, significantly shortening timelines to First-in-Human (FIH) manufacturing. \n• Right-First-Time GMP Execution: Directed CDMO selection, tech transfer governance, and process characterization/PPQ strategies to ensure seamless, right-first-time clinical GMP supply. \n​• Regulatory Strategy & Control Execution: Primary author and CMC lead for multi-regional IND/BLA submissions; established ICH Q8–Q12 compliant control strategies and led regulatory interactions and inspection readiness. \n​• Resolved Complex Modality Liabilities: Mitigated biophysical heterogeneity, aggregation, and stability liabilities inherent to asymmetric bispecifics and cytokine prodrugs, de-risking downstream manufacturing and clinical supply.\n\n• Pipeline Leadership: Led the CMC development strategy for a diverse pipeline of innovative biologics, consistently hitting aggressive milestones for clinical entry. \n• Process Innovation: Managed the implementation of a transposase-based CLD platform and advanced feeding strategies, achieving up to 3-fold higher titers in CHO fed-batch cultures to ensure cost-effective clinical supply. \n• Tech Transfer & MSAT Execution: Orchestrated the scale-up and transfer of processes to internal pilot sites and external CDMOs; served as the technical SME for cell culture and analytical data during deviation investigations. \n• CDMO Management & Technical Oversight: Directed global CDMOs through GMP scale-up (up to 2000L) and clinical manufacturing. \n• Maintained a consistent Right-First-Time record by providing technical oversight for manufacturing campaigns and reviewing master and executed batch records. \n• Late-Stage Oversight: Directed PC and PPQ activities for a Phase 3 program and contributed to, reviewed, and integrated CMC Module 3 documentation for a China-BLA submission.","skills":["CMC Strategy","Developability Assessment","Upstream Process Development","CDMO Oversight","Drug Substance","Tech Transfer","Bispecific Antibodies","Process Validation","External Manufacturing","Cell Line Development","Regulatory Submissions","Process Characterization"]},{"title":"Technical Consultant","company":"Independent Consultant · 合同","date_range":"2017年5月 - 2023年2月","duration":"5 年 10 个月","location":"","description":"Provided high-level technical advisory to biotech clients and CDMOs, focusing on the rapid optimization of expression platforms and upstream workflows. \n• CDMO Platform Build: Partnered with a Boston-based CDMO (BIB) to re-engineer their CLD platform; created a GS-KO CHO-K1 host and optimized vector design, achieving industrial standards of productivity while significantly reducing development timelines.\n\n• Advised global biotech and CDMO clients on expression platform optimization and upstream process workflows. \n• Platform Enhancement: Advised a global CDMO on CHO cell line development platform improvements, resolving integration and productivity issues to reach industry-competitive service standards.","skills":["Bispecific Antibodies","Cell Line Development"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Executive Director, US CMC Lead at AsymBio · 2026年 - 现在 | Strategic CMC Consultant at AskGene Pharma, Inc. · 2026年 - 2026年 | VP, CLD & Upstream PD / CMC at ASKGENE PHARMA, INC. · 2018年 - 2025年 | Technical Consultant at Independent Consultant · 2017年 - 2023年 | R&D Manager, Cell Biology at Thermo Fisher Scientific, Transplant Diagnostics (TDX) · 2016年 - 2018年 | Associate Director, R&D at Genesun Biopharmaceuticals (closed) · 2015年 - 2016年 | Associate Director at Shire Pharmaceuticals · 2006年 - 2015年 | R&D Scientist at Multispan, Inc. · 2005年 - 2006年 | Postdoc Fellow at Johnson & Johnson · 2002年 - 2005年 | Postdoctoral Research Associate at Salk Institute for Biological Studies · 2001年 - 2002年","education":[{"school":"University of Michigan - Rackham Graduate School","degree":"PhD","field_of_study":"Cell, Developmental and Neural Biology","date_range":"1995年 - 2001年","activities":"活动与社团: Society for Developmental Biology","grade":""},{"school":"National Taiwan University","degree":"MS","field_of_study":"Biochemical Science","date_range":"1990年 - 1992年","activities":"活动与社团: Ministry of Education Fellowship","grade":""},{"school":"成功大学","degree":"Bachelor's Degree","field_of_study":"Biology","date_range":"1986年 - 1990年","activities":"活动与社团: Psychology club","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | University of Michigan - Rackham Graduate School，PhD · 1995年 - 2001年 | National Taiwan University，MS · 1990年 - 1992年 | 成功大学，Bachelor's Degree · 1986年 - 1990年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Director Senior Director Vice President Senior Manager Principal Scientist 职位性质 全职 兼职 合同制 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 亚洲 远程办公: 美国 亚洲 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:39:21+08:00","record":{"name":"Wen-Hsuan Chang, PhD","current_title":"Research Scientist","current_company":"University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill · 全职","location":"罗利-达勒姆-查伯山地区","headline":"Scientist in Cancer Biology | Bioinformatics | Cell and Molecular Biology | Drug Discovery | Exosomes","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/wenhsuanchang","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAv2fKMBWMX1wDOd5hEi8XDTMsmawh1aB5U","core_skills":["Exosomes","Multi-omic analysis","BSL-2"],"positions":[{"title":"Research Scientist","company":"University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill · 全职","date_range":"2022年1月 - 现在","duration":"4 年 9 个月","location":"美国 北卡罗来纳州 教堂山","description":"Channing Der Laboratory – Investigating KEAP1-NRF2-mediated resistance to KRAS inhibitors in KRAS-mutant cancer \n \n• Integrate multi-omic analyses (CRISPR screen, RNA sequencing, proteomics) with wet-lab molecular biology techniques to identify genetic signatures associated with drug resistance in pancreatic and lung cancers \n• Develop in vitro and in vivo assays evaluating drug efficacy on tumors and demonstrate a novel combination therapy for treating KRAS-mutant pancreatic and lung cancers, leading to over 3-fold tumor reduction in mouse xenografts  \n• Develop computational pipeline to determine biomarkers predictive of drug responses and poor patient survival in pancreatic and lung cancer, validated by clinical genetic data from clinical trials and clinical research databases \n• Utilize AI tools (Claude, Gemini, Copilot) for prototyping bioinformatics codes with clear documentation and apply a robust human review process to guarantee logic correctness and clinical data precision. \n• Lead a multi-institutional project involving 7 research groups across 4 institutions, securing 2 new strategic collaborations with Bristol Myers Squibb and Vividion Therapeutics \n• Collaborate with Mirati Therapeutics, Verastem Oncology, and academic institutions (NYU, Dana Farber, U. Cincinnati) to advance therapies for pancreatic cancer with co-invention of a patent \n• Author or co-author 4 manuscripts for peer-reviewed journals and an IACUC protocol, present 2 invited talks hosted by UNC and MD Anderson, and serve as a peer reviewer twice for peer-reviewed journals \n• Mentor 2 junior scientists and support their research skill development and career advancement","skills":["Molecular Biology","Molecular Cloning","Amazon Web Services (AWS)","Transfection","Mammalian Cell Culture","Proteomics","Cell Biology","Bioinformatics","Biomedical Research","CRISPR Screen","RNAseq Analysis","Cancer Research","R (Programming Language)","Scientific Writing","Biochemistry"]},{"title":"Graduate Research Associate","company":"Cornell University · 全职","date_range":"2016年7月 - 2021年12月","duration":"5 年 6 个月","location":"美国 纽约 汤普金斯县","description":"Richard Cerione Laboratory – Exploring the Role of Survivin in Pancreatic Cancer \n \n• Investigated the role of Survivin in promoting drug resistance and cancer progression in pancreatic cancer. \n• Identified Survivin as a potential biomarker for pancreatic cancer through analysis of clinical samples \n• Demonstrated how oncogenic KRAS stabilizes MYC protein through Survivin upregulation, advancing the molecular understanding of pancreatic cancer progression. \n• Applied a broad set of techniques, including cell culture, genetic manipulation (siRNA, shRNA, overexpression, site-directed mutagenesis), fluorescence microscopy, biochemistry, metabolic assays, and exosome purification and characterization. \n• Independently managed projects and mentored multiple undergraduate students, summer students, and early-stage PhD students \n• Published three first-author papers in collaboration with multiple institutions\n\n• Discovered Survivin as a potential exosome-based liquid biopsy biomarker for pancreatic cancer detection in collaboration with UNC Chapel Hill and UNC Hospital. \n• Implemented cell culture, exosome purification and characterization to demonstrate that targeting Survivin can reverse drug resistance in pancreatic cancer cells. \n• Applied biochemical and genetic assays to uncover how Survivin regulates glycolysis and expression of the transcription factor MYC in KRAS-driven pancreatic cancer. \n• Published three first-author manuscripts and trained multiple undergraduate students, summer exchange students, and first-year graduate students.","skills":["Exosomes","Immunoblotting","Fluorescence Microscopy","Transfection","Mammalian Cell Culture","Cancer Research","Scientific Writing","Biochemistry","Chemistry"]},{"title":"Squad Leader (Second Lieutenant)","company":"Coast Guard Administration, Ocean Affairs Council, Taiwan · 全职","date_range":"2015年9月 - 2016年7月","duration":"11 个月","location":"台湾 台南市 台南市","description":"• Performed security inspection for incoming ships \n• Led patrol units to ensure safety of the harbor","skills":[]},{"title":"Graduate Research Assistant","company":"台湾大学","date_range":"5 年","duration":"2 年","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","description":"Hung-Wen Li Laboratory – Studying the Mechanism of DNA Repair and Homologous Recombination at Single-Molecule Level \n \n• Revealed the kinetic and mechanism of meiosis-specific DNA recombinase, Dmc1, binding on DNA to form nucleofilament. \n• Proved that Rad51 serves as an accessory protein for Dmc1 catalyzing Dmc1-DNA binding process\n\n• Performed single-molecule particle tracking and optical microscopy to elucidate the nucleoprotein filament formation process of DNA recombinases, RAD51 and DMC1. \n• Established a novel method for observing single-molecule rotation via gold nanorods by optical microscopes.","skills":["技能: Scientific Writing • Biochemistry • Optical Microscopy • Chemistry • Biophysical Chemistry","Scientific Writing","Biochemistry","Optical Microscopy","Chemistry","Biophysical Chemistry"]},{"title":"Graduate Teaching Assistant","company":"台湾大学","date_range":"5 年","duration":"2 年","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","description":"Hung-Wen Li Laboratory – Studying the Mechanism of DNA Repair and Homologous Recombination at Single-Molecule Level \n \n• Revealed the kinetic and mechanism of meiosis-specific DNA recombinase, Dmc1, binding on DNA to form nucleofilament. \n• Proved that Rad51 serves as an accessory protein for Dmc1 catalyzing Dmc1-DNA binding process\n\n• Performed single-molecule particle tracking and optical microscopy to elucidate the nucleoprotein filament formation process of DNA recombinases, RAD51 and DMC1. \n• Established a novel method for observing single-molecule rotation via gold nanorods by optical microscopes.","skills":["技能: Scientific Writing • Biochemistry • Optical Microscopy • Chemistry • Biophysical Chemistry","Scientific Writing","Biochemistry","Optical Microscopy","Chemistry","Biophysical Chemistry"]},{"title":"Undergraduate Research Assistant","company":"台湾大学","date_range":"5 年","duration":"2 年","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","description":"Hung-Wen Li Laboratory – Studying the Mechanism of DNA Repair and Homologous Recombination at Single-Molecule Level \n \n• Revealed the kinetic and mechanism of meiosis-specific DNA recombinase, Dmc1, binding on DNA to form nucleofilament. \n• Proved that Rad51 serves as an accessory protein for Dmc1 catalyzing Dmc1-DNA binding process\n\n• Performed single-molecule particle tracking and optical microscopy to elucidate the nucleoprotein filament formation process of DNA recombinases, RAD51 and DMC1. \n• Established a novel method for observing single-molecule rotation via gold nanorods by optical microscopes.","skills":["技能: Scientific Writing • Biochemistry • Optical Microscopy • Chemistry • Biophysical Chemistry","Scientific Writing","Biochemistry","Optical Microscopy","Chemistry","Biophysical Chemistry"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill - Research Scientist · 2022年 - 现在 | Graduate Research Associate at Cornell University · 2016年 - 2021年 | Squad Leader (Second Lieutenant) at Coast Guard Administration, Ocean Affairs Council, Taiwan · 2015年 - 2016年 | Graduate Teaching Assistant at National Taiwan University · 2013年 - 2014年 | Graduate Research Assistant at National Taiwan University · 2013年 - 2015年 | Undergraduate Research Assistant at National Taiwan University · 2010年 - 2013年","education":[{"school":"美国康奈尔大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Chemistry and Chemical Biology","date_range":"2016年 - 2021年","activities":"活动与社团: Field Representative at Graduate and Professional Student Association (2017-2018)","grade":""},{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Master of Science - MS","field_of_study":"Chemistry","date_range":"2013年 - 2015年","activities":"活动与社团: Instructor for teaching assistants orientation workshop with two times outstanding TA awards","grade":""},{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Bachelor of Science - BS","field_of_study":"Chemistry","date_range":"2009年 - 2013年","activities":"活动与社团: Vice chairman of NTU Promenade Organization; Chairman of Freshman Orientation Camp","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 美国康奈尔大学，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 2016年 - 2021年 | 台湾大学，Master of Science - MS · 2013年 - 2015年 | 台湾大学，Bachelor of Science - BS · 2009年 - 2013年 | 档案分析行 | 最新动态 | 1 次浏览 | 保存到项目 | 将Wen-Hsuan保存到项目 | 发消息给Wen-Hsuan | Wen-Hsuan Chang, PhD的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:39:36+08:00","record":{"name":"Inik Chang, Ph.D.","current_title":"Scientific AI Contributor & Evaluator","current_company":"Mercor · 合同","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 旧金山","headline":"Regulatory Strategy & R&D | IND-Enabling | FDA (INTERACT, Pre-IND, IND) & MFDS | Open to Contract / Fractional Roles","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/inik-chang-ph-d-ba0399a","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAHWIGgB9FZnIaawvc_F6fVPBWrGMZK5uQI","core_skills":["IND Preparation","In Vivo Animal Disease Models","Laboratory Animal Work"],"positions":[{"title":"Scientific AI Contributor & Evaluator","company":"Mercor · 合同","date_range":"2026年5月 - 现在","duration":"5 个月","location":"San Francisco Bay Area","description":"Building and evaluating expert-level AI model tasks across biology, translational research, and regulatory science domains.  \n \n• Evaluate technical quality, scientific reasoning, and research outputs of AI language models across discovery and applied science workflows.  \n• Design expert-level assessment tasks in cell biology, molecular biology, immunology, and regulatory science (IND/FDA frameworks).  \n• Provide structured, constructive feedback distinguishing rigorous scientific reasoning from surface-level plausibility, shortcuts, and ambiguity.  \n• Apply 25+ years of wet-lab and translational research expertise to assess scientific accuracy and identify model failure modes.  \n• Previously contributed to Aligned AI's evaluation campaigns, building expert-level biology and MFDS gene therapy regulatory tasks.","skills":[]},{"title":"Regulatory Strategy & R&D Consultant (U.S. & Korea)","company":"iGeneFix, Inc. · 合同","date_range":"2025年11月 - 现在","duration":"11 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"Lead regulatory strategy and IND-enabling program execution for gene editing therapeutics (AAV, CRISPR), supporting programs from early-stage research through IND readiness. \n \n• Lead FDA interactions including INTERACT, Pre-IND, and IND planning. \n• Guide IND-enabling strategy across CMC, nonclinical, and regulatory integration. \n• Support AAV regulatory strategy, including analytical and assay considerations supporting IND filings. \n• Oversee IND-enabling nonclinical study planning (biodistribution, off-target, GLP tox) in coordination with CROs. \n• Coordinate global CRO/CDMO and academic partnerships across U.S. and Korea. \n• Drive program execution including timelines, budgets, risk management, and milestone alignment. \n \nFocused on translating complex science into executable regulatory and development plans, ensuring efficient, IND-ready program progression in resource-constrained, early-stage environments.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director, Translational Research & Program Management (U.S. & Korea)","company":"BiomLogic / HLB Genex Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2020年6月 - 2025年6月","duration":"5 年 1 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"Led IND-enabling program execution and translational development across multiple therapeutic areas — inflammatory diseases, oncology, ophthalmology, and fibrosis — supporting progression from early discovery through clinical readiness.  \n \n• Secured CTN approval for a Phase 1 clinical trial in Australia (CT-2024-CTN-02639-1) for a wet AMD program, leading regulatory strategy, protocol design, and CRO oversight (Evidera, PPD, Scientia). \n• Led regulatory strategy and submissions as primary FDA liaison across the U.S., Korea, Australia, and China. \n• Led GLP-compliant IND-enabling preclinical programs across multiple therapeutic areas, coordinating CRO/CDMO execution across concurrent programs. \n• Directed cross-functional program execution across R&D, CMC, regulatory, and external partners. \n• Coordinated global partners, including CROs, CDMOs, and KOLs, to ensure regulatory-aligned study design and execution. \n• Managed program timelines, budgets, and risk mitigation across multi-year development programs. \n• Drove expansion of therapeutic indications through internal research leadership and external academic/industry collaborations. \n• Supported business development through scientific due diligence and evaluation of licensing opportunities. \n \nActed as a central driver of cross-functional alignment across science, regulatory, and operations, ensuring coordinated execution within a complex global development ecosystem.","skills":[]},{"title":"Principal Scientist, Clinical R&D","company":"GNT Pharma Co., Ltd · 全职","date_range":"2018年2月 - 2020年5月","duration":"2 年 4 个月","location":"韩国 京畿道 燕岐","description":"Led small-molecule discovery and preclinical program execution across oncology and inflammatory diseases, advancing early-stage research toward IND-enabling development. \n \n• Authored IND-enabling study reports supporting Phase 2 clinical trials in Korea and China (NCT02831088, NCT03651557, NCT05041010), ensuring regulatory-compliant submissions. \n• Secured orphan drug designation (DRU-2020-7470) and coordinated IND-enabling preclinical programs for Alzheimer’s disease and ALS first-in-human studies. \n• Directed R&D programs across oncology and anti-inflammatory pipelines, overseeing study design, data generation, and cross-functional coordination. \n• Coordinated CROs and external partners to execute GLP-compliant preclinical studies across multiple inflammatory indications, ensuring regulatory-aligned study design. \n• Led radiotherapy-related preclinical programs (pneumonitis, fibrosis, mucositis), supporting mechanism-based therapeutic development. \n• Supervised in-house anti-metastasis research, coordinating candidate validation and translational strategy. \n• Initiated and managed collaborative programs including immunomodulator development for cancer immunotherapy. \n \nAdvanced progression of discovery-stage programs into structured IND-enabling development through integrated internal and external execution.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出