{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:39:48+08:00","record":{"name":"Joshua C. Chang, Ph.D.","current_title":"Nonclinical and CMC, Lead","current_company":"Pantheon Bio · 全职","location":"旧金山湾区","headline":"Nonclinical & CMC | Gene Therapy in Oncology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/joshua-c-chang-ph-d-89a38069","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAA54gPYBFairCBRhRkZQW-neGjAFG6S2YkI","core_skills":["Neural development","Metabolic disease study","Xenotransplantation"],"positions":[{"title":"Nonclinical and CMC, Lead","company":"Pantheon Bio · 全职","date_range":"2026年 - 现在","duration":"9 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 南旧金山","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Lead, Preclinical Development","company":"Astellas Pharma","date_range":"8 年 9 个月","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 南旧金山","description":"Lead, Research & Preclinical Development:  \n• Develop program strategies for cardiac and CNS indications, advancing from early-stage preclinical studies through candidate nomination to IND submission.  \n• Contribute to identifying, evaluating, and initiating new programs to establish a cardiac portfolio.  \n \nResearch Project Lead:  \n• Led the cross-functional Research Project Team to complete the design, development, and delivery of a clinical candidate of AAV gene therapy (patent WO2023044424) from early research stage to IND filing, and successfully obtained FDA clearance with a fast track designation for a Phase 1 trial (NCT06483802).  \n• Drafted and finalized nonclinical sections of regulatory documents, including INTERACT, Pre-IND briefing package, and IND modules.  \n \nNonclinical Pharmacology/Toxicology:  \n• Collaborated with external CROs, KOLs, and academic partners to develop and execute non-GLP and GLP nonclinical studies, including pharmacology, biodistribution, toxicology, and potency assessments in rodents or non-human primates.  \n• Selected suitable animal models, conducted vendor due diligence, a