{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:40:37+08:00","record":{"name":"Chia-Hao Chang","current_title":"Scientist ll in Cell Biology","current_company":"Paraza Pharma Inc.","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","headline":"Scientist ll | Drug Discovery & Target Validation | Oncology & Immunology | HTS & Translational Biology | Relocating to Taiwan (Sept 2026)","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/chia-hao-chang-209930137","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACFrUCkBRIu6RVITjfXLG7nz7t5AYaBkBvE","core_skills":["Life Sciences","Laboratory Skills","DNA Sequencing"],"positions":[{"title":"Scientist ll in Cell Biology","company":"Paraza Pharma Inc.","date_range":"5 年 4 个月","duration":"4 年 2 个月","location":"加拿大 魁北克省 Saint -Laurent","description":"● Led/contributed to 10+ discovery programs with 8+ U.S. biotech startups, delivering data supporting target validation and early development decisions. \n● Developed mechanism-driven proof-of-concept assays for transcription factor-targeting compounds, advancing a lead candidate into clinical studies. \n● Advanced targeted protein degradation programs (PROTACs, molecular glues), evaluating ubiquitin proteasomal degradation (UPS) and target engagement. \n● Defined mechanisms of action of RNA-modifying small molecules impacting RNA splicing and chromosome segregation. \n● Validated 50+ anti-inflammatory natural product hits with integrated cytotoxicity profiling for lead prioritization. \n● Generated 10+ CRISPR single/double knockout cell lines to confirm selectivity and support IND-enabling studies. \n● Established 7+ ex vivo metabolic assays in DIO mice to assess lipid metabolism and translational PD. \n● Conducted multi-tissue mtDNA safety assessments across 5+ murine tissues. \n● Developed HiBiT-based platform to screen 100+ E3 ligase-targeting compounds and NanoBRET based ubiquitination assay. \n● Built phosphate colorimetric assay to screen 50+ enzyme antagonists selected by AI, enhancing throug