{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:41:24+08:00","record":{"name":"YU-TAI CHANG","current_title":"Quality Control Inspector","current_company":"Artivion, Inc. · 全职","location":"美国 德州 奥斯汀","headline":"Quality Control • Assay Development • NGS & Oncology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/yutai-chang","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAALI8OIBh4s8DHb7YNtI20lEW-VWTGmhhQw","core_skills":["CRISPR Knockout","high-throughput imaging","Transduction"],"positions":[{"title":"Quality Control Inspector","company":"Artivion, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2024年11月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 11 个月","location":"美国 德州 奥斯汀","description":"","skills":["Quality Assurance","Good Laboratory Practice (GLP)","Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP)","Quality Control"]},{"title":"AI Scientist - Biology Expert","company":"Outlier · 自由职业","date_range":"2024年4月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 6 个月","location":"美国 德州 奥斯汀","description":"• Generating prompts to train AI RLHP model for Image-To-Text (ITT), Audio-to-Text (ATT), and Video-to-Text (VTT) projects. \n• Reviewing ITT and ATT prompts before submitting to AI RLHP model. \n• Writing ideal response (IR) to feed AI RLHP model.","skills":["AI Prompting","Creative Writing","Technical Writing"]},{"title":"Senior Research Scientist | Translational Oncology","company":"Dell Medical School at the University of Texas at Austin · 全职","date_range":"2018年7月 - 2024年4月","duration":"5 年 10 个月","location":"Livestrong Cancer Institutes, Austin, United States","description":"• Published 3 papers (myeloma, leukemia, and pancreatic cancer) with 10 citations from 3 cross-departmental collaborations to investigate new cancer stem cell (CSC)-targeting strategies to fight drug resistance and resurgence in cancer. \n• Developed animal protocols and optimized ELISA immunoassays to monitor and validate myeloma engraftment in mice. \n• Introduced Benchling ELN to design primer, analyze Sanger data, and digitalize records of lab notebook, plasmids and reagents. \n• Designed multi-parameter flow panels for analyzing tumor engraftment, bone marrow transplant, and T-/B-cell infiltration on Cytek spectral Aurora. \n• Curated open-house events and presented seminars and lab tours to promote the LCI school program, branding, and UT Austin's reputation.\n\n• Published 3 papers with 55 citations with multi-omics studies from 3 collaborations to fight drug resistance and resurgence in cancer. \n• Using RNA-seq to discover inhibition of Notch signaling as a potential therapeutic to repress cancer relapse and drug resistance in p53-deficient multiple myeloma. \n• Identified novel roles of Erzin, a linker protein within the CD44-cytoskeleton adhesion complexes, in promoting cancer stemness in PDAC. \n• Designed qPCR assays (1) to compare the copy number of GFP reporters among different myeloma cell lines; (2) to detect the ratio of TP53 del-vs-WT in different myeloma cell lines. \n• Designed targeted sequencing assays to confirm the knockout of TP53 gene in myeloma cell lines. \n• Designed tissue-free minimal residual disease (MRD) assays using flow cytometry and qPCR to examine the bone marrow and blood samples from the IL-6 myeloma transgenic mice. \n• Designed sandwich ELISA assays to examine the level of abnormal antibodies from myeloma-transplanted mice serum. \n• Supervised and mentored 2 undergraduate and 1 rotation graduate student.","skills":["Inventory Management","Equipment Maintenance","Environment, Health, and Safety (EHS)","Vectors","Mammalian","Cell Lines","Test Procedures","Critical Thinking","Medical Technology","Chemical Hazards","Hematology","Quality Control","Technical Reports","Design Control","Creative Problem Solving","Calendaring","General Administration","Administrative Assistance","Biomedical Sciences","Statistical Data Analysis","Communication","Oral Communication","Attention to Detail","RNAseq","Cancer Research","Translational Medicine","Project Management","RNA","Purification","Bioassay","Transduction","Nucleic Acid","Statistical Analysis","GraphPad","Presentation Skills","Laboratory Equipment","Organization Skills","Drug Discovery","In Vitro Diagnostics (IVD)","Scientific Writing","Data Management","Analytical Skills","Laboratory Information Management System (LIMS)","NGS","Biotechnology","Protein Purification","Assay Development","Data Analysis","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)","Tumor Immunology","ELISA","CRISPR Knockout","Flow Cytometry"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Scientist | Translational Medicine","company":"Johns Hopkins School of Medicine · 全职","date_range":"2016年7月 - 2018年6月","duration":"2 年","location":"Sydney Kimmel Comprehensive Cancer Center, Baltimore, United States","description":"• Published 1 PDAC paper and 1 AACR meeting abstract to understand how stromal cells enhance cancer stem cell functions in pancreatic cancer. \n• Launched an innovative in vivo project on immuno-phototherapy targeting CSCs in mice to expand therapeutics from breast tumor model to PDAC model.","skills":["Equipment Maintenance","Vectors","Mammalian","Cell Lines","Test Procedures","Critical Thinking","Technical Reports","Design Control","Creative Problem Solving","Biomedical Sciences","Statistical Data Analysis","Communication","Oral Communication","Attention to Detail","RNAseq","Cancer Research","Translational Medicine","Project Management","Purification","Bioassay","Transduction","Nucleic Acid","Statistical Analysis","GraphPad","Presentation Skills","Laboratory Equipment","Organization Skills","In Vitro Diagnostics (IVD)","Scientific Writing","Data Management","Analytical Skills","Laboratory Information Management System (LIMS)","NGS","Biotechnology","Assay Development","Data Analysis","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)","Multi-color Flow Cytometry","Flow Cytometry","Mouse Models"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Quality Control Inspector at Artivion, Inc. · 2024年 - 现在 | AI Scientist - Biology Expert at Outlier · 202