{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:41:38+08:00","record":{"name":"Tzu-Pei (Peggy) Chang, Ph.D.","current_title":"Associate Principal Scientist","current_company":"Hansoh Bio","location":"美国","headline":"Project Leader, Discovery Biology and Pharmacology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/tzu-pei-chang","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABOUdQgBrNmJvCB9yQdellHrGEVTRwudCsY","core_skills":["PK/PD study","in vivo mice study","Engineered cell therapy"],"positions":[{"title":"Associate Principal Scientist","company":"Hansoh Bio","date_range":"4 年 2 个月","duration":"6 个月","location":"美国","description":"Discovery Biology and Pharmacology  \n \nBiology leader: Lead multiple projects in oncology, immunology&Inflammation and metabolic disease  \n \nHigh-throughput screening. Target discovery and validation. Assay development and precision medicine. Design, optimize and execute in vitro cellular assays to assess the potency, mechanism of action and functional properties of candidate molecules. Design and manage in vivo efficacy studies, PK/PD analysis and biomarker evaluation. Collaboration with internal teams and CROs. IND-enabling studies and documents preparation.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"Hansoh Bio","date_range":"4 年 2 个月","duration":"6 个月","location":"美国","description":"Discovery Biology and Pharmacology  \n \nBiology leader: Lead multiple projects in oncology, immunology&Inflammation and metabolic disease  \n \nHigh-throughput screening. Target discovery and validation. Assay development and precision medicine. Design, optimize and execute in vitro cellular assays to assess the potency, mechanism of action and functional properties of candidate molecules. Design and manage in vivo efficacy studies, PK/PD analysis and biomarker evaluation. Collaboration with internal teams and CROs. IND-enabling studies and documents preparation.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist II","company":"Kadmon, a Sanofi Company","date_range":"3 年 7 个月","duration":"1 年 7 个月","location":"美国 纽约 纽约","description":"Biologics Discovery and Development  \n \nMonoclonal antibody (checkpoint inhibitor, CPI) discovery and cytokine fusion protein development based on Kadmon’s Immuno-oncology (I-O) platform to harness the immune-stimulatory activity of IL-15 to treat cancer: PD-1/IL-15 (KD050) and B7-H4/IL50 fusion projects \n• Led Immunoassay Development \n• Characterized and evaluated biologics (to IND) for cancer immunotherapy \n• Interacted with the external contract research organizations","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist I","company":"Kadmon, a Sanofi Company","date_range":"3 年 7 个月","duration":"1 年 7 个月","location":"美国 纽约 纽约","description":"Biologics Discovery and Development  \n \nMonoclonal antibody (checkpoint inhibitor, CPI) discovery and cytokine fusion protein development based on Kadmon’s Immuno-oncology (I-O) platform to harness the immune-stimulatory activity of IL-15 to treat cancer: PD-1/IL-15 (KD050) and B7-H4/IL50 fusion projects \n• Led Immunoassay Development \n• Characterized and evaluated biologics (to IND) for cancer immunotherapy \n• Interacted with the external contract research organizations","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow","company":"Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center · 全职","date_range":"2015年6月 - 2018年12月","duration":"3 年 7 个月","location":"New York, New York","description":"Sloan Kettering Institutes/ Cancer Biology & Genetics Program \nCenter for Cell Engineering  \nCenter for Stem Cell Biology \n \nTranslational cancer research and immunology therapy: Identification of novel anti-tumor factors and development of a cell-based delivery system to treat leukemia and melanoma. \n• Job Scope: Developed hypotheses and experimental plans, collaborated resources to complete \nresearch projects, presented research results, and engaged in funding application and scientific \npublications. \n• Project: \"Cancer Immunotherapy Based on a Novel Anti-Tumor Factor Induced Immuno-Surveillance in the Tumor Microenvironment\". \n• Identified novel secretory factors from early embryogenesis that inhibit cancer cell malignancy and progression. \n• Designed and engineered in vitro and in vivo cell-based delivery systems, including engineered T cells and CAR T cells for leukemia and melanoma models. \n• Established and managed collaborations focused on T cell engineering, fusion protein design, and transgenic mouse models. \n• Authored and secured funding for one fellowship and one research grant. \n• Supervised one postdoctoral fellow and one technician within the team. \n• Research resulted in one publication and two presentations.","skills":[]},{"title":"Adjunct Instructor","company":"圣约翰科技大学","date_range":"5 年 5 个月","duration":"5 个月","location":"纽约地区","description":"Fundamentals of Biology II \nImmunology","skills":[]},{"title":"Doctoral Research Fellow","company":"圣约翰科技大学","date_range":"5 年 5 个月","duration":"5 个月","location":"纽约地区","description":"Fundamentals of Biology II \nImmunology","skills":[]},{"title":"Graduate Teaching Assistant","company":"圣约翰科技大学","date_range":"5 年 5 个月","duration":"5 个月","location":"纽约地区","description":"Fundamentals of Biology II \nImmunology","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Associate Principal Scientist at Hansoh Bio · 2026年 - 现在 | Senior Scientist at Hansoh Bio · 2022年 - 2026年 | Senior Scientist II at Kadmon, a Sanofi Company · 2021年 - 2022年 | Senior Scientist I at Kadmon · 2019年 - 2020年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow at Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center · 2015年 - 2018年 | Adjunct Instructor at St. John's University · 2015年 - 2015年 | Graduate Teaching Assistant at St. John's University · 2010年 - 2014年 | Doctoral Research Fellow at St. John's University · 2010年 - 2015年 | Graduate Researcher at National Taiwan University Hospital · 2005年 - 2009年","education":[{"school":"圣约翰科技大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Tumor Immunol