ker Discovery • Mentoring • Cross-functional Collaborations • SQL • Amazon Web Services (AWS) • R (Programming Language) • Molecular Diagnostics • Computational Biology • Python (Programming Language) • Resource Management • Cancer Research • Strategic Planning • Molecular Genetics • Data Science • Biopharmaceuticals • Bioinformatics"]},{"title":"Bioinformatics lead for oncology R&D","company":"Bristol-Myers Squibb","date_range":"2008年 - 2014年","duration":"6 年 1 个月","location":"Hopewell, NJ","description":"Successfully applied integrated cancer genomic analysis of mutations, copy number variations, and gene expression data for multiple clinical programs; identified potential biomarkers for patient stratification and made critical impact on clinical development plans \n \nSuccessfully managed BMS/Sanger cancer cell-line genomics consortium. Completed genomics characterization of 1,000 cancer cell lines with whole exome sequencing and RNAseq  \n \nSpearheaded BMS cancer genomics and immune-oncology analysis efforts: brought TCGA data in-house; led the first TCGA pan-cancer genomics analysis for immune context of cancer. \n \nInitialized and leading the multi-disciplinary BMS cancer genome biology data team. Have developed BMS cancer genomic data platforms and successfully applied to oncology and immuno-oncology discovery and biomarker programs \n \nCo-chaired a working group for oncology target identification and validation, and disease biology. Developed and successfully executed target identification and validation strategies \n \nInitiated an innovation team and evaluated liquid biopsies platforms and technologies for applications in oncology R&D  \n \nCo-led the BMS oncology Translational R&D strategy team \n \nChampioning BMS Next Generation Sequencing efforts for oncology and immune-oncology","skills":["Cross-functional Collaborations","SQL","Molecular Diagnostics","Computational Biology","Cancer Research","Data Science","Biopharmaceuticals","Bioinformatics"]},{