{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:42:52+08:00","record":{"name":"Ya-Ju Chang","current_title":"Research Scientist","current_company":"New York Blood Center · 全职","location":"纽约地区","headline":"Research scientist@ NYBCe","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ya-ju-chang-21222775","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAA_fem4B3xEbFb9iqLe-VAjnRU_r3iCLym8","core_skills":["Zeiss LSM880","Zeiss LSM800","imaris image analysis"],"positions":[{"title":"Research Scientist","company":"New York Blood Center · 全职","date_range":"2024年1月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 9 个月","location":"美国 纽约","description":"• Plans, conducts, and interprets scientific experiments for the development of CAR-macrophage (CAR-M) cellular therapy products. \n \n• CAR-M biofilm therapy to combat difficult-to-treat bacterial biofilm infections.\n\n• Peripheral blood mononuclear cells (human) isolation and culture. \n• Human monocytes differentiate into functional macrophages. \n• iPSC reprogramming, differentiation, cryopreservation, characterization, manipulation and release testing of iPSC cell banks. \n• Process development manufacturing and analytical method development for iPSC-based Immunol therapies. \n• Peptide and Bacterial conjugation with fluorescence probe for cellular trafficking processes in real time. \n• Establish quality control procedures required by FDA for the cGMP production of translational cellular therapy products. \n• Perform molecular and cellular immunological assays and to develop new in vitro culture and bioreactor system. \n• Scalable generation of functional human iPSC-derived CAR-M cell lines. \n• Patient-specific hematopoietic stem cell ion transduction machinery and pathways in HSC maintenance and self-renewal. \n• Optimization of isolation, purification, reprogramming and characterization of HLA (human leukocyte antigen)-homozygous lines from Cord Blood (CB) cells and establish the NYBC master bank of clinical-grade HLA homozygous iPSCs. \n• Bacteria antigen (polysaccharide) purification.","skills":["Zeiss LSM880","imaris image analysis","Leica Microsystems","Leica microscopy","Leica LAS X","Macrophages","CAR-M","peptide conjugation","Immunotherapy","Transfusion Medicine","ips cell","cell engineering","LNP","Primary Cell Isolation","Multi-color Flow Cytometry","Fluorescence Microscopy"]},{"title":"Scientist II (biology)","company":"PTC Therapeutics, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2023年1月 - 2023年12月","duration":"1 年","location":"美国","description":"• Drug-binding site verification: Identify pockets or grooves on the surface of the target protein/RNA/RNP by small molecular modifiers in alternative splicing events (U1-pre-mRNA interaction). \n• Early discovery of the small molecule splicing modifier that regulates the splicing mechanism. \n• MOA studies: identify how cells will respond to the FD type modifier in splicing regulation. And allow for the identification of off-target pathways regulated by chemical compounds.\n\n• Responsible for planning and performing scientific experiments that contribute to PTC’s splicing-associated research and small molecular discovery activities. \n• Works cross-functionally with internal departments (chemistry and biology teams), and external resources as appropriate cooperation, as part of PTC’s early discovery project teams. \n• Proteomics and click chemistry: Cells and lysates with a tag containing click alkyne handle for the biotin-azide labeling of proteins and RNAs of targeted.","skills":["Biochemistry","Mechanism Of Action Studies","Proteomics","Small Molecules"]},{"title":"postdoctoral/ Associate Research Scientist","company":"Columbia University Irving Medical Center · 全职","date_range":"2017年10月 - 2022年12月","duration":"5 年 3 个月","location":"美国","description":"• Designed, executed, and evaluated cell-based, functional assays to monitor the functional progression of iPS-derived RPE cells in patients with high-risk SNPs, and to better understand the underlying disease pathogenesis. \n• Identified the treatment of antioxidant agents and molecules on ARMS2/HTRA1-associated aging disease. \n• Cooperated with scientists to achieve project goals, by conducting and coordinating the evaluation and modification of existing gene editing protocols for isolating homo-edited isogeneic iPS cells.  \n• Updated and modification of existing flow cytometry cell sorting protocols for the isolation of single iPS cells. \n• Transitioned to the new therapeutic platform (CRISPR) in molecular biology conducted genome surgery on patient-specific iPS cells and tested for rescued functionality of CRISPR-corrected cells in animal models. \n• Developed Skills that are essential to studying human induced pluripotent stem cell (iPS) and understanding the pathogenesis in early AMD. \n• Support the research efforts to personalized and regenerative medicine with a main focus on age-related macular degeneration (AMD) disease. \n• Targeted metabolomics and lipidomics to understand more clinical and translational research in dry AMD. \n• Provide well-informed advice on potential genetic therapeutic and repurposing of drugs, supplements, and non-pharmacologic interventions for AMD.\n\n• Assimilate new information and advances in science into cohesive summary reports and presentations.","skills":["Stem Cells","Gene Editing","CRISPR"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Fellow","company":"National Chi Nan University","date_range":"2016年8月 - 2017年9月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"Taipei , Taiwan","description":"• Identified the functional extracts of Luobuma leaves. \n• Using the natural extracts from Luobuma leaves for cancer treatment. \n• Investigating the cytotoxicity of Gallic acid autoxidation causing activated hepatic stellate cell necroptosis to mitigate the process of fibrosis through the TNF-α signaling pathway. \n• Developed and performed an anti-tumor study between LNP delivery and traditional medicine.\n\n• Developed and performed an anti-tumor study between the LNP delivery and the traditional medicine and presented the results at the 2015 American Association for the Study of Liver Diseases (AASLD) conference.","skills":["Biochemistry","LNP"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Research Scientist at New York Blood Center · 2024年 - 现在 | Scientist II (biology) at PTC Therapeutics, Inc. · 2023年 - 2023年 | postdoctoral/ Associate Research Scientist at Columbia University Irving Medical Center · 2017年 - 2022年 | Postdoctoral Fellow at National Chi Nan University · 2016年 - 2017年 | Research Asistant at National Taiwan University · 2014年 - 2015年 | Research Assistant at Chung Shan Medical University · 2009年 - 2011年","education":[{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Biochemical Science and Technology","date_range":"2011年 - 2016年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"中山医学大学","degree":"Master of Science (M.S.)","field_of_study":"Biochemistry and Biotechnology","date_range":"2009年 - 2011年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"高雄海洋科技大学","degree":"Bachelor of Science (B.S.)","field_of_study":"Aquaculture","date_range":"2004年 - 2008年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 台湾大学，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 2011年 - 2016年 | 中山医学大学，Master of Science (M.S.) · 2009年 - 2011年 | 高雄海洋科技大学，Bachelor of Science (B.S.) · 2004年 - 2008年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Senior Scientist Senior Staff Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 纽约地区 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"中高级 (商务会话)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
