{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:43:35+08:00","record":{"name":"Jiun Chiun Chang","current_title":"Senior Scientist","current_company":"Confidential Startup · 全职","location":"旧金山湾区","headline":"Research Scientist","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jiun-chiun-chang-047891192","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAC1WH_cBS_Z6rqaW07xh1kbZGc01C3fyHjs","core_skills":["Stable Cell Line","Protein Analytics","Protein Refolding"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"Confidential Startup · 全职","date_range":"2024年8月 - 2025年5月","duration":"10 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 伯克利","description":"Lead protein and peptide conjugations to large complex molecules \nEstablish and improve protein expression, purification and quality control capabilities for various high-throughput formats \nEstablish a stable cell line generation team and generate stable cell lines for functional assays \nMentored and trained scientists, promoting skill development and fostering a collaborative research environment\n\n• Projects 1: Establish new and improve existing high-throughput (HTP) protein expression and quality control (QC) capabilities within the protein department. \n• Responsibilities: Setup protein purification and QC equipment. \n• Improve existing small scale (96-well format) and develop mid-scale up (less than 1L) HTP protein expression, purification and QC capabilities for antigens (primary antibodies), respectively. \n• In addition, utilize and improve Expi293 and CHO systems for transfection efficiency and protein expression yield. \n• Assist in coordinating collaborations within multiple teams for smooth material and data transfer. \n• Create workflow and set protein standards as a gateway to all outsourced protein QC and determining pass or fail before utilizing it for assays. \n• Perform analytical evaluations of outsourced large complex molecules including various antibodies formats by intact and reduced Mass Spectrometry (LC/MS). \n• Purpose and draft protein chemistry department layout, lab space, timelines, budgets (capital request), build vendor relationships for equipment, and job descriptions (for head count) to establish department needs and future projects. \n• Train and mentor various junior scientists. \n• Projects 2: Establish and generate stable cell line for functional assays. \n• Responsibilities: Generate stable cell lines to express antigen(s) of interest using HEK293s. \n• Support functional assays (internal and external) collaborations with generated stable lines. \n• Formulate and manage inventory to all available lines to coordinate projects. \n• Collaborate with teams to Fluorescence-activated cell sorting (FACS) and Flow cytometry staining to isolate and later validate stable antigen expression.","skills":["Protein Science","Stable Cell Line","Protein Analytics","Protein Conjugation"]},{"title":"Scientist 4 (Associate Scientist at EvoTec)","company":"Genentech","date_range":"3 年 11 个月","duration":"1 年 10 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 南旧金山","description":"Develop high throughput platform for antibody-small molecule conjugate screens \nHigh throughput (Mid-Scale) protein production/purification\n\n• Projects 1: Develop high throughput platform for antibody-small molecule conjugate screens. \n• Responsibilities: Generate Thiomab conjugation to support antibody drug conjugate (ADC) (internal and external) collaborations. \n• Technology development of high-throughput (HTP) conjugation and analytical protocols for Thiomabs. \n• Design and optimize low-drug to antibody (DAR) and high-DAR Thiomab conjugations. \n• Design and implement HTP conjugation outcome (via DAR) by analytical SEC and Mass Spectrometry (LC/MS) analysis. \n• Evaluate and implement robotic systems for automating preparation, conjugation, and purification. \n• Assist in coordinating contract research organization (CRO) requests. \n• Responsible for many HTP sample management and inventory. \n• Projects 2: High throughput (Mid-Scale) protein production/purification. \n• Responsibilities: Prepare protein supernatant or cell lysate for purification. \n• Perform 2-step protein purification. \n• Conduct quality control (QC) for all samples post purification, including intact and reduced evaluation by LC/MS to ensure correct mass. \n• Register and release requested samples to requester. \n• Perform additional QC and troubleshooting complex proteins with collaborators upon request. \n• Adopting techniques from protein conjugation to expanding the capacity for HTP analytical SEC and Mass Spec. \n• (LC/MS) data analysis.","skills":["技能: Protein Analytics • Protein Conjugation • Protein Chemistry","Protein Analytics","Protein Conjugation","Protein Chemistry","技能: Protein Production • Protein Refolding • Protein Chemistry","Protein Production","Protein Refolding"]},{"title":"Scientist 3 (Senior Research Associate at EvoTec)","company":"Genentech","date_range":"3 年 11 个月","duration":"1 年 10 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 南旧金山","description":"Develop high throughput platform for antibody-small molecule conjugate screens \nHigh throughput (Mid-Scale) protein production/purification\n\n• Projects 1: Develop high throughput platform for antibody-small molecule conjugate screens. \n• Responsibilities: Generate Thiomab conjugation to support antibody drug conjugate (ADC) (internal and external) collaborations. \n• Technology development of high-throughput (HTP) conjugation and analytical protocols for Thiomabs. \n• Design and optimize low-drug to antibody (DAR) and high-DAR Thiomab conjugations. \n• Design and implement HTP conjugation outcome (via DAR) by analytical SEC and Mass Spectrometry (LC/MS) analysis. \n• Evaluate and implement robotic systems for automating preparation, conjugation, and purification. \n• Assist in coordinating contract research organization (CRO) requests. \n• Responsible for many HTP sample management and inventory. \n• Projects 2: High throughput (Mid-Scale) protein production/purification. \n• Responsibilities: Prepare protein supernatant or cell lysate for purification. \n• Perform 2-step protein purification. \n• Conduct quality control (QC) for all samples post purification, including intact and reduced evaluation by LC/MS to ensure correct mass. \n• Register and release requested samples to requester. \n• Perform additional QC and troubleshooting complex proteins with collaborators upon request. \n• Adopting techniques from protein conjugation to expanding the capacity for HTP analytical SEC and Mass Spec. \n• (LC/MS) data analysis.","skills":["技能: Protein Analytics • Protein Conjugation • Protein Chemistry","Protein Analytics","Protein Conjugation","Protein Chemistry","技能: Protein Production • Protein Refolding • Protein Chemistry","Protein Production","Protein Refolding"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Scholar","company":"University of California, San Francisco","date_range":"2017年9月 - 2019年10月","duration":"2 年 2 个月","location":"","description":"Therapeutic delivery of proteins in an injectable and biodegradable hydrogel for enhanced fracture repair. \nIdentify the downstream mechanism by which drug delivery promotes bone healing through surface receptor activation\n\n• Project 1: Evaluating Post Traumatic Osteoarthritis (PTOA) outcomes using different animal models PTOA. \n• Project 2: Therapeutic delivery of Leukemia Inhibitory Factor in an injectable alginate hydrogel for enhanced fracture repair. \n• Project 3: Identify the downstream mechanism by which LIF promotes bone healing through Sox2 activation. \n• Responsibilities: Design and execute projects independently, manage independent project funding, lab management, lab safety manager, mentoring and training graduate students and technicians, and manage lab stock animal colonies. \n• Evaluate and determine the use of selected biologics before utilizing for in vivo studies.","skills":["Bone Fracture Healing","Immunohistochemistry"]},{"title":"Visiting Scientist and Postdoctoral Trainee","company":"Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory","date_range":"2016年8月 - 2017年8月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"美国","description":"Evaluating Post Traumatic Osteoarthritis (PTOA) outcomes using different animal models PTOA.","skills":["Osteoarthritis","Bone Fracture Healing","Immunohistochemistry"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Senior Scientist at Confidential Startup · 2024年 - 2025年 | Genentech - Scientist 4 (Associate Scientist at EvoTec) · 2022年 - 2023年 | Genentech - Scientist 3 (Senior Research Associate at EvoTec) · 2019年 - 2021年 | Postdoctoral Scholar at University of California, San Francisco · 2017年 - 2019年 | Visiting Scientist and Postdoctoral Trainee at Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory · 2016年 - 2017年 | PhD Candidate at Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (LLNL) · 2011年 - 2016年 | Graduate Student at University of California, Merced · 2009年 - 2016年 | Teaching Assistant at University of California, Merced · 2007年 - 2015年 | Graduate Student / Research Assistant at University of California, Merced · 2007年 - 2009年","education":[{"school":"University of California, Merced","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Quantitative and Systems Biology","date_range":"2016年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"University of California, Merced","degree":"Master of Science - MS","field_of_study":"Quantitative and Systems Biology","date_range":"2009年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"University of California, Merced","degree":"Bachelor of Science - BS","field_of_study":"Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","date_range":"2007年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | University of California, Merced，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2016年 | University of California, Merced，Master of Science - MS · 2009年 | University of California, Merced，Bachelor of Science - BS · 2007年 | 保存到项目 | 将Jiun Chiun保存到项目 | 发消息给Jiun Chiun | Jiun Chiun Chang的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"n