imization strategies, improving operational efficiency and resource allocation","skills":[]},{"title":"Research And Development Manager","company":"ICARE Biotech","date_range":"5 年 2 个月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"","description":"• Led the establishment and continuous improvement of GTP-compliant quality systems, ensuring readiness for regulatory inspections and successful audit execution \n• Oversaw CMC compliance and documentation for clinical-stage cell therapy products, facilitating collaboration with hospital partners and advancing translational applications \n• Directed cross-functional integration between R&D, manufacturing, and clinical operations, supporting product lifecycle development from early-stage to clinical validation \n• Implemented organizational restructuring and cost optimization strategies, improving operational efficiency and resource allocation","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Head of Laboratory at ICARE Biotech · 2025年 - 现在 | Manufacturing Manager at ICARE Biotech · 2023年 - 2025年 | Research And Development Manager at ICARE Biotech · 2021年 - 2023年","education":[{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Biochemical Science and Technology","date_range":"2015年 - 2020年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Biochemical Science and Technology","date_range":"2010年 - 2014年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 台湾大学，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2015年 - 2020年 | 台湾大学，Bachelor's degree · 2010年 - 2014年 | 保存到项目 | 将PoHsiang保存到项目 | 发消息给PoHsiang | PoHsiang Chang的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:44:38+08:00","record":{"name":"Lin-Chun (Linjun) Chang","current_title":"Scientist","current_company":"GSK","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","headline":"Scientist Specializing in Molecular and Cell Biology, Virology & Immunology | Advancing Drug Discovery","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/lin-chun-linjun-chang-90557472","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAA9jsxUBb7xjlHaifr2fP2WKfNRVL8DJud0","core_skills":["Transduction","Assay Development","Cell Lines"],"positions":[{"title":"Scientist","company":"GSK","date_range":"2026年3月 - 现在","duration":"7 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Staff Scientist","company":"New York Blood Center · 全职","date_range":"2023年9月 - 2025年7月","duration":"1 年 11 个月","location":"美国 纽约 纽约","description":"• Served as Co-PI on NIH funding applications, designed innovative assays to evaluate latency-reversing agents (LRAs) and their potential as therapeutic vaccines to rejuvenate immune function in chronic HIV-infected individuals. \n•Designed, validated, and executed pharmaceutical cellular and molecular assays to evaluate degrader/PROTAC activity in chronic HIV inflammation models (primary CD4+ T cells), resulting in a first- and corresponding-author publication in IJMS. \n•Engineered lentiviral CRISPR-edited systems (HiBiT, NanoBRET) and Western blotting to monitor target engagement and degradation kinetics, enabling mechanistic studies and potency profiling of degraders/PROTACs. \n•Performed antibody characterization, including neutralization, receptor occupancy, target binding, and competitive displacement via flow cytometry, ELISA, and SPR, to support biologics and ADC lead optimization. \n•Developed reporter cell line–based assays—both real-time and endpoint—on high-throughput platforms to assess small molecules' antiviral potency, cell viability/apoptosis, and downstream signaling using flow cytometry, immunofluorescence microscopy, Western blotting, and plate-based readouts. \n•Established primary immune cell-based disease models (PBMCs, CD4+, CD8+ T cells) from healthy blood to measure drug activity, on and off-target effects, and immunomodulatory signaling using flow cytometry, QVOA, and multiplex qPCR/dPCR. \n•Carried out chronic inflammatory patient PBMC/immune cell-based assays (MLR/CTL, ADCC, cytokine release, T-cell activation, proliferation, and exhaustion/rejuvenation, QVOA, IPDA) with ELISA, MSD, multiplex qPCR/dPCR, and flow cytometry to support MoA and lead selection. \n•Partnered with Pfizer on small-molecule programs for sickle cell disease and malaria, integrating ex vivo patient blood assays, in vivo disease models, metabolic biomarker validation, and immune durability analyses using ELISA/MSD, flow cytometry, and ImageStream.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Research Scientist","company":"Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center · 全职","date_range":"2020年8月 - 2023年8月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"美国 纽约 纽约","description":"• Cultured human colon cell lines (Caco-2, HT29) to polarization and applied with bacteria and fatty acid treatments to interrogate IBD-relevant immune signaling, conducting multiplex RT-qPCR and ELISA assays to profile IBD-relevant cytokines and chemokines and pathway-specific biomarkers, contributing to three publications. \n• Utilized chemical-induced inflammatory models and immune conditional or knockout mice (RAG, IL10^ko/flox, CD4-cre, TCR, etc.) to delineate cellular and molecular pathways regulating immune responses and tissue inflammation and repair, yielding mechanistic insights into microbiota- and diet-mediated immune regulation in IBD. \n• Applied multicolor flow cytometry and multiplex RT-qPCR to immunophenotype intestinal immune cell subsets and quantify gene expression profiles in mouse tissues, identifying pathway-specific targets and biomarkers linked to immune regulation in IBD. \n• Directed day-to-day laboratory operations, including personnel training, workflow optimization, and compliance with EHS and IACUC regulations.\n\n• ) to dissect cellular and molecular pathways driving immune regulation, inflammation, and tissue repair. \n• Applied multicolor flow cytometry, multiplex RT-qPCR, and cytokine profiling to characterize intestinal immune cell subsets and gene expression signatures, identifying pathway-specific targets and biomarkers. \n• Established microbiota- and diet-mediated IBD models to investigate host–microbe–immune interactions and validate therapeutic hypotheses.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow","company":"University of Southern California · 全职","date_range":"2014年10月 - 2019年12月","duration":"5 年 3 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 洛杉矶","description":"Dr. Jae Jung lab \n• Elucidated how RNA sensors trigger antiviral immune responses by mapping virus (HSV, CMV, vaccinia, IAV)-induced immunogenetic necroptotic complex via human leukocyte cDNA library screening and IP/LC-MS of interactome, published as first-author paper in Nature Cell Biology.  \n• Constructed a lentiviral CRISPR–gRNA library and employed commercial RNAi library to target interferon-inducible and kinomic genes in primary cells, enabling high-throughput, real-time kinetic screening in a 96-well platform to identify genes driving oncolytic virus–induced cell death. \n• Engineered plasmids for in vitro transcription of gene-specific gRNAs and miRNAs, enabling CRISPR- and RISC-mediated gene knockout and post-transcriptional gene silencing in target validation studies. \n• Conducted NGS libraries preparation and barcoding from inflamed tissues for sequencing and analysis, contributing to the identification of a therapeutic target function in post-stroke inflammation resolution and a co-author publication in Cell Reports.  \n• Utilized advanced live-cell imaging (FRAP, time-lapse, confocal, RI tomography, cryo-EM) to real-time quantify the dynamics and assembly of virus-induced phase condensates of the necroptotic complex in cells and in vitro. \n• Performed tissue and blood collection from immunized mice and conducted comprehensive immunological assays (IHC, IF, H&E staining, plaque assay, qPCR, ELISA, Luminex, neutralization, and multicolor flow-based immunophenotyping) to evaluate immunogenicity, innate and adaptive immune activation, viral persistence, dissemination, clearance, and durable immunity in infected mice. \n• Purified recombinant proteins for in vitro biochemical characterization, including SPR, protein–protein, protein–nucleic acid interactions, and enzymatic assays (kinase, ubiquitination).\n\n• Dissected RNA-sensing pathways and antiviral immunity by mapping oncolytic virus–induced necroptotic complexes via human leukocyte cDNA screening and IP–LC/MS, resulting in a first-author publication in Nature Cell Biology. \n• Developed lentiviral CRISPR–gRNA and siRNA/miRNA screening platforms for high-throughput identification and validation of interferon-inducible and cell-death regulatory genes, enabling RISC- and CRISPR-mediated target discovery. \n• Applied NGS-based transcriptomic profiling of inflamed tissues to identify therapeutic targets involved in post-stroke immune resolution (Cell Reports co-author). \n• Leveraged advanced live-cell imaging (FRAP, confocal, RI tomography, cryo-EM) to visualize RNA–protein condensates and dissect the dynamics of virus-induced signaling assemblies. \n• Conducted in vivo immunogenicity and MoA studies—encompassing IHC, flow cytometry, ELISA, and viral clearance assays—to link innate and adaptive immune activation with therapeutic efficacy. \n• Purified recombinant proteins and performed SPR-based binding, kinase, and ubiquitination assays to define RNA–protein and signaling interactions supporting mechanistic insight.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Scientist at GSK · 2026年 - 现在 | Staff Scientist at New York Blood Center · 2023年 - 2025年 | Senior Research Scientist at Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center · 2020年 - 2023年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow at University of Southern California · 2014年 - 2019年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow / Graduate student at National Taiwan University · 2006年 - 2014年","education":[{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Molecular Biology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"阳明大学","degree":"Master of Science - MS","field_of_study":"Pharmaceutical Sciences","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Taipei Medical University","degree":"Bachelor of Science - BS","field_of_study":"Medical Laboratory Science and Biotechnology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 台湾大学，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD | 阳明大学，Master of Science - MS | Taipei Medical University，Bachelor of Science - BS | 保存到项目 | 将Lin-Chun (Linjun)保存到项目 | 发消息给Lin-Chun (Linjun) | Lin-Chun (Linjun) Chang的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:44:52+08:00","record":{"name":"Edmund Chang","current_title":"Director, Clinical Biomarkers","current_company":"Annexon Biosciences · 全职","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 伯灵格姆","headline":"Translational Medicine | Clinical Biomarkers | Cell and Gene Therapy","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/edmundchang14","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAADkSDcB9_q_t4_9pi0OjFxDM14Uu3V1WLs","core_skills":["CAR-T","Pharmacodynamics","Clinical Data"],"positions":[{"title":"Director, Clinical Biomarkers","company":"Annexon Biosciences · 全职","date_range":"2022年5月 - 2026年5月","duration":"4 年 1 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"Biomarkers Lead for two autoimmune programs, systemic lupus erythematosus and autoimmune hemolytic anemia \n￭ Developed clinical biomarker objectives and led translational research for complement-driven autoimmune diseases \n￭ Managed external vendors and academic research alliances to advance Precision Medicine strategy for SLE and AIHA \n￭ Authored and reviewed relevant sections in clinical study documents for Ph1b studies (CAD-01, wAIHA-02, LN-01) \n￭ Presented correlative clinical biomarker studies at national nephrology and rheumatology conferences\n\n• Clinical Biomarkers for autoimmune, ophthalmology and neuroinflammatory programs Lead translational biomarker and computational analysis strategy across a portfolio of complement-targeted therapeutics in autoimmune, neuroinflammatory, and ophthalmologic diseases. \n• Partner with clinical development, biometrics, and discovery teams to integrate multi-omics, clinical biomarker, and imaging datasets to inform mechanism of action, patient stratification, and clinical development strategy Key Contributions: Directed translational biomarker strategy for multiple clinical programs including lupus nephritis, autoimmune hemolytic anemia, Huntington’s disease, ALS, and Guillain-Barré syndrome, integrating proteomics, metabolomics, and immunologic biomarkers to characterize complement pathway activation and pharmacodynamic response Led computational analysis of large-scale multi-omic datasets (Somalogic, Olink, Metabolon) to identify disease-specific molecular signatures and predictive biomarker panels supporting precision medicine approaches Developed cross-program data science workflows in R-based environments for reproducible biomarker analysis, longitudinal modeling, and clinical outcome integration Generated translational insights linking molecular biomarkers with clinical endpoints in Phase 1b and Phase 2 studies, informing clinical trial design and translational strategy Led post-hoc analysis of imaging and visual function data (OCT, fundus autofluorescence, BCVA, LLVA) for the ARCHER-1 Phase 2 ophthalmology trial, integrating anatomical and functional endpoints to characterize disease progression and therapeutic response Built and managed external collaborations with academic groups, CROs, and assay vendors to advance biomarker discovery and validation programs Authored biomarker and translational science sections for clinical study reports (CSR), investigator brochures (IB), and statistical analysis plans (SAP) supporting regulatory submissions and clinical program advancement. \n• Presented translational biomarker findings at major scientific meetings including ASN Kidney Week and ACR Convergence.","skills":["Pharmacodynamics","Strategic Thinking","Biomarker Development","Translational Science","Project Teams","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Analytical Skills","Clinical Trials","Clinical Data","Translational Medicine"]},{"title":"Director, Translational Medicine","company":"Hummingbird Bioscience · 全职","date_range":"2021年10月 - 2022年3月","duration":"6 个月","location":"美国 德州 休斯顿","description":"￭ Responsible for developing biomarker strategy for two clinical-stage programs across multiple solid tumor indications\n\n• Clinical Biomarkers Lead for two monoclonal antibody programs (anti-HER3 and anti-VISTA) Worked with Regulatory and Clinical teams on IVD testing platforms to advance CDx strategy Developed bioinformatics workflow using real world omic datasets to inform cancer selection strategy.","skills":["Pharmacodynamics","Strategic Thinking","Biomarker Development","Translational Science","Project Teams","Analytical Skills","Cancer Biology","Clinical Data"]},{"title":"Associate Director","company":"Takeda","date_range":"1 年 3 个月","duration":"4 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"CAR-NK program \n￭ Provided technical expertise on biomarker technologies (ddPCR, NGS, cytokine panels) and worked closely with Translational Scientific Manager to execute clinical biomarker collection strategy \n￭ Performed statistical analyses for recommendation regarding endpoints, study design, safety evaluations and dose selections \n￭ Co-authored biomarker analysis sections with Translational Scientific Leads for clinical stage CD19-directed CAR-NK program \n￭ Supported Pharmacovigilance and Drug Safety functions on genotoxicity characterization of vector insertions by NGS. Wrote analysis pipeline and led technical discussions","skills":["技能: Regulatory Approvals • Pharmacodynamics • Strategic Thinking • Cell Therapy • Translational Science • Project Teams • Cross-functional Team Leadership • Analytical Skills • Cancer Biology • Clinical Trials • Clinical Data • Molecular","Regulatory Approvals","Pharmacodynamics","Strategic Thinking","Cell Therapy","Translational Science","Project Teams","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Analytical Skills","Cancer Biology","Clinical Trials","Clinical Data","Molecular","技能: Regulatory Approvals • Pharmacodynamics • Cell Therapy • Translational Science • Analytical Skills • Cancer Biology • Clinical Trials • Clinical Data"]},{"title":"Sr Principal Statistician","company":"Takeda","date_range":"1 年 3 个月","duration":"4 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"CAR-NK program \n￭ Provided technical expertise on biomarker techn