{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:45:27+08:00","record":{"name":"L Chang","current_title":"Research Assistant Professor","current_company":"City of Hope National Medical Center and Beckman Research Institue","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 杜阿尔特","headline":"Assistant Research Professor at City Of Hope Cancer Center","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/l-chang-b89b6630","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAaUGRkBNR8c0Xe6WLNCnrQNk62yK4V90wg","core_skills":["Mesenchymal stem cells","Ubiquitination assay","Mouse animal models"],"positions":[{"title":"Research Assistant Professor","company":"City of Hope National Medical Center and Beckman Research Institue","date_range":"2014年11月 - 现在","duration":"11 年 11 个月","location":"Department of Cancer Genetics and Epigenetics","description":"Serve a team leader to study the molecular and cellular mechanisms of an ubiquitin E3 ligases involved in epigenetic control of cancer stem cell progression and metastasis of triple negative breast cancer. Execute an experimental platform for screening of a newer generation of small chemical inhibitors against an ubiquitin E3 ligase to suppress the growth of cancer cells.","skills":[]},{"title":"Assistant Research Professor","company":"City of Hope National Medical Center and Beckman Research Institue","date_range":"2006年9月 - 2014年11月","duration":"8 年 3 个月","location":"Department of Molecular Pharmacology","description":"Serve a team leader for the studies on Identification of genes and their mechanisms involved in chronic inflammation-associated diseases which is triggered by chromatin instability. Designs experiments to use an animal model to understand the mechanism and find therapies on type II diabetes mellitus resulting from chronic inflammation.","skills":[]},{"title":"Assistant Research Scientist","company":"City of Hope Medical Group","date_range":"2005年3月 - 2006年8月","duration":"1 年 6 个月","location":"Division of Cancer Immunotherapeutics & Tumor Immunology","description":"Serve a team leader for the development of tumor-targeting CD4+ T-cell expressing chimeric antigen receptors (CARs) that recognize cancer-specific antigens, allowing the cells to recognize and kill tumor cells that would otherwise escape immune detection. The process involves extracting a patient’s T cells, transfecting them with a gene for a CAR, then reinfusing the transfected cells into the patient.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow and Project Scientist","company":"University of California, San Diego","date_range":"1997年10月 - 2004年12月","duration":"7 年 3 个月","location":"La Jolla, CA","description":"Studies focusing on the role of Jun and IKK kinase signaling pathway in pathogenesis of inflammation associated diseases including cardiovascular, angiogenesis, neurodegeneration, rheumatoid arthritis, hepatitis, type II diabetes mellitus, and hepatocellular carcinoma.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Research Assistant Professor at City of Hope National Medical Center and Beckman Research Institue · 2014年 - 现在 | Assistant Research Professor at City of Hope National Medical Center and Beckman Research Institue · 2006年 - 2014年 | Assistant Research Scientist at City of Hope Medical Group · 2005年 - 2006年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow and Project Scientist at University of California, San Diego · 1997年 - 2004年","education":[{"school":"Vanderbilt University","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Cell/Cellular and Molecular Biology","date_range":"1992年 - 1997年","activities":"活动与社团: 1992 Interdisciplinary Graduate Fellowship at Vanderbilt University School of Medicine 1993-1994 NIH Neuroscience training grant awardee 1993-1994 NIH Cancer Biology training grant awardee (renounced)","grade":""},{"school":"University of California, Riverside","degree":"Master's degree","field_of_study":"Biochemistry","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Vanderbi