{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:45:40+08:00","record":{"name":"Hao-Ming Chang, Ph.D.","current_title":"Senior Director, Preclinical Research","current_company":"Cytovia Therapeutics","location":"波士顿地区","headline":"Every second counts","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hao-ming-chang","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAACLslIB_gEUvAh09oI6-4mhndk2dS-DDR0","core_skills":["Quantitative Analysis of Real-Time Data","Critical Thinking and Reasoning","Research"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Director, Preclinical Research","company":"Cytovia Therapeutics","date_range":"4 年 1 个月","duration":"2 年 1 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州","description":"Bispecific cell engager antibodies and iNK & CAR-iNK cell therapy research.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director, Preclinical Research","company":"Cytovia Therapeutics","date_range":"4 年 1 个月","duration":"2 年 1 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州","description":"Bispecific cell engager antibodies and iNK & CAR-iNK cell therapy research.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist, Principal","company":"NantKwest","date_range":"2018年 - 2021年","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"Greater Boston Area","description":"Immuno-Oncology: natural killer (NK) cell expressing chimeric antigen receptor (CAR); armored CAR NK cell (armed with engineered cytokines) and primary T cell interaction; the tumor microenvironment (TME) research","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Scientist II","company":"Alexion Pharmaceuticals, Inc.","date_range":"2015年 - 2017年","duration":"2 年 1 个月","location":"Lexington, MA","description":"Supervised and mentored scientists and associate scientists as Team Lead. \n• Conceived and supervised the development of a novel cell-based screening assay to differentiate targeted patients from patients with similar clinical manifestations. (Invention Disclosure submitted) \n• Led the organ-on-a-chip collaborative project in the Complement/Renal Disease team. \n• Managed a CRO for generating a knockout mouse model and directed the natural history study for a rare disease that stems from complement dysfunction. \n• Member of the Alexion Innovation Research (AIR) committee, which researches and evaluates current biotech innovations in industry and academia for collaboration and partnership opportunities. \n• Led the company’s stem cell group of 7-10 scientists/associate scientists to support the enzyme replacement therapy (ERT) pipeline. \n• Assisted and participated in antibody and mRNA therapeutics. \n• Rated ‘Exceeds Expectations’ in company’s annual performance review for three consecutive years. \n• Winner of the 2016 Alexion ‘Living the Values’ award in recognition of “establishing a new and innovative method for the generation of transgenic Protein Production Lines, which is a key milestone in the development of the Egg White platform”. (Patent pending)","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Research Scientist","company":"Synageva BioPharma Corp.","date_range":"2014年 - 2015年","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"Lexington, MA","description":"Supervised and mentored scientists and associate scientists as Team Lead. \n• Developed the novel primordial germ cell (PGC) technology. \n• Established the stem cell/targeted genome editing team from a 1-person effort to a 7-10 person cross-functional group. \n• Project lead of a metabolic/lysosomal storage disease program (SBC-520). \n• Improved Synageva’s proprietary protein production platform by instituting a precise insertion of the therapeutic genes into the genome to ensure a reliable and consistent protein production. \n• Devised high throughput screening for transgenic animals in the individual ERT programs and, together with the PGC technology, greatly reduced the workload for the genetic screening and expedited the timeline for all ERT programs. \n• Directed RNA-Seq to profile transcriptome of chicken tubular gland cells.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Senior Director, Preclinical Research at Cytovia Therapeutics · 2023年 - 2025年 | Director, Preclinical Research at Cytovia Therapeutics · 2021年 - 2023年 | Scientist, Principal at NantKwest · 2018年 - 2021年 | 显示列表中的全部职业档案中列出的工作经历项目。全部项目: 10","education":[{"school":"NYU School of Medicine, Sackler Institute","degree":"Ph.D.","field_of_study":"Molecular Oncology and Immunology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"美国纽约大学","degree":"M.S.","field_of_study":"Recombinant DNA Biotechnology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"清华大学","degree":"B.S.","field_of_study":"Molecular Biology and Biochemistry","date_range":"","activities":"活动与社团: President, Student Government Senator, Student Parliament","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | NYU School of Medicine, Sackler Institute，Ph.D. | 美国纽约大学，M.S. | 清华大学，B.S. | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":false,"detail_error":""}}
