{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:49:51+08:00","record":{"name":"YenPing Chang","current_title":"Analytical Scientist","current_company":"Takeda through Digital Prospectors · 合同","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 洛厄尔","headline":"Scientist specializing in HPLC/UPLC method development and troubleshooting","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/bert-chang","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACBhDQUB72j-Uoo6Qp1YuX6Wuj4kuR3UGB0","core_skills":["N-Linked oligosachride assay","peptide mapping","protein digest"],"positions":[{"title":"Analytical Scientist","company":"Takeda through Digital Prospectors · 合同","date_range":"2025年4月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 6 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 列克星敦","description":"Develop, optimize and validate analytical methods for product characterization and release testing.  \nPerform sample preparation for various analytical techniques. \nConduct HPLC and UPLC analysis  \nEvaluate and implement commercial kits for sample prep and analysis, ensuring accuracy and reproducibility.  \nMaintain laboratory documentation in compliance with GMP/GLP guidelines. \nCollaborate with cross functional teams including QC, R&D and Manufacturing to support method development and transfer activities  \nParticipate in method qualification, validation and technology transfer activities.","skills":[]},{"title":"Doctoral Researcher","company":"Massachusetts Bio-Manufacturing Center (MBMC), University of Massachusetts Lowell · 全职","date_range":"2020年9月 - 2024年12月","duration":"4 年 4 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 洛厄尔","description":"• Conducted structural and functional characterizations on therapeutic proteins to support process development and IND-enabling studies \n• Developed and optimized analytical workflows for manufacturing process changes and drug substance stability evaluations \n• Drafted and implemented numerous Standard Operation Protocols (SOPs) to enhance analytical processes\n\n• Accomplished the analytical development and characterization of a recombinant ApoE and its lipidated form Originated and conducted structural and functional characterizations on numerous therapeutic proteins (mAb, polypeptides, fusion protein, chimeric/bi-specific Ab, ADCs, ApoE, etc. \n• ) with various separation modes on HPLC/UPLC systems Developed, executed, and optimized analytical workflows for process development and IND-enabling studies Performed comparability studies to support manufacturing process changes Performed LCMS for protein characterization and used ChemStation for data analysis Evaluated developability and manufacturability of mAb and bi-specific antibody drug candidates Explored drug substance stability under various conditions prior to clinical trial Drafted and implemented numerous Standard Operation Protocols (SOPs) to enhance analytical processes.","skills":["Antibodies","Analytical Biochemistry","Liquid Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry (LC-MS)","High-Performance Liquid Chromatography (HPLC)","Protein Purification","N-Linked oligosachride assay","peptide mapping"]},{"title":"Teaching Assistant","company":"Department of Chemistry, University of Massachusetts Lowell","date_range":"2020年9月 - 2024年12月","duration":"4 年 4 个月","location":"","description":"• Administered general chemistry 1&2 lab, organic and modern inorganic lab, including giving lab lectures, grading course assignments and lab reports, and assisting course supervisors with materials. \n• Contributed significantly to fostering fair and consistent evaluation procedures Taught over 200+ STEM undergraduate students with essential scientific skills such as maintaining good records, plotting and lab safety, reagent & material prep, and basic instrumentation Conducted regular office hours to offer personalized academic support, clarifying complex concepts and assisting with assignments, resulting in a measurable increase in student comprehension and performance in lab courses.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist","company":"BMS through P