{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:52:16+08:00","record":{"name":"Ken Chang","current_title":"Senior Director, Translational Biomarkers, Precision Medicine","current_company":"Daiichi Sankyo Inc. · 全职","location":"美国 新泽西州 Warren","headline":"Senior Director, Clinical Biomarkers","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/kencnchang","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAAgU8wBWkU_er_EOh7JZQiyhs_IQo4dKkc","core_skills":["Pharmaceutical Industry","Biomarkers","Assay Development"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Director, Translational Biomarkers, Precision Medicine","company":"Daiichi Sankyo Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2023年4月","duration":"1 个月","location":"美国 新泽西州 Basking Ridge","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Director, Clinical Biomarkers","company":"Daiichi Sankyo, Inc.","date_range":"2017年3月 - 2023年3月","duration":"6 年 1 个月","location":"Basking Ridge, NJ","description":"Exploratory Biomarker Lead for Daiichi Sankyo's oncology programs. Initial focus was on identifying various Next Generation Sequencing (NGS) technologies, platforms, and their clinical applications to facilitate biomarker discovery work and to propose and implement clinical sample analysis plans. \n \nRecent activities: \n1. Conference Keynote Speaker for the \"9th Annual NGS & Clinical Diagnostics Congress\", November 2017, London, UK.","skills":[]},{"title":"Clinical Assay Development and Biomarker Lead/Director","company":"Merck","date_range":"2011年2月 - 2017年3月","duration":"6 年 2 个月","location":"","description":"Scientific Lead for genomics assay outsourcing projects. Scientific Lead for in-house mutation assay development and validation. Lead scientific direction for new technologies including Next Generation Sequencing \n• Lead in-house genomics assay development and validation efforts for KRAS/BRAF/NRAS mutation assay for prospective cancer patient enrollment in Phase I/II clinical trials \n• Managed many genomics assay outsourcing projects including qPCR, microarrays, SNP assays in supporting many disease areas of clinical trials at Merck Clinical Labs \n• Helped guide/design novel clinical patient stratification assays for phase I/II trials supporting Merck Immuno-Oncology Franchise, and filed several invention disclosures based on cutting-edge genomic assay platforms \n \nRecent Activities (invited speaker and session chair): \n1. Clinical Genomics, Boston, 28-30 January, 2014 \n2. Clinical Biomarkers and Diagnostics, Philadelphia, April 30-May 2, 2014 \n3. Cancer Diagnosis at the Cross Roads, Seattle, 15-17 September, 2014  \n4. Clinical Trial Phase I-IIA, Philadelphia, 15-16 October, 2014 \n5. Clinical Genome & Exome Sequencing, San Diego, 3-4 December, 2014 \n6. Molecular Medicine Tri-Conference, San Francisco, 15-18 February, 2015 \n7. Biomarkers & Diagnostics World Congress, Philadelphia, 5-7 May, 2015 \n8. Molecular Medicine Tri-Conference, San Francisco, 7-9 March, 2016","skills":[]},{"title":"Principal Research Scientist III","company":"Pfizer, Project Team Leader","date_range":"2008年1月 - 2010年","duration":"2 年 1 个月","location":"","description":"Transcriptional Targets, Tissue Repair \n \nResearch focus: Team leader for multiple drug discovery projects related to tendon repair and articular therapy taking both small molecule and macro-molecule approaches including siRNA/shRNA and peptide. Disease mechanism related signaling pathway identification and analysis.  \n \n \nResearch Expertise  \n \nTranscriptional targets, expression profiling (GeneChip & differential display), signaling pathway analysis, target identification and target validation, DNA sequencing, cell culture related technologies, cell-based assay development, antiviral/anticancer research, oligonucleotide modification, DNA replication, DNA polymerase characterization (including purification, kinetics, and sequence/substrate specificity), DNA structure conformation, DNA/RNA technology, high throughput assay development, and nucleoside nucleotide based drug metabolism and development.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Senior Director, Translational Biomarkers, Precision Medicine at Daiichi Sankyo Inc. · 2023年 | Director, Clinical Biomarkers at Daiichi Sankyo, Inc. · 2017年 - 2023年 | Clinical Assay Development and Biomarker Lead/Director at Merck · 2011年 - 2017年 | Principal Research Scientist III at Pfizer, Project Team Leader · 2008年 - 2010年 | Principal Research Scientist III at Wyeth Research, Project Team Leader · 2006年 - 2008年 | Principal Research Scientist II at Wyeth Research, Head of Expressional Profiling & Cell Culture Core Group · 2004年 - 2006年 | Principal Research Scientist at Wyeth Research, Head of Expressional Profiling & DNA Sequencing Group · 1999年 - 2004年 | Principal Scientist at Wyeth Research, Head of Nucleic Acids Technologies/DNA Sequencing Group · 1995年 - 1999年 | Sr. Research Scientist at Wyeth Research, Anti-Viral Research group · 1993年 - 1995年 | Associate Research Scientist (equivalent to Research Assistant Professor) at Yale University · 1992年 - 1993年 | Postdoc Research Fellow at Yale University · 1990年 - 1992年 | SUNY at Stony Brook - Postdoc Research Fellow · 1988年 - 1990年","education":[{"school":"Yale University School of Medicine","degree":"","field_of_study":"Pharmacology (postdoc research)","date_range":"1990年 - 1993年","activities":"活动与社团: Discovery and study of new drugs for the treatment of hepatitis B virus infection and hepatoma.","grade":""},{"school":"SUNY Stony Brook","degree":"Ph.D.","field_of_study":"Medicinal Chemistry & Pharmacology","date_range":"1984年 - 1988年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Tamkang University","degree":"","field_of_study":"Chemistry","date_range":"1981年 - 1983年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Yale University School of Medicine · 1990年 - 1993年 | SUNY Stony Brook，Ph.D. · 1984年 - 1988年 | Tamkang University · 1981年 - 1983年 | 台北科技大学 | 保存到项目 | 将Ken保存到项目 | 发消息给Ken | Ken Chang的更多操作","o