{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:53:23+08:00","record":{"name":"Qian Chang Gallo","current_title":"Dream Studio Lab Assistant","current_company":"Medical University of South Carolina · 全职","location":"查尔斯顿地区","headline":"PhD Student at the Medical University of South Carolina & Clemson University","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/qian-chang-gallo-261b001a0","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAC8mRWkBZibf0QGv6CQZItOtyG9NVG7LCW8","core_skills":["Databases","Kitchen Management","Drug Discovery"],"positions":[{"title":"Dream Studio Lab Assistant","company":"Medical University of South Carolina · 全职","date_range":"2025年4月 - 2026年7月","duration":"1 年 4 个月","location":"美国 南卡罗莱纳 查尔斯顿","description":"Member of Digital Strategies and Innovation (DSI). Creating Machine Learning Models for Colbert Learning Center optimization, NLP research in Communication Disorders, and other MUSC student research projects. Managing the DREAM studio involving 3-D design, 3-D Scanning, FDM (filament) printing, SLA (resin) printing, and post-processing techniques.","skills":["PyTorch","Pandas (Software)","Prototyping","Matplotlib","Biomedical Research","Natural Language Processing (NLP)","Core ML","Forecasting","Game Technology","Research Computing","Computer-Aided Design (CAD)","Machine Learning","Databases","Statistical Data Analysis","3D Modeling","3D Printing","Virtual Reality (VR)","Maintenance and Repair","Python (Programming Language)","Project Managers"]},{"title":"Data Science Graduate Researcher","company":"College of Charleston · 兼职","date_range":"2024年8月 - 2025年12月","duration":"1 年 5 个月","location":"查尔斯顿地区","description":"Completed the following data science research projects: \n \nDecoding Yelp Reviews: Can AI Predict Customer Rating Score Before Posting? Created a language model that investigated the relationship between review text and user ratings using the public Yelp API. Created an aggregate dataset containing business, review, and demographic datasets, aggregating United States census data. Explored word frequency trends and emotional importance metrics to predict review scores with a goal of creating a generalized model for inter-industrial application.  \n \nUncovering Kudzu’s Climate Niche: A Presence Analysis using Clustering and Density Modeling: Implemented unsupervised machine learning techniques like clustering (K-Means, DBSCAN). Also employed density modeling on 463 kudzu observations records from iNaturalist with PRISM climate data. Identified optimal growth conditions including mean annual temperature, annual rainfall, and solar radiation. These results inform conservation management and pave the way for drone-based ecological mapping.  \n \nEnhancing Sarcasm Detection Using Emotion-Sentiment Incongruity in Transformer and Non-Transformer Models: Developed a new sarcasm detection pipeline by combining the established RoBERTa model with an auxiliary feature named “emotion-incongruity score.” This design effectively used VADER and NRCLex libraries to supplement the RoBERTa model. After comparing performance using a logistic regression model as a control, the new pipeline showed improved model robustness compared to vanilla RoBERTa.","skills":["PyTorch","Pandas (Software)","NoSQL","Matplotlib","Natural Language Processing (NLP)","Core ML","Forecasting","Research Computing","Machine Learning","Databases","Statistical Data Analysis","Python (Programming Language)"]},{"title":"Cook","company":"Rosewood Market & Deli · 全职","date_range":"2023年5月 - 2024年5月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"","description":"Managed a high-volume kitchen, consistently preparing 100+ meals per service with a keen focus on quality, presentation, and speed, leading to a 20% increase in customer satisfaction ratings and rated one of the best in Columbia \n28053 Rosewood Dr, Columbia, SC, 29205 (803) 765-1083","skills":["Cooking","Food Preparation","Grocery","Customer Service","Kitchen Management","Spanish-speaking"]},{"title":"Research Assistant","company":"Arnold School of Public Health at the University of South Carolina","date_range":"2022年8月 - 2022年11月","duration":"4 个月","location":"","description":"Aided in off-site algae research tracking algae blooms in Columbia water systems. Created experimental groups with nitrogen, phosphorus, and sulfur treatments. Prepared rope pullies for tracking algae in Columbia lakes. 921 Assembly St, Columbia, SC 29208 (310) 980-2946","skills":["Cellular Analysis"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Dream Studio Lab Assistant at Medical University of South Carolina · 2025年 - 2026年 | Data Science Graduate Researcher at College of Charleston · 2024年 - 2025年 | Cook at Rosewood Market & Deli · 2023年 - 2024年 | Arnold School of Public Health at the University of South Carolina - Research Assistant · 2022年 - 2022年 | Cashier at Isle of Palms Marina · 2021年 - 2022年 | Research Scholar at Medical University of South Carolina · 2021年 - 2021年","education":[{"school":"Medical University of South Carolina","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy","field_of_study":"Biomedical Data Science & Informatics","date_range":"2026年 - 2030年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Clemson University College of Engineering, Computing and Applied Sciences","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy","field_of_study":"Biomedical Data Science & Informatics","date_range":"2026年 - 2030年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"College of Charleston","degree":"Master of Science - MS","field_of_study":"Artificial Intelligence & Data Science","date_range":"2024年 - 2025年","activities":"","grade":"4.0"}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Medical University of South Carolina，Doctor of Philosophy · 2026年 - 2030年 | Clemson University College of Engineering, Computing and Applied Sciences，Doctor of Philosophy · 2026年 - 2030年 | College of Charleston，Master of Science - MS · 2024年 - 2025年 | University of South Carolina，Bachelor of Science - BS · 2022年 - 2023年 | 美国南加州大学，Neuroscience ·