{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:58:00+08:00","record":{"name":"Soo-Ik Chang","current_title":"Professor of Biochemistry","current_company":"Chungbuk National University","location":"韩国 忠清北道","headline":"Professor of Biochemistry at Chungbuk National University","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/soo-ik-chang-6a572026","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAVyGd0B7ruT1raZbMywzJH-MM8eVo9K85I","core_skills":["Assay Development","Microarray","Lifesciences"],"positions":[{"title":"Professor of Biochemistry","company":"Chungbuk National University","date_range":"1991年3月 - 现在","duration":"35 年 7 个月","location":"","description":"Our group at Chungbuk National University has been actively engaged in the development and application of protein chip systems to pharmaceutical and biological problems. The primary focus of this research effort has been in the development and application of protein microarray systems for drug screening, and of protein nanoarray systems for measuring protein-protein interactions. In both areas we have used a new protein immobilization method using a bifunctional molecular linker, ProLinkerTM (PROTEOGEN Inc, Republic of Korea). Key projects within the group include highthroughput screening for new angiogenesis inhibitors using the protein microarray system, protein expression profiling for toxicoproteomics and high-throughput measurement for protein-protein interaction in a nano scale. \nIn addition, our group has been involved in the field of angiogenesis in general and in the study of an angiogenic factor angiogenin in particular. Various in vitro and in vivo angiogenesis assays have been developed, and gene therapy techniques using adeno-associated virus has been used for therapeutic angiogenesis therapy. \nCurrent facilities include atomic force microscope, microarrayer, laser fluorescence reader, fluorescence polirization spectroscope, stopped-flow kinetics system, BIAcore, and confocal microscope.","skills":[]},{"title":"Visiting Professor","company":"Imperial College London","date_range":"2009年9月 - 2011年8月","duration":"2 年","location":"","description":"Droplet-based microfluidics","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow","company":"Harvard Medical School","date_range":"1988年11月 - 1991年2月","duration":"2 年 4 个月","location":"","description":"Mechanism of action of angiogenin","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Professor of Biochemistry at Chungbuk National University · 1991年 - 现在 | Visiting Professor at Imperial College London · 2009年 - 2011年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow at Harvard Medical School · 1988年 - 1991年","education":[{"school":"美国康奈尔大学","degree":"Ph.D.","field_of_study":"Biophysical Chemistry","date_range":"1983年 - 1998年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"고려대학교","degree":"M.S.","field_of_study":"Physical Chemistry","date_range":"1981年 - 1983年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"고려대학교","degree":"Bachelor of Science (B.S.)","field_of_study":"Chemistry","date_range":"1977年 - 1981年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 美国康奈尔大学，Ph.D. · 1983年 - 1998年 | 고려대학교，M.S. · 1981年 - 1983年 | 고려대학교，Bachelor of Science (B.S.) · 1977年 - 1981年 | 保存到项目 | 将Soo-Ik保存到项目 | 发消息给Soo-Ik | Soo-Ik Chang的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"中高级 (商务会话)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T10:58:47+08:00","record":{"name":"Tzu-I Chao","current_title":"Director of drug development","current_company":"Senhwa","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","headline":"Ph.D., Certified Valuation Analyst (CVA), Cross-Functional Drug Development Professional, Preclinical Discovery, Clinical Development, Regulatory Submissions, Alliance Management, Licensing and Business Development","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/tzu-i-chao-29a08741","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAi7SNYB09dgyctLhbrw1IyvsXvssMbGmms","core_skills":["Hepatitis","Pharmacodynamics","Immunoprecipitation"],"positions":[{"title":"Director of drug development","company":"Senhwa","date_range":"2 年","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Manager","company":"Senhwa","date_range":"2 年","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Director","company":"SupremeCure Pharma","date_range":"7 年 3 个月","duration":"5 年 8 个月","location":"台湾","description":"Orchestrated collaborations with CROs, and effectively led the IND application in the USA and clinical trial application in Europe, culminating in the successful execution of Phase I clinical trial for a small molecule oncology drug. \n \nDirected and managed the phase I oncology trial, coordinating with the CRO for trial submission, initiation, safety oversight, AE/SAE reporting, DSMB collaboration, DSUR preparation, data summary, and maintaining budget control. Acted as the primary point of contact for the sponsor, ensuring streamlined and efficient trial progression. \n \n \nManaged a multidisciplinary team for the preclinical evaluation of a small molecule for the treatment of IPF and wAMD. \n \nProvide pivotal insights and strategic guidance during the rebuttal process, effectively steering the endeavor towards the successful issuance of a patent related to fibrosis therapies. \n \nEvaluated the potential of the drug for cancer immunotherapy in preclinical settings. \n \nOversaw the production of multiple batches of IMP and API, ensuring seamless advancement of the trial. \n \nRepresented the corporation at one-on-one partnering events, facilitating the development of alliances. \n \nMaintained a positive, transparent, and professional relationship with the partners, a key catalyst in propelling the forward trajectory of projects. \n \nSuccessfully established co-development agreement and MOU with international corporation, expanding the collaborative endeavors into diverse disease areas. \n \nStrategically in-licensed assets, successfully expanding the corporation’s pipeline. \n \nLeveraged R&D expenditure tax deductions, resulting in significant cost savings for the corporation.","skills":["技能: Clinical Trials","Clinical Trials"]},{"title":"Program Manager, Small molecule oncology drug development","company":"SupremeCure Pharma","date_range":"7 年 3 个月","duration":"5 年 8 个月","location":"台湾","description":"Orchestrated collaborations with CROs, and effectively led the IND application in the USA and clinical trial application in Europe, culminating in the successful execution of Phase I clinical trial for a small molecule oncology drug. \n \nDirected and managed the phase I oncology trial, coordinating with the CRO for trial submission, initiation, safety oversight, AE/SAE reporting, DSMB collaboration, DSUR preparation, data summary, and maintaining budget control. Acted as the primary point of contact for the sponsor, ensuring streamlined and efficient trial progression. \n \n \nManaged a multidisciplinary team for the preclinical evaluation of a small molecule for the treatment of IPF and wAMD. \n \nProvide pivotal insights and strategic guidance during the rebuttal process, effectively steering the endeavor towards the successful issuance of a patent related to fibrosis therapies. \n \nEvaluated the potential of the drug for cancer immunotherapy in preclinical settings. \n \nOversaw the production of multiple batches of IMP and API, ensuring seamless advancement of the trial. \n \nRepresented the corporation at one-on-one partnering events, facilitating the development of alliances. \n \nMaintained a positive, transparent, and professional relationship with the partners, a key catalyst in propelling the forward trajectory of projects. \n \nSuccessfully established co-development agreement and MOU with international corporation, expanding the collaborative endeavors into diverse disease areas. \n \nStrategically in-licensed assets, successfully expanding the corporation’s pipeline. \n \nLeveraged R&D expenditure tax deductions, resulting in significant cost savings for the corporation.","skills":["技能: Clinical Trials","Clinical Trials"]},{"title":"Project Manager (Post-Doctoral Scholar)","company":"NTUH · 全职","date_range":"2015年3月 - 2016年5月","duration":"1 年 3 个月","location":"","description":"Conducted partner assessments and facilitated engagements, skillfully negotiating pricing terms, orchestrating timeline development, implementing cost estimations, and exercising effective budget control. \n \nManaged the manufacturing process of the API, encompassing review of specifications, method validations, and batch records. \n \nCoordinated experimental design and protocol review, proficiently troubleshooting issues, assessing TK parameters, and ensuring the seamless completion of IND-enabling toxicology studies (GLP). \n \nLed the development of viable formulations, employing rigorous selection criteria for excipients based on solubility, stability, daily intake, and maximum potency considerations. Conducted PK studies to assess bioavailability. \n \nDesigned in vitro and in vivo experiments, critically reviewed protocols, and provided technical support for pharmacology studies.","skills":[]},{"title":"Post Doctoral Fellow","company":"UC Davis","date_range":"2013年4月 - 2014年12月","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"","description":"steatosi