{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:00:22+08:00","record":{"name":"William Ming-Wei Chao, PhD, DABT","current_title":"執行長","current_company":"Future PharmaTech · 正式","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","headline":"Future PharmaTech CEO","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/william-ming-wei-chao-phd-dabt-381336156","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACVsoZEByqzZt9XADOn_xMR2K6E9h29cdVQ","core_skills":["Design and management of pre-clinical and clinical safety tests","Identification of safety issues and design and management of safety programs","Design of studies for substantiation of safety related claims"],"positions":[{"title":"執行長","company":"Future PharmaTech · 正式","date_range":"2026年6月 - 现在","duration":"4 个月","location":"台湾 台北市","description":"Future PharmaTech Inc. is a Taiwan-based biotechnology company founded in 2021 that combines artificial intelligence, toxicology, pharmacology, and nanomedicine to accelerate the development of innovative therapies for neurological and vascular diseases. \n \nIts proprietary Future-AI Platform integrates disease biology, drug mechanisms, clinical evidence, molecular modeling, and safety data to identify and optimize multi-target drug candidates. By leveraging AI-driven drug repurposing and a 505(b)(2) development strategy, the company aims to reduce development timelines, costs, and risks while improving clinical success rates. \n \nFuture PharmaTech’s pipeline focuses on major unmet medical needs, including vascular dementia, Alzheimer’s disease, erectile dysfunction, benign prostatic hyperplasia, pulmonary arterial hypertension, and traumatic brain injury. \n \nA key differentiator is its proprietary blood-brain barrier (BBB) delivery and nanomedicine technology, designed to improve drug penetration into the central nervous system. \n \nThrough scientific innovation, strategic partnerships, and AI-powered drug discovery, Future PharmaTech is committed to delivering safer, faster, and more effective therapies to patients worldwide.","skills":["Pharmaceutical Research","人工智慧","Toxicology"]},{"title":"Toxicology Director","company":"Redox Medicare","date_range":"2014年12月 - 现在","duration":"11 年 10 个月","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","description":"As the co-founder and the chief toxicology director.  \n \n1. As the Toxicology Director in charging for the product safety in Redox Medicare®. \n2. Provide intellectual support to early drug discovery teams from a safety perspective. Design experimental plan to the target and chemistry, new modality, mechanism of modulation.  \n3. Work as core member of discovery drug project teams as the safety representative.  \n4. As part of the Toxicology Team work in interdisciplinary teams to provide OECD-based safety support to early discovery teams and engage in core activities within the Toxicology group.  \n5. Work as part of a team of safety assessment scientists and more broadly DMPK, pathology, pharmacology, and medicinal chemistry experts to implement discovery toxicology strategy to enable the selection and progression of optimized drug candidates.  \n6. Apply novel toxicity mechanism-based assays and integrated models to support early target safety and chemistry evaluation. \n7. Years industry relative experience.","skills":[]},{"title":"教授","company":"Chung Yuan Christian University · 正式","date_range":"2012年8月 - 2026年6月","duration":"13 年 11 个月","location":"台湾 桃园市 桃园市","description":"-Function as project investigator supporting pre-development and development toxicological, systemic and OTC project team.  \n-My research work regarding to Biomedical Science field is classified as molecular toxicology and neural pathology with using in vitro and in vivo biology-based research. \n-Simultaneously collaborate cross-field with studies of molecular regulation, biological signaling, neuroscience, pharmacokinetics, and toxin pathogenesis.  \n-Study Direct and Study Monitor non-clinical toxicology studies (toxicological, systemic, neural, reproductive, genetox, pharmacology, food safety) \n-Analyze results and write study conclusions that provide accurate assessment of the safety of test formulations. \n-In vitro evaluation, animal model, clinical connection are the professionals, and summarize nonclinical safety data  \n-The Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC) member \n-Being the editor member in three different Toxicology-related journals, which are Cardiovascular Regenerative Medicine, ROS, Medical and Clinical Toxicology, and FABAD Journal of Pharmaceutical Sciences  \n-The executive secretory in the research member of Toxicology Society of Taiwan (TSTA)","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Researcher","company":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology","date_range":"2009年10月 - 2012年6月","duration":"2 年 9 个月","location":"波士顿地区","description":"I was appointed as a postdoc in Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) Biological Engineering (BE), Professor Gerald Wogan’s lab right after I received my toxicology doctorate. Through that work, we devised a way to study the Biomarkers to assess how DNA lesions caused by oxidative stress and inflammation produce mutations. This led us to link the chemical formation of lesions with specific genetic changes. Those DNA lesions could also act as functional biomarkers to predict risk of free radicals, and evaluate future chemo-prevention strategies. Thus, we designed a specific genetic probe functioning as a biomarker which is able to pre-screen the potential genetic damage and calculate the mutation frequency in the tissue in response to the “micro-dosage” of xenobiotic exposure. Because of its uniqueness, this research topic was listed by the National Science Foundation (NSF) and the National Institutes of Health (NIH) simultaneously as an important research project, and became a novel subject in MIT. In addition to laboratory work, I also have comprehensive chemical biology training and worked as a training grant supported post-graduated teaching assistant for the toxicology class in BE department. These experiences gave me a deep understanding of how important teamwork, proactivity, and having a calm demeanor are. My time at MIT not only provided me with a great enthusiasm for my courses, but I also accumulated a strong academic foundation that will allow me to take on future challenges.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 執行長 at Future PharmaTech · 2026年 - 现在 | Toxicology Director at Redox Medicare · 2014年 - 现在 | 教授 at Chung Yuan Christian University · 2012年 - 2026年 | Postdoctoral Researcher at Massachusetts Institute of Technology · 2009年 - 2012年","education":[{"school":"美国罗格斯新泽西州立大学新布朗斯维克分校","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Toxicology","date_range":"","activities":"活动与社团: My PhD thesis titled “PM2.5 Diesel Exhaust Particles Alter Capillary Endothelial Tubes Permeability,” under the tutelage of Professor Marion Gordon. In the dissertation, I have built a reliable and multipurpose “in vitro 3D cardio blood vessels co-culture cell model,” which has proven that this simulation system can be effectively used to study the transmission path of PM2.5 into the pulmonary and cardio blood vessels.","grade":""},{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Agricultural Chemistry","date_range":"1999年 - 2002年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 美国罗格斯新泽西州立大学新布朗斯维克分校，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD | 台湾大学，Bachelor's degree · 1999年 - 2002年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":true,"detail_error":""}}
