cured £180K+ in competitive funding to support AML research, building persuasive, data‑driven cases for investment from clinical and charitable stakeholders. \n>   Engaged 50+ internal and external experts through invited talks, panel discussions and workshops, strengthening networks across the UK haematology and oncology community. \n>   Mentored 3 MSc students, supporting progression into PhD and industry‑relevant roles. \n>   Provided translational input that helped progress 5 preclinical projects towards clinical evaluation, including identifying potential biomarkers and patient subgroups. \n>   Published 4 peer-reviewed papers, including 2 first-author publications.","skills":["技能: Scientific Engagement • Medical Education • Scientific Communication • Mentorship & Supervision • Digital Learning Platforms • Evidence-based Education","Scientific Engagement","Medical Education","Scientific Communication","Mentorship & Supervision","Digital Learning Platforms","Evidence-based Education","技能: Scientific Engagement • Scientific Communication • Drug Discovery & Therapeutic Prioritisation • Cross-functional Collaborations • Goal-Oriented Project Leadership • Mentorship & Supervision • Multi-omics & Data Integration • Cross-Functional Team Coordination • Translational Research • Strategic Planning","Drug Discovery & Therapeutic Prioritisation","Cross-functional Collaborations","Goal-Oriented Project Leadership","Multi-omics & Data Integration","Cross-Functional Team Coordination","Translational Research","Strategic Planning"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow","company":"UCL Great Ormond Street Institute of Child Health","date_range":"5 年 6 个月","duration":"5 个月","location":"London, England, United Kingdom","description":"Integrated disease biology, biomarker discovery and stakeholder engagement to support evidence‑based therapeutic decisions. Led research, communication and funding activities that strengthened UK haematology networks and advanced preclinical projects towards clinical evaluation. \n \n• Insight generation: Led translational AML research programmes to generate clinically relevant insights, biomarker hypotheses and evidence‑based narratives for haematologists and multidisciplinary teams; provided translational input to preclinical projects moving towards clinical evaluation. \n \n• Scientific communication and relationships: Acted as a scientific point of contact for internal and external experts, communicating complex findings in tailored formats for clinicians, researchers, funders and lay stakeholders; strengthened networks across the UK haematology and oncology community through talks, panels and workshops.  \n \n• Governance and leadership: Developed data‑driven funding cases and secured competitive grants from charities; managed multi‑partner collaborations and applied GCP‑aligned principles and institutional SOPs when handling patient samples and data. \n \nKey Achievements: \n>   Secured £180K+ in competitive funding to support AML research, building persuasive, data‑driven cases for investment from clinical and charitable stakeholders. \n>   Engaged 50+ internal and external experts through invited talks, panel discussions and workshops, strengthening networks across the UK haematology and oncology community. \n>   Mentored 3 MSc students, supporting progression into PhD and industry‑relevant roles. \n>   Provided translational input that helped progress 5 preclinical projects towards clinical evaluation, including identifying potential biomarkers and patient subgroups. \n>   Published 4 peer-reviewed papers, including 2 first-author publications.","skills":["技能: Scientific Engagement • Medical Education • Scientific Communication • Mentorship & Supervision • Digital Learning Platforms • Evidence-based Education","Scientific Engagement","Medical Education","Scientific Communication","Mentorship & Supervision","Digital Learning Platforms","Evidence-based Education","技能: Scientific Engagement • Scientific Communication • Drug Discovery & Therapeutic Prioritisation • Cross-functional Collaborations • Goal-Oriented Project Leadership • Mentorship & Supervision • Multi-omics & Data Integration • Cross-Functional Team Coordination • Translational Research • Strategic Planning","Drug Discovery & Therapeutic Prioritisation","Cross-functional Collaborations","Goal-Oriented Project Leadership","Multi-omics & Data Integration","Cross-Functional Team Coordination","Translational Research","Strategic Planning"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Scientist in Human Genetics & Biology","company":"University of Oxford · 全职","date_range":"2019年9月 - 2021年3月","duration":"1 年 7 个月","location":"Oxford, England, United Kingdom","description":"Developed mismatch‑repair‑deficient endometrial and colorectal cancer models to investigate tumour–immune interactions and biomarker‑relevant mechanisms for immuno‑oncology. Focused on generating insights that support patient stratification, therapeutic prioritisation and the development of novel organoid‑based workflows. \n \n• Insight generation: Developed MLH1‑deficient, mismatch‑repair‑deficient (dMMR) endometrial and colorectal cancer models to investigate tumour–immune interactions and biomarker‑relevant mechanisms for immuno‑oncology; generated translational insights into patient stratification and therapeutic prioritisation in biomarker‑defined disease subsets. \n \n• Scientific communication and collaboration: Prepared posters and research presentations in collaboration with physicians and cross‑functional stakeholders for funding and review panels, clearly articulating translational impact, study rationale and future clinical directions; contributed to Wellcome Trust funding success. \n \n• Evidence review and workflow development: Conducted detailed literature review, protocol refinement and scientific documentation to establish a novel organoid banking workflow, supporting reproducible sample handling and downstream experimental consistency. \n \n• Compliance and governance: Managed patient samples in line with HTA, confidentiality and research governance requirements, maintaining high standards of quality, traceability and ethical oversight.","skills":["Scientific Engagement","Medical Education","Scientific Communication","Translational Oncology Research","Therapeutic Target Prioritisation","Precision Oncology"]},{"title":"Research Assistant","company":"Prince of Wales Hospital, Chinese University of Hong Kong · 全职","date_range":"2015年11月 - 2016年5月","duration":"7 个月","location":"香港特别行政区","description":"Supported delivery of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) trials in a hospital setting, with responsibilities spanning patient communication, site coordination and GCP‑aligned documentation. Helped ensure protocol‑compliant recruitment, informed consent and data quality across multidisciplinary teams. \n \n• Clinical research support: Supported delivery of IBD clinical trials in line with study protocols and GCP requirements, contributing to safe, compliant implementation of investigational studies in a busy hospital environment. \n \n• Patient communication and informed consent: Recruited patients into clinical trials and clearly explained study objectives, procedures and potential risks/benefits to support informed consent and patient understanding. \n \n• Stakeholder coordination: Liaised with gastroenterologists, research nurses and study coordinators to optimise site workflows, sample collection and visit scheduling, helping maintain trial momentum and patient experience. \n \n• Documentation and quality control: Maintained accurate study documentation, including the Investigator Site File and source data, to support data integrity, monitoring activities and audit readiness.","skills":["Good Clinical Practice (GCP)","Informed Consent","Clinical Trial Coordination","Patient Recruitment","Stakeholder Engagement"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Research Associate at UCL Great Ormond Street Institute of Child Health · 2026年 - 现在 | Teaching Associate (Cell, Gene and Novel Therapies MSc) at UCL Great Ormond Street Institute of Child Health · 2022年 - 2024年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow at UCL Great Ormond Street Institute of Child Health · 2021年 - 2024年 | John Goldman Fellow at UCL Great Ormond Street Institute of Child Health · 2021年 - 2026年 | Postdoctoral Research Scientist in Human Genetics & Biology at University of Oxford · 2019年 - 2021年 | Research Assistant at Prince of Wales Hospital, Chinese University of Hong Kong · 2015年 - 2016年","education":[{"school":"香港大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (PhD)","field_of_study":"Oncology and Cancer Biology","date_range":"2016年 - 2019年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"英国帝国理工学院","degree":"MRes","field_of_study":"Clinical Medicine - Translational Medicine","date_range":"2014年 - 2015年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"英国莱斯特大学","degree":"Bachelor of Science (BSc)","field_of_study":"Medical Biochemistry","date_range":"2011年 - 2014年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 香港大学，Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) · 2016年 - 2019年 | 英国帝国理工学院，MRes · 2014年 - 2015年 | 英国莱斯特大学，Bachelor of Science (BSc) · 2011年 - 2014年 | 保存到项目 | 将Noelia保存到项目 | 发消息给Noelia | Noelia Che, PhD的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:02:13+08:00","record":{"name":"Harvey C.","current_title":"Director","current_company":"NanoMolar.ai · 全职","location":"剑桥地区","headline":"Bioinformatics Solutions for Drug Discovery | NanoMolar.ai","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/harvey-c-a83725b4","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABhP3cMB1IiiK-XgIcOowc09lFjctKASWXQ","core_skills":["Cancer Epigenetics","Assay Development","Structural Biology"],"positions":[{"title":"Director","company":"NanoMolar.ai · 全职","date_range":"2023年8月 - 现在","duration":"3 年 2 个月","location":"英国 英格兰 Cambridge","description":"We offer bioinformatics solutions to pharmaceutical and biotech companies \n \n- One-week standard bulk RNAseq analysis and interpretation  \n- NGS, Proteomics and metabolomic data analysis \n- Multi-omics data integration \n- single cell RNAseq analysis \n- Knowledge graph \n- Cloud enablement \n- Assay development","skills":["Biological Data Analysis"]},{"title":"Principal Scientist","company":"Sitryx","date_range":"2021年3月 - 2023年7月","duration":"2 年 5 个月","location":"英国 英格兰 牛津","description":"• Perform RNAseq, Proteomic and Metabolomic analysis on human autoimmune disease \n• High Performance Computing on AWS \n• Develop interactive data visualisation platform (RShiny) \n• Drug targets discovery with Multi-omics database, such as DepMap, TCGA, gTEX, GEO, COSMIC \n• Single cell RNAseq analysis and scRNAseq browser (visualisation) \n• In silico metabolic modelling from single cell data \n• Competitive Intelligence in pharmaceutical sector \n• Literature text mining","skills":["Biological Data Analysis"]},{"title":"Lead Bioinformatician","company":"The Institute of Cancer Research","date_range":"2018年6月 - 2021年11月","duration":"3 年 6 个月","location":"英国伦敦地区","description":"As lead bioinformatician at the Cancer Therapeutics Unit and Pediatric Tumour Biology Unit at ICR, my work supports multi-disciplinary drug discovery scientists in projects that involve extensive data handling such as Next Generation Sequencing (Whole Genome Sequencing / RNA-seq / scRNAseq) and high throughput Mass Spectrometry.  \n \nI have delivered bioinformatics solutions in the following area: \n \n• Immunomodulatory imide Drugs (IMiDs) / Protac  \n• 16-plex TMT Mass Spectrometry Data analysis and visualisation \n• Small molecule drug screening. Data analysis, visualisation and target priortisation. \n• RNA Helicase inhibition and RNA splicing analysis \n• Identify key drug resistance pathway in cancer \n• Biomarker discovery \n• Machine Learning algorithm to predict drug blood brain barrier penetration \n• Develop of Interactive data visualisation platform \n• Setup and Maintain departmental wide bioinformatics dashboard for data visualisation. \n• Use of Container technology (docker) and NextFlow to accelerate data analytic pipeline.  \n• Facilitate data exchange with both internal and external collaborator and CROs. \n• Coronavirus SAR resources (https://corona.cansar.icr.ac.uk \n• Neuroblastoma and Medulloblastoma translational studies \n• Pediatric clinical data management  \n \nSupported scientist/clinician in the following oncology area: \nBreast cancer, colorectal cancer, multiple myeloma, pancreatic desmoplasia, Medulloblastoma, Glioblastoma, neuroblastoma","skills":["Biological Data Analysis"]},{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"Bicycle Therapeutics","date_range":"2017年6月 - 2018年6月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"剑桥地区","description":"• CRO management (protein production, SPR and X-crystallography projects) \n• Use of phage display technology to discover constrained peptide binders for important oncology targets \n• Use of NGS for phage display library quality assessment and peptide sequence analysis.  \n• Responsible for four discovery projects, delivered high affinity peptide binders for two immuno-oncology targets. \n• Analyse in vitro peptide binding assays data (SPR, AlphaScreen, Fluorescent Polarisation) \n• Analyse Cell based Assay including Luciferase Reporter Assay and Flow cytometry data \n• Develop bioinformatics tools for amino acid/DNA sequence analysis and visualisation \n• Established multiple academic collaborations","skills":["Biological Data Analysis"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Director at NanoMolar.ai · 2023年 - 现在 | Principal Scientist at Sitryx · 2021年 - 2023年 | Lead Bioinformatician at The Institute of Cancer Research · 2018年 - 2021年 | Senior Scientist at Bicycle Therapeutics · 2017年 - 2018年 | Postdoctoral Research Associate at University of Cambridge · 2013年 - 2017年 | University of Oxford - Graduate Research Student at the Botnar Research Centre · 2011年 - 2013年 | Graduate Research Student at The Structural Genomics Consortium (SGC) · 2009年 - 2011年 | Internship at ZymoGenetics · 2006年 - 2006年","education":[{"school":"英国牛津大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - DPhil","field_of_study":"Biochemistry, Biophysics and Molecular Biology","date_range":"2009年 - 2013年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 英国牛津大学，Doctor of Philosophy - DPhil · 2009年 - 2013年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Director Principal Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 远程办公: 剑桥地区 欧洲经济区 美国 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 远程办公"],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
