{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:03:53+08:00","record":{"name":"Lei Chen","current_title":"Senior Director, Translational Medicine","current_company":"SpringWorks Therapeutics","location":"纽约地区","headline":"Senior Director, Translational Medicine | Precision Medicine & Biomarkers (Oncology & Immunology) | IND → FIH → Early Clinical Development | MoA, Resistance & Combinations | Multi-omics Integration","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/leichen-phd","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAFR6wMBe_QupgEHVuGSdR8hcXhuNwatZvM","core_skills":["Translational Medicine and Biomarker Strategies","IND-Enabling Studies","Indication Expansion"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Director, Translational Medicine","company":"SpringWorks Therapeutics","date_range":"3 年 9 个月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"美国 康乃狄克州 斯坦福德","description":"(Acquired by Merck KGaA in 2025) \n \nDirected translational medicine and biomarker strategies across multiple oncology programs from pre-IND through clinical development and lifecycle expansion. Led indication expansion, patient selection, and biomarker strategy while driving rational combinations and asset differentiation. \nTEAD inhibitor SW-682 (Phase 1) \n• Led translational strategy, defining MoA, PK/PD, patient selection, and dose rationale for Phase 1; co-authored IND/IB \n• Developed rational combination strategies with multiple RAS/MAPK inhibitors by integrating scientific rationale with competitive landscape and preclinical data to prioritize partners and inform clinical trial design \n• Led translational and multi-omics data analysis in collaboration with bioinformatics to identify predictive biomarkers of response and resistance, informing patient selection/stratification \n• Guided NGS-based patient selection and enrollment strategy for Phase 1; led exploratory IHC CDx planning \nOgsiveo (nirogacestat)— FDA-approved Notch inhibitor \n• Led translational and biomarker strategies for Ogsiveo (nirogacestat), driving lifecycle and indication expansion, Phase 3 biomarker analyses, post-approval Phase 4 biomarker planning, and health-authority interactions \n• Developed a clinical protocol dashboard integrating biomarker endpoints, dosing, sample collection, and data interpretation across ADC, CAR-T, and TCE combinations in multiple myeloma to assess Ogsiveo contribution \nPP2A molecular glue program (Induced Proximity) \n• Directed translational research for a first-in-class PP2A molecular glue asset, including scientific evaluation of partner data, IND-enabling strategy, and in vivo PK/PD and biomarker analysis; co-authored IND/IB \nLeadership & portfolio \n• Built and led a translational medicine team and global CRO/vendor and academic network; partnered with senior leadership on portfolio strategy, governance presentation, resource prioritization, and multi-program budgets","skills":["技能: Translational Medicine and Biomarker Strategies • Clinical Development • Companion Diagnostic (CDx) Strategy • Precision Oncology • Rational Combinations • Post-Marketing Translational Support • Regulatory & IND Documentation • Cross-functional Team Leadership","Translational Medicine and Biomarker Strategies","Clinical Development","Companion Diagnostic (CDx) Strategy","Precision Oncology","Rational Combinations","Post-Marketing Translational Support","Regulatory & IND Documentation","Cross-functional Team Leadership","技能: IND-Enabling Studies • Indication Expansion • Mechanism of Action (MoA) • Regulatory & IND Documentation • Cross-functional Team Leadership • Predictive Biomarker and Indication Selection • Preclinical to Early Clinical Translation","IND-Enabling Studies","Indication Expansion","Mechanism of Action (MoA)","Predictive Biomarker and Indication Selection","Preclinical to Early Clinical Translation"]},{"title":"Director, Translational Medicine","company":"SpringWorks Therapeutics","date_range":"3 年 9 个月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"美国 康乃狄克州 斯坦福德","description":"(Acquired by Merck KGaA in 2025) \n \nDirected translational medicine and biomarker strategies across multiple oncology programs from pre-IND through clinical development and lifecycle expansion. Led indication expansion, patient selection, and biomarker strategy while driving rational combinations and asset differentiation. \nTEAD inhibitor SW-682 (Phase 1) \n• Led translational strategy, defining MoA, PK/PD, patient selection, and dose rationale for Phase 1; co-authored IND/IB \n• Developed rational combination strategies with multiple RAS/MAPK inhibitors by integrating scientific rationale with competitive landscape and preclinical data to prioritize partners and inform clinical trial design \n• Led translational and multi-omics data analysis in collaboration with bioinformatics to identify predictive biomarkers of response and resistance, informing patient selection/stratification \n• Guided NGS-based patient selection and enrollment strategy for Phase 1; led exploratory IHC CDx planning \nOgsiveo (nirogacestat)— FDA-approved Notch inhibitor \n• Led translational and biomarker strategies for Ogsiveo (nirogacestat), driving lifecycle and indication expansion, Phase 3 biomarker analyses, post-approval Phase 4 biomarker planning, and health-authority interactions \n• Developed a clinical protocol dashboard integrating biomarker endpoints, dosing, sample collection, and data interpretation across ADC, CAR-T, and TCE combinations in multiple myeloma to assess Ogsiveo contribution \nPP2A molecular glue program (Induced Proximity) \n• Directed translational research for a first-in-class PP2A molecular glue asset, including scientific evaluation of partner data, IND-enabling strategy, and in vivo PK/PD and biomarker analysis; co-authored IND/IB \nLeadership & portfolio \n• Built and led a translational medicine team and global CRO/vendor and academic network; partnered with senior leadership on portfolio strategy, governance presentation, resource prioritization, and multi-program budgets","skills":["技能: Translational Medicine and Biomarker Strategies • Clinical Development • Companion Diagnostic (CDx) Strategy • Precision Oncology • Rational Combinations • Post-Marketing Translational Support • Regulatory & IND Documentation • Cross-functional Team Leadership","Translational Medicine and Biomarker Strategies","Clinical Development","Companion Diagnostic (CDx) Strategy","Precision Oncology","Rational Combinations","Post-Marketing Translational Support","Regulatory & IND Documentation","Cross-functional Team Leadership","技能: IND-Enabling Studies • Indication Expansion • Mechanism of Action (MoA) • Regulatory & IND Documentation • Cross-functional Team Leadership • Predictive Biomarker and Indication Selection • Preclinical to Early Clinical Translation","IND-Enabling Studies","Indication Expansion","Mechanism of Action (MoA)","Predictive Biomarker and Indication Selection","Preclinical to Early Clinical Translation"]},{"title":"Lab Head / Senior Principal Scientist, Genomics Lab, Immunology & Respiratory Diseases","company":"Boehringer Ingelheim · 全职","date_range":"2020年7月 - 2022年5月","duration":"1 年 11 个月","location":"美国 康乃狄克州 里奇菲尔德","description":"Directed genomics and biomarker discovery strategies across immunology programs for autoimmune & inflammatory diseases. Built and led a genomics function supporting late-stage discovery programs through innovative technologies and multi-omics integration, enabling biomarker-driven translational insights. \n• Built and scaled the Genomics Lab developing and validating pharmacodynamic and target-engagement biomarkers using preclinical and clinical samples \n• Partnered with bioinformatics to integrate preclinical and clinical datasets, developing biomarker panels to guide indication selection, patient stratification, and disease differentiation \n• Implemented single-cell RNA-seq and spatial transcriptomics platforms to identify biomarkers and generate translational insights  \n• Established scalable NGS and CRO workflows to accelerate timelines and enable high-quality data delivery","skills":["Multi-Omics Data Integration","Lab Management","Genomics Biomarker Discovery","Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS) & Single-cell RNA-seq","PK/PD Biomarkers"]},{"title":"Senior Principal Scientist | Principal Scientist, Oncology Research","company":"辉瑞","date_range":"17 年 1 个月","duration":"11 年 1 个月","location":"美国 纽约 Pearl River","description":"Directed translational biomarker and combination research for targeted and immuno-oncology programs, advancing assets from target identification through IND-enabling studies. Integrated mechanism of action, pharmacodynamic and predictive biomarkers, and resistance modeling to inform translational strategy and clinical positioning. \n• Directed predictive biomarker and combination studies for a first-in-class KAT6 inhibitor (PF-07248144, Phase 3), driving indication selection and rational combinations; enabled IND filing, Phase 1 entry, and patent application \n• Designed and conducted reverse translational research by modeling clinically relevant resistance mutations in preclinical models to elucidate mechanisms of resistance and inform clinical strategy \n• Led in vivo combination and mechanistic studies across immuno-oncology programs (immune modulators, checkpoint inhibitors and T-cell engagers) using syngeneic models and immune profiling \n• Established CRISPR/shRNA functional genomics platforms for target identification and rational combinations \n• Built and mentored a high-performing team of scientists (PhD/MS), fostering professional growth and cross-functional collaboration within discovery and with external partners","skills":["技能: IND-Enabling Studies • Multi-Omics Data Integration • Targeted Cancer Therapy and Immuno-oncology • First-in-class small molecule inhibitor • Mechanism of Action (MoA) • Rational Combinations • Synthetic Lethality Screens • Lab Management • Regulatory & IND Documentation • Predictive Biomarker and Indication Selection • Drug Resistance Biology • PK/PD Biomarkers","IND-Enabling Studies","Multi-Omics Data Integration","Targeted Cancer Therapy and Immuno-oncology","First-in-class small molecule inhibitor","Mechanism of Action (MoA)","Rational Combinations","Synthetic Lethality Screens","Lab Management","Regulatory & IND Documentation","Predictive Biomarker and Indication Selection","Drug Resistance Biology","PK/PD Biomarkers","技能: Mechanism of Action (MoA) • Functional Genomics • Lab Management • Target Identification & Validation • Cross-functional Team Leadership • PK/PD Biomarkers","Functional Genomics","Target Identification & Validation","Cross-functional Team Leadership"]},{"title":"Principal Research Scientist | Senior Research Scientist, Oncology (formerly Wyeth)","company":"辉瑞","date_range":"17 年 1 个月","duration":"11 年 1 个月","location":"美国 纽约 Pearl River","description":"Directed translational biomarker and combination research for targeted and immuno-oncology programs, advancing assets from target identification through IND-enabling studies. Integrated mechanism of action, pharmacodynamic and predictive biomarkers, and resistance modeling to inform translational strategy and clinical positioning. \n• Directed predictive biomarker and combination studies for a first-in-class KAT6 inhibitor (PF-07248144, Phase 3), driving indication selection and rational combinations; enabled IND filing, Phase 1 entry, and patent application \n• Designed and conducted reverse translational research by modeling clinically relevant resistance mutations in preclinical models to elucidate mechanisms of resistance and inform clinical strategy \n• Led in vivo combination and mechanistic studies across immuno-oncology programs (immune modulators, checkpoint inhibitors and T-cell engagers) using syngeneic models and immune profiling \n• Established CRISPR/shRNA functional genomics platforms for target identification and rational combinations \n• Built and mentored a high-performing team of scientists (PhD/MS), fostering professional growth and cross-functional collaboration within discovery and with external partners","skills":["技能: IND-Enabling Studies • Multi-Omics Data Integration • Targeted Cancer Therapy and Immuno-oncology • First-in-class small molecule inhibitor • Mechanism of Action (MoA) • Rational Combinations • Synthetic Lethality Screens • Lab Management • Regulatory & IND Documentation • Predictive Biomarker and Indication Selection • Drug Resistance Biology • PK/PD Biomarkers","IND-Enabling Studies","Multi-Omics Data Integration","Targeted Cancer Therapy and Immuno-oncology","First-in-class small molecule inhibitor","Mechanism of Action (MoA)","Rational Combinations","Synthetic Lethality Screens","Lab Management","Regulatory & IND Documentation","Predictive Biomarker and Indication Selection","Drug Resistance Biology","PK/PD Biomarkers","技能: Mechanism of Action (MoA) • Functional Genomics • Lab Management • Target Identification & Validation • Cross-functional Team Leadership • PK/PD Biomarkers","Functional Genomics","Target Identification & Validation","Cross-functional Team Leadership"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Senior Director, Translational Medicine at SpringWorks Therapeutics · 2025年 - 2026年 | Director, Translational Medicine at SpringWorks Therapeutics · 2022年 - 2024年 | Lab Head / Senior Principal Scientist, Genomics Lab, Immunology & Respiratory Diseases at Boehringer Ingelheim · 2020年 - 2022年 | Senior Principal Scientist | Principal Scientist, Oncology Research at Pfizer · 2009年 - 2020年 | Principal Research Scientist | Senior Research Scientist, Oncology (formerly Wyeth) at Pfizer · 2003年 - 2009年","education":[{"school":"美国康奈尔大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Microbiology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Joan & Sanford I. Weill Medical College of Cornell University","degree":"Postdoctoral Research Associate","field_of_study"