{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:04:04+08:00","record":{"name":"Chun Chen","current_title":"Translational Medicine Lead","current_company":"Medley Therapeutics · 全职","location":"旧金山湾区","headline":"Director, Discovery Biology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/chun-chen-04097b22","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAATFTXABzv1m_dkdWukzfkAr2gZV8mrQE0U","core_skills":["Critical Thinking","Assay Development","Scientific Research"],"positions":[{"title":"Translational Medicine Lead","company":"Medley Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2025年7月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 3 个月","location":"","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Sr. Principal Scientist → Director, Discovery Biology","company":"NGM Biopharmaceutics","date_range":"2021年 - 现在","duration":"5 年 9 个月","location":"","description":"• Led and managed a team of 8 scientists (SRAs to Principal Scientists), consistently achieving and surpassing key corporate milestones. \n• Served as the program leader for NGM's first-ever novel bispecific ADC platform (RI-ACT), guiding its development from initial concept and proof-of-concept through to the successful delivery of a preclinical candidate. \n• Strategically designed and executed preclinical plans, resulting in the successful generation of comprehensive and high-quality preclinical data packages for two distinct ADC candidates. \n• Facilitated and directed complex cross-functional collaborations encompassing biology, biologics, and preclinical research teams. \n• Additionally, effectively managed external CROs and engaged with KOLs to advance high-value programs. \n• Provided expert oversight and critical support for target validation, development of in vitro and in vivo models, hit-to-lead progression, PK/PD assessments, and toxicology support, consistently meeting critical timelines to enable timely go/no-go decisions.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director of Biology","company":"NGM Biopharmaceuticals · 全职","date_range":"202