{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:04:16+08:00","record":{"name":"Jing Chen, PhD","current_title":"Biomarker Lead, Scientist","current_company":"Roche · 全职","location":"美国 亚利桑那州 图森","headline":"Translational Scientist | Companion Diagnostics (CDx) | Biomarker & IHC Assay Development | Precision Medicine","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jing-chen-phd-a93a95a2","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABXfmM8BMul8MsMZN5rE8xoNIJ85GZyl2Qw","core_skills":["IVDR","HPLC/UPLC/MS/NMR","Schrodinger","Python"],"positions":[{"title":"Biomarker Lead, Scientist","company":"Roche · 全职","date_range":"2022年10月 - 现在","duration":"4 年","location":"United States","description":" Serve as biomarker lead for oncology CDx programs, collaborating with global pharmaceutical partners to support biomarker-driven clinical trials and diagnostic strategy. \n Lead development and validation of CDx assays (IHC, ISH, multiplex IF, proximity assays) on automated diagnostic platforms supporting clinical trial biomarker testing and regulatory submissions. \n Partner with clinical, regulatory, and diagnostic development teams to align biomarker strategy with therapeutic development timelines. \n Support assay transfer to CAP/CLIA laboratories for clinical trial testing and ensure documentation meets regulatory expectations. \n Provide technical and strategic guidance across cross-functional teams including clinical study management, business development, pathology, and alliance management. \n Mentor junior scientists and manage contractors to ensure timely execution of biomarker development milestones.","skills":["Artificial Intelligence (AI)","Multiplexing","Companion Diagnostics (CDx)","IVDR","Communication","Pathology","Digital Image Processing","Project Management","Immunofluorescence/IHC","Cross-team Collaboration"]},{"title":"Research Scientist","company":"University of Arizona · 全职","date_range":"2021年3月 - 2022年10月","duration":"1 年 8 个月","location":"Tucson, Arizona, United States","description":"Leading the drug discovery program for therapeutic intervention in the area of cancer, ageing, and related diseases. Developing novel imaging and targeting techniques for precision medicine, including chemical-induced proximity, protein-protein interaction, and drug delivery.","skills":["Medicinal Chemistry","Drug Design","Data Analysis","Teaching","Presentation Skills","Problem Solving","Cell Biology","IVIS/Pearl Imaging","Optical, Photoacoustic"]},{"title":"Research Fellow","company":"University of Michigan · 全职","date_range":"2016年4月 - 2021年3月","duration":"5 年","location":"Ann Arbor","description":"Led the R&D by developing novel methodologies for early detection, staging, and image-guided surgery of cancer in the digestive tract. Invented heterobivalent peptide agents (1 patent) for detection of cancer biomarker in human patients, published 3 clinical research articles. Coordinated a team preparing IND application, led to approval for 3 clinical trials. Completed 3 clinical trials on > 150 patients.","skills":["Medicinal Chemistry","Drug Design","Data Analysis","Teaching","Presentation Skills","Problem Solving","Cell Biology","IVIS/Pearl Imaging","Optical, Photoacoustic","Medical device","Xenograft animal","Organoid culture"]},{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"WuXi AppTec · 全职","date_range":"2015年6月 - 2016年4月","duration":"11 个月","location":"Shanghai City, China","description":"Dedicated project manager, led the cross-functional teams for chemical process development, \noptimizing, and qualifying processes to produce active pharmaceutical ingredients (APIs) under current \ncGMP regulations, safety standards, and development technologies.","skills":["Medicinal Chemistry","Drug Design","Data Analysis","Teaching","Presentation Skills","Problem Solving"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Biomarker Lead, Scientist at Roche · 2022年 - 现在 | Research Scientist at University of Arizona · 2021年 - 2022年 | Res