{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:04:41+08:00","record":{"name":"Song Chen","current_title":"Principal Scientist Oncology","current_company":"Quarry Thera · 全职","location":"美国 康乃狄克州 纽黑文","headline":"Principle Scientist at Quarry Thera | Oncology | Tumor Immunology | In Vivo Pharmacology | Biomarker","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/song-chen-7907aa158","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACXZRdwB4yUs4cX8zF446Kun05xYxymgOs8","core_skills":["T cell differentiation","T cell ex vivo activation","Target Discovery"],"positions":[{"title":"Principal Scientist Oncology","company":"Quarry Thera · 全职","date_range":"2026年3月 - 现在","duration":"7 个月","location":"美国 康乃狄克州 纽黑文","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"Volastra Therapeutics","date_range":"4 年 2 个月","duration":"3 个月","location":"纽约地区","description":"1.  Spearheaded the predictive biomarker discovery for company’s KIF18A program, which included selecting a list of biomarker candidates, screening candidates in a panel of ovarian cancer cell lines, developed correlations between biomarker level and cell sensitivity to KIF18A inhibition. \n2.  The biomarker screening effort led to the discovery of MAD1 and p16INK4a as the potential biomarkers, validated their functional effect using genetic manipulation, and led further IHC assay development in patient samples.  \n3.   Led the evaluation of combination effect of KIF18A inhibitors and standard-of-care (SOC) agents in vitro and in vivo, served as first author of 2026 AACR poster. \n4.   Coordinated and managed CROs for assay development and in vivo animal experiments.  \n5.   Served as the PI of company's animal protocol and managing company's internal animal facility at CUNY.","skills":["技能: Project Management • Target Discovery • Target Validation • Cross-team Collaboration • Project Planning • Design of Experiments (DOE)","Project Management","Target Discovery","Target Validation","Cross-team Collaboration","Project Planning","Design of Experiments (DOE)"]},{"title":"Tumor Immunology Scientist II","company":"Volastra Therapeutics","date_range":"4 年 2 个月","duration":"3 个月","location":"纽约地区","description":"1.  Spearheaded the predictive biomarker discovery for company’s KIF18A program, which included selecting a list of biomarker candidates, screening candidates in a panel of ovarian cancer cell lines, developed correlations between biomarker level and cell sensitivity to KIF18A inhibition. \n2.  The biomarker screening effort led to the discovery of MAD1 and p16INK4a as the potential biomarkers, validated their functional effect using genetic manipulation, and led further IHC assay development in patient samples.  \n3.   Led the evaluation of combination effect of KIF18A inhibitors and standard-of-care (SOC) agents in vitro and in vivo, served as first author of 2026 AACR poster. \n4.   Coordinated and managed CROs for assay development and in vivo animal experiments.  \n5.   Served as the PI of company's animal protocol and managing company's internal animal facility at CUNY.","skills":["技能: Project Management • Target Discovery • Target Validation • Cross-team Collaboration • Project Planning • Design of Experiments (DOE)","Project Management","Target Discovery","Target Validation","Cross-team Collaboration","Project Planning","Design of Experiments (DOE)"]},{"title":"Tumor Immunology Scientist I","company":"Volastra Therapeutics","date_range":"4 年 2 个月","duration":"3 个月","location":"纽约地区","description":"1.  Spearheaded the predictive biomarker discovery for company’s KIF18A program, which included selecting a list of biomarker candidates, screening candidates in a panel of ovarian cancer cell lines, developed correlations between biomarker level and cell sensitivity to KIF18A inhibition. \n2.  The biomarker screening effort led to the discovery of MAD1 and p16INK4a as the potential biomarkers, validated their functional effect using genetic manipulation, and led further IHC assay development in patient samples.  \n3.   Led the evaluation of combination effect of KIF18A inhibitors and standard-of-care (SOC) agents in vitro and in vivo, served as first author of 2026 AACR poster. \n4.   Coordinated and managed CROs for assay development and in vivo animal experiments.  \n5.   Served as the PI of company's animal protocol and managing company's internal animal facility at CUNY.","skills":["技能: Project Management • Target Discovery • Target Validation • Cross-team Collaboration • Project Planning • Design of Experiments (DOE)","Project Management","Target Discovery","Target Validation","Cross-team Collaboration","Project Planning","Design of Experiments (DOE)"]},{"title":"Research Fellow","company":"Massachusetts General Hospital · 全职","date_range":"2021年2月 - 2022年2月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"The major responsibility was to independently formulate hypotheses and execute experiments to understand the role of chemokines and their receptors in T cell trafficking and function in the tumor microenvironment during immune checkpoint blockade therapy. Specifically, \n• Led a project to understand the development of CCR8 expressing regulatory T cells (Tregs), a highly immunosuppressive cell type present in many cancers, and their functional contribution on tumor resistance to immune checkpoint blockade therapy. Demonstrated that specific CCR8 deletion in Treg cells improved tumor control and host responsiveness to anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 combination therapy. \n• Initiated a project to determine the role of the CXCR3 chemokine system in CD8+ T cell heterogeneity and function during anti-PD-1 immunotherapy.","skills":["Hypothesis Testing","In vivo pharmacology","Cancer Immunotherapy","T cell differentiation","T cell ex vivo activation","Murine tumor model","Design of Experiments (DOE)","Flow Cytometry","Data Analysis"]},{"title":"Consultant","company":"miLEAD Consulting · 兼职","date_range":"2019年8月 - 2020年12月","duration":"1 年 5 个月","location":"Ann Arbor","description":"","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Principal Scientist Oncology at Quarry Thera · 2026年 - 现在 | Senior Scientist at Volastra Therapeutics · 2026年 - 2026年 | Tumor Immunology Scientist II at Volastra Therapeutics · 2024年 - 2026年 | Tumor Immunology Scientist I at Volastra Therapeutics · 2022年 - 2023年 | Research Fellow at Massachusetts General Hospital · 2021年 - 2022年 | Consultant at miLEAD Consulting · 2019年 - 2020年 | Teaching Assistant at University of Michigan · 2019年 - 2019年 | Graduate Research Fellow at University of Michigan · 2017年 - 2020年 | Predoctoral fellow at National Cancer Institute (NCI) · 2015年 - 2017年 | Teaching Assistant at University of Maryland · 2014年 - 2015年 | Graduate Student at University of Maryland · 2014年 - 2017年 | Graduate Student Researcher at Fudan University · 2011年 - 2014年","education":[{"school":"密西根大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Pharmacology","date_range":"2017年 - 2020年","activities":"","grade":"3.92/4.00"},{"school":"美国马里兰大学帕克分校","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Biophysics","date_range":"2014年 - 2017年","activities":"","grade":"3.95/4.00"},{"school":"复旦大学","degree":"Master of Science - MS","field_of_study":"Condensed Matter Physics","date_range":"2011年 - 2014年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 密西根大学，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2017年 - 2020年 | 美国马里兰大学帕克分校，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2014年 - 2017年 | 复旦大学，Master of Science - MS · 2011年 - 2014年 | 华东理工大学，Bachelor of Engineering - BE · 2007年 - 2011年 | 档案分析行 | 最新动态 | 1 个项目 | 2 次浏览 | 1 个备注 | 保存到项目 | 将Song保存到项目 | 发消息给Song | Song Chen的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"中高级 (商务会话)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:04:52+08:00","record":{"name":"Yan Chen","current_title":"Principle Scientist","current_company":"Novartis","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 列克星敦","headline":"Scientist | Translational Oncology & Immunology | Drug Discovery & Combination Therapies | Biomarker Development | Novartis","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/yan-chen20262027","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAGWSClgBmVkyJlvYKWag1TwRgmtzYmjj9TI","core_skills":["Target/drug discoveries and validations","Immunology & Flow Cytometry: Multicolor flow","FACS sorting","RTCC","TBNK assay","PBMC and T-cell prep","Primary","cell line and ex-vivo culture","proliferation/apoptosis assays","drug and combination screen"],"positions":[{"title":"Principle Scientist","company":"Novartis","date_range":"2003年12月 - 2026年2月","duration":"22 年 3 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"Combination Therapy and Resistance Mechanism in multiple projects: \n \nCDK4/6, PI3Kpan/PI3KCA, mTOR, ER, MDM2/p53/BH3 memetics & RTK \n• Established an estrogen receptor inhibitor (ERi) culture system; Identified synergistic effects between CD4/6, PI3KCA, and mTOR inhibitors with ERi; Authored US patent on CDK4/6 and ER therapeutic strategies, and contributed to development of FDA-approved therapies \n• Conducted MOA and efficacy studies of BH3 memetics in multiple cancer models; Generated and characterized acquired resistance AML models; Identified the strategies overcoming resistance; Developed and validated PD biomarker assays, supporting early clinical development of S64315 and Venetoclax \n• Led semi-high-throughput compound matrix and secretomic screening efforts. Identified novel resistance and sensitization mechanisms, supporting multiple peer reviewed publications and a US patent  \n \nImmuno-Oncology \n \n• Led the design, optimization, and execution of multicolor flow cytometry assays. Profiled cell surface antigens for various ex vivo models; Isolated specific sub-populations via FACS sorting from single PDX models; Quantified tumor cell killing and assessed T-cell activation using RTCC flow panels; Monitored TBNK depletion by ADCs through TBNK flow panel  \n• Developed an AML PDX derived ex vivo culture platform and characterized models using flow panels & functional assays; Accelerated in vivo model selections and enabled the integration of in vivo and in vitro studies \n \nTarget Discovery by RNAi and CRISPR \n \n• Pioneered a shRNA KD system; Established and optimized semi-high-throughput RNA extraction and RT-qPCR workflows  \n• Built the department's first end-to-end pooled shRNA screening workflow. Executed screens for synthetic lethality, rescue, and sensitization studies; It served as the foundation for the scalable platform broadly used for target discovery \n• Utilized siRNA as a complementary tool \n• Engineered and validate Cas9 cell lines and performed CRISPR screens","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Principle Scientist at Novartis · 2003年 - 2026年","education":[{"school":"美国俄克拉荷马州立大学","degree":"M.S.","field_of_study":"Microbiology & Molecular Genetics","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine","degree":"Doctor of Medicine","field_of_study":"Medicine","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 美国俄克拉荷马州立大学，M.S. | Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine，Doctor of Medicine | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Scientist Senior Scientist Principal Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥 美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:05:03+08:00","record":{"name":"Xinyuan Chen","current_title":"Postdoctoral Fellow","current_company":"GSK · 全职","location":"美国 宾夕法尼亚州 Collegeville","headline":"RNA Biologist | ASO Therapeutics | Target Identification & Validation | Neurodegeneration, Hepatology, Oncology | Ph.D., UCLA","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/xinyuan-chen-1565688b","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABMgSNIB3iB4gYxbvSgJvMxqLmdBiG4Sd1E","core_skills":["ASO","CRISPRi","Transfection"],"positions":[{"title":"Postdoctoral Fellow","company":"GSK · 全职","date_range":"2023年7月 - 现在","duration":"3 年 3 个月","location":"美国 宾夕法尼亚州 Collegeville","description":"·       Led experimental design as Biology Lead on a hepatology target ID program: built 2D and 3D in vitro model systems, established QC procedures, and drove data-based target triage decisions. \n·       Generated a foundational patient RNA-seq dataset now used organization-wide for target discovery, ASO tractability analysis, and AI/ML modeling. \n·       Curated and interpreted genetics, genomics, biology, and patent evidence using AI/ML tools to support target triage decisions. \n·       Designed and built a novel minigene splicing reporter system to enable in vivo target engagement studies for a neurodegenerative disease program, in partnership with external experts and AI/ML-assisted experimental design. \n·       Built the target validation plan and in vitro assay/tool molecule validation strategy for a neurodegenerative disease target; presented to internal stakeholders for program endorsement. \n·       Collaborated within a cross-functional matrix team of internal and external biotech partners on ASO therapeutics. Recognized for creative thinking in addition to providing constructive feedback on experimental design, execution, and project strategy.","skills":[]},{"title":"Graduate Student Researcher","company":"University of California, Los Angeles · 