{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:05:14+08:00","record":{"name":"Huan Chen","current_title":"Lab Head, Principal Scientist II, Immuno Oncology","current_company":"诺华","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","headline":"Immuno-Oncology PTL | T/Myeloid Engagers & Translational Immunology | Target Discovery & Immune Repertoire (NGS) | IND Enabling","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/huan-chen-b07755141","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACJ14PcB6-yGxecmXLM_lbvn_gYN2lQShyU","core_skills":["Multi-specific antibodies","IND enabling","translatioal immunology"],"positions":[{"title":"Lab Head, Principal Scientist II, Immuno Oncology","company":"诺华","date_range":"6 年 3 个月","duration":"4 年 1 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"• Lead discovery strategy and cross‑functional execution for two immune cell engager programs (T-cell, myeloid ) targeting solid tumors, incorporating multi-specific antibody platforms and logic-gating concepts to address tumor heterogeneity and improve therapeutic index. \n• Led development of an NK/T-cell modulating biologic from late discovery through IND-enabling studies and first-in-human clinical trial initiation. \n• Developed a reverse translational target ID platform leveraging patient auto-antibody repertoire profiling and TScan collaboration to identify tumor- or immune- centric targets and inform combination strategy with checkpoint inhibitors and CAR-T. \n• Designed mechanistic studies to evaluate immune activation, antigen recognition, and tumor–immune interactions in vitro and in vivo. \n• Evaluated conditional activated multi-specific biologic approaches through exploratory and BD efforts. \n• Contributed to early exploration of mRNA cancer vaccine strategies within immuno-oncology programs, integrating tumor antigen biology and immune response considerations. \n• Line manager and mentor for direct reports; led matrix teams of 20+ scientists across discovery and preclinical development","s