{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:05:40+08:00","record":{"name":"Hongyuan Chen, Ph.D","current_title":"Senior Scientist II","current_company":"Cidara Therapeutics · 全职","location":"San Diego Metropolitan Area","headline":"Senior Scientist | Drug Discovery | Medicinal Chemistry | Bioconjugation | Small Molecules, Peptides & Macrocycles | Open to Opportunities","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hongyuanchen","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAdtOfYBbM8nPfeEZLVvlPR1q3FQ0RoggYA","core_skills":["protease inhibitor","TLC","Protein Conjugation"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Scientist II","company":"Cidara Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2023年7月 - 现在","duration":"3 年 3 个月","location":"","description":"Development of novel small molecules and drug-Fc antibody conjugates (DFc) for oncology and antiviral therapeutics \n \n• Designed and executed complex multistep syntheses of small-molecule therapeutics targeting CD73, CCR4, CCR5, HIV, and RSV. \n• Developed and optimized core and scaffold chemistry supporting hit-to-lead and lead-optimization campaigns. \n• Implemented parallel synthesis workflows (core/scaffold/96-well), enabling rapid library generation and hit discovery across multiple programs. \n• Integrated biological activity, DMPK, pharmacology, and analytical data with chemistry strategy to guide compound prioritization and candidate progression. \n• Translated potent small-molecule inhibitors into targeted Drug–Fc conjugates through rational linker design and bioconjugation strategies. \n• Optimized linker chemistry, conjugation sites, DAR, and molecular physicochemical properties to improve efficacy and PK. \n• Designed and prepared fluorescently labeled compounds and conjugates, including BODIPY- and Fluor 488-type probes, to support biodistribution and tumor-penetration studies. \n• Played a key role in the discovery of CBO421, a first-in-class Drug-Fc conjugate that demonstrated exceptional tumor growth inhibition and minimal toxicity in preclinical mouse models. \n• Led process development of CBO421, scaling production to over 10 grams to support in vivo efficacy and rat tolerability studies","skills":["Parallel Synthesis","Protein Conjugation","Drug Development","Organic Synthesis","Medicinal Chemistry","Small Molecules","Biotechnology"]},{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"Cidara Therapeutics","date_range":"2020年1月 - 2022年12月","duration":"3 年","location":"","description":"Development of drug-Fc conjugates (DFCs) targeting oncologic and viral diseases","skills":["Parallel Synthesis","Drug Development","Organic Synthesis","Medicinal Chemistry","Small Molecules","Biotechnology"]},{"title":"Scientist","company":"BroadPharm","date_range":"2015年10月 - 2019年12月","duration":"4 年 3 个月","location":"San Diego","description":"• Developed multifunctional crosslinkers, click chemistry reagents, and fluorescent probes for drug conjugation applications, including ADCs, enzyme conjugates, oligonucleotide conjugates, therapeutic delivery, diagnostics, and imaging. \n• Developed a diverse linker toolkit, including cleavable peptide linkers, disulfide linkers, hydrazone linkers, lysine- and cysteine-reactive handles, and branched PEG linkers for ADCs and multivalent bioconjugation. \n• Designed and prepared conjugation-ready cyanine, fluorescein, and rhodamine-based fluorescent dyes for labeling and bioconjugation applications. \n• Coordinated with external patent attorneys to draft and file a patent application, securing competitive advantages. \n• Successfully managed custom synthesis projects, consistently delivering high-quality, client-focused solutions ahead of schedule.","skills":["Organic Synthesis","Medicinal Chemistry","Small Molecules","Biotechnology"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Fellow","company":"UC Irvine","date_range":"2012年2月 - 2015年8月","duration":"3 年 7 个月","location":"","description":"• Designed and executed multi-step syntheses of small molecule RAD51 inhibitors targeting homologous recombination. \n• Identified key SAR and conformational drivers (ring contraction, dihedral angle optimization), achieving >4× potency gains. \n• Delivered IBR120 as a lead candidate with 4.8× potency improvement and ~10× therapeutic window over normal cells, demonstrating broad-spectrum anticancer activity. \n• Developed a highly stereoselective synthesis of the lead RAD51 inhibitor, IBR120, achieving exceptional enantiomeric control. \n• Established chiral resolution methods to improve purity and enantiomeric excess, improving IBR120 potency against breast cancer cells. \n• Developed peptide and macrocyclic RAD51 inhibitors targeting the BRCA2 BRC-motif, enhancing RAD51 binding affinity.","skills":["Drug Development","Organic Synthesis","Medicinal Chemistry","Small Molecules","Biotechnology","Peptidomimetics"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Senior Scientist II at Cidara Therapeutics · 2023年 - 现在 | Senior Scientist at Cidara Therapeutics · 2020年 - 2022年 | Scientist at BroadPharm · 2015年 - 2019年 | Postdoctoral Fellow at UC Irvine · 2012年 - 2015年 | Graduate Researcher at University of Canterbury · 2007年 - 2011年","education":[{"school":"美国加州大学尔湾分校","degree":"Postdoctoral Fellow","field_of_study":"Biochemistry","date_range":"2012年 - 2015年","activities":"活动与社团: \"Synthesis, molecular modeling, and biological evaluation of novel RAD51 inhibitors\"","grade":""},{"school":"新西兰坎特伯雷大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Chemistry","date_range":"2007年 - 2011年","activities":"活动与社团: Development of macrocyclic β-strand peptides as calpain cysteine protease inhibitors PhD Advisors: Professor Andrew Abell and Professor Jim Coxon","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 美国加州大学尔湾分校，Postdoctoral Fellow · 2012年 - 2015年 | 新西兰坎特伯雷大学，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 2007年 - 2011年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Senior Scientist Principal Scientist Scientist 职位性质 合同制 兼职 全职 所在地点 现场办公: San Diego Metropolitan Area 美国 加利福尼亚 奥朗热 旧金山湾