{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:06:05+08:00","record":{"name":"Yi-Fan Chen, MS, DVM, PhD., DABT","current_title":"Senior Scientist/Study Director","current_company":"Pharmaron · 全职","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 维斯塔","headline":"Toxicologist & Veterinary Scientist | Preclinical Study Director | Toxicology | Immunology | Cardiovascular Research | Cancer Research","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/yfchen86","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABXirUwB2uQfOTqugAep3P9z9P6lyONgw1s","core_skills":["Mitochondrial research","Cardiovascular Toxicology","Respirometry"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Scientist/Study Director","company":"Pharmaron · 全职","date_range":"2025年7月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 3 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 卡尔斯巴德","description":"• Lead the design, execution, and reporting of exploratory, non-GLP, and GLP-compliant in vivo studies, ensuring adherence to study protocols and regulatory standards. \n• Collaborate with clients to design and implement preclinical studies involving medical device technologies, providing scientific guidance tailored to device-specific requirements. \n• Support surgical studies by performing or assisting with pre-operative preparations (e.g., catheterization, intubation), intra-operative anesthesia and physiological monitoring, and post-operative care, including imaging modalities such as ICE and C-arm. \n• Serve as a liaison between internal teams, clients, and vendors to coordinate and communicate study-related activities and project milestones. \n• Conduct necropsies and contribute to pathological evaluations across various study types. \n• Author and revise standard operating procedures (SOPs) to align with institutional policies and regulatory standards, enhancing operational compliance and quality. \n• Provide regulatory and technical support for Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC) activities, including protocol development, programmatic review, and facility inspections. \n• Ensure facility compliance with animal welfare regulations and standards (e.g., USDA, FDA, ISO, AAALAC) through continuous quality assurance and training. \n• Assist the Attending Veterinarian with clinical case management and routine health monitoring of research animals. \n• Actively engage with clients to understand project goals, offer scientific consultation, and deliver customized, value-driven preclinical solutions. \n• Oversee scientific planning, execution, and coordination of cross-functional projects within the Service Line to ensure on-time and on-budget delivery.","skills":["Good Laboratory Practice (GLP)","Medical Devices"]},{"title":"Study Director/Senior Scientist","company":"Pharmaron-San Diego","date_range":"2025年7月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 3 个月","location":"","description":"• Lead the design, execution, and reporting of exploratory, non-GLP, and GLP-compliant in vivo studies, ensuring adherence to study protocols and regulatory standards. \n• Collaborate with sponsors to design and implement preclinical studies involving medical device technologies, providing scientific guidance tailored to device-specific requirements. \n• Support surgical studies by performing or assisting with pre-operative preparations (e. \n• g. \n• , catheterization, intubation), intra-operative anesthesia and physiological monitoring, and post-operative care, including imaging modalities such as ICE, TTE, TEE, and C-arm. \n• Serve as a liaison between internal teams, clients, and vendors to coordinate and communicate study-related activities and project milestones. \n• Conduct necropsies and contribute to pathological evaluations across various study types. \n• Author and revise standard operating procedures (SOPs) to align with institutional policies and regulatory standards, enhancing operational compliance and quality. \n• Provide regulatory and technical support for Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC) activities, including protocol development, programmatic review, and facility inspections. \n• Ensure facility compliance with animal welfare regulations and standards (e. \n• g. \n• , USDA, FDA, ISO, AAALAC) through continuous quality assurance and training. \n• Assist the Attending Veterinarian with clinical case management and routine health monitoring of research animals. \n• Actively engage with clients to understand project goals, offer scientific consultation, and deliver customized, value-driven preclinical solutions. \n• Oversee scientific planning, execution, and coordination of cross-functional projects within the Service Line to ensure on-time and on-budget delivery.","skills":[]},{"title":"NIH IRTA Fellow","company":"National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences (NIEHS) · 全职","date_range":"2024年1月 - 2025年6月","duration":"1 年 6 个月","location":"美国 北卡罗来纳州 达勒姆","description":"● Investigate the effects of chronic anti-HIV therapeutics on tissue resident macrophages that addresses significant public health challenges in long-term use and prophylactic use of combination antiretroviral therapy (cART). \n● Isolate cardiac tissue resident macrophages using multicolor panel flow cytometry. \n● Examine the immune phenotypes of primary and/or immortalized cardiac tissue resident macrophages. \n● Mentor undergraduate scholar and assist peer-fellows with their projects.\n\n• Lead research on immune-mediated cardiotoxicity from prenatal antiretroviral exposure, with emphasis on identifying translational biomarkers and mechanistic pathways. \n• Oversee spatial tissue imaging, immune profiling, and cell-line model development to support human-relevant hazard evaluation. \n• Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams to align experimental models with regulatory and translational endpoints. \n• Mentor junior researchers and provide technical oversight of laboratory operations and instrumentation.","skills":["Primary Cell Isolation","Project Management","Mentoring","RNAseq","Flow Cytometry"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Associate","company":"Texas A&M University System Health Science Center -College of Medicine · 全职","date_range":"2020年9月 - 2023年8月","duration":"3 年","location":"美国 德州 Bryan–College Station","description":"Project: Type I Interferon Responses in the Pathobiology of Anthracycline-induced Cardiotoxicity.  \n● Delineated mitochondria's role in cardiac innate immunity in responds to doxorubicin-induced cardiotoxicity. \n● Bred and establish mouse colonies that has tissue-specific gene-of-interest knockout.  \n● Optimized cardiac perfusion and cardiac cell isolation protocols to acquire cardiac isolates for examining different cardiac cell populations using flow cytometry.  \n● Mastered echocardiogram in doxorubicin-challenged mice to monitor cardiac function. \n● Collaborated with laboratory members and co-authored on one high-impact publication.\n\n• Conducted in vivo toxicology studies to elucidate mitochondrial signaling in anthracycline-induced cardiotoxicity. \n• Applied mouse models, cardiac functional imaging, and immune-cell phenotyping to characterize toxicological mechanisms. \n• Supported research strategy and grant development through collaborative study design and manuscript contributions.","skills":["Analytical Skills","Life Sciences","Laboratory Skills","Microsoft Excel","Panel Design","In Vitro","Cytometry","Pharmacology","GraphPad Prism","Mouse","GraphPad","Ex Vivo","Animal Models","Mitochondrial research","Cardiovascular Toxicology","Science","In Vivo","Toxicology"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Senior Scientist/Study Director at Pharmaron · 2025年 - 现在 | Study Director/Senior Scientist at Pharmaron-San Diego · 2025年 - 现在 | NIH IRTA Fellow at National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences (NIEHS) · 2024年 - 2025年 | Postdoctoral Research Associate at Texas A&M University System Health Science Center -College of Medicine · 2020年 - 2023年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow at Oak Ridge Institute for Science and Education · 2019年 - 2020年 | Research Assistant at School of Veterinary Medicine, Louisiana State University · 2014年 - 2019年 | Graduate Assistant at Louisiana State University School of Veterinary Medicine · 2014年 - 2019年 | Research Associate at Academia Sinica, Taiwan · 2013年 - 2014年 | Research Associate at Division of Celluar and System Medicine, National Health Research Institutes · 2010年 - 2012年","education":[{"school":"Louisiana State University School of Veterinary Medicine","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Comparative Biomedical Sciences; Toxicology","date_range":"2014年 - 2019年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"阳明大学","degree":"Master's Degree","field_of_study":"Biopharmaceutical Science","date_range":"2009年 - 2013年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"中兴大学","degree":"D.V.M.","field_of_study":"Veterinary Medicine","date_range":"2004年 - 2009年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Louisiana State University School of Veterinary Medicine，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2014年 - 2019年 | 阳明大学，Master's Degree · 2009年 - 2013年 | 中兴大学，D.V.M. · 2004年 - 2009年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["所在地点 现场办公: 美国 加利福尼亚 维斯塔 美国 德州 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":true,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:06:18+08:00","record":{"name":"Chaojia Chen","current_title":"Postdoctoral Associate","current_company":"The Jackson Laboratory · 全职","location":"美国","headline":"Postdoctoral Associate @ The Jackson Laboratory | PhD in Immunology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/chaojia-chen-97bbb927b","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAERX8S8B6uqtqtYO6GBtTJ6CMiq4A96vSS4","core_skills":["Multiplex Imaging analysis","in vivo mouse model","Fibroblast culture"],"positions":[{"title":"Postdoctoral Associate","company":"The Jackson Laboratory · 全职","date_range":"2023年1月 - 现在","duration":"3 年 9 个月","location":"美国","description":"• Led independent project demonstrating that senescent lung microenvironments harbor increased immunosuppressive B-cell populations, using single-cell profiling and flow cytometry-based functional validation to identify a CXCL13⁺ fibroblast subset driving this fibroblast–B-cell immunosuppressive axis; \n• Led independent project integrating single-cell RNA sequencing, multiplex imaging, and an in vivo knockdown model to uncover a chemotherapy-induced tissue damage signaling axis that drives expansion of a CXCR4⁺ pericyte-like population and promotes breast cancer lung metastasis; \n• Designed and executed preclinical mouse models of breast cancer and osteosarcoma metastasis, coordinating with core facilities (scRNA-seq, pathology, imaging) on sample processing and experimental design, while independently leading downstream computational analysis; \n• Contributed to grant writing and presented research findings at scientific conferences;  \n• Mentored and supervised both graduate and undergraduate students, supporting their scientific development and project execution.","skills":["Multiplex Imaging analysis","in vivo mouse model","Fibroblast culture","Multi-color Flow Cytometry","Viral Transduction","Stem Cells","Cell Biology","Tumor Immunology","Research Projects","Biotechnology","Biology","Live imaging","Microscopy","Cell Culture","Flow Cytometry","R (Programming Language)","scRNA-seq analysis","Intra-cardiac injection"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Postdoctoral Associate at The Jackson Laboratory · 2023年 - 现在","education":[{"school":"山东大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Immunology","date_range":"2017年 - 2022年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 山东大学，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2017年 - 2022年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Scientist Senior Scientist Staff Scientist Associate Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":true,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:06:29+08:00","record":{"name":"Yuhong Chen","current_title":"Consultant","current_company":"Self-Employed · 自由职业","location":"美国 马里兰州 洛克维","headline":"Clinical Pharmacology & Pharmacometrics, Early Clinical Development, Bioanalysis, DMPK, Regulatory Affair and Business Development","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/yuhong-chen-15aa1b59","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAxuZBYBLTBV1tJCSH408lrXDsEoMD7LJKQ","core_skills":["Drug Development from FIH to Marketing","Exposure and Response Analysis","Early Drug Development"],"positions":[{"title":"Consultant","company":"Self-Employed · 自由职业","date_range":"2024年3月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 7 个月","location":"","description":"Clinical Pharmacology & Pharmacometrics, Early Clinical Development, Bioanalysis, DMPK, Regulatory Affair and Business Development","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Director, Clinical Pharmacology","company":"FibroGen","date_range":"2024年6月 - 2025年4月","duration":"11 个月","location":"","description":"• Lead submission efforts on the ClinPharm section and interactions with FDA for phase 2 dose optimization study, including PIND briefing book, PIND meeting with FDA, IND submission package for phase 2 study and question responses. \n• Lead dose selection for phase 2 dose optimization study and work with CRO on PPK/ER analysis to support dose selection. \n• Lead submission efforts on the ClinPharm section and interactions with FDA DIRM for phase 1 study for Immune PET agent, including PIND briefing book, IND submission package for phase 1 study and question responses. \n• Lead due diligent activity for evaluating radiopharmaceutical targeting CD46 for prostate cancer treatment. \n• Monitor CROs for clinical sample testing for ADC PK and ADA. \n• Collaborative review and approval of clinical documents including IB, protocol, CSR, health authority briefing documents and regulatory responses.","skills":[]},{"title":"Executive Director, Clinical Pharmacology","company":"TopAlliance Biosciences · 全职","date_range":"2022年11月 - 2024年2月","duration":"1 年 4 个月","location":"","description":"• Lead submission efforts on the ClinPharm section and interactions with world health authorities, including BLA, MAA, EOP2 and IND submissions for phase 3 studies. \n• Oversee pipeline programs in clinical development and life cycle management. \n• Collaborative review and approval of clinical documents including IB, protocol, CSR, marketing application sections, health authority briefing documents and regulatory responses. \n• Plan and execute clinical pharmacology strategy from FIH to LCM.","skills":[]},{"title":"Executive Director, Head of Clinical Pharmacology","company":"Elpiscience Biopharmaceuticals, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2021年5月 - 2022年10月","duration":"1 年 6 个月","location":"美国 马里兰州 洛克维","description":"• Build and manage Clinical Pharmacology team. \n• Plan and execute clinical pharmacology strategy from FIH to LCM. \n• Oversee pipeline programs in clinical development. \n• Supervise ClinPharm and PMx activities. \n• Lead FIH Pre-IND and IND submission efforts on the ClinPharm section and interactions with FDA. \n• Collaborative review and approval of clinical documents including IB, CSR, health authority briefing documents and regulatory responses. \n• Participate in or lead Department- or Company-level initiatives or cross-functional Advisory Teams. \n• Support evaluation of candidates for in/out-licensing.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Consultant at Self-Employed · 2024年 - 现在 | Senior Director, Clinical Pharmacology at FibroGen · 2024年 - 2025年 | Executive Director, Clinical Pharmacology at TopAlliance Biosciences · 2022年 - 2024年 | Executive Director, Head of Clinical Pharmacology at Elpiscience Biopharmaceuticals, Inc. · 2021年 - 2022年 | Executive Director, Head of Clinical Pharmacology at Haihe Biopharma · 2020年 - 2021年 | Senior Director, Head of Clinical Pharmacology at Haihe Biopharma · 2020年 - 2020年 | Principal Clinical Pharmacokineticist at MedImmune · 2017年 - 2020年 | Clinical Pharmacology Reviewer (Oncology) at FDA · 2015年 - 2017年 | PK Expert at Bayer HealthCare · 2013年 - 2015年 | Associate Director, Clinical Research Physician at Merck · 2012年 - 2013年 | Research Investigator at Bristol-Myers Squibb · 2010年 - 2012年","education":[{"school":"中国医科大学","degree":"Doctor of Medicine (M.D.)","field_of_study":"Medicine","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"The City University of New York","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Biology/Biological Sciences, General","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 中国医科大学，Doctor of Medicine (M.D.) | The City University of New York，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Senior Director Vice President Consultant 职位性质 全职 合同制 兼职 所在地点 远程办公: 美国 马里兰州 洛克维 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 远程办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English, Japanese and Chinese","proficiency":""}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:06:40+08:00","record":{"name":"Chien-Sin Chen","current_title":"Postdoctoral Scientist","current_company":"University of Pittsburgh · 全职","location":"PhD Immunologist | Target Discovery & Validation","headline":"PhD Immunologist | Target Discovery & Validation · In Vivo Pharmacology · Translational Immunology | Autoimmune & Inflammatory Disease | Scientist / Senior Scientist","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/chien-sin-chen-36a70a6a","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAA6y-YIBs5BjmvlX2O3JpbhvxawsXzYFE8I","core_skills":["Immune cell tracking","lab animal neurosurgery","Lymph cannulation"],"positions":[{"title":"Postdoctoral Scientist","company":"University of Pittsburgh · 全职","date_range":"2021年2月 - 现在","duration":"5 年 8 个月","location":"美国 宾夕法尼亚州 匹兹堡","description":"In vivo and in vitro skin neuro-immunology in autoimmunity, infection and allergy \n \n[Science and Skills] \n• Led in vitro/in vivo skin inflammation and autoimmunity studies, resulting in 2 co-authored papers (Science, Science Transl Med) and 1 first-authored manuscript (revision). \n• Explored disease mechanism of action with genetic and pharmacologic approaches in mouse disease models to provide preclinical insights. \n• Developed and optimized primary immune cell-based assays (mast cells, DCs) using multicolor flow cytometry, ICS, cytokine bead array (LEGENDplex), and ELISA to characterize immune mechanisms and compound efficacy. \n• Performed multi-organ whole-mount and conventional fluorescence imaging of neurons and immune cells to map neuroimmune interactions at the tissue level \n• Identified biomarkers using RNAseq and qPCR and developed assays to track disease progression and molecular kinetics.  \n• Established and optimized protocols and assays to enhance data accuracy and streamline resource utilization. \n \n[Documentation, Collaboration and Recognition] \n• Established a 3,000+ sample bulk RNA library as a lasting translational resource for biomarker discovery. \n• Cross-functionally collaborated to build a spatial transcriptomics analysis pipeline, ready for clinical sample integration.  \n• Mentored 4 trainees in experimental design and data interpretation. \n• Awarded NIH Ruth L. Kirschstein NRSA T32 Fellowship ($120,000) in Autoimmunity. \n• Awarded 2 travel awards to international conferences (FASEB Autoimmunity, Keystone Skin-Immune Crosstalk). \n \nKeywords: \nImmunology · Flow Cytometry · Spectral Cytometry · ICS · Primary Cell Culture · Mast Cell Biology · Neuroimmunology · Skin Immunology · Biomarker Development · RNA-seq · Spatial Transcriptomics · In Vivo Pharmacology · Target Validation · Translational Research\n\n• ​ Developed cell-based functional assays to profile DC activation and mast cell responses in primary mouse cells. \n• ​ Designed multi-color spectral flow cytometry panels (15+ color) and built the gating strategy and analysis pipeline. \n• ​ Optimized assay protocols into repeatable workflows, resolving sources of variability to improve reproducibility. \n• ​ Cultured primary mouse immune cells (DC, mast cell) and primary neurons for mechanistic and target validation studies. \n• ​ Discovered mechanism of action for neuroimmune targets, including GluK2 glutamate receptor agonism, advancing from in vitro functional assays to in vivo proof of concept. \n• ​ Analyzed RT-qPCR and bulk RNA-seq data to link gene- and construct-driven changes to cell function. \n• ​ Integrated immunofluorescence (confocal microscopy) and quantitative image analysis with flow cytometry readouts. \n• ​ Published first-author Immunity (2026); contributed to Science (2025) and Sci Transl Med (2024); mentored 4 junior scientists; secured NIH T32 Fellowship ($120,000).","skills":["Molecular Biology","Assay Development","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)","Primary Cells","Cytometry","Manuscript","Posters","Research Skills","Peer Reviews","Presentations","Dissection","Laboratory Skills","Animal Handling","Cellular Communications","Team Management","Written Communication","Mentoring","Image Analysis","Immunology","Flow Cytometry","Immunofluorescence","qRT-PCR"]},{"title":"External Collaborator","company":"Bayer Pharmaceuticals · 合同","date_range":"2018年5月 - 2019年5月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"德国 拜恩 慕尼黑","description":"Immunotoxicity and safety of candidate drugs at preclinical stage \n \n• Designed and executed multi-color flow cytometry-based immunophenotyping assays to assess immune cell activation and distribution for immunotoxicity evaluation of drug candidates. \n• Generated and compiled high-quality preclinical datasets to support go/no-go decision-making \n• Operated under rigorous industry data quality, compliance, and documentation standards \n• Contributed to successful contract renewal through consistent delivery of high-quality data \n \nKeywords:  \nFlow Cytometry · Immunophenotyping · Immunotoxicology · Drug Discovery · Preclinical Research · Data Documentation\n\n• ​ Executed multi-color flow cytometry immunophenotyping assays for drug candidate immunotoxicity evaluation. \n• ​ Analyzed datasets and presented findings to internal stakeholders to support preclinical decisions.","skills":["Molecular Biology","Primary Cells","Cytometry","Manuscript","Research Skills","Dissection","Laboratory Skills","Animal Handling","Cellular Communications","Immune cell tracking","Project Coordination","Workflow Management"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Scientist / Doctoral candidate","company":"Ludwig-Maximilians Universität München · 全职","date_range":"2015年6月 - 2020年10月","duration":"5 年 5 个月","location":"德国 拜恩 慕尼黑","description":"Neuron-T cell interactions, immune cell trafficking and adaptive immune responses \n \n[Science and Skills] \n• Led in vivo studies of neuron-T cell interactions using surgical, pharmacological, and genetic approaches; primary findings published in J Exp Med (2021) \n• Characterized cell trafficking and activation in vivo, via flow cytometry and live cell-imaging. \n• Conducted cell-based assays to define functional effects of biomolecules on primary immune cells. \n• Analyzed cytokines, antibodies, epitopes, and cell numbers, using qPCR, ELISA, flow cytometry and microscopy. \n• Conducted whole-mount and conventional fluorescence imaging of neurons and immune cells across multiple tissue types using confocal microscopy \n• Developed an automated image analysis toolkit that reduced manual processing time by 50% \n \n[Collaboration and Mentorship] \n• Partnered with vascular and neutrophil biology teams on multi-disciplinary studies, contributing to 2 co-authored publications in Eur Heart J and J Immunol. \n• Trained 30+ researchers on flow cytometers and confocal microscopes; established SOPs to standardize workflows across the laboratory. \n• Led a hand-on training workshop for mouse recovery surgeries. \n• Supervised 2 junior doctoral students on experimental design and technical execution \n \nKeywords:  \nT Cell Biology · Innate Immunity · Dendritic Cell Assays · Neuroimmunology · Flow Cytometry · Whole-Mount Imaging · Confocal Microscopy · In Vivo Models · Adaptive Immunity · Scientific Mentoring · SOP Development\n\n• ​ Developed and executed T cell activation, CFSE proliferation, and DC-T cell co-culture assays to characterize primary immune cell responses. \n• ​ Executed pharmacological and genetic (RNAi/shRNA) perturbation of adrenergic receptor pathways to define neural–immune signaling mechanism of action. \n• ​ Profiled molecular and immune endpoints by flow cytometry, ELISA, RT-qPCR, and Western blot; conducted confocal fluorescence imaging and built an automated image analysis toolkit that cut processing time by 50%. \n• ​ Authored lab-wide SOPs, trained 30+ researchers on flow cytometry and confocal microscopy, and supervised 2 junior doctoral researchers; first author on J Exp Med (2021) plus three additional publications. \n• ​ Executed in vivo neuroimmune pharmacology studies covering recovery surgery, multi-route dosing, and tissue harvest.","skills":["Molecular Biology","Assay Development","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)","Primary Cells","Cytometry","Manuscript","Posters","Research Skills","Peer Reviews","Presentations","Dissection","Laboratory Skills","Animal Handling","Cellular Communications","Written Communication","Serology","Immunology","Flow Cytometry","mouse neurosurgery","Microscopy"]},{"title":"Research Assistant","company":"Academia Sinica, Taiwan · 全职","date_range":"2012年8月 - 2015年4月","duration":"2 年 9 个月","location":"Taipei–Keelung Metropolitan area","description":"Conducted target discovery and validation research in oncology and autoimmune disease integrating in vitro, in vivo and clinical data. \n \n• Discovered and validated 2 therapeutic targets for B-cell lymphoma and colitis using RNAi-based functional screens and in vivo xenograft tumor models. \n• Isolated and profiled primary human PBMCs and tumor-infiltrating immune cells from patient samples via gradient and magnetic separation. \n• Generated 9 lentiviral reporter and shRNA knockdown cell lines for systematic in vitro and in vivo target screening. \n• Conducted IVIS imaging and tumor burden assessments to evaluate therapeutic efficacy in xenograft models. \n• Supported translational oncology projects by managing 7 mouse colonies and coordinating patient sample workflows. \n \nKeywords:  \nTarget Validation · RNAi · Lentiviral Vectors · Xenograft Models · Tumor Immunology · Primary Human Cells · PBMC Isolation · Magnetic Separation · Biochemical Assays · Translational Oncology\n\n• ​ Validated two therapeutic targets for B-cell lymphoma and colitis through RNAi functional screening.","skills":["Molecular Biology","Assay Development","Research Skills","Presentations","Dissection","Laboratory Skills","Cell Lines","Animal Handling","Cellular Communications","Mouse Models","RNAi","Expense Management","Project Coordination"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Postdoctoral Scientist at University of Pittsburgh · 2021年 - 现在 | External Collaborator at Bayer Pharmaceuticals · 2018年 - 2019年 | Postdoctoral Scientist / Doctoral candidate at Ludwig-Maximilians Universität München · 2015年 - 2020年 | Research Assistant at Academia Sinica, Taiwan · 2012年 - 2015年 | Personnel Officer at ROC Army (Taiwan) · 2011年 - 2012年","education":[{"school":"Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Immunology","date_range":"2015年 - 2019年","activities":"活动与社团: Pint of Science - science for public Philo 5 Munich - social issues, science and technology for public Deutsche Gesellschaft für Immunologie American Society for Investigative Pathology The American Association of Immunologists","grade":""},{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Master of Science - MS","field_of_study":"Molecular Biology","date_range":"2009年 - 2011年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Bachelor of Science - BS","field_of_study":"Biochemistry","date_range":"2005年 - 2009年","activities":"活动与社团: Department badminton team","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2015年 - 2019年 | 台湾大学，Master of Science - MS · 2009年 - 2011年 | 台湾大学，Bachelor of Science - BS · 2005年 - 2009年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Scientist Project Manager Consultant 职位性质 全职 合同制 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 宾夕法尼亚州 匹兹堡 美国 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[{"name":"German","proficiency":"初级 (入门)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
