{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:07:34+08:00","record":{"name":"Huadong Chen","current_title":"Specialist","current_company":"University of California, San Francisco","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 旧金山","headline":"Senior Cancer Biologist | Oncology Drug Discovery | Functional Genomics | CRISPR Screening | Synthetic Lethality | Cell Therapy |Translational Oncology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/huadong-chen-6182943a6","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAGNab3QBbocTi4IC0sHQvysTkHhYm4iFtdU","core_skills":["Drug Discovery Platforms","In Vivo Cell Therapy Evaluation","Tumor Xenograft Models"],"positions":[{"title":"Specialist","company":"University of California, San Francisco","date_range":"7 年 2 个月","duration":"2 年 3 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"p53 Precision Oncology & Synthetic Lethality \nTarget Discovery | Precision Oncology | Genome Editing \n \nDiscovered a novel synthetic lethal therapeutic target for p53 loss-of-function (LOF) cancers, establishing the foundation for a first-in-class precision oncology program and currently advancing the development of a selective small-molecule inhibitor. \nContributed to the development of Cas12a2-enabled mutation-selective cancer therapeutics in collaboration with the Jennifer Doudna laboratory, resulting in a co-authored Nature publication on RNA-triggered chromatin shredding for precision cancer therapy.  \nApplied CRISPR functional genomics approaches to identify and validate genetic dependencies associated with TP53-deficient tumors and support next-generation targeted therapeutic strategies. \n \n \nCell Therapy & Genome Engineering \nCAR-T | CAR-NK | CRISPR Knock-in | In Vivo CAR \n \nContributed to the development of next-generation in vivo CAR and PSMA-targeted CAR-T/CAR-NK therapies for solid tumors through integrated genome engineering and translational research. \nDeveloped CRISPR-mediated targeted knock-in platforms for precise CAR integration and engineering of immune cells, enabling next-generation cell therapy approaches. \nDesigned and executed in vitro and in vivo pharmacology studies to evaluate efficacy, persistence, and functional performance of engineered CAR-T/CAR-NK cells. \nCollaborated across multidisciplinary teams spanning immuno-oncology, genome engineering, cancer biology, and translational medicine to advance preclinical cell therapy programs.","skills":["技能: Drug Discovery Platforms • In Vivo Cell Therapy Evaluation • Tumor Xenograft Models • Leadership & Collaboration • Drug Discovery Technologies • Omics & Bioinformatics • Molecular & Cellular Biology • Cell Therapy • Functional Genomics • Cancer Research • Drug Discovery • Cancer Biology","Drug Discovery Platforms","In Vivo Cell Therapy Evaluation","Tumor Xenograft Models","Leadership & Collaboration","Drug Discovery Technologies","Omics & Bioinformatics","Molecular & Cellular Biology","Cell Therapy","Functional Genomics","Cancer Research","Drug Discovery","Cancer Biology"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Scientist","company":"University of California, San Francisco","date_range":"7 年 2 个月","duration":"2 年 3 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"p53 Precision Oncology & Synthetic Lethality \nTarget Discovery | Precision Oncology | Genome Editing \n \nDiscovered a novel synthetic lethal therapeutic target for p53 loss-of-function (LOF) cancers, establishing the foundation for a first-in-class precision oncology program and currently advancing the development of a selective small-molecule inhibitor. \nContributed to the development of Cas12a2-enabled mutation-selective cancer therapeutics in collaboration with the Jennifer Doudna laboratory, resulting in a co-authored Nature publication on RNA-triggered chromatin shredding for precision cancer therapy.  \nApplied CRISPR functional genomics approaches to identify and validate genetic dependencies associated with TP53-deficient tumors and support next-generation targeted therapeutic strategies. \n \n \nCell Therapy & Genome Engineering \nCAR-T | CAR-NK | CRISPR Knock-in | In Vivo CAR \n \nContributed to the development of next-generation in vivo CAR and PSMA-targeted CAR-T/CAR-NK therapies for solid tumors through integrated genome engineering and translational research. \nDeveloped CRISPR-mediated targeted knock-in platforms for precise CAR integration and engineering of immune cells, enabling next-generation cell therapy approaches. \nDesigned and executed in vitro and in vivo pharmacology studies to evaluate efficacy, persistence, and functional performance of engineered CAR-T/CAR-NK cells. \nCollaborated across multidisciplinary teams spanning immuno-oncology, genome engineering, cancer biology, and translational medicine to advance preclinical cell therapy programs.","skills":["技能: Drug Discovery Platforms • In Vivo Cell Therapy Evaluation • Tumor Xenograft Models • Leadership & Collaboration • Drug Discovery Technologies • Omics & Bioinformatics • Molecular & Cellular Biology • Cell Therapy • Functional Genomics • Cancer Research • Drug Discovery • Cancer Biology","Drug Discovery Platforms","In Vivo Cell Therapy Evaluation","Tumor Xenograft Models","Leadership & Collaboration","Drug Discovery Technologies","Omics & Bioinformatics","Molecular & Cellular Biology","Cell Therapy","Functional Genomics","Cancer Research","Drug Discovery","Cancer Biology"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Specialist at University of California, San Francisco · 2024年 - 现在 | Postdoctoral Research Scientist at University of California, San Francisco · 2019年 - 2024年","education":[{"school":"Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica","degree":"Doctor of Pharmacy","field_of_study":"Cancer Pharmacology","date_range":"2014年 - 2019年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica，Doctor of Pharmacy · 2014年 - 2019年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["所在地点 现场办公: 旧金山湾区 工作场所类型 现场办公"],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
