{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:07:59+08:00","record":{"name":"JJ Chen","current_title":"Vice President, Head of Discovery Biology Unit","current_company":"HitGen Inc. · 全职","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","headline":"Immunologist | Vice President, Head of Discovery Biology | Translational Science | Bioanalysis | GLP Toxicology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jjchenmed","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAKsbdgBAderSU6bOcx8sl55ZsS5ZtcpR9c","core_skills":["Pharmaceutical Industry","Data analysis using R","R studio and Bioconductor","Biomarkers"],"positions":[{"title":"Vice President, Head of Discovery Biology Unit","company":"HitGen Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2026年3月 - 现在","duration":"7 个月","location":"US/UK/China","description":"Lead HitGen's Discovery Biology Unit, a multidisciplinary organization of approximately 100 scientists supporting programs from early drug discovery through IND-enabling studies and clinical translation. \n \nModalities: small molecules, oligonucleotides, PROTACs, cyclic peptides, RIPTACs, etc. \n \nKey responsibilities: \n►Directing integrated biology functions spanning in vitro biology, in vivo pharmacology, translational research, bioanalysis, and development support \n►Building a seamless scientific framework from discovery through IND and into clinical translation \n►Strengthening cross-functional collaboration across biology, chemistry, and development teams to improve program efficiency and decision-making \n►Expanding organizational capabilities in translational science, biomarker strategy, preclinical biology, and development support \n►Developing scientific talent, leadership depth, and operational excellence across a large multidisciplinary organization \n►Advancing an integrated platform strategy to improve success rates and reduce timelines for innovative drug development","skills":[]},{"title":"Vice President | Testing Facility Management (GLP TFM)","company":"BioLegacy Research · 全职","date_range":"2025年2月 - 2026年3月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","description":"As Site Head, fully responsible for company operations, strategic growth, and team leadership.  \n► Fostered a high-performance culture by leading with A.R.T. — Appreciation, Respect, and Trust. \n► Overhauled the GLP quality system for both vivarium and in vitro laboratories, ensuring compliance and inspection readiness, leading the company through a successful regulatory inspection. \n► Built GLP-compliant bioanalytical platforms from scratch, including clinical pathology, clinical histology, flow cytometry (FACS), PCR, and PK/TK/ADA. \n► Delivered record-high revenue in 2025. \n► Oversaw all aspects of site operations, including quality systems, scientific platforms, financial performance, and organizational development.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Director — PD, Bioanalysis, Translational sciences/Biomarker","company":"InnoStar · 全职","date_range":"2020年11月 - 2025年1月","duration":"4 年 3 个月","location":"中国 上海市","description":"► Leading more than one hundred scientists of different levels in support of PD animal model, pre-clinical exploratory, GLP Tox and clinical studies, especially in new modalities (cell and gene therapy) \n• PK \n• ADA \n• Translational Sciences/Biomarker  \n► Building muti-high-dimensional platforms and analytical workflows to support first-in-class drug development:  \n• HD flow cytometry \n• Single-cell omics \n• Spatial omics \n► Leading translational efforts integrating pre-clinical studies in small animal and NHP PD/Tox models and Phase I/II clinical studies \n► Developing/implementing translational/bioanalytical strategies for new modalities: \n• Antibodies: bi/tri/quad -specifics  \n• ADCs \n• Cell therapy \n• Gene therapy  \n• Oncolytic virus  \n• Oligonucleotides \n► Conducting research projects supported by national funding \n► Mentoring post-graduates","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"AstraZeneca · 全职","date_range":"2019年4月 - 2020年11月","duration":"1 年 8 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"Lead in pre-clinical and clinical bioanalysis / biomarker","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Vice President, Head of Discovery Biology Unit at HitGen Inc. · 2026年 - 现在 | Vice President | Testing Facility Management (GLP TFM) at BioLegacy Research · 2025年 - 2026年 | Senior Director — PD, Bioanalysis, Translational sciences/Biomarker at InnoStar · 2020年 - 2025年 | Senior Scientist at AstraZeneca · 2019年 - 2020年 | Scientist - Clinical Immunology, Translational Sciences at MedImmune · 2018年 - 2019年 | Scientist - Experimental Immunology, Biologics, Global R&D at Teva Pharmaceuticals · 2015年 - 2018年 | Research Scientist- Immunology, immuno-oncology at University of Chicago · 2013年 - 2015年 | Postdoctoral Researcher - Immuno-oncology, Immunology at University of Chicago · 2008年 - 2013年","education":[{"school":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Chinese Academy of Sciences，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":""}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:08:15+08:00","record":{"name":"Zhe (Jerry) Chen","current_title":"Co-Founder & CEO","current_company":"ENU Medicines · 全职","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 帕罗奥图","headline":"Co-founder &CEO @ENU Medicines | Drug Discovery Scientist | Physician Scientist","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhe-jerry-chen-4aa64323","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAATmUwIBWNwEy14QBxiHhpG1TbY4sT1cgEU","core_skills":["Pharmaceutical Industry","Virology","Life Sciences"],"positions":[{"title":"Co-Founder & CEO","company":"ENU Medicines · 全职","date_range":"2025年10月 - 现在","duration":"1 年","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 帕罗奥图","description":"Building ENU Medicines into a next-generation therapeutics company, advancing a pipeline of first-in-class, genetically validated therapies through a forward genetics-driven discovery platform. \nInitially focused on food allergy, where we are developing oral, disease-modifying therapies targeting IgE at its source to address a large, underserved patient population with limited effective treatment options. \nSelected for California Life Sciences Spring 2026 FAST Cohort.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Director of Biology","company":"BridGene Biosciences, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2024年10月 - 2025年10月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣荷西","description":"Lead immunology/neurology assets for both internal projects and external pharma collaborations","skills":[]},{"title":"Director of Cancer Pharmacology","company":"REVOLUTION Medicines · 全职","date_range":"2022年8月 - 2024年10月","duration":"2 年 3 个月","location":"","description":"Be part of the team dedicated to delivering first- and best-in-class therapeutics to patients.  \nIn vivo pharmacology support (PK/PD and efficacy) for multiple IND-enabling studies to clinical candidates (RMC-6291, RMC6236, RMC9805, RMC-5127, and undisclosed), corporate presentations, and combination PoC through supervising internal team and external CRO partnerships. Supported DC nomination and IND filings (RMC-9805, RMC-5127) through cross-functional collaboration. Biology project leader of the RMC-5127 asset.","skills":[]},{"title":"Associate Director, Biology","company":"Quanta Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2020年11月 - 2022年7月","duration":"1 年 9 个月","location":"Greater Philadelphia Area","description":"Built and led a fully functional biology site in PA, establishing core capabilities for oncology drug discovery. Directed preclinical and translational research supporting early IND-enabling programs, including the hit discovery and lead series validation. Managed internal scientists and CRO collaborations; supported Series C fundraising ($60M, 2021).","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Co-Founder & CEO at ENU Medicines · 2025年 - 现在 | Senior Director of Biology at BridGene Biosciences, Inc. · 2024年 - 2025年 | Director of Cancer Pharmacology at REVOLUTION Medicines · 2022年 - 2024年 | 显示列表中的全部职业档案中列出的工作经历项目。全部项目: 8","education":[{"school":"Kyoto University","degree":"Doctorate","field_of_study":"Medical Science","date_range":"2007年 - 2011年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"复旦大学","degree":"Master","field_of_study":"Medical Virology and Bioinformatics","date_range":"2002年 - 2006年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"复旦大学","degree":"MD","field_of_study":"General Clinical Medicine","date_range":"1997年 - 2002年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Kyoto University，Doctorate · 2007年 - 2011年 | 复旦大学，Master · 2002年 - 2006年 | 复旦大学，MD · 1997年 - 2002年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":""}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:08:26+08:00","record":{"name":"Shuangling Chen","current_title":"Clinical Biomarker Study Lead (Principal-Level) / Senior Scientist","current_company":"Moderna · 全职","location":"波士顿地区","headline":"Clinical Biomarker Lead, PhD MD | Principal-Level Translational & Bioanalytical | Biomarkers|Immunology, Inflammation, Autoimmune, Vaccines | Phase I–III","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/shuangling-chen-2085b152","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAsfXugBjqkvOLTxHFnCZIa2vtfin5Cvht8","core_skills":["Clinical Trials Biomarkers","Ligand Binding Assays","Analytical Study Report"],"positions":[{"title":"Clinical Biomarker Study Lead (Principal-Level) / Senior Scientist","company":"Moderna · 全职","date_range":"2025年6月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 4 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"As Clinical Biomarker Study Lead at Moderna, I lead a team of seven scientists and serve as a strategic partner on cross-functional program teams, driving biomarker strategy from concept through execution across mRNA vaccine programs. My work spans understanding mechanism of action, selecting the right biomarkers and platforms, authoring analytical study reports (ASRs), and delivering high-quality biomarker data that informs clinical development decisions. \n \nHighlights: \nLead a team of seven scientists to execute end-to-end biomarker strategy across mRNA vaccine programs (Lyme, RSV, influenza, COVID-19, mpox), aligned with mechanism of action and pharmacodynamic readouts. \nLead biomarker assay method development, fit-for-purpose qualification, and validation across manual and automated MSD platforms, including single-replicate workflows with Hamilton automation that improve testing throughput. \n \nDirect biomarker testing for the Lyme disease vaccine Phase I and II program in adult and pediatric populations, spanning 1,000 clinical samples and 10,000 data points, and contribute to Phase III biomarker strategy. \n \nOversee end-to-end sample management, from collection and shipment through testing and return, ensuring chain-of-custody traceability, consent documentation, and data integrity. \n \nAuthor analytical study reports (ASRs) and revise biomarker SOPs to align with current FDA guidance. \n \nPartner across QC, QA, Clinical Operations, Data Management, and Biostatistics to deliver on timeline and budget in compliance with GCLP and FDA guidance. \n \nManage direct reports' scientific training, compliance, and career development.\n\n• Lead a team of 7 scientists executing vaccine immunogenicity and biomarker assays across Phase I-II mRNA vaccine programs (influenza, RSV, COVID-19, Lyme, norovirus). \n• Direct immunogenicity assay execution for influenza, RSV, and COVID-19 mRNA vaccine studies, including multiplex serology panels of 20 assays supporting exploratory Phase I analysis and data interpretation. \n• Provide scientific and platform guidance on assay feasibility and selection (MSD, ELISA, HAI, HBGA binding, and microneutralization) to keep vaccine immunogenicity programs fit-for-purpose and aligned with regulatory expectations. \n• Author biomarker sections of clinical assay protocols, validation plans, validation reports, and analytical study reports (ASRs); revise and maintain biomarker SOPs in alignment with FDA guidance. \n• Spearheaded singlicate MSD workflows integrated with Hamilton liquid-handling automation and Thermo Fisher Momentum scheduling, reducing reagent use, hands-on labor, and turnaround while sustaining data quality at scale. \n• Oversee biomarker sample management for over 3,000 clinical samples across global Phase I-II studies (US, Canada, UK) with full chain-of-custody and data integrity; drove over 20,000 tests across programs.","skills":["Clinical Trials Biomarkers","Ligand Binding Assays","Analytical Study Report","Lab automation Hamilton","Audit & Inspection Readiness","Fit-for-purpose biomarker assay validation","Vaccine Assay","LabVantage","People Management","Clinical biomarkers","Translation medicine","Program Management","Translational Biomarkers","Team Leadership","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Clinical sample testing","Pharmacodynamics","Biomarker assay validation","Biomarker assay development","Biomarker","ELISA","MSD","Infectious Diseases","Data Analysis","Supervisory Skills","Leadership","Clinical Research","Immunology"]},{"title":"Biomarker Lead | Translational Biomarkers & Clinical Bioanalysis","company":"Worldwide Clinical Trials","date_range":"3 年 10 个月","duration":"2 年 11 个月","location":"美国 德州 奥斯汀","description":"-Built and led the biomarker and PK/PD laboratory from the ground up at a global CRO, designing and executing fit-for-purpose biomarker and translational strategies for pharmaceutical sponsors across preclinical and Phase I-II programs; hired, trained, and managed a team of 7 including 3 PhDs, with budgets exceeding 3 million dollars and 100+ assays. \n- Delivered biomarker programs across neurodegenerative and neuroinflammatory disease - multiple sclerosis, Alzheimer's disease, and Parkinson's disease - implementing biofluid biomarkers across matrices including cerebrospinal fluid, plasma, and serum, and bridging preclinical findings with clinical objectives. \n- Designed and validated fit-for-purpose biomarker assays across MSD multiplex, ELISA, qPCR/ddPCR, and flow cytometry platforms, including inflammatory cytokine and complement panels (IL-17, BAFF, IL-6, TNF-alpha, IFN-gamma, complement C3/C4) and a translational acute kidney injury panel (KIM-1, NGAL, clusterin, cystatin C), across immunology, autoimmune, neuroscience, oncology, and cardiometabolic programs. \n- As biomarker subject matter expert on sponsor program teams, analyzed and interpreted biomarker data to inform asset strategy and translational decisions; collaborated with clinical, pharmacology, and data-management colleagues and with academic partners. \n- Authored biomarker sections of clinical protocols, validation plans, and validation reports under ICH M10, GCP, and GLP; supported Health Authority responses; established SOPs, instrument qualification, and LIMS-based sample tracking (LabVantage, Watson). \n- Provided scientific support to business development through proposals and bid defense; managed timelines, scope, change orders, and sponsor communication. \n- Presented at WRIB 2024 on parallelism assessment for ligand-binding biomarker assay validation. \n \nAlzheimer's, Parkinson's, MS, RA, Lupus, Psoriasis, MM, Acute kidney injury, Obesity and cardiometabolic, Neuromuscular (DMD) and Osteoporosis\n\n• Built the biomarker and PK/PD laboratory function from the ground up (SOPs, instrument qualification, GLP/GCLP/ICH M10 frameworks, LIMS (LabVantage, Watson), and Hamilton/MSD automation). \n• Hired, trained, and managed 7 scientists (3 PhDs). \n• Provided scientific and technical oversight of assay execution and delivery for pharmaceutical sponsors, directing development and fit-for-purpose validation of over 100 clinical biomarker and PK assays (MSD multiplex, ELISA, ligand-binding, qPCR/ddPCR, flow cytometry). \n• Served as sponsor-facing biomarker subject matter expert across autoimmune, neurodegeneration, oncology, cardiometabolic, and inflammatory programs; aligned biomarker plans with each sponsor's mechanism of action and regulatory expectations for Phase I-II. \n• Authored biomarker sections of clinical protocols, Investigator's Brochures, ICFs, validation plans, and analytical study reports (ASRs) aligned with ICH M10, GCP, and GLP. \n• Managed sponsor biomarker projects end-to-end (timelines, budgets exceeding 3 million dollars, contract scope, and change orders), ensuring on-time, on-budget, compliant delivery.","skills":["技能: Clinical Trials Biomarkers • Ligand Binding Assays • Autoimmune Diseases • Analytical Study Report • Lab automation Hamilton • Audit & Inspection Readiness • Fit-for-purpose biomarker assay validation • Laboratory Management • Watson LIMS • People Management • Clinical biomarkers • Translation medicine • Program Management • Translational Biomarkers • Team Leadership • Cross-functional Team Leadership • Clinical sample testing • Pharmacodynamics • Pharmacokinetics • Biomarker assay validation • Biomarker assay development • Biomarker • ELISA • MSD • Pre-clinical Studies • Neuromuscular • Translational Research • Infectious Diseases • Biopharmaceuticals • Data Analysis • Supervisory Skills • Inflammation • Cardiology • Data Management • Project Management Software • Clinical Development • Business Management • Oncology Clinical Research • Good Clinical Practice (GCP) • Quality Control • Leadership • Project Management • Business Development • Immunoassays • Team Management • Interpersonal Skills • Data Interpretation • Neurology • Clinical Trials • Clinical Research • Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) • Good Laboratory Practice (GLP) • Bioanalysis • Oncology • Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)","Clinical Trials Biomarkers","Ligand Binding Assays","Autoimmune Diseases","Analytical Study Report","Lab automation Hamilton","Audit & Inspection Readiness","Fit-for-purpose biomarker assay validation","Laboratory Management","Watson LIMS","People Management","Clinical biomarkers","Translation medicine","Program Management","Translational Biomarkers","Team Leadership","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Clinical sample testing","Pharmacodynamics","Pharmacokinetics","Biomarker assay validation","Biomarker assay development","Biomarker","ELISA","MSD","Pre-clinical Studies","Neuromuscular","Translational Research","Infectious Diseases","Biopharmaceuticals","Data Analysis","Supervisory Skills","Inflammation","Cardiology","Data Management","Project Management Software","Clinical Development","Business Management","Oncology Clinical Research","Good Clinical Practice (GCP)","Quality Control","Leadership","Project Management","Business Development","Immunoassays","Team Manageme