{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:08:42+08:00","record":{"name":"Jun-Jie (Vincent) Chen, Ph.D.","current_title":"Senior Director of Translational Medicine","current_company":"Laborencheng Biomedicine","location":"台湾","headline":"Senior Director","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jun-jie-vincent-chen-ph-d-32aa541b","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAQ_mdIB5_EFhFCEKLCPf6lviYx9Zt3n_L4","core_skills":["Ingenuity pathway analysis (IPA)","Biomarkers","Assay Development"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Director of Translational Medicine","company":"Laborencheng Biomedicine","date_range":"2025年3月 - 2025年10月","duration":"8 个月","location":"","description":"• Translational Medicine Experiments: Led the full-cycle translational medicine experiments, including protocol design, sample testing, target validation, and result evaluation, ensuring efficient project advancement; established KPIs for subordinates and organized cross-departmental communication meetings to strengthen team collaboration. \n• Project Management & Initiation: Spearheaded technical due diligence and initiation support, evaluating technical risks; assisted in peptide platform construction to ensure strategic pipeline needs. \n• Regulatory Filing & Collaboration: Deeply participated in IND filing, organizing and reviewing documentation; promoted external technical collaboration projects to enhance corporate professional image. \n• R&D Platform Innovation: Built core technology platforms and introduced new technologies to improve R&D efficiency. \n• Project Communication & Coordination: Collaborated with the clinical department to provide professional advice, coordinated resources to advance R&D projects toward clinical stages; communicated and coordinated with external partners and CRO companies to ensure smooth project execution.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Director of R. & D.","company":"Lions King Group - Huarong Pharma · 正式","date_range":"2024年4月 - 2025年2月","duration":"11 个月","location":"中国 广东省 深圳","description":"Novel peptide discovery for the therapy of cancer, immune and degenerative disease including PDC and RDC projects.\n\n• Formulated the company's peptide pipeline R&D strategy, including target screening, market/indication decision-making, and technology platform construction, covering PDC/RDC. \n• Evaluated the development potential of externally introduced projects, participated in technical due diligence, and promoted project initiation. \n• Responsible for biology department team and laboratory setup, technology platform/methodology development and optimization. \n• Screened and connected with external collaboration resources—universities and CROs—for project management. \n• Provided team technical consultation based on biological expertise, collaborated with other departments (AI + Chemistry) to accelerate project progress.","skills":[]},{"title":"Chief Scientific Officer 7","company":"iCarbonX · 正式","date_range":"2023年2月 - 2023年12月","duration":"11 个月","location":"中国 广东省 深圳","description":"1.Lead and manage multiple projects of therapeutic peptide including PDC.  \n2.Explore and determine potential target for unmet medical need in the field of neurological disorder, cancer therapy and immune disease. \n3.Develop and design biochemical assay and cell-based platform for functional screening of peptide-based therapeutics \n4.collaborate with AI-simulation platform for precision modification and optimization of peptide candidate. \n5.Evaluate and coordinate potential license-in projects from external collaborators.\n\n• Led multiple therapeutic peptide projects, including advancement and management of PDC (Peptide-Drug Conjugate) projects. \n• Explored and evaluated potential novel therapeutic targets for applications in neurological diseases, oncology, and immunological disorders. \n• Developed and designed cell-based functional screening technologies for peptide drugs, collaborating with the AI computational bioinformatics department to optimize candidate drugs. \n• Evaluated and integrated externally partnered projects, expanding collaboration channels.","skills":[]},{"title":"Sr. Director of Cell Biology（Innovation R & D center) 6.5","company":"Kexing Biopharm Co.,Ltd.","date_range":"2021年12月 - 2023年1月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"中国 广东省 深圳","description":"1. Lead and execute in the project of therapeutic recombinant protein and antibody, including multiple therapeutic target ex: VEGF/Ang2, ANGPLT3, IL4/IL-31, collagen III et. al. \n2. Evaluate and determine potential new target for unmet medical need indication and therapy. \n3. Develop and design biochemical assay and cell-based platform for functional screening for therapeutic candidate, including cell adhesion/binding, ELISA, reporter assay, flow cytometry etc.\n\n• Led and executed therapeutic recombinant protein and antibody projects, covering multiple therapeutic targets including: angiogenesis (VEGFR/Ang2), protein ANGPLT3, cytokines (IL4/IL-31), and collagen III. \n• Participated in project initiation decisions, evaluated clinical value of novel targets, and advanced projects from early-stage R&D to clinical phases. \n• Developed bioanalytical methods, established cell-based platforms, and screened new therapeutic drug candidates.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Senior Director of Translational Medicine at Laborencheng Biomedicine · 2025年 - 2025年 | Huarong Pharma - Senior Director of R. & D. at Lions King Group · 2024年 - 2025年 | Chief Scientific Officer 7 at iCarbonX · 2023年 - 2023年 | 显示列表中的全部职业档案中列出的工作经历项目。全部项目: 9","education":[{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Pharmacology","date_range":"2002年 - 2007年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Master's degree","field_of_study":"Pharmacology","date_range":"1998年 - 2000年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"大仁科技大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Pharmacy","date_range":"1990年 - 1996年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 台湾大学，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 2002年 - 2007年 | 台湾大学，Master's degree · 1998年 - 2000年 | 大仁科技大学，Bachelor's degree · 1990年 - 1996年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:09:36+08:00","record":{"name":"Joseph Chen","current_title":"Director, Preclinical Strategy","current_company":"Legend Biotech · 全职","location":"旧金山湾区","headline":"Director of Preclinical Translational Biology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/joseph-chen-07353b55","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAulyZcBi1PIYN7ycj1f7enznKRMjiHPZ4A","core_skills":["Assay Development","Histopathology","In Vitro"],"positions":[{"title":"Director, Preclinical Strategy","company":"Legend Biotech · 全职","date_range":"2026年4月 - 现在","duration":"6 个月","location":"","description":"Legend Biotech is a pioneer in cell therapy and a leader in CAR-T innovation, advancing transformative treatments for patients with hematologic malignancies and other serious diseases. As Director of Preclinical Project Development and Strategic Lead, I provide strategic leadership and operational support for IND-ready and early clinical-stage programs. I partner across research, translational sciences, technical development, regulatory affairs, clinical development, and business functions, as well as with the FDA and global regulatory agencies, to align development strategy, drive cross-functional execution, and advance innovative therapies from preclinical development into the clinic.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director, Preclinical Translational Biology","company":"ReCode Therapeutics","date_range":"2023年5月 - 2026年4月","duration":"3 年","location":"","description":"This organization and its founders have revolutionized the LNP platform for delivery of genetic medicines and vaccines, which was shown to be a game-changing technology during the COVID pandemic. My responsibility at Recode is to provide guidance and support to pre-clinical studies utilizing our first-in-class Selective Organ Targeting (SORT) LNP platform, which can target a variety of genetic disorders. My long-term goal here is to help grow our expanding pipeline and address unmet needs in the patient community.\n\n• Provide translational leadership for genetic‑medicine programs (CF, PCD) Spearheaded LNP pharmacology across PK/PD, biodistribution, immune‑tox, MetID Led CRO oversight and governance, KOL outreach, and fundraising efforts (CF, PCD) Draft/author IND components (IB, Module 2 and 4 pharmacology, Type C briefings).","skills":["FACS analysis","Liver Disease","Pulmonology","Rare Diseases","Bioinformatics","Assay Development","In Vivo","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Mentoring"]},{"title":"Associate Director, Biology and Pharmacology","company":"Theravance Biopharma US, Inc.","date_range":"2023年2月 - 2023年4月","duration":"3 个月","location":"","description":"The focus of Theravance Biopharma is centered on specialty pulmonary and neurological inflammatory diseases. At Theravance, my role was to help develop protocols for GLP PK/PD and toxicology studies to support the inhaled JAK inhibitor program. This program aims to treat acute lung injuries associated with COVID-19 and preventing/delaying graft rejection among individuals receiving lung transplantation.","skills":["Flow Cytometry","Pulmonology","Team Management","In Vivo","Mentoring"]},{"title":"Associate Director, Translational Biotherapeutics and Gene Therapy","company":"Codexis, Inc.","date_range":"2021年3月 - 2023年2月","duration":"2 年","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"Codexis is a leader in protein evolution and bio-engineering. Our Code Evolver platform utilizes directed evolution protein technology to create novel first-in-class / best-in-class biotherapeutics. At Codexis, my role was to provide translational support to our outstanding, multi-disciplinary research team, and help shepherd therapeutic modalities from the bench to the clinic to support our rare disease communities.\n\n• Built and grew internal preclinical translational biology function Incepted and acted as PTL for the GM1 gangliosidosis program Led rodent/NHP PK/PD studies; partnered on IND‑enabling packages.","skills":["Gene Therapy","In Vitro","Protein Expression","Rare Diseases","Assay Development","In Vivo","Cross-functional Team Leadership"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Director, Preclinical Strategy at Legend Biotech · 2026年 - 现在 | Director, Preclinical Translational Biology at ReCode Therapeutics · 2023年 - 2026年 | Associate Director, Biology and Pharmacology at Theravance Biopharma US, Inc. · 2023年 - 2023年 | Associate Director, Translational Biotherapeutics and Gene Therapy at Codexis, Inc. · 2021年 - 2023年 | Scientist 2 at BioMarin Pharmaceutical Inc. · 2019年 - 2021年 | Associate Professor at Dominican University of California · 2018年 - 2022年 | Scientist 1 at BioMarin Pharmaceutical Inc. · 2017年 - 2019年 | Senior Scientist at Siemens Healthineers · 2015年 - 2017年 | Postdoctoral Scholar at UCSF · 2010年 - 2015年 | Graduate Assistant at Rutgers University · 2005年 - 2010年 | Assistant Scientist at Schering-Plough Research Institute · 2001年 - 2005年 | Assistant Scientist at Unigene Laboratories, Inc. · 2000年 - 2001年","education":[{"school":"University of California, San Francisco","degree":"Postdoctoral Fellowship","field_of_study":"Reproductive Endocrinology/Infectious Diseases","date_range":"2010年 - 2014年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"美国罗格斯新泽西州立大学新布朗斯维克分校","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Endocrinology and Animal Biosciences","date_range":"2005年 - 2010年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Rutgers University–Newark","degree":"Master's degree","field_of_study":"Biology/Biological Sciences, General","date_range":"2000年 - 2004年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | University of California, San Francisco，Postdoctoral Fellowship · 2010年 - 2014年 | 美国罗格斯新泽西州立大学新布朗斯维克分校，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 2005年 - 2010年 | Rutgers University–Newark，Master's degree · 2000年 - 2004年 | 美国罗格斯新泽西州立大学新布朗斯维克分校，BA · 1996年 - 2000年 | 保存到项目 | 将Joseph保存到项目 | 发消息给Joseph | Joseph Chen的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":""}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
