{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:09:49+08:00","record":{"name":"Jian Chen","current_title":"Associate Professor","current_company":"The Feinstein Institutes · 全职","location":"纽约地区","headline":"Translational Medicine I Cancer Biology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jian-chen-4b0a1388","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABKo4AQBETlgq2qCf8B8OEzBMZSCbxhH5YA","core_skills":["precilinical model","Cellular immunotherapy","Scientific target evaluation"],"positions":[{"title":"Associate Professor","company":"The Feinstein Institutes · 全职","date_range":"2026年7月 - 现在","duration":"3 个月","location":"美国 纽约","description":"Associate Professor, Center for Translational Research","skills":[]},{"title":"Director, Translational Research and Preclinical Development","company":"BioAtla, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2021年6月 - 2026年5月","duration":"5 年","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","description":"• Led R&D preclinical and translational programs for ADCs and bispecific biologics across oncology, inflammation, neurodegeneration, and aging; developed in vitro/ex vivo/in vivo models (CDX, PDX, syngeneic, transgenic) to drive candidate selection and mechanistic insights for CAB platform. \n• Led a cross-functional innovation strategy program, expanded the company's early-stage pipeline including: a novel hydrophilic sugar moiety for ADC linkers to improve PK within the TME and an ADC payload targeting non-proliferating cells in the TME for CAB technology. \n• Led anti-senescence/aging programs; identified novel surface targets and demonstrated in vivo efficacy in fibrosis (UUO) and Alzheimer’s (5xFAD) models; established BBB shuttle models.  \n• Advanced CAB-ADC (BA3361) to IND clearance; directed GLP tox, PK/PD, TK, and ADA studies and partnered with Regulatory Affairs on IND submission. \n• Oversaw IND-enabling activities, program timelines, and cross-functional execution; managed CROs and external partners to meet key milestones.  \n• Led biomarker strategy, developing translational in-house/CRO biomarker studies to support IND and clinical studies, including a Phase II clinical trial of BA3011 (NCT04681131) in NSCLC; a Phase I of BA3182 (NCT05808634) and BA3361 IND filling and initiated a Phase I clinical trial of BA3361 in pancreatic cancer; and initiated a Phase III clinical trial of Ozuriftamab Vedotin (BA3021) in OPSCC, and an anti-senescence program.  \n• Directed biology discovery and target portfolio strategy for CAB, ADC, and bispecific platforms, supported patent filings and business development initiatives. \n• Led anti-inflammatory programs (IL-22, IL-6R) and developed in vivo inflammatory CRC mouse model and evaluated anti-IL-22 antibody anti-tumor/inflammation efficacy. \n• Collaborated across CMC, Clinical, Pharmacology, and Regulatory teams; contributed to pipeline strategy and presented to executive leadership and board.\n\n• Lead translational strategy and preclinical development across ADC and bispecific programs spanning oncology, inflammation, neurodegeneration, and aging.","skills":["in vivo pharmacology","Translational Medicine","Biomarker Development","Pre-clinical Studies","Research and Development (R&D)","CRO Management","IND enabling"]},{"title":"Scientific Consultant","company":"Salarius Pharmaceuticals, Inc. Business Development Team","date_range":"2021年5月 - 2022年2月","duration":"10 个月","location":"美国 德州 休斯顿","description":"• Led scientific due diligence (MoA, preclinical, ADME), competitive positioning, clinical strategy, and IP assessment. \n• Executed license-in for an oral small-molecule targeted protein degradation portfolio, including lead asset and related patents.","skills":["Business Development","Consulting","Strategy","Scientific target evaluation"]},{"title":"Director of Translational Research","company":"Sandhill Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2020年6月 - 2021年5月","duration":"1 年","location":"美国 德州 休斯顿","description":"• Established an immune cell–based cell cu