{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:10:57+08:00","record":{"name":"Yiyang Chen","current_title":"Research Scientist","current_company":"Mantle Therapeutics · 全职","location":"美国 纽约 纽约","headline":"Chemical and cell biologist | Early phase drug development | Oncology | Rare neurological diseases","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/yiyang-chen-40194514b","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACRExAEB0m9tEHXvQrlJF5Eiajsdei0pKYQ","core_skills":["incucyte","Protein Conjugation","Stem Cell Technology"],"positions":[{"title":"Research Scientist","company":"Mantle Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2025年1月 - 2025年10月","duration":"10 个月","location":"纽约地区","description":"1. Spearhead the development of research pipelines for small-molecule and marco-molecule therapeutics targeting rare, fatal neurological disorders. \n2. Establish an iPSC platform to support preclinical drug discovery and development efforts. \n3. Provide technical and operational support for an in-house, company-sponsored Phase I clinical trial. \n4. Lead the setup of a new research laboratory, including strategic equipment procurement and infrastructure development.","skills":["Stem Cell Technology","Startup Development","Project Management"]},{"title":"Doctoral Research Fellow","company":"Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai · 全职","date_range":"2019年9月 - 2024年12月","duration":"5 年 4 个月","location":"Greater New York City Area","description":"1. Drug Development: Developed a first-in-class adjuvant molecule targeting the apoptosis pathway to reprogram cancer cell into death-prone state. conducted high-throughput screening and MoA study in 96/384-well formats using recombinant protein and a wide variety of cell lines.  \n2. Protein Biochemistry: Discovered and characterized a novel regulatory region of BAX which interacts with mitochondrial-generated lipid to potentiate BAX-mediated apoptosis. \n3. Protein Purification: Optimized and scaled up purification protocols for cytosolic and membrane proteins, achieving high-yield of aggregation-prone proteins at milligram-per-liter scale in bacterial culture. \n4. Diagnostic Antibody Development: Screened and validated a novel recombinant monoclonal antibody for the use as a biomarker in an IHC-based melanoma prognosis assay (2021 Mount Sinai Innovation Award). \n5. Assay Development: Developed a high-throughput fluorescence-based plate assay to investigate ligand-protein interactions, providing a powerful tool for drug discovery and molecular interaction analysis. \n6. Investigated mitochondrial protein misfolding response and its impact on metabolic reprogramming, cellular senescence, and melanomagenesis, contributing to novel insights for targeted therapeutic strategy.\n\n• Drug Discovery: Developed a first-in-class molecule targeting BCL-2 protein to reprogram cancer cell into apoptosis-competent state, improving cancer therapies success (US patent application filed). \n• Protein Purification: Enhanced and scaled purification protocol for recombinant proteins (cytosolic and membrane proteins), achieving high yields of aggregation-prone proteins at milligram-per-liter level in bacterial cultures. \n• Assay Development: Developed a fluorescence-based assay to investigate ligand-protein interaction. \n• Departmental instrument specialist: providing SOP, training and technical support for Cytiva ÄKTApure, BIoTek microplate spectrometry reader, and Zeiss wide-field microscope.","skills":["Protein Expression","Protein-protein Interactions","Cell Based Assays","Fast Protein Liquid Chromatography (FPLC)","Drug Discovery","High Throughput Screening","Protein Characterization","Ligand Binding","Protein Chemistry","Molecular Cloning","Assay Development","Scientific Writing","Scientific Presentation","Scientific Analysis","Drug Development","Protein Purification"]},{"title":"Graduate Research Assistant","company":"McGill University","date_range":"2017年 - 2019年","duration":"2 年 1 个月","location":"","description":"• Discovered key cytosolic regulators of mitochondrial fusion using advanced reductionist methodologies, including chromatography and genome-wide RNAi screening. \n• Investigated mitochondrial quality control mechanisms with a focus on rare neurological diseases, contributing to therapeutic insights. \n• Completed Training Shop: Basic and Specialized Techniques in Protein Chemistry and Mass Spectrometry.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Research Scientist at Mantle Therapeutics · 2025年 - 2025年 | Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai - Doctoral Research Fellow · 2019年 - 2024年 | Graduate Research Assistant at McGill University · 2017年 - 2019年","education":[{"school":"Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Oncology and Cancer Biology","date_range":"2019年 - 2024年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"加拿大麦吉尔大学","degree":"Master of Science - MS","field_of_study":"","date_range":"2016年 - 2019年","activities":"","grade":"3.8/4.0"},{"school":"南京大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Biological and Biomedical Sciences","date_range":"2013年 - 2017年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2019年 - 2024年 | 加拿大麦吉尔大学，Master of Science - MS · 2016年 - 2019年 | 南京大学，Bachelor's degree · 2013年 - 2017年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:11:12+08:00","record":{"name":"Li Chen","current_title":"Director of Product","current_company":"Direct2Lab","location":"波士顿地区","headline":"Oncology R&D Leader | Biology & Genomics • HTS Drug Screening • Biomarkers & Diagnostics • Translational Medicine | Scaling NGS, DNA Barcoding & CDx Platforms | Ex-HMS, Co-Founder, PhD","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/li-chen-72252374","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAA-9NkoBfKRr8yCQdW8Zrs244KdGr7mJPh4","core_skills":["Molecular Cloning","Oncology Clinical Research","Cancer Research"],"positions":[{"title":"Director of Product","company":"Direct2Lab","date_range":"2025年12月 - 现在","duration":"10 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"- Led initial US operations setup and provide ongoing technology strategy for a smart laboratory procurement platform, defining product portfolio, vendor partnerships, and competitive differentiation for biotech customers.","skills":[]},{"title":"Consultant","company":"Freelance · 自由职业","date_range":"2024年2月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 8 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"·       Advise biotechnology CROs, NGS platforms, and life science organizations on translational biomarker strategies, platform differentiation, and genomic assay validation.   \n \n·       Conduct computational biology and multi-omic data integration focusing on resistance profiling and translational target validation (MS Bioinformatics candidate, Brandeis University).\n\n• US Infrastructure Architecture: Orchestrate the initial United States operational framework and launch roadmap for an innovative smart laboratory procurement platform, aligning technical portfolios and localized vendor partnerships. \n• Strategic Advisory & Lifecycle Design: Deliver robust technical and scaling strategy consulting to a prominent NGS service provider and a biologics CRO, focusing on workflow automation, platform differentiation, and high-throughput scalability. \n• Data Layer Integration: Deploy computational biology methods and translational multi-omics data interpretation architectures utilizing R and Python during advanced bioinformatics frameworks.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director of Molecular Technology","company":"Honeycomb Biotechnologies","date_range":"3 年 4 个月","duration":"2 年 5 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 沃尔瑟姆","description":"·       R&D: Led R&D for single-cell genomics platforms, pioneering target-enrichment, scRNA-seq, CITE-seq, and single-cell variant detection workflows applied to oncology microenvironment analysis (Patent Pending US20230287396).   \n \n·       Operations: Built and managed an NGS service core executing ~5,000 libraries across 400+ sequencing runs for ~50 biopharma partners under rigorous quality standards.\n\n• Service Core Operations Engineering: Spearheaded the architecture, launch, and day-to-day operation of a high-throughput single-cell NGS core service program from inception, scaling to serve ~50 global biopharma and premium academic partners. \n• Throughput & Quality Optimization: Directly managed >400 complex sequencing runs and ~5,000 library preparations under strict design-control standards, substantially reducing turnaround times and optimizing unit economics without sacrificing data fidelity. \n• Advanced Multi-Omics Scaling: Led molecular assay scaling and validation for the HIVE single-cell platform, spanning scRNA-seq, scTCR-seq, CITE-seq, single-cell target enrichment, and antibody-oligo tagging workflows.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist, Mol.Bio.","company":"Honeycomb Biotechnologies","date_range":"3 年 4 个月","duration":"2 年 5 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 沃尔瑟姆","description":"·       R&D: Led R&D for single-cell genomics platforms, pioneering target-enrichment, scRNA-seq, CITE-seq, and single-cell variant detection workflows applied to oncology microenvironment analysis (Patent Pending US20230287396).   \n \n·       Operations: Built and managed an NGS service core executing ~5,000 libraries across 400+ sequencing runs for ~50 biopharma partners under rigorous quality standards.\n\n• Service Core Operations Engineering: Spearheaded the architecture, launch, and day-to-day operation of a high-throughput single-cell NGS core service program from inception, scaling to serve ~50 global biopharma and premium academic partners. \n• Throughput & Quality Optimization: Directly managed >400 complex sequencing runs and ~5,000 library preparations under strict design-control standards, substantially reducing turnaround times and optimizing unit economics without sacrificing data fidelity. \n• Advanced Multi-Omics Scaling: Led molecular assay scaling and validation for the HIVE single-cell platform, spanning scRNA-seq, scTCR-seq, CITE-seq, single-cell target enrichment, and antibody-oligo tagging workflows.","skills":[]},{"title":"Co-founder and Head of R&D","company":"HeliTec Biotechnologies · 全职","date_range":"2016年5月 - 2020年5月","duration":"4 年 1 个月","location":"中国 广东省 深圳","description":"·       Co-founded and scaled an oncology NGS diagnostic company; built a CAP-accredited clinical NGS testing laboratory from scratch and directed technical operations.   \n·       Invented dual-template DNA+RNA targeted NGS and ultrasensitive qRT-PCR assays for cancer Dx, overseeing biomarker development and clinical validation across 1,300+ patient cases.\n\n• Greenfield Laboratory Buildout: Engineered and executed the blueprint for a state-of-the-art clinical cancer NGS diagnostics laboratory from zero (new chemistry, new city, gutted building, $3M venture funding, 15 FTEs), scaling physical operations to a 100 sample/week high-throughput capacity. \n• Regulatory Governance: Authored and implemented the comprehensive facility layout, QA/QC workflow validation protocols, and standard operating procedures (SOPs) required to successfully secure full CAP accreditation. \n• Liquid Biopsy Program Leadership: Directed end-to-end laboratory execution for tissue and liquid biopsy programs involving 1,300+ clinical oncology cases; successfully led the lab operations for a milestone 300-patient cfDNA early detection breast cancer pilot. \n• Assay-to-Ops Integration: Co-developed and commercialized a patented first-in-class dual-template DNA+RNA targeted NGS chemistry, stabilizing delicate co-extraction protocols into reproducible, high-throughput production runs.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Director of Product at Direct2Lab · 2025年 - 现在 | Consultant at Freelance · 2024年 - 现在 | Director of Molecular Technology at Honeycomb Biotechnologies · 2021年 - 2024年 | Senior Scientist, Mol.Bio. at Honeycomb Biotechnologies · 2020年 - 2021年 | Co-founder and Head of R&D at HeliTec Biotechnologies · 2016年 - 2020年 | Instructor at Harvard Medical School/MGH Cancer Center · 2011年 - 2016年 | Instructor of Medicine & Assistant of Genetics at Harvard Medical School and Massachusetts General Hospital · 2011年 - 2016年 | Research Scientist, Immunology at Harvard Medical School and Massachusetts General Hospital · 2010年 - 2011年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow, Pediatric Hematology & Oncology at Harvard Medical School and Massachusetts General Hospital · 2004年 - 2009年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow, Neurology at Boston Children's Hospital and Harvard Medical School · 2003年 - 2004年 | Research Associate in Molecular Genetics at University of Vermont · 2002年 - 2003年","education":[{"school":"University of Vermont","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Microbiology and Molecular Genetics","date_range":"1996年 - 2002年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Brandeis University","degree":"Master of Science","field_of_study":"Bioinformatics","date_range":"2024年 - 2026年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"复旦大学","degree":"Bachelor of Science (B.S.)","field_of_study":"Genetics and Genetic Engineering","date_range":"1991年 - 1996年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 