{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:11:36+08:00","record":{"name":"Lihong Chen","current_title":"Owner and Consultant","current_company":"NBMet consulting · 自雇","location":"美国 北卡罗来纳州 达勒姆","headline":"Scientific Leader & Strategic Facilitator | Preclinical & Translational Drug Development","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/lihongchenphd","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAEagIMBLNip0dxfgOhplaFaCA5uEFg1j08","core_skills":["Data analysis and interpretation","Pharmaceutical Industry","Pharmacodynamics"],"positions":[{"title":"Owner and Consultant","company":"NBMet consulting · 自雇","date_range":"2015年10月 - 现在","duration":"11 年","location":"罗利-达勒姆-查伯山地区","description":"Consult clinical-stage biotech firms on early discovery and IND-enabling studies to IND filing for cardiometabolic diseases, such as diabetes, obesity, and MASLD. Mitigate technical and financial risk by interpreting complex pharmacological data and identifying assay missteps, preventing costly delays in gene therapy and metabolic drug development. Enable practical solutions to resolve issues, developing new biomarker assays and researching side effects to prevent reactions. \n·     Accelerated regulatory readiness by reviewing and refining 10+ contract research organization (CRO) study reports and IND submission documents to ensure scientific integrity and compliance.  \n·     Designed high-fidelity in vivo pharmacology studies (rodent to primate), guiding data-driven decision making for novel modalities like gene therapy.  \n \n·     Interpreted difficult pharmacological issues and guided outcomes to avoid costly missteps (e.g., using incorrect assays for gene therapy products), which prevented the failure of a multi-million-dollar primate study.","skills":["Pharmaceutical Research","Pharmacodynamics","Data Analysis","Clinical Research","Chronic Illness","Protocol Writing","Pre-clinical Studies","PK/PD"]},{"title":"Director of Clinical Evidence Development","company":"Genova Diagnostics · 全职","date_range":"2016年7月 - 2019年11月","duration":"3 年 5 个月","location":"阿什维尔地区","description":"Influenced CEO and CMO on strategic directions for functional medicine program, optimizing informed decision making by delivering data-driven visualization tools and clinical evidence. Discovered clinical indications for novel tests and biomarkers of human health and chronic conditions — inflammation, cardiovascular, and metabolic diseases. Established partnerships and supported external investigators on research projects. Led IRB-approval clinical research studies for the first time in the company history.  \n·     Developed novel, clinical evidence algorithm that transformed raw lab data into actionable diagnostic indexes for chronic health conditions, enabling clinical interpretation in test reports for doctors and patients. \n \n·     Published results of research in peer-reviewed journals (one published, one submitted) and gave presentations at international conferences as the first author.","skills":["Data Analysis","Clinical Research","Chronic Illness","Health Sciences","Medical Research"]},{"title":"Manager, pre-clinical R&D, Enteroendocrine DPU","company":"荷商葛蘭素史克藥廠","date_range":"13 年 9 个月","duration":"7 年","location":"RTP, NC","description":"Led preclinical drug development projects and managed in vivo pharmacology team of 10+ scientists ranging from BS to PhD. Guided scientific research proposal development and pitched funding proposals to senior leaders. Supervised, mentored, and developed 9 scientists at undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral levels, improving productivity in preclinical in vivo pharmacology studies. Developed project plans that aligned with business strategies to generate critical decision-making evidence for senior management teams.  \n  \n·     Led 5+ preclinical projects through lead optimization to candidate selection, providing the foundational evidence required for IND progression. \n·     Reduced lead optimization timelines 50%, managing resources proactively and aligning project objectives to boost efficiency. \n·     Validated 22 gastrointestinal targets in early discovery studies for use in therapeutic roles in obesity/diabetes, applying clinical translatability. \n \n·     Secured $0.5 million funding and completed external/academic collaborations to understand MOA of bariatric surgery and develop treatment for nonalcoholic steatohepatitis (NASH) under budget and time restrictions. Research results were published peer-reviewed scientific papers.","skills":["技能: In Vivo Pharmacology • Project Leadership • Data analysis and interpretation • Pharmaceutical Research • Mentoring • Cross-Functional Team Building • Stakeholder Engagement • Pharmacodynamics • Chronic Illness • Protocol Writing • IACUC • Biomarkers • Pre-clinical Studies • PK/PD • IND","In Vivo Pharmacology","Project Leadership","Data analysis and interpretation","Pharmaceutical Research","Mentoring","Cross-Functional Team Building","Stakeholder Engagement","Pharmacodynamics","Chronic Illness","Protocol Writing","IACUC","Biomarkers","Pre-clinical Studies","PK/PD","IND","技能: In Vivo Pharmacology • Project Leadership • Data analysis and interpretation • Pharmaceutical Research • Cross-functional Team Leadership • Mentoring • Protocol Writing • Ex Vivo • Biomarkers • Pre-clinical Studies • PK/PD • In Vitro • Cell Biology","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Ex Vivo","In Vitro","Cell Biology","技能: Data analysis and interpretation • Pharmaceutical Research • Protocol Writing • Ex Vivo • Biomarkers • Pre-clinical Studies • In Vitro • Efficacy • Cell Biology • Pharmacology","Efficacy","Pharmacology"]},{"title":"Section Head, pre-clinical R&D, Molecular Pharmacology for metabolic diseases","company":"荷商葛蘭素史克藥廠","date_range":"13 年 9 个月","duration":"7 年","location":"RTP, NC","description":"Led preclinical drug development projects and managed in vivo pharmacology team of 10+ scientists ranging from BS to P