te_range":"1995年 - 2000年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"UT MD Anderson UTHealth Houston Graduate School of Biomedical Sciences","degree":"Postdoctoral Fellow","field_of_study":"Oncology and Cancer Biology","date_range":"2000年 - 2003年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"加拿大多伦多大学","degree":"Postdoctoral Fellow","field_of_study":"Oncology and Cancer Biology","date_range":"2003年 - 2006年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Weizmann Institute of Science，Ph.D · 1995年 - 2000年 | UT MD Anderson UTHealth Houston Graduate School of Biomedical Sciences，Postdoctoral Fellow · 2000年 - 2003年 | 加拿大多伦多大学，Postdoctoral Fellow · 2003年 - 2006年 | Ben-Gurion University of the Negev，M.Sc · 1987年 - 1995年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Biotechnology Consultant Research And Development Manager Business Development Manager Grants Writer Partnerships Specialist 职位性质 合同制 全职 兼职 所在地点 现场办公: 以色列 北美洲 亚洲 欧洲经济区 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:12:19+08:00","record":{"name":"Hongjie Chen","current_title":"Sr. Scientist - Clinical Development","current_company":"Tessera Therapeutics","location":"波士顿地区","headline":"Scientist - Clinical Development at Tessera Therapeutics","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hongjie-chen-89bb55a2","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABXiH7cB6_JsqbgSkmDGA6tFRVBRYV0_COY","core_skills":[],"positions":[{"title":"Sr. Scientist - Clinical Development","company":"Tessera Therapeutics","date_range":"5 年 1 个月","duration":"3 个月","location":"波士顿地区","description":"Applying expertise in clinical science and epidemiology to 1) shape indication and target prioritization to inform portfolio and discovery strategy, 2) support the design and execution of clinical trials, and 3) contribute to translational medicine efforts integrating laboratory, biomarker, and clinical data to accelerate therapeutic development. Core duties include: \n \nClinical Science Strategy and Innovation: \n• Participate in the design, authoring, and review of key clinical documents including Target Product Profiles, Clinical Development Plans, study protocols, informed consents, Investigator’s Brochures, and Clinical Study Reports. \n• Provide strategic insights through targeted literature reviews and competitive analyses to inform development decisions and differentiation strategies. \n \nClinical Development and Operations: \n• Develop and implement recruitment strategies to identify and enroll eligible study participants, liaising with clinical sites, investigators, and patient advocacy groups to ensure timely recruitment and enrollment of study subjects. \n• Assist in preparation of documents for regulatory submissions (IND, CTA [EU], CTN [Australia]), ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements, guidelines, and submission timelines. \n \nTranslational Medicine: \n• Integrate pre-clinical and clinical pharmacology, biomarker, and imaging data analysis to enhance portfolio decisions across the pipeline, in order to predict and interpret therapeutic responses, optimize dosing regimens, and gain insight into the safety and efficacy of Tessera's therapeutics. \n \nIndications and Discovery Strategy: \n• Identify optimal therapeutic indications for Tessera’s gene writing platform by assessing epidemiology, disease biology, mutation landscape, unmet medical need, technical feasibility, and competitive landscape.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist II - Clinical Development","company":"Tessera Therapeutics","date_range":"5 年 1 个月","duration":"3 个月","location":"波士顿地区","description":"Applying expertise in clinical science and epidemiology to 1) shape indication and target prioritization to inform portfolio and discovery strategy, 2) support the design and execution of clinical trials, and 3) contribute to translational medicine efforts integrating laboratory, biomarker, and clinical data to accelerate therapeutic development. Core duties include: \n \nClinical Science Strategy and Innovation: \n• Participate in the design, authoring, and review of key clinical documents including Target Product Profiles, Clinical Development Plans, study protocols, informed consents, Investigator’s Brochures, and Clinical Study Reports. \n• Provide strategic insights through targeted literature reviews and competitive analyses to inform development decisions and differentiation strategies. \n \nClinical Development and Operations: \n• Develop and implement recruitment strategies to identify and enroll eligible study participants, liaising with clinical sites, investigators, and patient advocacy groups to ensure timely recruitment and enrollment of study subjects. \n• Assist in preparation of documents for regulatory submissions (IND, CTA [EU], CTN [Australia]), ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements, guidelines, and submission timelines. \n \nTranslational Medicine: \n• Integrate pre-clinical and clinical pharmacology, biomarker, and imaging data analysis to enhance portfolio decisions across the pipeline, in order to predict and interpret therapeutic responses, optimize dosing regimens, and gain insight into the safety and efficacy of Tessera's therapeutics. \n \nIndications and Discovery Strategy: \n• Identify optimal therapeutic indications for Tessera’s gene writing platform by assessing epidemiology, disease biology, mutation landscape, unmet medical need, technical feasibility, and competitive landscape.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist I - Genetic Epidemiology & Clinical Development","company":"Tessera Therapeutics","date_range":"5 年 1 个月","duration":"3 个月","location":"波士顿地区","description":"Applying expertise in clinical science and epidemiology to 1) shape indication and target prioritization to inform portfolio and discovery strategy, 2) support the design and execution of clinical trials, and 3) contribute to translational medicine efforts integrating laboratory, biomarker, and clinical data to accelerate therapeutic development. Core duties include: \n \nClinical Science Strategy and Innovation: \n• Participate in the design, authoring, and review of key clinical documents including Target Product Profiles, Clinical Development Plans, study protocols, informed consents, Investigator’s Brochures, and Clinical Study Reports. \n• Provide strategic insights through targeted literature reviews and competitive analyses to inform development decisions and differentiation strategies. \n \nClinical Development and Operations: \n• Develop and implement recruitment strategies to identify and enroll eligible study participants, liaising with clinical sites, investigators, and patient advocacy groups to ensure timely recruitment and enrollment of study subjects. \n• Assist in preparation of documents for regulatory submissions (IND, CTA [EU], CTN [Australia]), ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements, guidelines, and submission timelines. \n \nTranslational Medicine: \n• Integrate pre-clinical and clinical pharmacology, biomarker, and imaging data analysis to enhance portfolio decisions across the pipeline, in order to predict and interpret therapeutic responses, optimize dosing regimens, and gain insight into the safety and efficacy of Tessera's therapeutics. \n \nIndications and Discovery Strategy: \n• Identify optimal therapeutic indications for Tessera’s gene writing platform by assessing epidemiology, disease biology, mutation landscape, unmet medical need, technical feasibility, and competitive landscape.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Scholar","company":"Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California · 全职","date_range":"2020年12月 - 2021年10月","duration":"11 个月","location":"洛杉矶地区","description":"Studied the role of genetic disposition, modifiable risk factors and racial disparity in the development and outcome of the cancer and liver diseases, based on the data from the Multiethnic Cohort Study (MEC).","skills":[]},{"title":"Summer Intern","company":"GSK · 实习","date_range":"2019年6月 - 2019年8月","duration":"3 个月","location":"Collegeville, PA","description":"11-week summer internship experience with the Oncology Epidemiology Team.  \nConducted a systematic literature review to support development of the epidemiology section for regulatory submissions and internal knowledge packages. \nDeveloped a preliminary data analysis protocol to compare the incidence of adverse events from an ongoing Phase II clinical trial with approved breast cancer therapies using commercial claims data.","skills":[]},{"title":"Doctoral Student & Graduate Research Assistant","company":"University of Washington School of Public Health · 全职","date_range":"2016年10月 - 2020年12月","duration":"4 年 3 个月","location":"西雅图地区","description":"Investigated the epidemiology and genetic basis of mammographic density (MD) phenotypes.  \nMain projects included 1) a meta-analysis of genome-wide association study (GWAS) of MD phenotypes based on ~25,000 women of European descent, and 2) a case-control study to quantify the multiplicative interaction between MD phenotypes and established risk factors, in relation to the risk of breast cancer. \n \nPerformed bioinformatic analyses to study the shared genetic basis across various cancer types.  \nMain projects included 1) a systemic investigation of shared inherited basis of fourteen types of cancers by the estimation of pair-wise local genetic correlation, subset-based meta-analysis, and multi-trait statistical fine-mapping, and 2) a comprehensive categorization of GWAS significant signals of breast and prostate cancer through tissue-specific functional regulatory regions across the genome.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Sr. Scientist - Clinical Development at Tessera Therapeutics · 2026年 - 现在 | Scientist II - Clinical Development at Tessera Therapeutics · 2024年 - 2026年 | Scientist I - Genetic Epidemiology & Clinical Development at Tessera Therapeutics · 2021年 - 2024年 | Postdoctoral Scholar at Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California · 2020年 - 2021年 | Summer Intern at GSK · 2019年 - 2019年 | Doctoral Student & Graduate Research Assistant at University of Washington School of Public Health · 2016年 - 2020年 | Epidemiologist at Alabama Medicaid Agency · 2015年 - 2016年 | Graduate Research Assistant at Georgia Center for Cancer Statistics · 2014年 - 2015年 | Research Assistant at Shanghai Institutes for Biological Sciences · 2012年 - 2013年","education":[{"school":"美国华盛顿大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Epidemiology","date_range":"2016年 - 2020年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Emory University","degree":"Master of Public Health (MPH)","field_of_study":"Epidemiology","date_range":"2013年 - 2015年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"华东理工大学","degree":"Bachelor of Engineering (BE)","field_of_study":"Pharmaceutical Science","date_range":"2009年 - 2013年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_