{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:13:32+08:00","record":{"name":"Jack SH Chen","current_title":"Senior Director","current_company":"Johnson & Johnson Innovative Medicine · 全职","location":"San Diego Metropolitan Area","headline":"Senior Director - Precision Medicine | Clinical Biomarker | Translational Science","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jack-sh-chen","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAQCxvQBNgraMmFH-3D6f4_uq2w-A8gqldM","core_skills":["Predictive biomarkers","PD biomarkers","Clinical Biomarker"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Director","company":"Johnson & Johnson Innovative Medicine · 全职","date_range":"2026年6月 - 现在","duration":"4 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚","description":"","skills":["Predictive biomarkers","PD biomarkers","Clinical Biomarker","Translational Science"]},{"title":"Director, Precision Medicine Oncology - I/O and ADC","company":"AbbVie · 全职","date_range":"2022年1月 - 2026年5月","duration":"4 年 5 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 南旧金山","description":"- Built and executed translational research strategy to support development of oncology assets including IO and ADC (3+ preclinical transitioned to FIH; 2+ Ph1b transitioned to Ph2/3) \n- Worked collaboratively with cross-functional stakeholders in alignment of asset advancement to support disease area strategies (DAS) for solid tumor indications including NSCLC and CRC \n- Mentored translational research scientists (including 7+ PhD) across sites within four years to drive translational research oncology strategy/execution across different modalities including ADCs, small molecules, antibodies, immune cell engagers, and others. \n- Served as a PMed biomarker lead for programs in strategic co-development with external partners (ie. Calico)  \n- Explored biomarkers of sensitivity and resistance based on data from tissue NGS, IHC, ctDNA, multi-omics, and AI/ML models to inform patient stratification/selection in cross-functional teams \n- Contributed in biomarker related sections of regulatory documents, pre-IND meeting preparation, and advisory board interaction \n- Contributed in Ph2 biomarker translational research plans based on emerging Ph1 data \n- Characterized target prevalence, spatial distribution, genomic profile and molecular subtype of solid tumors to inform indication selection \n- Presented precision medicine translational research strategies/data package to leadership teams/governance bodies \n- Performed reverse translation studies by integrating preclinical, clinical, and real-world data to inform potential new targets, patient populations, and combination treatment \n- Co-authors for presentations - ESMO 2026, AACR 2026, AACR 2025, ASCO 2024, SITC 2024\n\n• Led translational strategy and the execution of biomarker plans to support clinical development of oncology assets including tumor-targeting therapeutics and immunotherapies (3+ preclinical transitioned to FIH; 2+ Ph1b transitioned to Ph2/3) within cross-functional program teams (i.e. ABBV-151/livmoniplimab in combination with ABBV-181/budigalimab (NCT03821935), ABBV-400/telisotuzumab adizutecan (NCT05029882), ABBV-303 (NCT06158958), ABBV-973).","skills":["Multi-omics","Cancer Immunotherapy","Antibody drug conjugates","Immune cell engagers","Cross-functional Collaborations","Program Management","Team Leadership","Reverse Translation","Indication Selection","Biomarker of sensitivity/resistance","Combination","Pharmacodynamics"]},{"title":"Associate Research Fellow (equivalent to Director) & Research Group Lead, Oncology R&D","company":"辉瑞","date_range":"5 年 7 个月","duration":"4 个月","location":"La Jolla & South San Francisco","description":"- Discovery Program Lead managed cross-functional teams and advanced programs from target validation, HIT-to-Lead, candidate selection, to IND/FIH dose escalation (i.e. PF-07257876/PD-L1xCD47 bispecific antibody; NCT04881045; WO/2021/124073; 1st & corresponding authored publication) \n- Team partner contributed to advancement of programs to FIH/Ph1b (i.e. PF-07209960/PD1-IL15 (NCT04628780), PF-07329640/LTbR, avelumab combination with utomilumab and PF-04518600/OX40 (NCT02554812) \n- Biology team lead managing 5 PhD/non-Ph.D. scientists to ensure timely delivery of IND-enabling data package for program milestones \n- Presented program strategy, data package, timeline, risk/opportunity assessment on behalf of teams to Leadership/governance/scientific boards to enable go/no-go decision \n- Collaborated with clinical, safety, clin pharm to design exploratory tox/PD/PK studies and GLP regulatory tox studies to predict FIH/efficacious dose range dose for IND  \n- Led in vitro & in vivo pharmacology section in Nonclinical Overview for IND preparation  \n- Co-led preclinical translational biomarker and patient selection strategy in early clinical development teams and participated in clinical protocols, IND, IB, and combination strategy for FIH clinical development plan \n- Worked closely with computational biologists on RWD analysis for (1) target discovery using reverse translation concept, (2) ID of biomarkers of response/resistance for combination strategy, and (3) selection of tumor indication \n- Participated in selection, validation, and optimization of clinical biomarker assays with internal clinical labs and CROs \n- Designed the preclinical combination studies of targeted therapies with I/O assets to support Ph1/2 clinical study design  \n- Worked with commercial & project managers to define the timeline and market differentiation in competitive landscape \n- Participated in external collaboration with biotech and research institutes to identify potential new targets and programs","skills":["技能: Investigational New Drug Application (IND) • Drug Discovery • Candidate Selection • Biologics • Bispecific antibodies • Program Leadership • Cross-functional Collaborations • Project Management • Biomarker Discovery","Investigational New Drug Application (IND)","Drug Discovery","Candidate Selection","Biologics","Bispecific antibodies","Program Leadership","Cross-functional Collaborations","Project Management","Biomarker Discovery"]},{"title":"Sr Principal/Principal/Sr Scientist, Program Team Lead, Oncology R&D","company":"辉瑞","date_range":"5 年 7 个月","duration":"4 个月","location":"La Jolla & South San Francisco","description":"- Discovery Program Lead managed cross-functional teams and advanced programs from target validation, HIT-to-Lead, candidate selection, to IND/FIH dose escalation (i.e. PF-07257876/PD-L1xCD47 bispecific antibody; NCT04881045; WO/2021/124073; 1st & corresponding authored publication) \n- Team partner contributed to advancement of programs to FIH/Ph1b (i.e. PF-07209960/PD1-IL15 (NCT04628780), PF-07329640/LTbR, avelumab combination with utomilumab and PF-04518600/OX40 (NCT02554812) \n- Biology team lead managing 5 PhD/non-Ph.D. scientists to ensure timely delivery of IND-enabling data package for program milestones \n- Presented program strategy, data package, timeline, risk/opportunity assessment on behalf of teams to Leadership/governance/scientific boards to enable go/no-go decision \n- Collaborated with clinical, safety, clin pharm to design exploratory tox/PD/PK studies and GLP regulatory tox studies to predict FIH/efficacious dose range dose for IND  \n- Led in vitro & in vivo pharmacology section in Nonclinical Overview for IND preparation  \n- Co-led preclinical translational biomarker and patient selection strategy in early clinical development teams and participated in clinical protocols, IND, IB, and combination strategy for FIH clinical development plan \n- Worked closely with computational biologists on RWD analysis for (1) target discovery using reverse translation concept, (2) ID of biomarkers of response/resistance for combination strategy, and (3) selection of tumor indication \n- Participated in selection, validation, and optimization of clinical biomarker assays with internal clinical labs and CROs \n- Designed the preclinical combination studies of targeted therapies with I/O assets to support Ph1/2 clinical study design  \n- Worked with commercial & project managers to define the timeline and market differentiation in competitive landscape \n- Participated in external collaboration with biotech and research institutes to identify potential new targets and programs","skills":["技能: Investigational New Drug Application (IND) • Drug Discovery • Candidate Selection • Biologics • Bispecific antibodies • Program Leadership • Cross-functional Collaborations • Project Management • Biomarker Discovery","Investigational New Drug Application (IND)","Drug Discovery","Candidate Selection","Biologics","Bispecific antibodies","Program Leadership","Cross-functional Collaborations","Project Management","Biomarker Discovery"]},{"title":"Cancer Biology & Immuno-oncology","company":"OncoMed Pharmaceuticals","date_range":"2015年8月 - 2016年7月","duration":"1 年","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"- Pricipal investigator to support internal immunotherapy pipelines anti-TIGIT and GITR-L for in vivo efficacy and PD/predictive-marker studies in immunocompetent models via analysis of tumor growth/re-challenge/survival, T-cell population, NK cytotoxicity, cytokine, and gene expression \n \n- Study lead to execute the combination treatment of anti-cancer stem cell pipelines with SOC in PDX models to achieve superior efficacy and maintain manageable toxicity.\n\n• Principal investigator designing and executing preclinical PD marker studies and combination treatment with standard of care to support GITRL-Fc (NCT03295942) and TIGIT (NCT03119428) translational and clinical development.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Senior Director at Johnson & Johnson Innovative Medicine · 2026年 - 现在 | Director, Precision Medicine Oncology - I/O and ADC at AbbVie · 2022年 - 2026年 | Associate Research Fellow (equivalent to Director) & Research Group Lead, Oncology R&D at Pfizer · 2021年 - 2022