ational Medicine • Cancer Research • Grant Preparation • Project Management • Good Clinical Practice (GCP)","Study Reports","Research Skills","Literature","Building Trust","Public Relations","Interpersonal Skills","Presentation Skills","Presentations","Research Ethics","supervision","Leadership","Team Management","Biobanking","Data Management","Pre-clinical Studies","Clinical Research","Communication","Translational Medicine","Cancer Research","Grant Preparation","Project Management","Good Clinical Practice (GCP)","技能: Study Reports • Research Skills • Literature • Interpersonal Skills • Presentation Skills • Presentations • supervision • Biobanking • Project Coordination • Communication • Translational Medicine • Cancer Research • Project Management • Molecular & Cellular Biology","Project Coordination","Molecular & Cellular Biology"]},{"title":"Clinical Research Scientist","company":"Södersjukhuset · 全职","date_range":"2016年8月 - 2018年6月","duration":"1 年 11 个月","location":"Södersjukhuset, Södermalm, Stockholm, Sweden","description":"Dept. Clinical Pathology and Cancer Diagnostic, Stockholm South General Hospital. \n \nA unique clinical/translational research experience within the Swedish healthcare system and clinical environments. Took this role to better understand both the clinical trial & pre-clinical study design, including relevant guidelines and documents management (GCP/Ethical approval/patient informed consent/Biobank approval etc.), and to bridge the communication between researchers, industrial partners and clinicians. \n \nThe focus of work: Establishing and utilizing novel organotypic cancer models to test the treatment predictive value in a prospective clinical setting. Participation in breast cancer patient retrospective cohort analysis for studying the mechanisms behind endocrine and anti-HER2 therapy resistance. In research collaboration with both academia and pharmaceutical partners. \n \nAchievements: \n- Assisted in several clinical studies and population-based cohort studies regarding breast cancer treatment resistance. \n- Helped the PhD study of 3 clinicians within the department of clinical pathology and cancer diagnostics at SÖS. \n- Established good communication channels with HCPs and gain knowledge of how to conduct research in a clinical setting.","skills":["Study Reports","Research Skills","Literature","Public Relations","Interpersonal Skills","Presentation Skills","Presentations","Pre-clinical Studies","Clinical Research","Communication","Cancer Research","Good Clinical Practice (GCP)"]},{"title":"Research Intern","company":"GSK · 实习","date_range":"2016年3月 - 2016年5月","duration":"3 个月","location":"中国 北京市","description":"Intern experience at GSK to better understand medical science from the business point of view, as well as how to translate research findings into a product. \nSupporting projects at the department of immunology/vaccination against infectious diseases (seasonal flu). Helped with the performance optimization for an influenza vaccine.","skills":[]},{"title":"PhD Graduate Student","company":"Karolinska Institutet · 全职","date_range":"2010年3月 - 2015年12月","duration":"5 年 10 个月","location":"Greater Stockholm Metropolitan Area","description":"Performed my PhD study at KI to extend my knowledge and vision within virology, tumor biology, and immunology. As well as advanced my abilities to analyze, interpret and communicate science. \n \nWork focus:  \n- Studied the virus-host immune interaction during different infection stages. \n- Research on the roles of DNA damage repair pathways and reactive oxygen species during oncogenesis, as well as the opportunities of targeting them for cancer therapeutics.  \n- Supervisor for 2 master project students and lecturer in cell & molecular biology for medical students at KI (3 years). \n \nAchievements: \n- 4 publications in outstanding international scientific journals. \n- Poster and oral presentations at different international conferences. \n- Travel grants awardee from KI and Wellcome Trust Funding UK.","skills":["Research Skills","Literature","Presentations"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Senior Research Specialist/Senior Researcher at Karolinska Institutet · 2026年 - 现在 | Research Specialist/Researcher at Karolinska Institutet · 2022年 - 2026年 | Postdoctoral Fellow at Karolinska Institutet · 2018年 - 2022年 | Clinical Research Scientist at Södersjukhuset · 2016年 - 2018年 | Research Intern at GSK · 2016年 - 2016年 | PhD Graduate Student at Karolinska Institutet · 2010年 - 2015年","education":[{"school":"Karolinska Institutet","degree":"","field_of_study":"Entrepreneurship coaching with KI innovation office","date_range":"2018年 - 2020年","activities":"活动与社团: Participation and 2nd prize awardee in entrepreneurship contest “Win the future” Venture Contest for International Entrepreneurs (European Division) 2018. Participation in Stockholms Innovationsstipendium 2019.","grade":""},{"school":"Karolinska Institutet","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Infectious disease and cancer","date_range":"2010年 - 2015年","activities":"活动与社团: Served as committee member for new PhD candidates registration at Department of Cell and Molecular Biology, Karolinska Institutet. Served as teaching assistant for Biomedicine undergraduate student course: “Cell biology and Genetics” at Karolinska Institutet.","grade":"2015"},{"school":"Karolinska Institutet","degree":"Research assistant","field_of_study":"Infectious disease and Cancer","date_range":"2009年 - 2010年","activities":"","grade":"2010"}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Karolinska Institutet · 2018年 - 2020年 | Karolinska Institutet，Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) · 2010年 - 2015年 | Karolinska Institutet，Research assistant · 2009年 - 2010年 | 中国科学技术大学，Bachelor’s Degree · 2005年 - 2009年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":false,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:16:02+08:00","record":{"name":"Hung-Chang Chen","current_title":"Senior Scientist","current_company":"AstraZeneca · 全职","location":"剑桥地区","headline":"Senior Scientist at AstraZeneca","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hung-chang-chen-84989a35","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAdtkTkBskHuJZgcSJYhOvE_nCX0N_90QE0","core_skills":["Assay Development","Life Sciences","Immunology"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"AstraZeneca · 全职","date_range":"2022年5月 - 现在","duration":"4 年 5 个月","location":"英国 英格兰 Cambridge","description":"","skills":["Pre-clinical Studies","Cellular Communications","Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR)","Drug Discovery","Research and Development (R&D)","Laboratory Skills","Microsoft Office","Assay Development","Data Analysis"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Affiliate","company":"Trinity College Cambridge · 全职","date_range":"2020年1月 - 2022年4月","duration":"2 年 4 个月","location":"英国 英格兰 Cambridge","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Research Associate","company":"University of Cambridge","date_range":"2016年5月 - 2022年4月","duration":"6 年","location":"CRUK Cambridge Institute","description":"Main Research Projects \n• Characterising the molecular mechanisms leading to a compositional change on γδ T cell repertoire in peripheral lymph node that skew the balance of tumour microenvironment (TME) during ageing. \n• Developing therapeutic ADC, CAR-T and BiTE derived from an array of high-affinity mAbs against leukaemia and cancer stem cells in solid tumours, as well as senescent cells in pre-malignant lesions. \n• Characterising the peripheral immune cell landscape in basal cell carcinoma and Gorlin patients with Vismodegib treatment over on-off cycles by CyTOF and Cite-Seq.  \n \nCollaboration projects  \n• Characterising the effect of ageing on functional variability in CD4 T cells upon activation at single cell level.  \n• Characterising the peripheral immune cell composition of a novel transgenic mouse model for studying autophagy.  \n• Dissecting the immune cell infiltration in the TME of KPC combinational therapy with immune-modulatory therapeutics and immune check point inhibitors, by FACs and a novel bioinformatic algorithm, concensusTME, for deconvoluting immune cell composition in TME from bulk RNA-Seq dataset.  \n \nStudent supervision \n• Trained 6 PhD, 4 master and 2 summer students in de la Roche group and other groups in CRUK Cambridge for various experiment techniques.  \n• Co-supervising a PhD student investigating the role of hedgehog signalling in controlling the lineage differentiation and functions of mouse and human γδ T cells in cancer and other pathogenic settings.  \n \nOther Professional activities \n• Serving as steering committee for flow cytometry core facility at CRUK Cambridge Institute.  \n• Reviewing manuscripts for high-impact journals such as EMBO Journal. \n• Evaluating graduate student reports and theses for Cambridge Cancer Centre.","skills":["Pre-clinical Studies","Cellular Communications","High-Performance Liquid Chromatography (HPLC)","Protein Purification","Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR)","Research and Development (R&D)","Laboratory Skills","Microsoft Office","Assay Development","Data Analysis"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Senior Scientist at AstraZeneca · 2022年 - 现在 | Postdoctoral Affiliate at Trinity College Cambridge · 2020年 - 2022年 | Senior Research Associate at University of Cambridge · 2016年 - 2022年","education":[{"school":"英国卡地夫大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)","field_of_study":"Immunology","date_range":"2011年 - 2015年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"长庚大学","degree":"Master's Degree","field_of_study":"Biomedical Sciences","date_range":"2007年 - 2010年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"长庚大学","degree":"Bachelor's Degree","field_of_study":"Biomedical Sciences","date_range":"2003年 - 2007年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业