{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:16:12+08:00","record":{"name":"Pei-Yu Chen","current_title":"Doctoral Student","current_company":"Washington University in St. Louis · 全职","location":"圣路易斯地区","headline":"Ph.D. candidate in cancer biology| Mechanism-Driven Discovery| Integrating in In Vivo models, Genomics, and Cancer Immunology","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/peiyuchen1994","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAGM41poB0PuBrLyDoXUHcL2QpltkT_O3Z0U","core_skills":["Leadership","Cancer Research","Investigative Research"],"positions":[{"title":"Doctoral Student","company":"Washington University in St. Louis · 全职","date_range":"2020年9月 - 现在","duration":"6 年 1 个月","location":"美国 密苏里州 圣路易斯","description":"• Led mechanism-driven research to identify the role of ARID1A/B in melanoma progression and tumor immunity modulation. \n• Generated GEMM-derived stable melanoma cell lines with ARID1A and/or ARID1B deficiency to support mechanistic studies. \n• Designed and optimized a 9-color flow cytometry panel to profile TILs and characterize changes in the tumor microenvironment. \n• Integrated transcriptomic analyses (GSEA) to uncover a novel interaction between ARID1B and the MHC-I antigen presentation pathway, informing early target discovery in melanoma.","skills":["Tumor Immunology","Communication","Leadership","Molecular Biology","Cell Biology"]},{"title":"Research Assistant","company":"清华大学","date_range":"4 年 1 个月","duration":"4 年","location":"台湾 台湾省 or 台湾省 新竹市","description":"• Led to two research projects investigating the roles of genetic, epigenetic, and cytokine-driven regulation in cancer plasticity. \n• Provided experimental and analytical support across multiple projects to advance shared discovery goals.","skills":["技能: Mentoring • Time Management • Troubleshooting • Molecular Biology • Cell Biology","Mentoring","Time Management","Troubleshooting","Molecular Biology","Cell Biology","技能: Investigative Research •