{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:16:24+08:00","record":{"name":"Wanyi Chen","current_title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow","current_company":"Dana-Farber Cancer Institute · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","headline":"Postdoc at Dana Farber| Harvard Medical School | Ph.D. at Weill Cornell Graduate School | MSKCC | Antibody Drug Conjugate | Drug Resistance mechanism | Entrepreneurial spirit | Accelerating BioVenture Innovation","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/wanyi-chen-8a058723a","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAADuHmDgB0Z2Mznl3a470AVrKj9AcMnuRduk","core_skills":["Efficient Presentations","Antibody drug conjugate","telomerase activity assay"],"positions":[{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow","company":"Dana-Farber Cancer Institute · 全职","date_range":"2025年7月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 3 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"In the devision of Medical Oncology under supervision of Dr. Pasi Janne on identifying novel therapeutic targets and developing new strategies to treat residual cancer cells after targeted therapies in lung cancer.","skills":["Efficient Presentations"]},{"title":"Research Fellow","company":"Harvard Medical School · 全职","date_range":"2025年7月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 3 个月","location":"","description":"","skills":["Efficient Presentations"]},{"title":"Ph.D student Mentor","company":"Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center","date_range":"2023年12月 - 2024年7月","duration":"8 个月","location":"","description":"Mentor two first-year Ph.D. rotation students involved in ADC projects, providing guidance to help them understand the core principles and methodologies behind the research. I assist them in developing key experimental techniques, offering hands-on support to improve their lab skills, problem-solving abilities and presentation skills. Additionally, I emphasize the importance of maintaining well-organized lab practices, encouraging them to adopt good habits such as keeping accurate experimental records and staying systematic in their approach to research. My goal is to help them build a strong foundation for their academic and research careers.","skills":["Cell Biology","Biology","organization and time management","research methodolgy","scientific writing and presentation","Experimental Design","Coaching & Mentoring"]},{"title":"Ph.D student","company":"Weill Cornell Graduate School of Medical Sciences","date_range":"5 年 10 个月","duration":"5 年 10 个月","location":"纽约地区","description":"Conducted translational research focused on understanding resistance mechanisms to antibody-drug conjugates (ADCs) in breast cancer, specifically Trastuzumab Deruxtecan (T-DXd). Identified two key resistance mechanisms: loss of HER2 expression and mutations happened at Trastuzumab binding sites. Additionally, proposed and validated a novel combination therapy approach through ADC-ADC combinaton to overcome resistance. \n1st author paper published in Cancer Discovery: https://aacrjournals.org/cancerdiscovery/article/16/2/235/772114/Trastuzumab-Deruxtecan-Resistance-via-Loss-of-HER2 \nThesis published on ProQuest: https://www.proquest.com/docview/3227716075?sourcetype=Dissertations%20&%20Theses","skills":["技能: Business Planning • Market Research • Business Modeling • Fundraising • Research and Development (R&D) • Intellectual Property • Competitive Analysis","Business Planning","Market Research","Business Modeling","Fundraising","Research and Development (R&D)","Intellectual Property","Competitive Analysis"]},{"title":"Accelerating BioVenture Innovation 1st place winner","company":"Weill Cornell Graduate School of Medical Sciences","date_range":"5 年 10 个月","duration":"5 年 10 个月","location":"纽约地区","description":"Conducted translational research focused on understanding resistance mechanisms to antibody-drug conjugates (ADCs) in breast cancer, specifically Trastuzumab Deruxtecan (T-DXd). Identified two key resistance mechanisms: loss of HER2 expression and mutations happened at Trastuzumab binding sites. Additionally, proposed and validated a novel combination therapy approach through ADC-ADC combinaton to overcome resistance. \n1st author paper published in Cancer Discovery: https://aacrjournals.org/cancerdiscovery/article/16/2/235/772114/Trastuzumab-Deruxtecan-Resistance-via-Loss-of-HER2 \nThesis published on ProQuest: https://www.proquest.com/docview/3227716075?sourcetype=Dissertations%20&%20Theses","skills":["技能: Business Planning • Market Research • Business Modeling • Fundraising • Research and Development (R&D) • Intellectual Property • Competitive Analysis","Business Planning","Market Research","Business Modeling","Fundraising","Research and Development (R&D)","Intellectual Property","Competitive Analysis"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow at Dana-Farber Cancer Institute · 2025年 - 现在 | Research Fellow at Harvard Medical School · 2025年 - 现在 | Ph.D student Mentor at Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center · 2023年 - 2024年 | Accelerating BioVenture Innovation 1st place winner at Weill Cornell Graduate School of Medical Sciences · 2022年 - 2022年 | Ph.D student at Weill Cornell Graduate School of Medical Sciences · 2019年 - 2025年 | Research Assistant at UCI School of Medicine · 2018年 - 2019年 | Exchange Student at University of Helsinki · 2017年 - 2017年","education":[{"school":"Weill Cornell Graduate School of Medical Sciences","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Cancer Biology, Antibody Drug Conjugates (ADCs), Biophysics","date_range":"2019年 - 2025年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Weill Cornell Graduate School of Medical Sciences，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2019年 - 2025年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Postdoctoral Research Fellow 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿 美国 纽约 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:16:38+08:00","record":{"name":"Xiaoqing C.","current_title":"Director, Protein Science","current_company":"ChemPartner · 正式","location":"中国 上海市 浦东新区","headline":"Protein Science Lead","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/chenxq2015","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABXgoeYBuNI2pb9a2JUNskBy0GpVpW6kZZU","core_skills":["cell culture and transfection","Medical Translation (English to Chinese)","Molecular & Cellular Biology"],"positions":[{"title":"Director, Protein Science","company":"ChemPartner · 正式","date_range":"2022年11月 - 现在","duration":"3 年 11 个月","location":"中国 上海市","description":"• Leading and recruiting a team of scientists (30-40) responsible for recombinant antibody and protein production, specializing in integrated early-stage R&D services and customized solutions. Provided reagent supports to cross-functional teams including antibody discovery/engineering/optimization/developability assessment, structural biology, small molecule screening, assay development, and pre-clinical evaluation projects. \n \n• Managing FFS/FTE-based protein/antibody production projects (hundreds annually) by developing SOWs, mitigating risks, and aligning resources/strategies. Supporting PM teams in contract finalization and BD teams in establishing long-term partnerships with global biotech/pharmaceutical companies. Created promotional materials and represented capabilities at international exhibitions. \n \n• Continuous process optimization to increase team productivity, competitive advantage, and profit margins:  \n- Established mammalian HTP expression/purification workflows to support Ab candidate  \nscreening/optimization; \n- Optimized transient/stable CHO pool expression platforms and achieved 2–3× average  \nyield increase across multiple antibody constructs; \n- Streamlined workflows for diverse formats of antibodies (bi-specific/multi-specific/VHH/Fc  \nfusion/Ab fragments) expression/purification/characterization to fit for different purposes; \n- Established and streamlined mammalian/insect cell workflows for membrane protein  \ngeneration, including FSEC based HTP construct screening/expression/purification;  \n \n• Leading internal innovation initiatives to produce challenging protein reagents for high-value targets - including transmembrane proteins (GPCR/non-GPCR), PROTAC reagents, pMHC complexes, cytokines, and diverse kinases/proteases - enabling critical workflows for LM/SM in vitro analysis, structural biology, and antibody discovery platforms. Several reagents became exclusive domestic offerings with sustained international client demand.","skills":[]},{"title":"Associate Director, Protein Science","company":"Clover Biopharmaceuticals · 正式","date_range":"2021年12月 - 2022年10月","duration":"11 个月","location":"中国 上海市","description":"• Led and established in-house developability assessment workflow to enable early-stage molecule engineering and to ensure developability at pre-CMC stage. Led reagent generation and molecular assessment for immune-oncology project by coordinating and collaborating with R&D, CLD, PD, QC and formulation teams. \n• Led and optimized of protein science platforms to provide discovery support in candidate selection, optimization, and development; established transient expression platforms (including mammalian and insect platforms) to enable vaccine/biologics reagent supply with high productivity and cost-efficiency in R&D stage.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director, Project Management","company":"Eminence · 正式","date_range":"2020年11月 - 2021年11月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"中国 江苏省","description":"• Established and standardized external PM process for CLD (cell line development) and MD (media development) projects to ensure projects to be delivered on time and within budget. Working closely with R&D/finance/BD teams to implement PM process. \n• Managed external projects and supported successful delivery: support project teams to complete contract and work plan; identify project scopes and risks; hold/attend project review or client meetings; review finance reports and facilitate budget control;  \n• Managed internal projects including new platform and product development projects. Standardized process for new product development. Working closely with R&D/BD/marketing/PD/QA teams to drive new products from idea to launch. \n• Established and recruited project management and product management team.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist (promoted from prior role), Protein Platform Lead","company":"安进","date_range":"4 年 4 个月","duration":"6 个月","location":"中国 上海市","description":"• Led and coordinated protein reagent supply activities among CRO, Amgen global and Shanghai teams. Supported recombinant protein reagents for 6+ cross-functional projects in Amgen CNRS.Accomplished multiple biologics generation for 20+ global projects to enable lead optimization and in vitro/in vivo assays in global project teams during COVID-19 lockdown.  \n• Further expanded recombinant protein production platform, including CEPA (cloning/expression/purification/assays) with mammalian, insect and E. coli systems.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Associate Scientist, Protein Expression Platform Lead","company":"安进","date_range":"4 年 4 个月","duration":"6 个月","location":"中国 上海市","description":"• Led and coordinated protein reagent supply activities among CRO, Amgen global and Shanghai teams. Supported recombinant protein reagents for 6+ cross-functional projects in Amgen CNRS.Accomplished multiple biologics generation for 20+ global projects to enable lead optimization and in vitro/in vivo assays in global project teams during COVID-19 lockdown.  \n• Further expanded recombinant protein production platform, including CEPA (cloning/expression/purification/assays) with mammalian, insect and E. coli systems.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Director, Protein Science at ChemPartner · 2022年 - 现在 | Associate Director, Protein Science at Clover Biopharmaceuticals · 2021年 - 2022年 | Director, Project Management at Eminence · 2020年 - 2021年 | Scientist (promoted from prior role), Protein Platform Lead at 安进 · 2020年 - 2020年 | Senior Associate Scientist, Protein Expression Platform Lead at 安进 · 2016年 - 2020年 | Senior Research Scientist, Cell Line Development Group Lead at 上海睿智化学研究有限公司 · 2015年 - 2016年 | Translator (part time) at 《环球科学》杂志社有限公司 · 2015年 - 2015年 | Translator (part time) at Science & Vie Magazine (China)-《新发现》杂志中文版 · 2014年 - 2015年 | Postdoctoral Researcher at Washington University in St. Louis · 2010年 - 2014年","education":[{"school":"复旦大学医学院","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (PhD)","field_of_study":"pharmacology","date_range":"2004年 - 2010年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"复旦大学医学院","degree":"Bachlor","field_of_study":"Basic Medicine","date_range":"1999年 - 2004年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 复旦大学医学院，Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) · 2004年 - 2010年 | 复旦大学医学院，Bachlor · 1999年 - 2004年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Team Lead 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 中国 上海市 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":true,"detail_error":""}}
