{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:17:46+08:00","record":{"name":"Lan Chen","current_title":"Associate Principal Scientist II | Associate Director | Team Leader","current_company":"MSD","location":"中国","headline":"Associate Principal Scientist of Computational Biologist","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/lan-chen-935a199","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAHAmvkB18lD6y9v7btvGPYLzCQqvDwwYEM","core_skills":["eQTL","GWAS","Systems Biology"],"positions":[{"title":"Associate Principal Scientist II | Associate Director | Team Leader","company":"MSD","date_range":"18 年 2 个月","duration":"12 年 9 个月","location":"Beijing","description":"In the Bioinformatics Group: \n• Led a team to develop advanced analytical methods and pipelines for the comprehensive analysis of genomic datasets across various cancer types. \n• Investigated the mechanisms of action (MoA) and resistance mechanisms of diverse treatments in multiple cancer types, contributing to the development of more effective therapeutic strategies.\n\n• Lead a team of scientists that develop analytics methods and computational pipelines (Quality Control, Somatic Mutation, Mutation Burden, Copy Number Variation, Tumor Clonality) to analyze genomic datasets of different cancer types of human tumor organoid models to evaluate the genomic characteristics of models and genomic changes across passages, and help build a searchable database for organoids models, to support the target identification, biomarker studies and novel drug screening in pre-clinical oncology studies. \n• Lead a team of scientists that develop computational pipelines to analyze the genomic characteristics (Somatic Mutation, Mutation Burden, Copy Number Variation, Neoantigen) of WES (whole exome sequencing) data for Syngeneic Mouse tumor cell lines to investigate the targets and biomarkers in pre-clinical oncology studies. \n• Evaluate the models, genomic analysis pipelines and results provided by varied vendors of human tumor organoid models. \n• Performs single cell total-Seq data analysis as a means of evaluating cell hashing technology. \n• Analyzes the WES and RNA-Seq data of human acute myeloid leukemia samples to investigate biomarkers that associated with drug response. \n• Conducts analysis of atherosclerotic plaque expression datasets to understand the composition and origin of different types of plaques. \n• Collaborates with cross-functional teams (research, technology staff) during all drug discovery projects, drafts presentations about the findings, with protocols and recommendations to senior management. \n• Stay updated with the latest advancements in computational biology and related fields and apply this knowledge to drive innovation. \n• Trains junior computational biologists within the team.","skills":["技能: Python (Programming Language) • Amazon Web Services (AWS) • Linux • High Performance Computing (HPC) • Cancer Genomics • Single Cell Sequencing • R (Programming Language) • Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS) • Bioinformatics","Python (Programming Language)","Amazon Web Services (AWS)","Linux","High Performance Computing (HPC)","Cancer Genomics","Single Cell Sequencing","R (Programming Language)","Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS)","Bioinformatics","技能: MATLAB • Linux • High Performance Computing (HPC) • GWAS • eQTL • R (Programming Language) • Genomics • Perl • Statistical Genetics","MATLAB","GWAS","eQTL","Genomics","Perl","Statistical Genetics"]},{"title":"Sr. Scientist","company":"MSD","date_range":"18 年 2 个月","duration":"12 年 9 个月","location":"Beijing","description":"In the Bioinformatics Group: \n• Led a team to develop advanced analytical methods and pipelines for the comprehensive analysis of genomic datasets across various cancer types. \n• Investigated the mechanisms of action (MoA) and resistance mechanisms of diverse treatments in multiple cancer types, contributing to the development of more effective therapeutic strategies.\n\n• Lead a team of scientists that develop analytics methods and computational pipelines (Quality Control, Somatic Mutation, Mutation Burden, Copy Number Variation, Tumor Clonality) to analyze genomic datasets of different cancer types of human tumor organoid models to evaluate the genomic characteristics of models and genomic changes across passages, and help build a searchable database for organoids models, to support the target identification, biomarker studies and novel drug screening in pre-clinical oncology studies. \n• Lead a team of scientists that develop computational pipelines to analyze the genomic characteristics (Somatic Mutation, Mutation Burden, Copy Number Variation, Neoantigen) of WES (whole exome sequencing) data for Syngeneic Mouse tumor cell lines to investigate the targets and biomarkers in pre-clinical oncology studies. \n• Evaluate the models, genomic analysis pipelines and results provided by varied vendors of human tumor organoid models. \n• Performs single cell total-Seq data analysis as a means of evaluating cell hashing technology. \n• Analyzes the WES and RNA-Seq data of human acute myeloid leukemia samples to investigate biomarkers that associated with drug response. \n• Conducts analysis of atherosclerotic plaque expression datasets to understand the composition and origin of different types of plaques. \n• Collaborates with cross-functional teams (research, technology staff) during all drug discovery projects, drafts presentations about the findings, with protocols and recommendations to senior management. \n• Stay updated with the latest advancements in computational biology and related fields and apply this knowledge to drive innovation. \n• Trains junior computational biologists within the team.","skills":["技能: Python (Programming Language) • Amazon Web Services (AWS) • Linux • High Performance Computing (HPC) • Cancer Genomics • Single Cell Sequencing • R (Programming Language) • Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS) • Bioinformatics","Pytho