{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:19:07+08:00","record":{"name":"Jerry Chen, Ph.D.","current_title":"Marketing Associate Director","current_company":"HanchorBio Inc. 漢康生技股份有限公司 · 全职","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","headline":"Head of Medical Affairs & Marketing @ HanchorBio | Building Scientific Credibility in Oncology & Autoimmune | Medical & Marketing Operations | KOL Engagement | IR/PR & BD","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jerry-chen-ph-d-310a1612","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAKkUzwB9FNt6ncHxZDlfjcElLIWne14vnw","core_skills":["生命科学","Sales","实验室"],"positions":[{"title":"Marketing Associate Director","company":"HanchorBio Inc. 漢康生技股份有限公司 · 全职","date_range":"2026年1月 - 现在","duration":"9 个月","location":"台湾 台北市","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Marketing Excellence Manager, Hong Kong & Taiwan","company":"賽諾菲-安萬特集團 · 全职","date_range":"2023年7月 - 2026年1月","duration":"2 年 7 个月","location":"Hong Kong & TW","description":"1. Establish Marketing Excellence Framework: Develop comprehensive HKTW Marketing Training Roadmap through dual initiatives \n-\"Marketing Academy\" - Enhance foundational marketing skills and strategic thinking. \n-\"Precision Marketing\" - Optimize HCP engagement through data-driven approaches. \n-Design & implement new marketer onboarding training, ensuring rapid integration and productivity. \n \n2. Strengthen Leadership Development:  \n-Co-lead \"FLSM Leadership\" program implementing analytics-based decision-making methodologies to drive measurable team performance improvements. \n-Collaborate with marketers to establish first AI role-play platform using internal AI system (Concierge), enhancing sales capabilities and performance. \n \n3. Execute Launch Excellence Strategy:  \n-Prioritize growth drivers through streamlined business planning processes and effective cross-BU collaboration. \n-Facilitate seamless integration of Business Planning (BP) and Operational Planning (OP) from marketing strategies to sales execution, e.g. conduct comprehensive needs assessment across all BUs; align strategies with on-ground sales tactics; drive business growth through X-functional synergy. \n \n4. Implement Digital Transformation:  \n-Co-lead \"GtM Transformation & Omnichannel\" initiative to modernize marketing capabilities, resulting in enhanced team performance and accelerated business growth. \n-Leverage digital tools and AI technologies to optimize marketing strategies and sales effectiveness.","skills":[]},{"title":"Country Medical Head (Associate Director, Medical Affairs)","company":"Everest Medicines · 全职","date_range":"2021年9月 - 2023年7月","duration":"1 年 11 个月","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","description":"1. Product Positioning and Regulatory Success: \n-Establish Trodelvy as mTNBC treatment standard through collaboration with TW Breast Cancer Society. \n-Secure TFDA Accelerated Approval Designation for Nefecon in IgAN disease. \n \n2. Cross-functional Alliance Management: \n-Co-lead team in forming strategic alliance with Harvester for Trodelvy. \n-Orchestrate integrated approach covering - regulatory approval process, reimbursement dossier preparation, MAs program development, clinical study execution across multiple therapeutic areas. \n \n3. Medical Affairs Strategy and Team Development: \n-Develop & implement comprehensive MA strategy; enhance KOL engagement initiatives. \n-Optimize resource allocation across company pipeline. \n-Expand team structure by creating two new medical manager positions with direct reports.\n\n• ⚫ Successful build-up Trodelvy as a standard of care in mTNBC treatment consensus with Taiwan Breast Cancer Society in pre-launch phase (Apr-2022). \n• ⚫ Successful serve as drafter and lead cross-functional team to get TFDA granted Accelerated Approval Designation (AAD) of Nefecon in IgAN disease (Nov-2022). \n• ⚫ Successful lead cross-functional team to alliance with Harvester getting Trodelvy regulatory approval (License approval in Nov-2022), and reimbursement dossier preparations, medical related programs (Named Patient Program, Continuous Medical Education) and KOLs development plan execution. \n• ⚫ As an expert and first contact to provide support, monitor and execute on the process of clinical trials and studies (Oncology, IgAN and IBD) included SIV, COV, RMV for patients’ recruitment acceleration, AEs management, PIs/SCs engagement and protocol updates through working closely with local CRO and global medical team accelerating patient enrollment of ES101002 (NCT04176588) phase 3 study in UC and Tropics-02 (NCT03901339) phase 3 study in HR+/HER- mBC in TW successfully. \n• ⚫ Take responsibility for leading medical strategy development, tactics implementation, KOLs engagement and resource allocation for current and future pipelines (Oncology, Immunology, CVRM and Anti-infection therapeutic areas) to meet company objectives, policies, regulations and maintaining high level scientific knowledge, provide scientific education activities and competitive environment analysis from medical perspectives to international team. \n• ⚫ Successful create 2 headcounts of medical manager role and direct report to me.","skills":[]},{"title":"Franchise Lead, Oncology Hematology","company":"Takeda · 全职","date_range":"2020年7月 - 2021年8月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","description":"1. Team Leadership and Business Management: \n-Lead integrated hematology portfolio team: 5 sales representatives and 2 product managers. \n-Develop and execute comprehensive brand strategies, product positioning, and KOL/patient segmentation. \n \n2. Product Launch and Market Expansion: \n-Successfully launch 2 new indications for Adcetris; implement new business case for Ninlaro turning around the business and driving market penetration. \n-Achieve 80% business coverage through strategic expansion to 30 healthcare providers. \n \n3. Exceptional Business Performance: \n-Adcetris: 123% achievement rate, 74% YOY growth (7M, FY20). \n-Ninlaro: 126% patient target; increase 30% diagnosis rate in driving double-digit sales growth (2M). \n \n4. Market Access and Reimbursement Strategy: \n-Co-lead X-functional team to propose and submit new reimbursement dossier for Adcetris to NHIA. \n-Accelerate & complete NHIA submissions for 3 new Adcetris indications within limited time.\n\n• ⚫ Successful launch 2 new indications of Adcetris (Hodgkin Lymphoma: FL PTCL and R/R CTCL) and 1 new business case (Patient Access Program, PAP) of Ninlaro (Multiple Myeloma) to achieve company goals in FY21. \n• ⚫ Successful lead cross-functional team to complete and submit new reimbursement dossier of Adcetris to NHIA within 1 month. \n• ⚫ Successful complete 30 hospitals listing and increase 30% FISH testing rate of Ninlaro to deliver double-digit sales revenue within 1 year. \n• ⚫ Take charge of hematology business (Adcetris in HL and TCL, Ninlaro in MM and Pipelines), and lead both sales (5 MRs) and marketing (2 PMs) team to develop brand strategies, products positioning, KOLs/patients’ segmentation, and tactics execution to achieve company goals/targets.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Marketing Associate Director at HanchorBio Inc. 漢康生技股份有限公司 · 2026年 - 现在 | Marketing Excellence Manager, Hong Kong & Taiwan at 賽諾菲-安萬特集團 · 2023年 - 2026年 | Country Medical Head (Associate Director, Medical Affairs) at Everest Medicines · 2021年 - 2023年 | Franchise Lead, Oncology Hematology at Takeda · 2020年 - 2021年 | Marketing Manager, FMI (Foundation Medicine) at Roche · 2020年 - 2020年 | Brand Manager, Oncology, Women's Cancer at AstraZeneca Taiwan · 2019年 - 2020年 | Diagnosis Lead, Asia Area at AstraZeneca Taiwan · 2018年 - 2018年 | Therapeutic Area Lead, Oncology at AstraZeneca Taiwan · 2017年 - 2017年 | Diagnostic Lead at AstraZeneca Taiwan · 2015年 - 2018年 | Laboratory Operations Manager, Pharmacogenomics at 國立臺灣大學 · 2013年 - 2015年 | Research Assistant, NTU Center of Genomic Medicine at Nati