{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:19:43+08:00","record":{"name":"Evelyn Chen, PhD, PMP","current_title":"Senior Manager of Drug Development and Regulatory Affairs","current_company":"Topmunnity Therapeutics Limited","location":"Taipei–Keelung Metropolitan area","headline":"Director","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/evelyn-chen-phd-pmp-96842b74","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAA-5oaABk3hrZ2lrEMXHGgONowgWKb6OmXQ","core_skills":["ISO standard","Sequencing Specialization","臨床開發"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Manager of Drug Development and Regulatory Affairs","company":"Topmunnity Therapeutics Limited","date_range":"2025年2月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 8 个月","location":"","description":"1. CAR-T Oncology Program Leadership Orchestrate the end-to-end development lifecycle and capital strategy to maximize asset valuation and project-wide milestone achievement. \n2. Regulatory and Translational Governance  Spearhead the global regulatory roadmap and translational defense to effectively mitigate clinical risks and accelerate high-stakes agency interactions.  \n3. Cross-functional Asset Management Direct integrated workstreams across CMC, nonclinical, and clinical domains to govern robust transitions throughout IIT/IND and FIH development phases.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Manager of Drug Development and Regulatory Affairs","company":"Immunwork","date_range":"2021年2月 - 2024年9月","duration":"3 年 8 个月","location":"","description":"1. Small Molecule Drug Development Oversee preclinical and clinical studies while integrating regulatory activities for IND and FIH trials focused on obesity and rare endocrine disease. \n2. Regulatory Documentation System Establish and implement regulatory documentation system to ensure qualitative IND-enabling documents.  \n3. Regulatory Strategies Develop and provide regulatory strategies to enhance pharmaceutical developability and mitigate risk effectively.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director of Preclinical and Clinical Research","company":"United Biomedical, Inc., Asia (UBIA)","date_range":"4 年 2 个月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"台湾 台湾省 or 台湾省 新竹市","description":"1. Vaccine Research and Study Oversight Oversee and manage GLP/GCLP-compliant pharmacology and toxicology studies for allergic and COVID-19 diseases in preparation for IND and FIH clinical trials. \n2. Translational Research Leadership Build and lead a robust translational research department dedicated to ensuring safety and efficacy in drug development.  \n3. Recognition Received the Outstanding Contribution Award for significant contributions.  \n \nI participate in the development of human designer peptide/protein-based vaccines to provide safety as well as efficacy evaluations and communicate with FDA/CDE. I also act as Study Monitor to design and oversee finely 2 GLP-compliant toxicity studies. Meanwhile, I successfully lead our team to study the immunogenicity and pharmacodynamics, including method development/validation and sample bioanalysis in GLP Lab. Further, IND‐enabling toxicity and safety pharmacology studies for 2 FIH trials was approved without comment. In addition, clinical team develops and validates various GCLP-compliant methods and trial sample bioanalysis (immunogenicity and pharmacodynamics) under my direction.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Manager of Preclinical and Clinical Research Department","company":"United Biomedical, Inc., Asia (UBIA)","date_range":"4 年 2 个月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"台湾 台湾省 or 台湾省 新竹市","description":"1. Vaccine Research and Study Oversight Oversee and manage GLP/GCLP-compliant pharmacology and toxicology studies for allergic and COVID-19 diseases in preparation for IND and FIH clinical trials. \n2. Translational Research Leadership Build and lead a robust translational research department dedicated to ensuring safety and efficacy in drug development.  \n3. Recognition Received the Outstanding Contribution Award for significant contributions.  \n \nI participate in the development of human designer peptide/protein-based vaccines to provide safety as well as efficacy evaluations and communicate with FDA/CDE. I also act as Study Monitor to design and oversee finely 2 GLP-compliant toxicity studies. Meanwhile, I successfully lead our team to study the immunogenicity and pharmacodynamics, including method development/validation and sample bioanalysis in GLP Lab. Further, IND‐enabling toxicity and safety pharmacology studies for 2 FIH trials was approved without comment. In addition, clinical team develops and validates various GCLP-compliant methods and trial sample bioanalysis (immunogenicity and pharmacodynamics) under my direction.","skills":[]},{"title":"Manager of Preclinical Research Department","company":"United Biomedical, Inc., Asia (UBIA)","date_range":"4 年 2 个月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"台湾 台湾省 or 台湾省 新竹市","description":"1. Vaccine Research and Study Oversight Oversee and manage GLP/GCLP-compliant pharmacology and toxicology studies for allergic and COVID-19 diseases in preparation for IND and FIH clinical trials. \n2. Translational Research Leadership Build and lead a robust translational research department dedicated to ensuring safety and efficacy in drug development.  \n3. Recognition Received the Outstanding Contribution Award for significant contributions.  \n \nI participate in the development of human designer peptide/protein-based vaccines to provide safety as well as efficacy evaluations and communicate with FDA/CDE. I also act as Study Monitor to design and oversee finely 2 GLP-compliant toxicity studies. Meanwhile, I successfully lead our team to study the immunogenicity and pharmacodynamics, including method development/validation and sample bioanalysis in GLP Lab. Further, IND‐enabling toxicity and safety pharmacology studies for 2 FIH trials was approved without comment. In addition, clinical team develops and validates various GCLP-compliant methods and trial sample bioanalysis (immunogenicity and pharmacodynamics) under my direction.","skills":[]},{"title":"Lab Director","company":"TVGH Lihpao Lab of Cancer Genomic Medicine (CAP Accredited)","date_range":"2015年6月 - 2016年9月","duration":"1 年 4 个月","location":"Taipei Veterans General Hospital","description":"1. Medical Laboratory Management \nOversee a medical laboratory delivering high-quality and precise genetic testing services for cancer patients. \n2. NGS Diagnosis Improvement \nEnhance customer satisfaction by providing rapid NGS diagnoses through streamlined processes and improved operational efficiency.  \n3. CAP Accreditation Renewal \nSuccessfully renew CAP accreditation by demonstrating strong organization and effective time management. \n \nAs CAP Accredited Medical Lab Director, I had to coordinate all the activities, including continuous improvement of laboratory and negotiation with my co-workers from different backgrounds. Next Generation Sequencing (NGS) genetic testing for the companion diagnostics in cancers with target drugs was routinely provided according to physician order. During my year as director, I successfully led the team to complete the on-site laboratory review without major comment to renew the accreditation.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Senior Manager of Drug Development and Regulatory Affairs at Topmunnity Therapeutics Limited · 2025年 - 现在 | Senior Manager of Drug Development and Regulatory Affairs at Immunwork · 2021年 - 2024年 | Director of Preclinical and Clinical Research at United Biomedical, Inc., Asia (UBIA) · 2019年 - 2020年 | 显示列表中的全部职业档案中列出的工作经历项目。全部项目: 10","education":[{"school":"National Taiwan University","degree":"PhD","field_of_study":"Medical Microbiology and Bacteriology","date_range":"2001年 - 2008年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | National Taiwan University，PhD · 2001年 - 2008年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 總監 資深經理 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: Taipei–Keelung Metropolitan area 开始日期 我在随便看看，时间可灵活安排 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[{"name":"英文","proficiency":"高级 (无障碍商务沟通)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:20:36+08:00","record":{"name":"Shuai Chen","current_title":"Director, Clinical Development","current_company":"Disc Medicine · 全职","location":"波士顿地区","headline":"Director, Clinical Development | AI in Drug Development | MBA candidate at Carnegie Mellon University","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/shuai-chen-417ab66b","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAA7vTdMBNwoakVLDXfHBlELG8kRKUSubSco","core_skills":["DCF Valuation","Life Sciences","Computational Biology"],"positions":[{"title":"Director, Clinical Development","company":"Disc Medicine · 全职","date_range":"2026年2月 - 现在","duration":"8 个月","location":"波士顿地区","description":"","skills":["Global Drug Development","Clinical Study Management","Drug Development","Clinical Affairs"]},{"title":"Senior Lead, Clinical Data Science","company":"诺和诺德","date_range":"2 年 2 个月","duration":"2 年 2 个月","location":"波士顿地区","description":"• Investment Analysis & Due Diligence. \n• Serve as scientific SME for investment decision-making, performing therapeutic market analysis and building financial models to prioritize and select investment candidates across cardiovascular, oncology, metabolic, and rare disease portfolios. \n• Decision Science STA: Led due diligence and competitive assessment for the $5.2B acquisition of Akero Therapeutics; benchmarked internal vs. \n• external assets to inform valuation and go/no-go recommendations. \n• Conducted comprehensive due diligence and clinical trial data analysis supporting in-licensure of United Laboratories' UBT251 for Type 2 diabetes and obesity. \n• Collaborate cross-functionally with R&D, business development, and commercial teams to integrate data-driven insights into pipeline prioritization and investment strategy. \n• Translational Science Leadership. \n• Lead translational and data science strategy across multiple therapeutic programs spanning early discovery through pivotal Phase 3 outcome studies (