{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:20:59+08:00","record":{"name":"Alan Chen","current_title":"Principal Scientist - Precision Medicine","current_company":"Regeneron","location":"纽约地区","headline":"Computational Biology | Translational Drug Development | Clinical Biomarker Analysis","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/alan-chen-267919158","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACXd-y8B0HuokItEwJ-QMU6iP_CNtsMV61A","core_skills":["Molecular & Cellular Biology","Cancer Research","Bioinformatics"],"positions":[{"title":"Principal Scientist - Precision Medicine","company":"Regeneron","date_range":"2025年3月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 7 个月","location":"纽约地区","description":"- Lead oncology and non-oncology biomarker analyses across multi-dimensional data modalities (genomics, pathology, clinical, and digital) for 7+ portfolio pipelines, informing critical clinical decisions on efficacy, safety, dose optimization, disease biology, and patient enrichment strategies. \n- Drive digital biomarker and pathology initiatives leveraging advanced machine learning methodologies to enable precise patient stratification and predict treatment response. \n- Build and strengthen strategic cross-functional partnerships with clinical, translational, and research teams to foster seamless collaboration and accelerate biomarker-driven drug development. \n- Establish an automated data cleaning framework that enhance data storage, standardization, and secure data integrity for internal and external biomarker data from clinical trials.\n\n• Lead biomarker strategy across 6 oncology and 2 non-oncology clinical trials spanning 5 disease indications, integrating genomics, digital pathology, and clinical data to inform critical clinical decisions on dose selection, patient stratification, and Phase 2/3 trial design.","skills":["Biomarker Development","Computational Biology","Drug Development","Clinical Trials","Statistical Modeling","Data Analysis"]},{"title":"Research Investigator - Computational Biology","company":"MD Anderson Cancer Center","date_range":"2023年11月 - 2025年3月","duration":"1 年 5 个月","location":"美国 德州 休斯顿","description":"- Integrated multi-omics, clinical, and pre-clinical datasets to drive drug discovery programs in partnership with external collaborators on the Therapeutics Research & Drug Discovery platform. \n- Orchestrated cross-functional teams of experimental and data scientists to progress drug development across key modalities, including Antibody-Drug Conjugates (ADCs) and bispecific T-cell engagers. \n- Leveraged statistical modeling and machine learning to elucidate cancer-related mechanisms and support data-driven target discovery and validation. \n- Developed scalable, automated data workflows and pipelines that significantly improved data infrastructure, accessibility, and usability for research and translational teams.\n\n• Integrated multi-omics, clinical, and pre-clinical datasets to drive 4 drug discovery programs in partnership with 3 external collaborators/pharma partners.","skills":["Bioinformatics","Machine Learning","Statistical Modeling","Data Analysis","NGS","Single Cell Sequencing"]},{"title":"Computational Biology Intern","company":"Genentech · 全职","date_range":"2023年5月 - 2023年8月","duration":"4 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"Investigated relapse mechanism in multiple sclerosis (MS) in response to B-cell depletion therapies using single-cell RNA Sequencing gene expression coupled with immune repertoire (BCR/TCR) in Translational Medicine OMNI Biomarker Development team to support drug discovery \n \n- Integrated single-cell transcriptomics with immune repertoire (BCR/TCR) \n- Contributed to a computational pipeline for integration of single-cell datasets \n- Assessed the potentials of biomarker development strategies utilizing the status of clonal hematopoiesis and presented the results to Translational Medicine department team\n\n• Led scRNA-seq and BCR/TCR analysis of MS patients, identifying a CD8+ immune sub-population associated with treatment response, contributing to a published manuscript.","skills":["Bioinformatics","Statistical Modeling","Data Analysis","NGS","Single Cell Sequencing"]},{"title":"Doctoral Researcher","company":"Baylor College of Medicine","date_range":"2018年7月 - 2023年10月","duration":"5 年 4 个月","location":"休斯敦地区","description":"Investigate malignant and non-malignant hematopoietic stem cell biology focusing on epigenetic landscape, during which I am trained in both wet and dry lab biomedical research. \n \n- Performed in Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS) library prep and bioinformatics analysis \n- Established bioinformatics pipelines for various NGS tools (RNAseq, ChIP-seq, and scRNAseq)  \n- Experienced in multi-omics integration (genomics, transcriptomics, and epigenomics) \n- In-depth knowledge across fields including Aging, Immunology, and Oncology \n- Experienced in CRISPR technology and flow cytometry (analyzer and FACS sorting) \n- Trained for stem cell culturing, isolation, and differentiation \n- Led 5 internal and external collaborations including scientists, clinicians, and biotech companies. \n \nAdvisor: Dr. Margaret A. Goodell, Ph.D.\n\n• Performed 15+ molecular, cellular, and in vivo assays to investigate somatic mosaicism of hematopoietic stem cells in aging and hematologic malignancies.","skills":["Bioinformatics","Statistical Modeling","Data Analysis","NGS","Single Cell Sequencing","Epigenetics","DNA methylation","Crispr","Stem Cells","Flow Cytometry"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Principal Scientist - Precision Medicine at Regeneron · 2025年 - 现在 | Research Investigator - Computational Biology at MD Anderson Cancer Center · 2023年 - 2025年 | Computational Biology Intern at Genentech · 2023年 - 2023年 | Doctoral Researcher at Baylor College of Medicine · 2018年 - 2023年 | Scientist at UT Health San Antonio · 2017年 - 2018年 | Summer Intern at University of Science and Technology of China · 2015年 - 2015年 | Undergraduate Researcher at National Tsing Hua University · 2014年 - 2016年 | Marketing Strategist Intern at 4CAREER: Welcome to your career! · 2014年 - 2014年","education":[{"school":"Baylor College of Medicine","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Integrative Molecular and Biomedical Sciences","date_range":"2018年 - 2023年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"清华大学","degree":"Bachelor of Science - BS","field_of_study":"Life Science","date_range":"2012年 - 2016年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Baylor College of Medicine，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2018年 - 2023年 | 清华大学，Bachelor of Science - BS · 2012年 - 2016年 | 保存到项目 | 将Alan保存到项目 | 发消息给Alan | Alan Chen的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":""}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:21:11+08:00","record":{"name":"Bao Jing Chen","current_title":"Head of Clinical Research/ Clinical Research Manager","current_company":"Beacon Hospital · 全职","location":"马来西亚 吉隆坡 WP. Kuala Lumpur","headline":"Clinical Research | Medical Affairs","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/bao-jing-chen-phd","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABbKm2EBDbTcD-bCL92rjuY3q-vaVezQY1g","core_skills":["Pharmaceutical Industry","Research Data Analysis","Anti-inflammatory"],"positions":[{"title":"Head of Clinical Research/ Clinical Research Manager","company":"Beacon Hospital · 全职","date_range":"2022年3月 - 2024年8月","duration":"2 年 6 个月","location":"","description":"• Project management and oversight: responsible for clinical studies management (oncology and hematology) from feasibility, budget negotiation, study startup to study closure in accordance with ICH-GCP and local regulations \n• NDA and CTA review with internal legal department and all relevant parties \n• Clinical studies patient recruitment and retention strategy development \n• Budgeting \n• Line Management\n\n• Primary Point of Contact (POC) for all clinical projects and link between Beacon clinical trial team (CTT) and external collaborative partners, fostering relationship with associated stakeholders/partners. \n• Lead and manage multiple clinical projects, ensuring adherence to scope, timelines, and budget. \n• Prepare site regulatory documents, reviewing for completeness and accuracy. \n• Project management and oversight: responsible for delivering quality studies clinical studies (Oncology and haematology) within assigned timelines by leading end-to-end study from feasibility, budget negotiation, study startup to study closure in accordance with ICH-GCP and local regulations. \n• Plan, manage, and maintain oversight of clinical study execution in accordance with the company program strategy. \n• Prepares and attends bid defense meetings. \n• Manage applicable study vendor activities including CROs, laboratories and medical devices. \n• Contract review: negotiated and obtained fully-executed contracts, ensuring smooth site activation processes. \n• Feasibility and strategy planning: accountable for robust feasibility process and collaborates with Trial Sponsor and Principal Investigators to determine effective strategies to drive patient recruitment and retention. \n• Budget negotiation: communicate and review trial budget to ensure appropriate level of financial oversight. \n• Timely budget updates based on trial changes. \n• Line Management: providing oversight, coaching, and technical support to team managing high-priority and complex clinical trials. \n• Plan and deliver training to study coordinator. \n• Reviews study scope of work, budget, and protocol content, ensuring awareness among the clinical project team. \n• Develops and maintains SOPs and WIs for clinical study monitoring. \n• Collaborates with cross-functional teams to ensure site compliance and delivery according to protocol and regulatory requirements. \n• Plans and leads regular clinical study team calls to provide status updates and ongoing training. \n• Prepare manuscripts and scientific presentations. \n• Served as the point of contact for site's ethics review board (ERB/MREC/regulatory authority) and competent authority (CA) for local independent ethic committee establishment and documents submission.","skills":["Informed Consent","Contract Negotiation","Cancer Research","Clinical Development","Healthcare","Teamwork","Goal Setting","ICH","Trial Management","Trial Master File (TMF)","Clinical Trial Management System (CTMS)","Oncology Clinical Research","Ethics","Clinical Site Management","Budgeting","Project Management","Good Clinical Practice (GCP)"]},{"title":"Medical Science Liaison","company":"Novartis · 全职","date_range":"2020年1月 - 2022年3月","duration":"2 年 3 个月","location":"马来西亚","description":"• Served as a strong advocate for patients by striving to increase disease awareness and resource programs. \n• Researched, collected, and communicated the latest scientific information concerning therapeutic treatment options and the highest standards of care.  \n• Coordinate publications, develop local consensus and local registry.  \n• Lead collaboration with scientific associations for SpA Accelerated Management Program aims to improve SpA patient journey \n• Awarded Champion for APMA (Asia Pacific, Middle East and Africa) Build Innovative Partnership Award 2021 \n• Shortlisted and showcased on global platform for field medical best practice sharing \n• Won Impact Award at the APMA region Field Medical Excellence Village 2021 \n• Received Value and Behaviors (V&B) Award of APMA region Field Medical Excellence Village 2021\n\n• Establish, develop and partner with Health Care Professionals (HCPs) to ensure the appropriate dissemination of clinical and scientific information regarding Novartis’ compounds in a timely, ethical and stakeholder-focused manner. \n• Developed and managed relationships with professional medical leaders and clinicians in Malaysia and Brunei. \n• Served as a rheumatology/ anti-inflammatory expert at key medical and scientific conferences and meetings. \n• Lead the SpA Accelerated Management (SAM) program to improve SpA patient journey and develop local consensus and registry. \n• Provided tailored medical training (disease state and product) to internal colleagues in line with strategy and local needs. \n• Provided scientific educational activities to support study accrual for key trials as appropriate. \n• Participated clinical project management by providing feasibility and research site recommendation for Novartis sponsored clinical trials. \n• Work as a team to assist in set-up, implementation and execution of company-sponsored local clinical studies. \n• Liaised between potential researcher and the company on Investigator initiated trials submission process or requests for research grade substance (Material Transfer Agreements) to support independent clinical/preclinical research.","skills":["Healthcare","Teamwork","Goal Setting","Anti-inflammatory","Rheumatology","pharmaceutical","Medical Affairs","Presentation Skills","Communication"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Head of Clinical Research/ Clinical Research Manager at Beacon Hospital · 2022年 - 2024年 | Medical Science Liaison at Novartis · 2020年 - 2022年","education":[{"school":"Universiti Putra Malaysia","degree":"Research Doctorate","field_of_study":"Molecular Medicine","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Universiti Putra Malaysia","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Biomedical Sciences","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":"3.976"}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Universiti Putra Malaysia，Research Doctorate | Universiti Putra Malaysia，Bachelor's degree | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Clinical Trial Manager Clinical Study Manager Clinical Project Manager 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 马来西亚 新加坡 远程办公: 马来西亚 吉隆坡 WP. Kuala Lumpur 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"中高级 (商务会话)"}],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:21:23+08:00","record":{"name":"Pin-I Chen","current_title":"Research Scientist","current_company":"Stanford University School of Medicine · 全职","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 斯坦福","headline":"Research Scientist at Stanford University","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/pin-i-chen-6959a586","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABJM25EB8J2rxWPrpb_f8MPCsHOAwK5bk2M","core_skills":["Reagent formulation","equipment optimization and protocol writing.","CYTOF","Viral infection"],"positions":[{"title":"Research Scientist","company":"Stanford University School of Medicine · 全职","date_range":"2019年3月 - 现在","duration":"7 年 7 个月","location":"","description":"Using genetically modified T/Treg cell therapies to rebalance immune system in allogeneic bone marrow transplantation and autoimmune disorders, like T1D. \n· Analyzed the cytotoxicity, cytokine profile and proliferation of CAR-transduced Tregs towards their target tissues and discovered a safer choice for CAR Treg therapies in tolerance induction. \n· Established reduced intensity conditioning regimens to improve stem cell or islet engraftment in murine models. \n· Demonstrated therapeutic efficacy of simultaneous alloreactive T cell depletion and shielding of CRISPR-edited Tregs in a murine model of GvHD. \n· Profile the immune signature of T1D patient native Tregs and CAR-transduced Tregs to evaluate the clinical efficacy of CAR-Treg autologous cell transfer for T1D therapy.","skills":["Molecular Cloning","Flow Cytometry","ELISA","Confocal Microscopy","Immunohistochemistry","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction (qPCR)","Cell Culture","Cell Based Assays","Mouse Handling","Immunocytochemistry","Primary Cell Isolation","Bacterial Cell Culture","FACS","RNA-seq","Viral infection","Multi-color Flow Cytometry"]},{"title":"Research Scientist","company":"IncellDx · 全职","date_range":"2017年8月 - 2019年3月","duration":"1 年 8 个月","location":"San Carlos, CA, USA","d