{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:21:50+08:00","record":{"name":"Jia-Yun Chen","current_title":"Research Associate (Lab of Systems Pharmacology)","current_company":"Harvard Medical School","location":"美国","headline":"Research Associate at Harvard Medical School","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jia-yun-chen","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAjC0rIBLqqfZ88DCarwqr4Kl9iKJWwbEKY","core_skills":["Imaging & Microscopy","Molecular & Cell Biology","Genomics & Bioinformatics"],"positions":[{"title":"Research Associate (Lab of Systems Pharmacology)","company":"Harvard Medical School","date_range":"13 年","duration":"4 年 6 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"• Developed and validated innovative one-shot Multiplexed Immunofluorescence (MIF) imaging platforms for kidney and rare cancer diagnostics, successfully demonstrating practical application in patient biopsy diagnosis. \n \n• Engineered targeted MIF panels and established an analysis pipeline to stratify kidney transplant rejection types, enabling precise immune signature categorization. \n \n• Led cross-functional collaborations on spatially-resolved tissue imaging of murine cancer models, identifying key immune regulators of tumorigenesis.\n\n• Developed/validated one-shot MIF imaging platforms for kidney/rare cancer diagnostics in patient biopsies. \n• Engineered MIF panels/analysis pipeline for kidney transplant rejection stratification by immune signature. \n• Collaborated on spatially-resolved tissue imaging of mouse cancer models for immune regulator discovery.","skills":["技能: Research Collaboration • Imaging & Microscopy • Molecular & Cell Biology • Genomics & Bioinformatics • Computational & Data Analysis","Research Collaboration","Imaging & Microscopy","Molecular & Cell Biology","Genomics & Bioinformatics","Computational & Data Analysis","技能: Research Collaboration • Imaging & Microscopy • Molecular & Cell Biology • Screening & Automation • Comput