t biopsy diagnosis. \n \n• Engineered targeted MIF panels and established an analysis pipeline to stratify kidney transplant rejection types, enabling precise immune signature categorization. \n \n• Led cross-functional collaborations on spatially-resolved tissue imaging of murine cancer models, identifying key immune regulators of tumorigenesis.\n\n• Developed/validated one-shot MIF imaging platforms for kidney/rare cancer diagnostics in patient biopsies. \n• Engineered MIF panels/analysis pipeline for kidney transplant rejection stratification by immune signature. \n• Collaborated on spatially-resolved tissue imaging of mouse cancer models for immune regulator discovery.","skills":["技能: Research Collaboration • Imaging & Microscopy • Molecular & Cell Biology • Genomics & Bioinformatics • Computational & Data Analysis","Research Collaboration","Imaging & Microscopy","Molecular & Cell Biology","Genomics & Bioinformatics","Computational & Data Analysis","技能: Research Collaboration • Imaging & Microscopy • Molecular & Cell Biology • Screening & Automation • Computational & Data Analysis","Screening & Automation"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow (Dept. of Chemical and Systems Biology)","company":"Stanford University School of Medicine","date_range":"8 年 1 个月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"Stanford, CA","description":"• Demonstrated dosage-dependent effects of a Down syndrome-related kinase (Dyrk1a) on G1 cell cycle phase duration and variability using live microscopy and single-cell analysis. \n \n• Probed Dyrk1a dosage in Down syndrome patient-derived cell lines, linking protein dosage to pathogenesis. \n \n• Characterized the stoichiometry between cyclin D1 and p21 in controlling proliferation-quiescence decisions using high-content imaging.","skills":["技能: Research Collaboration • Imaging & Microscopy • Molecular & Cell Biology • Genomics & Bioinformatics • Screening & Automation • Computational & Data Analysis","Research Collaboration","Imaging & Micros