{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:22:02+08:00","record":{"name":"Andrew Chen","current_title":"Senior Scientist, Discovery Oncology","current_company":"Merck · 全职","location":"波士顿地区","headline":"Drug discovery biologist and biological engineer","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/andrewchen109","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABJ978ABCiRW5T4ciOu2WSTKXgnj8fQAQLY","core_skills":["Assay Development","Cell Based Assays","Oncology"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Scientist, Discovery Oncology","company":"Merck · 全职","date_range":"2025年3月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 7 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist, Discovery Biology","company":"Kronos Bio","date_range":"5 年 4 个月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"• Drove nine programs in oncology, immuno-oncology and autoimmune disease to go/no-go decisions through target validation, transcriptional network mapping, hit discovery and optimization, target engagement and mechanistic studies. \n• Led discovery biology efforts for four programs involving screening in early discovery phases, hit optimization and mechanistic studies to nominate development candidate KB-7898. \n• Leveraged automated liquid handling robotics for routine high-throughput compound screens (e.g. HiBiT, qPCR, cell viability) to inform medicinal chemistry efforts (SAR studies) and develop miniaturized cell-based assays for oncology and autoimmune disease programs. \n• Developed ex vivo assays utilizing Sjögren’s disease patient PBMCs and healthy human Th17 cells, B cells and PBMCs. \n• Implemented techniques including shRNA / siRNA-mediated knockdown, CRISPR-mediated knock-out / knock-in, lentiviral infection, single cell cloning, transient transfection, electroporation, live cell imaging (Incucyte), transcriptional reporter assays, co-immunoprecipitation, immunoblots, MSD and ELISA. \n• Mentored colleagues on lab techniques and organizational methods. \n• Served as a functional representative to develop automated analyses in the electronic lab notebook and as a safety representative. \n• Managed CRO work for data sets from SHARE-Seq, RNA-Seq, mass spectrometry, bead-based immunoassays and cell viability studies.","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Scientist, Biology","company":"Kronos Bio","date_range":"5 年 4 个月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"• Drove nine programs in oncology, immuno-oncology and autoimmune disease to go/no-go decisions through target validation, transcriptional network mapping, hit discovery and optimization, target engagement and mechanistic studies. \n• Led discovery biology efforts for four programs involving screening in early discovery phases, hit optimization and mechanistic studies to nominate development candidate KB-7898. \n• Leveraged automated liquid handling robotics for routine high-throughput compound screens (e.g. HiBiT, qPCR, cell viability) to inform medicinal chemistry efforts (SAR studies) and develop miniaturized cell-based assays for oncology and autoimmune disease programs. \n• Developed ex vivo assays utilizing Sjögren’s disease patient PBMCs and healthy human Th17 cells, B cells and PBMCs. \n• Implemented techniques including shRNA / siRNA-mediated knockdown, CRISPR-mediated knock-out / knock-in, lentiviral infection, single cell cloning, transient transfection, electroporation, live cell imaging (Incucyte), transcriptional reporter assays, co-immunoprecipitation, immunoblots, MSD and ELISA. \n• Mentored colleagues on lab techniques and organizational methods. \n• Served as a functional representative to develop automated analyses in the electronic lab notebook and as a safety representative. \n• Managed CRO work for data sets from SHARE-Seq, RNA-Seq, mass spectrometry, bead-based immunoassays and cell viability studies.","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Assistant in the Laboratory of Professor Angela N. Koehler","company":"美国麻省理工学院","date_range":"6 年 2 个月","duration":"6 年 2 个月","location":"Cambridge, Massachusetts","description":"• Evaluated lead compounds in a variety of cellular assays. \n• Elucidated mechanism of action and target engagement for lead compounds. \n• Mentored lab members in various biochemistry techniques, small molecule microarray printing and general lab safety.  \n• Conducted high-throughput small molecule microarray screens to identify putative binders of proteins involved in cancer. \n• Managed purchase orders, organized equipment set-up and established a bank of 20 cell lines to help new lab become operational.","skills":[]},{"title":"Teaching Assistant","company":"美国麻省理工学院","date_range":"6 年 2 个月","duration":"6 年 2 个月","location":"Cambridge, Massachusetts","description":"• Evaluated lead compounds in a variety of cellular assays. \n• Elucidated mechanism of action and target engagement for lead compounds. \n• Mentored lab members in various biochemistry techniques, small molecule microarray printing and general lab safety.  \n• Conducted high-throughput small molecule microarray screens to identify putative binders of proteins involved in cancer. \n• Managed purchase orders, organized equipment set-up and established a bank of 20 cell lines to help new lab become operational.","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Scientist, Process Development","company":"Bristol-Myers Squibb","date_range":"2011年10月 - 2013年8月","duration":"1 年 11 个月","location":"Syracuse, New York","description":"• Improved upstream bioprocesses for biologics production with Chinese hamster ovary cells by optimizing bioreactor operating parameters for four projects. \n• Designed advanced cell culture media free of proteins and peptides. \n• Investigated the role of growth factors in cell growth and biologics production.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Senior Scientist, Discovery Oncology at Merck · 2025年 - 现在 | Senior Scientist, Discovery Biology at Kronos Bio · 2022年 - 