{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:22:36+08:00","record":{"name":"Ko-Chien C.","current_title":"PHD Candidate, Cancer Biology","current_company":"UT MD Anderson Cancer Center UTH GSBS · 全职","location":"美国","headline":"Cancer Biology PhD | Translational Oncology Scientist | Functional Genomics, Tumor Resistance & Biomarker Discovery | In Vivo Oncology & Multi-omics","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/kochienchen","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABhVIOABktCmd1PwoIO-0bK8RM0sBiU_sl4","core_skills":["Mammalian cell culture and functional assays","Molecular cloning and gene expression analysis","Experimental design and data analysis"],"positions":[{"title":"PHD Candidate, Cancer Biology","company":"UT MD Anderson Cancer Center UTH GSBS · 全职","date_range":"2019年5月 - 2026年5月","duration":"7 年 1 个月","location":"Houston, Texas","description":"* Investigate how sulfation influences cancer initiation and progression. \n* Employ molecular, cellular, and in vivo approaches to characterize metabolic and signaling mechanisms that govern tumor behavior. \n* Integrate gene editing, multi-omics, and bioinformatics analyses to identify distinct paralogue-specific dependencies with therapeutic implications. \n* Collaborate with academic and industry teams to translate mechanistic findings into potential intervention strategies. \n\n\n• Defined distinct and nonredundant functions of key enzymes (PAPSS1 and PAPSS2) in the sulfation pathway, challenging the prevailing assumptions of paralogue equivalence in cancer. \n• Identified PAPSS1 as a context-specific oncogenic dependency in PTEN-null cancers, establishing its potential as a therapeutic target. \n• Further investigated residual tumor growth following pathway disruption, revealing adaptive survival mechanisms and secondary vulnerabilities. \n• Integrated genetic perturbation, RNA-sequencing, and tissue-level analyses to connect tumor cell states with microenvironmental responses, informing mechanisms of therapeutic response and resistance. \n• Demonstrated that sulfation paralogue enzyme constrains tumor progression, in part through enhanced immune surveillance.","skills":[]},{"title":"Research Assistant","company":"台湾大学","date_range":"5 年 1 个月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"台湾 台北市","description":"* Studied molecular mechanisms underlying breast cancer progression using proteomic and miRNA profiling. \n* Applied mass spectrometry (LC–MS, LA-ICP-MS) and synchrotron-based imaging for biomarker discovery and tissue analysis. \n* Collaborated with academic and industry partners on exosome biomarker research in breast cancer.\n\n• Conducted translational biomarker discovery in cross-institutional and international collaborations, including partnership with academic laboratories (National Cancer Center Japan) and industry (Toray Industries), using exosomal miRNA profiling from breast cancer patient plasma across multiple TNM stages and molecular subtypes (DCIS, ER+, PR+, HER2+, TNBC). \n• Prepared tumor tissues and plasma-derived exosomes for advanced molecular imaging and mass spectrometry-based analyses (MALDI, LC-MS, LA-ICP-MS) enabling cross-platform data integration to support translational diagnostics.","skills":[]},{"title":"Master Student","company":"台湾大学","date_range":"5 年 1 个月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"台湾 台北市","description":"* Studied molecular mechanisms underlying breast cancer progression using proteomic and miRNA profiling. \n* Applied mass spectrometry (LC–MS, LA-ICP-MS) and synchrotron-based imaging for biomarker discovery and tissue analysis. \n* Collaborated with academic and industry partners on exosome biomarker research in breast cancer.\n\n• Conducted translational biomarker discovery in cross-institutional and international collaborations, including partnership with academic laboratories (National Cancer Center Japan) and industry (Toray Industries), using exosomal miRNA profiling from breast cancer patient plasma across multiple TNM stages and molecular subtypes (DCIS, ER+, PR+, HER2+, TNBC). \n• Prepared tumor tissues and plasma-derived exosomes for advanced molecular imaging and mass spectrometry-based analyses (MALDI, LC-MS, LA-ICP-MS) enabling cross-platform data integration to support translational diagnostics.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | PHD Candidate, Cancer Biology at UT MD Anderson Cancer Center UTH GSBS · 2019年 - 2026年 | Research Assistant at National Taiwan University · 2015年 - 2018年 | Master Student at National Taiwan University · 2013年 - 2015年","education":[{"school":"UT MD Anderson UTHealth Houston Graduate School of Biomedical Sciences","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Cancer Biology","date_range":"2018年 - 2025年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"台湾大学","degree":"Anatomy and Cell Biology","field_of_study":"Developmental Neuroscience","date_range":"2015年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"The University of British Columbia","degree":"Bachelor of Science (B.Sc.)","field_of_study":"Life Science","date_range":"2012年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | UT MD Anderson UTHealth Houston Graduate School of Biomedical Sciences，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2018年 - 2025年 | 台湾大学，Anatomy and Cell Biology · 2015年 | The University of British Columbia，Bachelor of Science (B.Sc.) · 2012年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Scientist Research And Development Scientist Postdoctoral Scientist Biomedical Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿 旧金山湾区 美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥 美国 德州 休斯顿 美国 北卡罗来纳州 达勒姆 远程办公: 美国 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
