{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:22:58+08:00","record":{"name":"Wendy Chen","current_title":"Senior Scientist (In Vivo Pharmacology / Oncology)","current_company":"安进","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 南旧金山","headline":"In Vivo Pharmacology / Oncology @ Amgen South SF","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/wendy-s-chen","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAA4bu1YBVdeBAci8Y-I5jShKTNylyE5l5oI","core_skills":["Mouse Surgery","Animal Husbandry","GraphPad Prism"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Scientist (In Vivo Pharmacology / Oncology)","company":"安进","date_range":"4 年 11 个月","duration":"2 年","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 南旧金山","description":"Design and execute in vivo studies in support of Amgen Oncology's preclinical pipeline programs of multiple modalities at various stages of preclinical development. Primary experience in large molecule programs, secondary experience in small molecules. \nReported study results for IND applications (2) and patents (2). \n \nOrganizer for group-wide and site-wide social and networking activities at Amgen.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist (In Vivo Pharmacology / Oncology)","company":"安进","date_range":"4 年 11 个月","duration":"2 年","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 南旧金山","description":"Design and execute in vivo studies in support of Amgen Oncology's preclinical pipeline programs of multiple modalities at various stages of preclinical development. Primary experience in large molecule programs, secondary experience in small molecules. \nReported study results for IND applications (2) and patents (2). \n \nOrganizer for group-wide and site-wide social and networking activities at Amgen.","skills":[]},{"title":"Graduate Student (PhD program)","company":"University of California San Diego · 全职","date_range":"2015年9月 - 2021年11月","duration":"6 年 3 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","description":"Graduate Studies in Dr. Gen-Sheng Feng's Lab \nMy graduate study is on mechanisms of liver cancer development using murine and in vitro models. Specifically looking at microenvironmental and cell-intrinsic modifications after genetic manipulation, in relation to tumor development. \nManuscript title: Single Cell Transcriptomics Reveals Opposite Roles of Shp2 in Myc-driven Liver Tumor Cells and Microenvironment (Cell Reports) \nSpecific key terms: Hepatocellular Carcinoma, cMyc, Shp2, B-catenin, macrophage polarization. \n \nCo-lab manager: Lab safety, IACUC mouse protocols, Controlled Substances, Lab Safety, properly documented lab resources and general management of existing lab processes and implementing additional procedures.","skills":[]},{"title":"Staff Research Associate II","company":"UCSF Diabetes Center · 全职","date_range":"2014年9月 - 2015年7月","duration":"11 个月","location":"San Francisco, CA","description":"SRAII at Dr. Anil Bhushan's Lab at the UCSF Diabetes Center.  \nSet up lab at UCSF by purchasing of necessary materials, wrote IACUC and BUA protocols, managed mouse transfer, \nLab Managerial role: Take responsibility to manage daily operations of lab including lab safety, lab supplies and equipment, organization, and maintaining mouse colonies. \nAlso perform consistent islet isolation procedure for all lab members, assist postdocs in projects.","skills":[]},{"title":"Staff Research Associate I","company":"UCLA Dept of Medicine, Endocrinology","date_range":"2014年3月 - 2014年9月","duration":"7 个月","location":"Los Angeles, CA, USA","description":"SRA I at Dr. Anil Bhushan's Lab at UCLA. Lab Technician duties involved lab management, lab safety, chemical inventory. Lab's main mouse contact, and maintained a mouse colony of 400+ cages with 15+ strains. Other duties include tissue collection, pancreas and islets, and techniques such as RRBS.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Senior Scientist (In Vivo Pharmacology / Oncology) at Amgen · 2024年 - 现在 | Scientist (In Vivo Pharmacology / Oncology) at Amgen · 2021年 - 2024年 | Graduate Student (PhD program) at University of California San Diego · 2015年 - 2021年 | Staff Research Associate II at UCSF Diabetes Center · 2014年 - 2015年 | Staff Research Associate I at UCLA Dept of Medicine, Endocrinology · 2014年 - 2014年 | Research Assistant I at UCLA Department of Medicine · 2012年 - 2014年 | Undergraduate Intern at Amgen Inc. · 2012年 - 2012年","education":[{"school":"美国加州大学圣迭戈分校","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Biology/Biological Sciences, General","date_range":"2015年 - 2021年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"美国加州大学洛杉矶分校","degree":"","field_of_study":"","date_range":"2010年 - 2014年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 美国加州大学圣迭戈分校，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2015年 - 2021年 | 美国加州大学洛杉矶分校 · 2010年 - 2014年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Senior Scientist Research And Development Scientist Principal Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 旧金山湾区 开始日期 我在随便看看，时间可灵活安排 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:23:12+08:00","record":{"name":"Zeming Chen, Ph.D., MD","current_title":"Associate Director of Process Development","current_company":"Aurion Biotech · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","headline":"Accelerating Innovation to cGMP-Ready Cell Therapies | Regenerative Medicine | First-in-human Through Pivotal Trials | System Builder | People Developer I Ambivert I Scuba Diver","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/zeming-chen-phd","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAG6woQBlNsF-1yaif7FzU2upjS8jtIEvgU","core_skills":["Inventor Engagement","solid tumor","Medical teaching"],"positions":[{"title":"Associate Director of Process Development","company":"Aurion Biotech · 全职","date_range":"2024年9月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 1 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"1. Led the Process Characterization (PC) program to advance readiness for Process Validation (PV), Process Performance Qualification (PPQ), and large-scale commercial manufacturing of a human corneal endothelial cell (hCEC)-derived allogeneic cell/small-molecule combination therapy. \n2. Optimized the clinical manufacturing process, championed technology transfer, and developed a comprehensive multiple-day training program to derisk the ASTRA Phase 3 pivotal trial, delivered a reusable training package for future Technology Transfer and internal/external On-The-Job (OJT) training.  \n3. Expand organizational capability and resilience by recruiting one-third of the Process Development team and empowering team members to establish six self-managed working groups that improved operational efficiency, data analysis, cost-effective testing management, and knowledge sharing. \n3. Forecasted and coordinated critical starting materials to overcome resource constraints, ensuring timely execution of the PC program and other key R&D initiatives.","skills":["Team Development"]},{"title":"Principal Scientist, Cell Therapy Process Development","company":"Intellia Therapeutics, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2022年7月 - 2024年1月","duration":"1 年 7 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"Led clinical-scale cell therapy process development team, developing and optimizing autologous and allergenic CRISPR-edited cell therapy platforms with significant improvement in output and Cost-of-Goods (COG) reduction.  \n \n• 1. Achieved a 30% higher viable cell yield, a 15% increase in cell viability, and a 70% Cost Of Goods (COG) reduction per clinical-scale manufacturing run. Streamlined the process, reducing the need for additional cell processors. \n• 2. Managed and guided a high-performing team of 4 to 6 (two direct reports had their co-op or intern), consistently delivering amid rapidly changing priorities and resource constraints.  \n• 3. Actively contributed to CDMO vetting, Bid Defense meetings, site selection visits, and tech transfer activities. \n• 4. Defined project timelines and provided input for cost prediction, COG reduction, and budgets. Strategically mapped and prioritized development activities for efficient clinical-scale manufacturing. \n• 5. Tracked and trended process performance through a 6000+ data point tracker, analyzing different process scales to identify major areas for improvement/innovation.  \n• 6. Drove change and innovation, influencing not only my team but also spearheading the introduction of new technologies across departments by fostering collaborations among Research and Technical Operations departments and external SMEs.","skills":["Team Development","Presentations","Nanoparticles","Technical Leadership","Problem Solving","Attention to Detail","Study Reports","Stakeholder Management","solid tumor","Leadership Development","Protocol Development","Cell & Gene Therapy","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Technology Transfer","Closed system GMP manufacturing","Research and Development (R&D)","Hematology","CAR-T","Data Management","Process Improvement","Immuno-oncology","Data Analysis","CDMO","Analytical Skills","Cancer Research","Viral Transduction","Flow Cytometry","People Development"]},{"title":"Senior Manager, Cellular Process Development","company":"Editas Medicine · 全职","date_range":"2021年6月 - 2022年7月","duration":"1 年 2 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"Led Cellular Process Development team for CRISPR-edited stem cell therapy for severe sickle cell disease (SCD) and transfusion-dependent- beta-thalassemia (TDT), played a pivotal role in the successful engraftment of Cas12a-edited HSC for first-in-human during the RUBY trial.  \n \n• 1. Overcame the challenges of adapting the clinical-scale manufacturing process to work robustly for the patient cells (EDIT 301 program) in a very intense timeline. \n• 2. Managed and completed 15 PD projects within a year, with the scope expanding from Drug Substance Isolation to Drug Product infusion and all the pertaining technical documentation (Mater Batch Records (MBRs), SOPs, Technical Reports, and Memos.) \n• 3. Championed technology transfer, training, troubleshooting, and clinical manufacturing support. Collaborated closely with Internal Manufacturing, external CDMO, Quality, CMC Regulatory, and Supply Chain Management daily.  \n• 4. Strategically designed, planed and let the PD team to support the implementation of the comprability study of a major process change and the delivery of technical report; spearheaded the timely completion of Major Change Controls which involve six functional departments.  \n5. Collaborated with Quality Assurance (QA), Quality Control (QC), and IMG to address and resolve any quality issues related to clinical manufacturing processes; Represented Cell PD SME in the deviation investigation, CAPAs, and change controls. \n• 6. Recruited and mentored junior lab members, fostering an environment encouraging active learning and cross-functional training.","skills":["Team Development","Presentations","Technical Leadership","Problem Solving","Attention to Detail","Study Reports","Stakeholder Management","Stem Cell Therapy","Protocol Development","Cell & Gene Therapy","Cross-functional Team Leadership","Technology Transfer","Rare Diseases","Closed system GMP manufacturing","Research and Development (R&D)","Hematology","Data Management","Drug Development","cGMP manufacturing","Process Improvement","Data Analysis","CDMO","Quality Management","Cross-functional Collaborations","SOP Development","Analytical Skills"]},{"title":"Process Development Scientist","company":"Tessa Therapeutics Ltd · 全职","date_range":"2019年8月 - 2021年6月","duration":"1 年 11 个月","location":"休斯敦地区","description":"As the department's second hire, spearheaded the establishment of the Tessa Cell Therapy Process Development Lab, creating a closed-system manufacturing process entirely from scratch.  \n \n1. Developed and optimized a cGMP-compliant, closed-system clinical manufacturing process for a pivotal CAR-T trial within a year, achieving a 40% increase in transduction efficiency and a 50% enhancement in engineered CAR-T cell expansion. \n2. Planned, designed, and executed 13 clinical-scale runs (development runs and engineering runs) and the analytical evaluation during the COVID-19 outbreak, ensuring successful tech transfer and troubleshooting processes with the MSAT team and CDMO in three continents.  \n3. Established close collaboration with the CMC regulatory team, directly contributed to the data package assembly for FDA type B and type C meetings, and ensured acceptance of comparability studies between the phase 1/2 trial process vs. the pivotal trial process. \n4. Demonstrated supply chain expertise by negotiating with vendors, achieving a 40% cost reduction for a critical reagent, and effectively managing procurement.","skills":["Team Development","Presentations","Technical Leadership","Attention to Detail","Study Reports","Stakeholder Management","Regulatory Interactions","Protocol Development","Cell & Gene Therapy","Technology Transfer","Closed system GMP manufacturing","Research and Development (R&D)","CAR-T","Data Management","Drug Development","Biomarkers","cGMP manufacturing","Process Improvement","Immuno-oncology","Data Analysis","CDMO","Quality Management","Cross-functional Collaborations","Analytical Skills","Cancer Research","Viral Transduction","Flow Cytometry","Leadership"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Associate Director of Process Development at Aurion Biotech · 2024年 - 现在 | Principal Scientist, Cell Therapy Process Development at Intellia Therapeutics, Inc. · 2022年 - 2024年 | Senior Manager, Cellular Process Development at Editas Medicine · 2021年 - 2022年 | Process Development Scientist at Tessa Therapeutics Ltd · 2019年 - 2021年 | Postdoctoral Research Fellow at MD Anderson Cancer Center · 2012年 - 2014年 | Graduate Research Assistant at University of Texas Medical Branch · 2005年 - 2011年 | Resident Physician in Cardiology/Internal Medicine at The 2nd Affiliated Hospital of Guangzhou Medical University · 2000年 - 2003年","education":[{"school":"The University of Texas Medical Branch","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Microbiology and Immunology","date_range":"","activities":"活动与社团: James McLaughlin Pre-doctoral fellow Graduate School of Biomedical Science (GSBS) Ph.D. program admission committee, student delegate American Society of Virology Received 10 honors and awards during PhD training (please see selected honors in Awards )","grade":""},{"school":"Guangzhou Medical University","degree":"MD","field_of_study":"Medicine","date_range":"","activities":"活动与社团: President of Medical Student Association","grade":"Magna Cum Laude"},{"school":"MD Anderson Cancer Center","degree":"Postdoctoral Training","field_of_study":"Immuno-Oncology","date_range":"2012年 - 2014年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | The University of Texas Medical Branch，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD | Guangzhou Medical University，MD | MD Anderson Cancer Center ，Postdoctoral Training · 2012年 - 2014年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Director Senior Director 职位性质 兼职 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥 美国 德州 休斯顿 远程办公: 美国 开始日期 我在随便看看，时间可灵活安排 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公 远程办公"],"languages":[{"name":"English","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":false,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:23:25+08:00","record":{"name":"Jay (Jiamin) Chen","current_title":"Associate Director","current_company":"Shinobi Therapeutics","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 南旧金山","headline":"NGS | Analytical Development | Biomarkers | Single-Cell Omics | Gene & Cell Therapy","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jay-jiamin-chen-5a238a7b","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABD2osoBeG7imxv-LP7JpAwAeaUkrujmHo4","core_skills":["WGS","Off-target identification","Single-cell Omics"],"positions":[{"title":"Associate Director","company":"Shinobi Therapeutics","date_range":"2 年 6 个月","duration":"9 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"Genomics lead. MCB clone selection, product safety and understanding.","skills":["技能: WGS • Off-target identification • RNAseq Analysis • NGS • Droplet Digital PCR (ddPCR)","WGS","Off-target identification","RNAseq Analysis","NGS","Droplet Digital PCR (ddPCR)"]},{"title":"Senior Principal Scientist","company":"Shinobi Therapeutics","date_range":"2 年 6 个月","duration":"9 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"Genomics lead. MCB clone selection, product safety and understanding.","skills":["技能: WGS • Off-target identification • RNAseq Analysis • NGS • Droplet Digital PCR (ddPCR)","WGS","Off-target identification","RNAseq Analysis","NGS","Droplet Digital PCR (ddPCR)"]},{"title":"Principal Scientist | Genomic Molecular Analytics | PPD","company":"Allogene Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2021年7月 - 2024年2月","duration":"2 年 8 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 南旧金山","description":"• Lead a genomic team focused on enhancing the development and understanding of CAR T cells. \n• Act as the NGS and genomic SME within the organization and draft related technical reports. Collaborate closely with teams in PPD, Research, QC, IT, and Translational Sciences on various projects.  \n• Manage CROs and external consultants for assay development and associated data analysis/transfer. \n• Oversee the development of analytical pipelines to determine on-target genome editing efficiency and to predict potential off-target loci for IND submission and BLA readiness.  \n• Leverage single-cell omics techniques (RNA-seq, CITE-seq, TCR clonality) to characterize donor materials, in-process samples, drug products (DPs), and CAR T cell potency following extended target stimulation. Provide the comprehensive landscape of the donor heterogeneity and process impact on CAR T expansion and persistence. \n• Spearhead the establishment of a state-of-the-art NGS core, and implement a GUI-based single-cell visualization and analytical platform within the organization.  \n• Experience in developing cell-based potency assays and cytokine detection assays.  \n• Perform discover-seq based ChIP-seq assay to unbiasedly profile genome-wide off-target sites. Develop in-house targeted amplicon sequencing assays for on-/off-target validation. \n• Lead the development and optimization of a single cell DNA sequencing assay for targeted amplicon sequencing and structural variant detection. \n• Implement Oxford Nanopore Technologies (ONT) long-read whole genome sequencing to investigate structural variations in activated T cell and drug product during the clinical hold. Lead the assay development for target enrichment. \n• Employ a combination of ONT direct RNA sequencing and Illumina-based NGS for assessing the identity and integrity of nucleic acid based raw materials, such as TALEN mRNAs and lentiviral vectors.\n\n• Optimize a Cas9-based target enrichment assay to enhance variant detection (200X) by ONT sequencing. \n• Supervise the implementation of a Benchling-based LIMS for workflows related to NGS library preparation and sequencing.","skills":["Single-cell Omics","Technical Reports","Project Management","People Management","Amazon Web Services (AWS)","DNA Extraction","Sequence Analysis","Genomics","CRO Management","Independent Research","Cell Therapy","AWS SageMaker","Biomarker Discovery","Nanopore Sequencing","Molecular Oncology","Data Analysis","Genetics","NGS"]},{"title":"Staff Scientist | Hanlee Ji Lab","company":"Stanford University School of Medicine · 全职","date_range":"2014年8月 - 2021年7月","duration":"7 年","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 斯坦福","description":"• Identified distinct cell types and niche signaling in a primary gastric organoid model using single cell RNAseq and RNA in situ hybridization (Project lead). \n• Applied CRISPR/Cas9 functional screening to identify kinases and associated pathways that modulate FGFR inhibitor response in gastric cancer (Project lead). \n• Established a novel ex vivo tissue culture system for immune modulation and characterized perturbations across immune cells within the tissue (Project lead). \n• Characterized the functional impact of a novel gene mutation in the autophagy pathway (Project lead). \n• Identified cell types and immune repertoires in PBMCs associated with immune-related adverse events upon checkpoint blockade using single cell sequencing (Project lead, in collaboration with Intermountain Health). \n• Profiled microbiomes in gastric mucosa using 16s metagenomics (Project lead). \n• Performed the sequencing assays and droplet digital PCR based copy number detection to resolve genomic structural variations in gastric cancer. \n• Conducted the sequencing related experiments in the studies that examined lymphomas (in collaboration with Ron Levy lab) and GI cancers using single cell sequencing. \n• Collaborated with a team in Electrical Engineering to assess drug efficacy using a novel lab-on-a-chip platform \n• Conducted molecular genetic analysis in the study profiled SARS-CoV-2 mutational fingerprints from patients \n• Established the tissue culture and molecular cloning systems in the lab.  \n• Provided technical feedbacks to Illumina,10X genomics, and BD during sequencing product development. \n• Experience with informed consent forms, laboratory SOPs, and data transfer agreements related to clinical studies. \n• Mentored over 10 summer students, research assistants, visiting scholars and postdoc trainees.","skills":["Single-cell Omics","People Management","DNA Extraction","Sequence Analysis","Genomics","Translational Science","Independent Research","Biomarker Discovery","Molecular Oncology","Precision Medicine","Western Blotting","Flow Cytometry","Cell Biology","Molecular Biology","Cell Culture","Cancer Research","Data Analysis","Genetics","Single cell RNA-seq","organoid culture (\"mini-organ\" in vitro)","Crispr","NGS","Cancer Genomics","ex vivo model","Droplet Digital PCR (ddPCR)"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Fellow | David Huntsman Lab","company":"BC Cancer Agency","date_range":"2012年6月 - 2014年8月","duration":"2 年 3 个月","location":"加拿大 英属哥伦比亚 温哥华","description":"• Characterized recurrent “Hotspot” mutations and their impacts on microRNA expression and transcriptome profile in cancer using NGS technologies. \n• Established isogenic DICER-/- cell lines using adeno-associated virus mediated gene targeting and CRISPR/Cas9. \n• Performed experiments and conducted data analysis, including TCGA/cBioPortal genomic data analysis, patient tumor collection, DNA/RNA extraction, Fluidigm Access Array for amplicon preparation, Illumina targeted resequencing, small RNA deep sequencing, sanger sequencing, real-time PCR, gene expression array, NanoString based gene expression, IncuCyte cell analysis, and cell-based functional studies.","skills":["DNA Extraction","Sequence Analysis","Genomics","Translational Science","Independent Research","RNAseq Analysis","miRNA","Molecular Oncology","Western Blotting","Cell Biology","Molecular Biology","Cell Culture","Cancer Research","Data Analysis","NGS","Cancer Genomics"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Associate Director at Shinobi Therapeutics · 2026年 - 现在 | Senior Principal Scientist at Shinobi Therapeutics · 2024年 - 2026年 | Principal Scientist | Genomic Molecular Analytics | PPD at Allogene Therapeutics · 2021年 - 2024年 | Staff Scientist