{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:23:59+08:00","record":{"name":"Zhishan Chen","current_title":"Computational Biologist","current_company":"Novo Nordisk · 全职","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 列克星敦","headline":"Computational Biologist @ Novo Nordisk | Drug Discovery | Translating human genetics into actionable biological insights and drug hypotheses.","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhishan-chen-314b9b136","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACFHiQAByzqzvs_8MYjFmngpEE-YNw8mM-Y","core_skills":["Development Biology","WGS","TWAS"],"positions":[{"title":"Computational Biologist","company":"Novo Nordisk · 全职","date_range":"2023年12月 - 现在","duration":"2 年 10 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 列克星敦","description":"Leveraging human genetics to discover and validate drug target candidates for metabolic diseases\n\n• Build and maintain reproducible human genetics datasets and analysis workflows supporting target concept, mechanism, and safety assessment across discovery programs. \n• Nominated two siRNA therapeutic targets by integrating genetic and functional evidence into decision-ready recommendations for biology and translational teams. \n• Design and lead scalable fine-mapping, TWAS, and single-cell initiatives; apply Linux/HPC and AWS resources to process large biological datasets. \n• Generate analysis summaries, visualizations, and presentations for project teams and senior leadership, influencing target prioritization and program direction. \n• Serve as a computational genetics expert in cross-functional discussions, aligning analyses with experimental strategy, data quality expectations, and research milestones.","skills":[]},{"title":"Staff Scientist","company":"Vanderbilt University Medical Center","date_range":"6 年 2 个月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"Nashville, TN","description":"• Develop standard bioinformatic pipelines for mRNA-seq and miRNA-seq \n• Analyze of ~900 mRNA-seq and ~400 miRNA-seq data from colorectal cancers (CRC) \n• Lead the transcriptome wide association study (TWAS) to identify susceptibility genes for CRC risk \n• Lead the fine-mapping project in the international CRC consortium, integrated large-scale GWAS data and public functional genomic data to uncover potential causal genes underlying CRC genetic susceptibility\n\n• Led fine-mapping, QTL, and functional-genomics integration to nominate causal genes for colorectal cancer and prioritize follow-up biology. \n• Built RNA-seq and microRNA-seq analysis pipelines supporting causal gene and microRNA discovery in cancer genetics programs. \n• Applied TWAS and transcriptomic integration to identify candidate genes and microRNAs; interpreted results in the context of disease mechanisms. \n• Produced reproducible outputs, figures, and scientific summaries for collaborative studies with high attention to data quality and method documentation.","skills":[]},{"title":"postdoctoral fellow","company":"Vanderbilt University Medical Center","date_range":"6 年 2 个月","duration":"3 年 1 个月","location":"Nashville, TN","description":"• Develop standard bioinformatic pipelines for mRNA-seq and miRNA-seq \n• Analyze of ~900 mRNA-seq and ~400 miRNA-seq data from colorectal cancers (CRC) \n• Lead the transcriptome wide association study (TWAS) to identify susceptibility genes for CRC risk \n• Lead the fine-mapping project in the international CRC consortium, integrated large-scale GWAS data and public functional genomic data to uncover potential causal genes underlying CRC genetic susceptibility\n\n• Led fine-mapping, QTL, and functional-genomics integration to nominate causal genes for colorectal cancer and prioritize follow-up biology. \n• Built RNA-seq and microRNA-seq analysis pipelines supporting causal gene and microRNA discovery in cancer genetics programs. \n• Applied TWAS and transcriptomic integration to identify candidate genes and microRNAs; interpreted results in the context of disease mechanisms. \n• Produced reproducible outputs, figures, and scientific summaries for collaborative studies with high attention to data quality and method documentation.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Computational Biologist at Novo Nordisk · 2023年 - 现在 | Staff Scientist at Vanderbilt University Medical Center · 2020年 - 2023年 | postdoctoral fellow at Vanderbilt University Medical Center · 2017年 - 2020年","education":[{"school":"北京大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Botany/Plant Biology","date_range":"2010年 - 2016年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"华侨大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Biotechnology","date_range":"2006年 - 2010年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 北京大学，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2010年 - 2016年 | 华侨大学，Bachelor's degree · 2006年 - 2010年 | 保存到项目 | 将Zhishan保存到项目 | 发消息给Zhishan | Zhishan Chen的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:24:11+08:00","record":{"name":"Xiaowen Chen, PhD","current_title":"Senior Bioinformatics Scientist","current_company":"ViiV Healthcare · 全职","location":"美国","headline":"Computational Biologist | Bioinformatics | Multi-omics | Cancer Research | Cardio-metabolic Diseases | NGS | ML","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/xiaowen-chen-phd-035431163","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAACcKWekBHuOu7kx2CDGlLtvWqAAcjcXUVl4","core_skills":["cardio-metabolic diseases","TCGA","CCLE","non-coding RNA"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Bioinformatics Scientist","company":"ViiV Healthcare · 全职","date_range":"2024年12月 - 现在","duration":"1 年 10 个月","location":"","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist II","company":"Merck · 全职","date_range":"2022年6月 - 2024年8月","duration":"2 年 3 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 南旧金山","description":"Worked within an interdisciplinary team of scientists to perform and support bioinformatic analysis of multi-omics data (microarrays, bulk RNA-seq, single-cell RNA-seq, DRUG-seq, Infinium Methylation microarrays, metabolomics, proteomics, lipidomics) to understand disease biology, identify therapeutic mechanisms of action, and discover/validate new targets or biomarkers.","skills":["cardio-metabolic diseases","Amazon Web Services (AWS)","Metabolomics","Proteomics","Real World Data (RWD)","Machine Learning","Public Speaking"]},{"title":"Research Scientist","company":"The Jackson Laboratory","date_range":"5 年 3 个月","duration":"1 年 6 个月","location":"美国 康乃狄克州","description":"• Led computational analysis to study the source of epigenetic heterogeneity in AML using microarray, RNA-seq, and Bisulfite sequencing data from AML patients, mouse models, patient-derived xenograft models. \n• Analyzed TET2 deficiency impact on cytosine methylation patterning and aberrant transcriptional regulation in GC B-cells in mice and DLBCL patients. \n• Developed deep learning models to predict gene expression change in AML comparing with normal controls utilizing bulk RNA-seq and ATAC-seq and built gene regulatory network. \n• Conducted integrative single-cell multi-omics analysis to study aging and clonal hematopoiesis influence the propensity of blood stem cells to adapt to altered environments. \n• Utilized HiC and PCHiC data to identify the key 3D genomics features of Tet2-mutated blood stem cells that change with age.","skills":["技能: Docker • Netflow • deep learning application • chromosomal structure • Single Cell Sequencing","Docker","Netflow","deep learning application","chromosomal structure","Single Cell Sequencing","技能: Keras • Deep Learning • Epigenetics • Python (Programming Language)","Keras","Deep Learning","Epigenetics","Python (Programming Language)"]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Associate","company":"The Jackson Laboratory","date_range":"5 年 3 个月","duration":"1 年 6 个月","location":"美国 康乃狄克州","description":"• Led computational analysis to study the source of epigenetic heterogeneity in AML using microarray, RNA-seq, and Bisulfite sequencing data from AML patients, mouse models, patient-derived xenograft models. \n• Analyzed TET2 deficiency impact on cytosine methylation patterning and aberrant transcriptional regulation in GC B-cells in mice and DLBCL patients. \n• Developed deep learning models to predict gene expression change in AML comparing with normal controls utilizing bulk RNA-seq and ATAC-seq and built gene regulatory network. \n• Conducted integrative single-cell multi-omics analysis to study aging and clonal hematopoiesis influence the propensity of blood stem cells to adapt to altered environments. \n• Utilized HiC and PCHiC data to identify the key 3D genomics features of Tet2-mutated blood stem cells that change with age.","skills":["技能: Docker • Netflow • deep learning application • chromosomal structure • Single Cell Sequencing","Docker","Netflow","deep learning application","chromosomal structure","Single Cell Sequencing","技能: Keras • Deep Learning • Epigenetics • Python (Programming Language)","Keras","Deep Learning","Epigenetics","Python (Programming Language)"]},{"title":"Associate Professor","company":"Harbin Medical University · 全职","date_range":"2013年9月 - 2017年4月","duration":"3 年 8 个月","location":"中国 黑龙江省 哈尔滨","description":"1. Led a research team focused on developing methodologies in computational systems biology and and applying statistical models to study regulatory mechanism of non-coding RNAs in cancer diagnosis and therapy, drug resistance, and identify biomarkers of adverse drug reactions. \n2. Taught Linear Algebra, Operations Research and Numerical Analysis. \n3. Guided 2 graduate students to publish 4 scientific publications, leading to their academic and professional success.","skills":["Systems Biology","TCGA, CCLE","non-coding RNA","pharmagenomics","drug response","Cancer Research"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Senior Bioinformatics Scientist at ViiV Healthcare · 2024年 - 现在 | Senior Scientist II at Merck · 2022年 - 2024年 | Research Scientist at The Jackson Laboratory · 2021年 - 2022年 | Postdoctoral Associate at The Jackson Laboratory · 2017年 - 2020年 | Associate Professor at Harbin Medical University · 2013年 - 2017年","education":[{"school":"哈尔滨医科大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Bioinformatics","date_range":"2008年 - 2011年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"哈尔滨工业大学","degree":"Master's degree","field_of_study":"Mathematics","date_range":"2004年 - 2006年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"哈尔滨师范大学","degree":"Bachelor's degree","field_of_study":"Mathematics","date_range":"2000年 - 2004年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | 哈尔滨医科大学，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2008年 - 2011年 | 哈尔滨工业大学，Master's degree · 2004年 - 2006年 | 哈尔滨师范大学，Bachelor's degree · 2000年 - 2004年 | 保存到项目 | 将Xiaowen保存到项目 | 发消息给Xiaowen | Xiaowen Chen, PhD的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
