{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:26:16+08:00","record":{"name":"Yu-Ching (Ashley) Chen, Ph.D.","current_title":"Quality Control Manager","current_company":"iCell Gene Therapeutics","location":"美国 维吉尼亚州 夏洛茨维尔","headline":"Biochemistry Ph.D. with 15+ years of experience in biochemistry and molecular biology including multi-omics, bioassays and platforms development, cell line development and engineering, and protein expression systems.","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ashley-yu-ching-chen","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAA9RoroB15L7zy1R9s1L6BPE4cpQkkd2M1g","core_skills":["Octet® R Series: Label-Free Biomolecular Interaction Analysis","Immunoprecipitation","Assay Development"],"positions":[{"title":"Quality Control Manager","company":"iCell Gene Therapeutics","date_range":"2 年 3 个月","duration":"9 个月","location":"美国 维吉尼亚州 夏洛茨维尔","description":"• Developed and optimized CAR-T cell manufacturing workflows, employing advanced molecular cloning and flow cytometry-based isolation to generate diverse therapeutic cell libraries, including BCMA-CD19 CAR-T therapies for autoimmune diseases. \n• Executed CAR-T manufacturing in a cGMP facility, including T cell activation, retroviral transduction, expansion, and tumor cell coculture. \n• Conducted QC testing using ELISA, qPCR, and flow cytometry to assess potency, purity, and stability. \n• Authored and reviewed cGMP-compliant SOPs and Batch Production Records (BPRs), supporting regulatory submissions and contributing to successful FDA IND approvals. \n• Assisted in bioanalytical assay development and method validation per cell and gene therapy regulatory standards. \n• Performed QC testing on raw materials and final products, including sterility, identity, potency, and endotoxin assays. \n• Conducted environmental and in-process monitoring, maintained instruments, validated methods, and analyzed results to ensure compliance and product quality.","skills":["技能: Analytical Method Validation • Quality Control • Gene Therapy • Chemistry, Manufacturing, and Controls (CMC) • cGMP manufacturing","Analytical Method Validation","Quality Control","Gene Therapy","Chemistry, Manufacturing, and Controls (CMC)","cGMP manufacturing"]},{"title":"Scientist","company":"iCell Gene Therapeutics","date_range":"2 年 3 个月","duration":"9 个月","location":"美国 维吉尼亚州 夏洛茨维尔","description":"• Developed and optimized CAR-T cell manufacturing workflows, employing advanced molecular cloning and flow cytometry-based isolation to generate diverse therapeutic cell libraries, including BCMA-CD19 CAR-T therapies for autoimmune diseases. \n• Executed CAR-T manufacturing in a cGMP facility, including T cell activation, retroviral transduction, expansion, and tumor cell coculture. \n• Conducted QC testing using ELISA, qPCR, and flow cytometry to assess potency, purity, and stability. \n• Authored and reviewed cGMP-compliant SOPs and Batch Production Records (BPRs), supporting regulatory submissions and contributing to successful FDA IND approvals. \n• Assisted in bioanalytical assay development and method validation per cell and gene therapy regulatory standards. \n• Performed QC testing on raw materials and final products, including sterility, identity, potency, and endotoxin assays. \n• Conducted environmental and in-process monitoring, maintained instruments, validated methods, and analyzed results to ensure compliance and product quality.","skills":["技能: Analytical Method Validation • Quality Control • Gene Therapy • Chemistry, Manufacturing, and Controls (CMC) • cGMP manufacturing","Analytical Method Validation","Quality Control","Gene Therapy","Chemistry, Manufacturing, and Controls (CMC)","cGMP manufacturing"]},{"title":"Vice President ( Taiwanese Graduate Student Association)","company":"Stony Brook University Graduate School","date_range":"2018年5月 - 2020年5月","duration":"2 年 1 个月","location":"美国 纽约 石溪","description":"Taiwanese Graduate Student Association","skills":[]},{"title":"Ph.D./Research Assistant","company":"Stony Brook University","date_range":"6 年 10 个月","duration":"6 年 10 个月","location":"美国 纽约 石溪","description":"In this position, I contributed to diverse research projects in the areas of bacteria genetic engineering, action elucidation, and others with excellent critical thinking and laboratory skills. I also taught classes as a Graduate TA, introducing students to essential topics in biochemistry with clear communication and strong organization.  \nSelected projects include: \n» Uncovering Role of Mycobacterium tuberculosis (Mtb) Epoxide hydrolase b in Redox and Bioenergetic Homeostasis: Implications for Antitubercular Therapy – manuscript submitted to mBio; presented at Center for Infectious Diseases Seminar Series in 2023 and at ACS in 2022. \n• Created gene knock-out models in Mtb and Mm through recombination-mediated genetic engineering. \n• Designed constructs and purified Mtb proteins and protein complexes using E. coli and Rhodococcus jostii. \n• Led biophysical, biochemical, and structural characterization of protein-substrate interaction through thermal shift assays, computational simulations, competition activity assays, biochemical assays, and others. \n• Completed untargeted metabolite profiles using Agilent HPLC and BRUKER Q-TOF IMPACTII. \n• Conducted in-depth bioinformatic data analysis, utilizing advanced software tools. \n» Chemoproteomic Approach to Elucidate Mechanism of Action of Novel 6-Azasteroid with Unique Activity in Mycobacteria – manuscript published in ACS Infectious Diseases \n• Screened anti-TB hit small molecule compounds with Minimum Inhibitory Concentration (MIC) and phenotypic screens in Biosafety Level 3 Lab; completed in-depth characterization and elucidation of mechanism of action of anti-TB hit compounds with assays, RT-qPCR, and RNA-seq data analysis.\n\n• Implemented recombinant protein purification (E coli, mammalian) using AKTA FPLC (IMAC, affinity, ion exchange, SEC, HIC), LC/MS, SDS-PAGE, and Western blot for quality control. \n• Experienced in protein design, cloning, mutagenesis, and bioinformatics. \n• Developed cell-based phenotypic screening platforms in a BSL-3 Lab to discover potential small molecule drugs, conducting comprehensive analyses including proteomics and NGS (WGS, RNA-seq) to characterize drug mechanisms of action. \n• Validated targets through biophysical assays (TSA) and RT-qPCR. \n• Established comprehensive SOPs for sample preparation, LC-MS analyte detection, instrument calibration, data acquisition, quantification, and multi-omics data analysis (R, Python), and completed untargeted metabolomics to understand the microbial metabolism using Agilent HPLC and Bruker Q-TOF Mass Spectrometry. \n• Contributed to the establishment of a Mass Spectrometry Core Facility, including equipment procurement, laboratory management, database development, and quality control, while providing expert support to users with troubleshooting, data analysis guidance, and experimental design optimization to enhance research efficiency.","skills":["技能: GraphPad • Genetic Engineering • Problem Solving • Microbiology • Immunoassays • High-Performance Liquid Chromatography (HPLC) • Protein Characterization • Liquid Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry (LC-MS) • Assay Development • ELISA • Data Analysis • Gel Electrophoresis • Presentation Skills • Drug Development • Bioanalysis • Experimental Design • Chemical Engineering","GraphPad","Genetic Engineering","Problem Solving","Microbiology","Immunoassays","High-Performance Liquid Chromatography (HPLC)","Protein Characterization","Liquid Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry (LC-MS)","Assay Development","ELISA","Data Analysis","Gel Electrophoresis","Presentation Skills","Drug Development","Bioanalysis","Experimental Design","Chemical Engineering","技能: Presentation Skills"]},{"title":"Teaching Assistant","company":"Stony Brook University","date_range":"6 年 10 个月","duration":"6 年 10 个月","location":"美国 纽约 石溪","description":"In this position, I contributed to diverse research projects in the areas of bacteria genetic engineering, action elucidation, and others with excellent critical thinking and laboratory skills. I also taught classes as a Graduate TA, introducing students to essential topics in biochemistry with clear communication and strong organization.  \nSelected projects include: \n» Uncovering Role of Mycobacterium tuberculosis (Mtb) Epoxide hydrolase b in Redox and Bioenergetic Homeostasis: Implications for Antitubercular Therapy – manuscript submitted to mBio; presented at Center for Infectious Diseases Seminar Series in 2023 and at ACS in 2022. \n• Created gene knock-out models in Mtb and Mm through recombination-mediated genetic engineering. \n• Designed constructs and purified Mtb proteins and protein complexes using E. coli and Rhodococcus jostii. \n• Led biophysical, biochemical, and structural characterization of protein-substrate interaction through thermal shift assays, computational simulations, competition activity assays, biochemical assays, and others. \n• Completed untargeted metabolite profiles using Agilent HPLC and BRUKER Q-TOF IMPACTII. \n• Conducted in-depth bioinformatic data analysis, utilizing advanced software tools. \n» Chemoproteomic Approach to Elucidate Mechanism of Action of Novel 6-Azasteroid with Unique Activity in Mycobacteria – manuscript published in ACS Infectious Diseases \n• Screened anti-TB hit small molecule compounds with Minimum Inhibitory Concentration (MIC) and phenotypic screens in Biosafety Level 3 Lab; completed in-depth characterization and elucidation of mechanism of action of anti-TB hit compounds with assays, RT-qPCR, and RNA-seq data analysis.\n\n• Implemented recombinant protein purification (E coli, mammalian) using AKTA FPLC (IMAC, affinity, ion exchange, SEC, HIC), LC/MS, SDS-PAGE, and Western blot for quality control. \n• Experienced in protein design, cloning, mutagenesis, and bioinformatics. \n• Developed cell-based phenotypic screening platforms in a BSL-3 Lab to discover potential small molecule drugs, conducting comprehensive analyses including proteomics and NGS (WGS, RNA-seq) to characterize drug mechanisms of action. \n• Validated targets through biophysical assays (TSA) and RT-qPCR. \n• Established comprehensive SOPs for sample preparation, LC-MS analyte detection, instrument calibration, data acquisition, quantification, and multi-omics data analysis (R, Python), and completed untargeted metabolomics to understand the microbial metabolism using Agilent HPLC and Bruker Q-TOF Mass Spectrometry. \n• Contributed to the establishment of a Mass Spectrometry Core Facility, including equipment procurement, laboratory management, database development, and quality control, while providing expert support to users with troubleshooting, data analysis guidance, and experimental design optimization to enhance research efficiency.","skills":["技能: GraphPad • Genetic Engineering • Problem Solving • Microbiology • Immunoassays • High-Performance Liquid Chromatography (HPLC) • Protein Characterization • Liquid Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry (LC-MS) • Assay Development • ELISA • Data Analysis • Gel Electrophoresis • Presentation Skills • Drug Development • Bioanalysis • Experimental Design • Chemical Engineering","GraphPad","Genetic Engineering","Problem Solving","Microbiology","Immunoassays","High-Performance Liquid Chromatography (HPLC)","Protein Characterization","Liquid Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry (LC-MS)","Assay Development","ELISA","Data Analysis","Gel Electrophoresis","Presentation Skills","Drug Development","Bioanalysis","Experimental Design","Chemical Engineering","技能: Presentation Skills"]},{"title":"Research Assistant","company":"Academia Sinica, Taiwan · 全职","date_range":"2013年8月 - 2017年8月","duration":"4 年 1 个月","location":"台湾 台北市","description":"In this role, I collaborated on numerous research projects in the Life Sciences Division of Taiwan’s premier academic institution. I partnered with colleagues from chemistry, biomedical, physics, genetics, and clinical disciplines on techniques, implications, and further study ideas with excellent teamwork and communication. Selected projects include: \n» Rational Design of Galectin-3 Inhibitors: Integrating Fragment-Based Drug Design, NMR, X-Ray Crystallography, and Computer Modeling \n• Employed advanced biophysical techniques to validate interactions between galectin-3 and its inhibitors, evaluating in-vivo liver fibrosis in mouse models, utilizing ELISA and Immunohistochemistry. \n• Gained experience in small molecule compound screening and development. \n» Discovery of Colorectal Cancer (CRC) Biomarkers \n• Prepared human tumor resections and biopsies into both slow-frozen samples and formalin-fixed samples and then conducted microarray assay data analysis and validated with immunohistochemistry. \n• Unveiled novel glycan biomarkers essential for diagnosing CRC recurrence and metastasis after comprehensive bioinformatic analysis of glycomics data to interpret complex glycan data. \n» Human Infant Clinical Sample Collection \n• Managed entire blood sample collection process, guaranteeing accurate and timely handling, adhering to strict study protocols, determining participant eligibility, and obtaining informed consent.\n\n• Collaborated with cross-functional teams to design and execute high-throughput screening for small molecules and biologics targeting galectin-3. \n• Utilized molecular dynamics simulations and fragment-based docking from the ZINC fragment-like database, identifying 57 high-affinity fragments for further development. \n• Developed and applied biophysical techniques (SPR, ITC, Octet BLI, MST) to assess the kinetics and binding affinities of galectin-3 inhibitors. \n• Conducted PK/PD analysis and evaluated drug activity in liver fibrosis mouse models to support therapeutic advancement. \n• Engineered and validated gene-edited mammalian cell lines through CRISPR/Cas9, optimizing experimental conditions for single-cell clone isolation and genotyping to study galectin-3 gene function. \n• Conducted functional studies to evaluate small molecules for therapeutic potential, leading to the discovery of novel drug candidates. \n• Performed ELISA assays to evaluate the effects of potential galectin-3 inhibitors on binding affinities with ligands (IgE and glycoprotein ASF), utilizing bioconjugate techniques and competition validation. \n• Managed clinical CRC samples, processing tumor resections and biopsies into slow-frozen and formalin-fixed formats, performing cDNA, miRNA, PTM methylation microarray, and glycomics analyses. \n• Conducted bioinformatic and mass spectrometry data analysis to identify novel glycan biomarkers for cancer recurrence and metastasis, validating target gene expression with RT-qPCR and IHC/ICC.","skills":["GraphPad","Genetic Engineering","Problem Solving","Immunoassays","Protein Characterization","Assay Development","Pharmacokinetics","ELISA","Data Analysis","Gel Electrophoresis","Presentation Skills","Drug Development","Immunoprecipitation","Bioanalysis","Fluorescence Microscopy","Experimental Design","Confocal Microscopy"]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Quality Control Manager at iCell Gene Therapeutics · 2026年 - 现在 | Scientist at iCell Gene Therapeutics · 2024年 - 2026年 | Vice President ( Taiwanese Graduate Student Association) at Stony Brook University Graduate School · 2018年 - 2020年 | Teaching Assistant at Stony Brook University · 2018年 - 2019年 | Ph.D./Research Assistant at Stony Brook University · 2017年 - 2024年 | Research Assistant at Academia Sinica, Taiwan · 2013年 - 2017年 | Teaching Assistant at National Yang Ming University · 2012年 - 2012年 | Graduate Research Assistant at National Yang-Ming University · 2011年 - 2013年 | Graduate Student at National Yang Ming University · 2011年 - 2013年 | Graduate Research Assistant at National Yang Ming University · 2011年 - 2013年 | Vice President at Biology Student Association · 2010年 - 2011年 | Lecturer (Biology) at Tzu Chi University · 2009年 - 2011年 | Undergraduate Research Assistant at Tzu Chi University · 2008年 - 2011年","education":[{"school":"Stony Brook University","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Biochemistry and Structural Biology","date_range":"2017年 - 2024年","activities":"活动与社团: Vice President - Taiwanese Graduate Student Association","grade":""},{"school":"阳明大学","degree":"Master's degree","field_of_study":"Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","date_range":"2011年 - 2013年","activities":"","grade":"3.71"},{"school":"慈济大学","degree":"Bachelor of Sciences","field_of_study":"Life Science","date_range":"2007年 - 2011年","activities":"活动与社团: Dean’s List","grade":"3.67"}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Stony Brook University，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2017年 - 2024年 | 阳明大学，Master's degree · 2011年 - 2013年 | 慈济大学，Bachelor of Sciences · 2007年 - 2011年 | 保存到项目 | 将Yu-Ching (Ashley)保存到项目 | 发消息给Yu-Ching (Ashley) | Yu-Ching (Ashley) Chen, Ph.D.的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[{"name":"Chinese","proficiency":"母语"}],"native_chinese":true,"detail_error":""}}
