年 | Department of Interdisciplinary Oncology - PhD Candidate - Dr. Marcel Bally's Lab at University of British Columbia · 2016年 - 2020年 | Research Student at BC Cancer Research Center · 2014年 - 2015年 | Youth Engagement Intern at Vancouver School Board · 2011年 - 2011年 | Science Outreach Volunteer at Let’s Talk Science (Award winning, national, charitable program) · 2009年 - 2012年 | Biology 140 Instructor at The University of British Columbia · 2009年 - 2013年 | Full-Time Summer Research Assistant at Agriculture and Agri-Food Canada · 2008年 - 2008年 | Recreations and Music Therapy Volunteer at George Pearson Rehabilitation Center · 2005年 - 2007年","education":[{"school":"The University of British Columbia","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Interdisciplinary Oncology","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"The University of British Columbia","degree":"Master of Science","field_of_study":"Plant Molecular Biology in Forestry","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"The University of British Columbia","degree":"Bachelor of Science","field_of_study":"Biology Major","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | The University of British Columbia，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD | The University of British Columbia，Master of Science | The University of British Columbia，Bachelor of Science | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["所在地点 现场办公: 加拿大 安大略 加拿大 英属哥伦比亚 埃德蒙顿地区 温哥华地区 卡尔加里地区 加拿大多伦多地区"],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:27:22+08:00","record":{"name":"Dr. Wei Chen","current_title":"Scientist — Pharmaceutical Development & Analytical Sciences","current_company":"Roche · 全职","location":"CMC Development Scientist | Control Strategy","headline":"CMC Development Scientist | Control Strategy · Formulation · Excipient Science | Biologics & Complex Sterile Products","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/dr-wei-chen-34670526","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAVxl6YBpQ6yywuF1J97-gBP16iekb62LWQ","core_skills":["Particle Characterization","Excipient Science","Regulatory Submissions (Module 3 / IMPD)"],"positions":[{"title":"Scientist — Pharmaceutical Development & Analytical Sciences","company":"Roche · 全职","date_range":"2020年2月 - 现在","duration":"6 年 8 个月","location":"瑞士 巴塞尔城市","description":"Excipient control strategy, particle risk mitigation, and formulation robustness for parenteral biologics across the Roche portfolio. \n \n• Raw material variability → product quality risk: Poloxamer 188 supplier variability threatened formulation consistency. Built the end-to-end control strategy — identified CQAs, defined specifications, developed the analytical method (LCCC), and transferred it to the supplier (BASF) for incoming quality control. Secured supply chain quality from development through commercial supply. (Published, patent filed) \n \n• Excipient degradation → visible particle risk: PS and Px188 degradation generates particles — a patient safety concern and active HA focus. Investigated degradation mechanisms and translated findings into formulation/process design decisions: surfactant selection, hold times, contact materials, storage conditions. Supports control strategy and regulatory defense in CTD P.2. (Published) \n \n• Particle events across portfolio → root cause & corrective action: Leading particle investigations across products (CT-868, Faricimab, Hemlibra) — identifying root cause (protein aggregates vs. FFA vs. silicone oil vs. process contaminants) and translating each into formulation, process, or packaging design changes. \n \n• Development timeline risk: Developing predictive stability methods (SPR, THC, Flow Cytometry) to enable earlier go/no-go decisions in formulation screening — reducing late-stage reformulation risk. Introduced these as new platform capabilities. \n \n• Cross-functional alignment: Built a CMC development knowledge base mapping the end-to-end process (milestones, risks, dependencies). Initiated pRED collaboration on ML-based particle morphology analysis to scale root cause capability.","skills":[]},{"title":"CMC Analytics, scientist / Team leader","company":"Ablynx","date_range":"2019年7月 - 2019年12月","duration":"6 个月","location":"根特地区","description":"CMC Scientist — Team Leader, Pharmaceutical Development for nanobody-based biologics (pre-clinical stage). \n \n• Early-stage CMC ownership: Headed a team of 3 research associates. Designed and coordinated the pharmaceutical development work packages — formulation screening, lead candidate selection, and stability programs — to advance nanobody molecules toward clinical readiness. \n \n• Formulation strategy: Coordinated high-throughput formulation screening to evaluate excipient compositions, pH ranges, and storage conditions, and nominated the lead formulation candidate for IND-enabling studies. \n \n• Regulatory preparation: Authored CMC sections of the IMPD (CTD Module 3 — P.2 Pharmaceutical Development). Conducted immunogenicity risk assessments and proposed mitigation strategies to support clinical trial application.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist","company":"Polpharma Biologics","date_range":"2019年1月 - 2019年6月","duration":"6 个月","location":"Utrecht Area, Netherlands","description":"Scientist — CMC development support for biosimilar mAbs (Adalimumab, Nivolumab, Pembrolizumab). \n \n• Process & analytical packages for tech transfer: Developed downstream purification workflows and coordinated analytical method development, validation, and transfer to generic pharmaceutical company partners — ensuring comparability and release testing readiness across sites.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist--project lead","company":"Teva Pharmaceuticals","date_range":"2014年9月 - 2018年11月","duration":"4 年 3 个月","location":"尼德兰 北荷兰 哈勒姆","description":"Project Lead — CMC development of complex sterile products (liposomes, microparticles, nanoparticles, peptides) for oncology. Full lifecycle from early formulation through EMA registration. \n \n• Program ownership: Led 2 CMC development programs simultaneously — owning formulation development, process scale-up, analytical characterization, stability, and regulatory submission as a single integrated scope. Coordinated across QA, RA, engineering, and manufacturing functions. \n \n• Regulatory outcome: Authored the CMC sections of Module 3 for a liposomal drug that received EMA marketing authorization. Responded to health authority questions during MAA review — defending the control strategy, specifications, and process design. \n \n• CDMO strategy & tech transfer: Designed the outsourcing model — develop study packages internally to build process understanding, then transfer to CDMO for scale-up and validation. This enabled large programs with limited internal FTE while retaining scientific ownership of the control strategy. \n \n• QbD & risk management: Applied quality by design to formulation and process development — risk assessment to prioritize development activities, DoE to define process design space, root cause analysis to resolve failures. Managed lab-to-pilot scale-up. \n \n• Resource management: Calculated FTE requirements, managed project budgets, and allocated internal vs. external resources to meet supply timelines.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Scientist — Pharmaceutical Development & Analytical Sciences at Roche · 2020年 - 现在 | CMC Analytics, scientist / Team leader at Ablynx · 2019年 - 2019年 | Scientist at Polpharma Biologics · 2019年 - 2019年 | Scientist--project lead at Teva Pharmaceuticals · 2014年 - 2018年 | Researcher at National Center for Nanoscience and Technology · 2008年 - 2010年","education":[{"school":"Rijksuniversiteit Groningen","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy - PhD","field_of_study":"Polymer Chemistry and Bioengineering","date_range":"2010年 - 2014年","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"四川大学","degree":"Bachelor of Engineering","field_of_study":"Polymer Science and Engineering","date_range":"2004年 - 2008年","activities":"","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Rijksuniversiteit Groningen，Doctor of Philosophy - PhD · 2010年 - 2014年 | 四川大学，Bachelor of Engineering · 2004年 - 2008年 | 档案意向行装饰","open_to_work":["职位头衔 Director Principal Scientist 职位性质 全职 所在地点 现场办公: 瑞士 巴塞尔城市 巴塞尔 开始日期 我在积极找工作，可以马上开始 工作场所类型 现场办公 混合办公"],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:27:31+08:00","record":{"name":"Lishan Chen","current_title":"Chief Scientific Officer","current_company":"Molecular Axiom, Inc. · 全职","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","headline":"Scientist","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/lishanchen","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAEUHaIBBUyo3kT9Wa71FllVw2Wa0YwQ8CI","core_skills":["Immunology","RNAi","Microbiology"],"positions":[{"title":"Chief Scientific Officer","company":"Molecular Axiom, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2022年1月 - 现在","duration":"4 年 9 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","description":"","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientific Fellow","company":"Ultragenyx","date_range":"5 年 9 个月","duration":"3 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 诺瓦托","description":"• In charge of nucleic acid therapeutic programs in Ultragenyx, including multiple mRNA, siRNA and antisense therapeutic projects in rare diseases. Involved in new project concept formation, proposals and prioritization, candidate sequence design and optimization, delivery strategy selection and verification, POC study design and milestone and stage-up criteria.  \n• Lead nucleic acid therapeutic platform research to plan and identify strategies to improve and expand current nucleic acid therapeutic opportunities. Improve the current nucleic therapy and delivery platform. Explore novel technology in both industry and academia, and conduct feasibility studies for due diligent and verification. \n• Evaluate external nucleic acid therapeutic projects and technology business opportunities, and providing scientific opinion of various gene therapies strategies. Provide scientific investigation for FTO and partner IP evaluation. \n• Project team lead for multiple mRNA based therapeutic projects for rare genetic diseases with external business partner. Recently transfer one therapeutic program to development in preparation for IND.  \n• Manage an internal research team to establish and execute in vitro/ex vivo