{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:28:20+08:00","record":{"name":"Tom Chen","current_title":"Senior Director, Head of Drug Substance and MSAT","current_company":"Dianthus Therapeutics, Inc.","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","headline":"Senior Director @ Dianthus Therapeutics | Drug substance, CMC Lead","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/taotaochen","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAfcCugB9nSNzmoUleV1xRz7Pr-SK0lFUi8","core_skills":["Analytical development","Anti-hemophilia drug development","Pharmaceutical Industry"],"positions":[{"title":"Senior Director, Head of Drug Substance and MSAT","company":"Dianthus Therapeutics, Inc.","date_range":"5 年 9 个月","duration":"1 年 10 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"• Lead and manage the Drug Substance team to support discovery, candidate evaluation, and early CMC development of biologics, including monoclonal antibodies, bispecifics, and fusion proteins. \n• Design phase-appropriate CMC strategies and detailed work plans, and drive execution through internal resources and strategic partnerships with CDMOs. \n• Evaluate CDMO proposals and develop statements of work (SOWs) for clinical drug substance manufacturing; conduct onsite audits and provide final recommendations. \n• Lead formulation development, including high-concentration liquid formulations (150–200 mg/mL) for early- and late-stage programs, supporting the development of APFS and autoinjector presentations. \n• Direct all CMC Drug Substance activities, including clone selection, MCB/WCB generation, upstream cell-culture development, downstream purification development, product characterization, GMP manufacturing, and preparation of IND/BLA documentation. \n• Oversee stability programs, comparability studies, and the establishment of phase-appropriate specifications and control strategies. \n• Lead late-stage scale-up from 500 L to 2000 L, including process characterization (PC), process validation (PV), and PPQ activities in support of BLA and commercial manufacturing. \n• Support drug product and device development, including PFS filling, APFS, and autoinjector development. \n• Lead the tech transfer team to ensure smooth and efficient knowledge transfer and process transfer between sending and receiving CMOs.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director, Drug Substance and Early Development CMC Lead","company":"Dianthus Therapeutics, Inc.","date_range":"5 年 9 个月","duration":"1 年 10 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"• Lead and manage the Drug Substance team to support discovery, candidate evaluation, and early CMC development of biologics, including monoclonal antibodies, bispecifics, and fusion proteins. \n• Design phase-appropriate CMC strategies and detailed work plans, and drive execution through internal resources and strategic partnerships with CDMOs. \n• Evaluate CDMO proposals and develop statements of work (SOWs) for clinical drug substance manufacturing; conduct onsite audits and provide final recommendations. \n• Lead formulation development, including high-concentration liquid formulations (150–200 mg/mL) for early- and late-stage programs, supporting the development of APFS and autoinjector presentations. \n• Direct all CMC Drug Substance activities, including clone selection, MCB/WCB generation, upstream cell-culture development, downstream purification development, product characterization, GMP manufacturing, and preparation of IND/BLA documentation. \n• Oversee stability programs, comparability studies, and the establishment of phase-appropriate specifications and control strategies. \n• Lead late-stage scale-up from 500 L to 2000 L, including process characterization (PC), process validation (PV), and PPQ activities in support of BLA and commercial manufacturing. \n• Support drug product and device development, including PFS filling, APFS, and autoinjector development. \n• Lead the tech transfer team to ensure smooth and efficient knowledge transfer and process transfer between sending and receiving CMOs.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director, Analytical and Formulation Development - CMC Lead","company":"Dianthus Therapeutics, Inc.","date_range":"5 年 9 个月","duration":"1 年 10 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 波士顿","description":"• Lead and manage the Drug Substance team to support discovery, candidate evaluation, and early CMC development of biologics, including monoclonal antibodies, bispecifics, and fusion proteins. \n• Design phase-appropriate CMC strategies and detailed work plans, and drive execution through internal resources and strategic partnerships with CDMOs. \n• Evaluate CDMO proposals and develop statements of work (SOWs) for clinical drug substance manufacturing; conduct onsite audits and provide final recommendations. \n• Lead formulation development, including high-concentration liquid formulations (150–200 mg/mL) for early- and late-stage programs, supporting the development of APFS and autoinjector presentations. \n• Direct all CMC Drug Substance activities, including clone selection, MCB/WCB generation, upstream cell-culture development, downstream purification development, product characterization, GMP manufacturing, and preparation of IND/BLA documentation. \n• Oversee stability programs, comparability studies, and the establishment of phase-appropriate specifications and control strategies. \n• Lead late-stage scale-up from 500 L to 2000 L, including process characterization (PC), process validation (PV), and PPQ activities in support of BLA and commercial manufacturing. \n• Support drug product and device development, including PFS filling, APFS, and autoinjector development. \n• Lead the tech transfer team to ensure smooth and efficient knowledge transfer and process transfer between sending and receiving CMOs.","skills":[]},{"title":"Director, Analytical and Pharmaceutical Science","company":"Eagle Pharmaceuticals, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2021年","duration":"1 个月","location":"美国 马萨诸塞州 剑桥","description":"• Manage day-to-day analytical activities including timeline, budget management, objective setting, and internal lab operations for small molecule drug development \n• Lead phase appropriate analytical method development and validation from preclinical through commercialization in compliance with ICH and related guidance. \n• Lead the characterization of the process- and product-related impurities as well as product structure. \n• Provide technical support for laboratory investigations, deviation investigation, and review of investigation reports. \n• Author and review analytical documents including study protocols, reports, SOPs, and CMC sections/responses in regulatory submissions or questions.","skills":[]},{"title":"Associate Director of Analytical Development","company":"STC Biologics Inc · 全职","date_range":"2019年 - 2021年","duration":"2 年 1 个月","location":"Newton, Great Boston Area, Massachusetts","description":"• Head of the Analytical group, which includes one Ph.D. Scientist and two associates. I communicated with Directors or CEOs from clients to write the proposal to meet the clients’ needs. \n• Complete 12 projects in 4 months, including method development of test methods for release assay and process development samples. Troubleshoot five long-standing issues in two weeks and saved the company from losing more than 1 million US Dollars.  \n• Led the Development of Cell line, Cell culture, Formulation, and Bioprocess of Fc-fusion proteins for Preclinical and Phase one study. I have overcome numerous issues during the development, such as low cell viability, high aggregate, low yield during the bioprocess, high HCP, high endotoxin, and severe degradation. Science-driven innovations were across the formulation and bioprocess to reach a high-quality product.  \n• Led the tech transfer of stability program for a small molecule drug. Supervised five analysts who were involved in this program, which includes WFI, osmolality, endotoxin, HIAC, HPLC based impurity, and content uniformity, and Cell-based potency bioassay. Overcame dramatical challenges, including tight timeline, translation of the test method, lack of details of the source document, compliance of USP, and QA document review since the original product was based on JP from Japan. Delivered the mandatory tests of stability time points, tech transfer reports, and full stability report for the IND in 2 months. \n• Oversight and management of two biologics CMC programs from the sequence to process development and manufacturing of drug products for Phase I clinical trial. Troubleshoot the expected issues in time to meet the project timeline.","skills":[]},{"title":"LC-MS & GC-MS Product Specialist - Analytical instrumentation","company":"Agilent Technologies · 全职","date_range":"2018年 - 2019年","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"旧金山湾区","description":"• Worked with various customers and developed new assays for the impurity of small molecule and structural elucidation using mass spectrometry in two weeks.  \n• Initiated the new intact mass quantification for biopharma PK study using LCMS \n• Strong knowledge of GC-MS and LC-MS applications on extractable and leachable for drug products. \n• Acquired strong expertise in mass spectrometry and automation by running the customer’s demo samples under competitive situations. Fully understood the pros and cons of mass spectrometries from different vendors (Scix, Thermo fisher, and waters) and utilized the knowledge to facilitate the instrument purchase and drug development strategy.  \n• Strong capability to troubleshoot the issues of instrumentation and method hiccup immediately to win the credibility. \n• Organized a 700 people pharma and Biopharma summit at the SF bay area by coordinating the resources from Agilent and Pharma industry in 2019.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | Senior Director, Head of Drug Substance and MSAT at Dianthus Therapeutics, Inc. · 2024年 - 现在 | Director, Drug Substance and Early Development CMC Lead at Dianthus Therapeutics, Inc. · 2022年 - 2024年 | Director, Analytical and Formulation Development - CMC Lead at Dianthus Therapeutics, Inc. · 2021年 - 2022年 | Director, Analytical and Pharmaceutical Science at Eagle Pharmaceuticals, Inc. · 2021年 | Associate Director of Analytical Development at STC Biologics Inc · 2019年 - 2021年 | LC-MS & GC-MS Product Specialist - Analytical instrumentation at Agilent Technologies · 2018年 - 2019年 | Analytical Development Scientist - Program Leader at Bayer · 2015年 - 2018年 | Scientific Manager - (formerly Lakepharma) at Curia · 2013年 - 2015年 | Postdoctoral Researcher & LC/MSMS specialist at Stanford University · 2011年 - 2012年 | Postdoctoral Researcher at UCSF · 2011年 - 2012年","education":[{"school":"Max Planck Society","degree":"Ph,D","field_of_study":"Biochemistry","date_range":"","activities":"","grade":""},{"school":"Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München","degree":"PhD","field_of_study":"Biochemistry","date_range":"","activities":"活动与社团: Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","grade":""}],"education_fallback":"职业档案中列出的教育经历 | Max Planck Society，Ph,D | Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München，PhD | 档案分析行 | 最新动态 | 1 次浏览 | 申请了 1 个职位 | 保存到项目 | 将Tom保存到项目 | 发消息给Tom | Tom Chen的更多操作","open_to_work":[],"languages":[],"native_chinese":null,"detail_error":""}}
