{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:30:09+08:00","record":{"name":"Elizabeth C.","current_title":"Principal Scientist","current_company":"强生公司","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","headline":"Principal Scientist in Translational Sciences & Medicine, Computational Immunology-Dermatology at J&J","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/elizabethchen1","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAAAq_iYYBmil2ehHQjNjpxipEVXgmr3Vc33w","core_skills":["Immunoprecipitation","Protein Purification","Alzheimer's Disease"],"positions":[{"title":"Principal Scientist","company":"强生公司","date_range":"2 年 5 个月","duration":"6 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","description":"Leading biomarker data analysis from Phase I-III clinical trials in dermatology.","skills":[]},{"title":"Senior Scientist","company":"强生公司","date_range":"2 年 5 个月","duration":"6 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 圣地亚哥","description":"Leading biomarker data analysis from Phase I-III clinical trials in dermatology.","skills":[]},{"title":"Institute Research Investigator","company":"MD Anderson Cancer Center · 全职","date_range":"2021年11月 - 2024年5月","duration":"2 年 7 个月","location":"美国 德州 休斯顿","description":"• Conducted bioinformatic analysis of omics datasets (CyTOF, RNA-seq, RPPA datasets) \n• Created visualization applications for analysis of above datasets using Python DASH linked to SQL database files\n\n• Analyzed RNA-sequencing and reverse protein phase array datasets to discover new predictive biomarkers of success for cancer therapeutic indications Conducted spatial transcriptomic analysis using R packages such as Azimuth, Giotto, Seurat, BayesSpace, STdeconvolve, SpaCET, and SpatialDecon to identify novel transcriptional markers of tumor cells and infiltrating immune cells in both human and mouse brain metastases samples Developed and deployed Python Dash applications for program biologists to probe mechanism of action of various cancer therapeutics including a Wee1 inhibitor, CDK4/CDK6 inhibitor, and KRASG12C inhibitor in various patient derived xenograft (PDX) models.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist","company":"Tempus Labs, Inc. · 全职","date_range":"2020年8月 - 2021年11月","duration":"1 年 4 个月","location":"美国 伊利诺伊州 芝加哥","description":"• Troubleshot Tempus' cell-free DNA assay for assessing tumor mutations in cancer patients \n• Implemented process improvements to reduce error in sequencing workflows for exome, RNA, and target-capture DNA sequencing\n\n• Performed root cause analysis to identify reasons for batch failures and sample swaps in Tempus sequencing workflows. \n• Implemented process improvements to reduce error in automated high-throughput sequencing workflows for exome, RNA, and target-capture DNA sequencing involving Perkin Elmer Janus and Sciclone instruments Troubleshot Tempus’ cell-free DNA assay for assessing tumor mutations in cancer patients Used Datagrip (SQL) to mine sequencing datasets and discover insights about new assay versions.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist","company":"Orchard Therapeutics · 全职","date_range":"2019年11月 - 2020年6月","duration":"8 个月","location":"美国 加利福尼亚 门洛帕克","description":"• Developed flow cytometry panels to characterize hematopoietic stem cell health  \n• Analyzed Cellular Indexing of Transcriptomics and Epitopes by Sequencing (CITE-SEQ) data of 10X sequenced CD34+ Prodigy-enriched cells and drug product (CD34+ cells transduced with lentiviral vectors) \n• Drafted SOP’s and reports for cellular assays including MitoSOX, JC-1, Hoechst, and EdU and instruments including the BD FACS Melody Cell sorter\n\n• Worked under analytical development department to characterize hematopoietic stem cell phenotype with an advanced panel of antibodies derived from literature and in-house testing. \n• The optimized panel was used to monitor in-process intermediates and drug product produced during process development activities. \n• Developed and utilized a bioinformatic pipeline using both R package Seurat and Python package ScanPy to analyze Cellular Indexing of Transcriptomics and Epitopes by Sequencing (CITE-SEQ) data of 10X sequenced CD34+ Prodigy-enriched cells and drug product (CD34+ cells transduced with lentiviral vectors) Drafted standard operating procedures, protocols, and reports for cellular assays including MitoSOX, JC-1, Hoechst, and EdU and instruments including the BD FACS Melody Cell sorter Worked in a cross functional team including R&D and Process Development groups to define molecules for phenotyping panel and define experimental plan for the aforementioned CITE-SEQ experiments.","skills":[]}],"experience_fallback":"职业档案中列出的工作经历 | 已添加简历进行完善 | Principal Scientist at Johnson & Johnson · 2026年 - 现在 | Senior Scientist at Johnson & Johnson · 2024年 - 2026年 | Institute Research Investigator at MD Anderson Cancer Center · 2021年 - 2024年 | Scientist at Tempus Labs, Inc. · 2020年 - 2021年 | Scientist at Orchard Therapeutics · 2019年 - 2020年 | Process Development and Transfer Intern at Illumina · 2019年 - 2019年 | Stanford Interdisciplinary Graduate Fellow at Stanford University · 2013年 - 2019年 | Project Undergraduate Advised by Dr. Maria Oden at Rice University · 2011年 - 2012年 | Tissue Engineering Intern under Dr. Helen Lu at Columbia University · 2011年 - 2011年 | Research Undergraduate under Dr. Weiwei Zhong at Rice University · 2011年 - 2011年 | Tissue Engineering Intern under Dr. Savio L-Y. Woo at Pittsburgh Tissue Engineering Initiative · 2010年 - 2010年","education":[{"school":"美国斯坦福大学","degree":"Doctor of Philosophy (PhD)","field_of_study":"Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine","date_range":"2012年 - 2019年","activities":"活动与社团: Advanced Degrees Consulting Club (2016-2017), TA for Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine Lecture Course (2013), Sustainability Intern (2017-2018), Community Associate for Lyman Graduate Residence (2017-2018)","grade":"Dr. Michael Clarke"},{"school":"Rice University","degree":"Bachelor of Science (B.S.)","field_of_study":"Bioengineering","date_ra