{"type":"record","version":2,"saved_at":"2026-09-17T11:30:46+08:00","record":{"name":"Yu-Hsuan (Zack) Chen, PhD","current_title":"Chief Scientific Officer & Chief Operating Officer","current_company":"Biomedical Elitecell Corp.","location":"美国 德州 Woodway","headline":"Biotech Scientist & Executive | Therapeutic & Platform Builder | Antibody Innovation • Engineered Immunocytokines • Cell Therapy • hPL Therapeutics • Regenerative Medicine | CSO & COO @ EliteCell (US & TW)","public_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/yu-hsuan-zack-chen-phd-21b7377a","recruiter_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/talent/profile/AEMAABDWl3cBADMwRFV99_ZnfHY4GbkNVfC2K8Y","core_skills":["Biomarker Discovery"],"positions":[{"title":"Chief Scientific Officer & Chief Operating Officer","company":"Biomedical Elitecell Corp.","date_range":"1 年 6 个月","duration":"6 个月","location":"美国 德州","description":"Leading scientific strategy, R&D portfolio development, manufacturing operations, quality systems, and strategic business development across EliteCell’s Taiwan and U.S. operations. \n \nMy work focuses on building biotechnology programs from scientific concept through experimental validation, process development, scale-up, and commercialization. \n \n• Creating and leading R&D programs across hPL therapeutics, regenerative biologics, NK / γδ T / CB-NK platforms, immune cell culture systems, and artificial platelet technologies \n \n• Building new projects from the ground up - from scientific hypothesis and experimental design to translational strategy, platform development, and multidisciplinary team execution \n \n• Leading process development, manufacturing optimization, and cross-functional operations across R&D, PD, QC, QA, manufacturing, logistics, and BD \n \n• Strengthening quality and regulatory readiness across U.S. and Taiwan operations, including U.S. FDA 21 CFR Part 820 / QMSR and ISO 9001 / ISO 13485 initiatives, product quality oversight, and serving as a key company representative during external customer and quality audits \n \n• Driving global business development and strategic partnerships across the U.S., China, Southeast Asia, India, and the Middle East, working with biotech companies, CDMOs, academic collaborators, suppliers, distributors, and other life-science partners \n \nI continue to bring my background in protein biochemistry, immunology, immuno-oncology, therapeutic design, and in vivo disease models into the creation of new biologics and advanced therapeutic opportunities.","skills":[]},{"title":"Vice President","company":"Biomedical Elitecell Corp.","date_range":"1 年 6 个月","duration":"6 个月","location":"美国 德州","description":"Leading scientific strategy, R&D portfolio development, manufacturing operations, quality systems, and strategic business development across EliteCell’s Taiwan and U.S. operations. \n \nMy work focuses on building biotechnology programs from scientific concept through experimental validation, process development, scale-up, and commercialization. \n \n• Creating and leading R&D programs across hPL therapeutics, regenerative biologics, NK / γδ T / CB-NK platforms, immune cell culture systems, and artificial platelet technologies \n \n• Building new projects from the ground up - from scientific hypothesis and experimental design to translational strategy, platform development, and multidisciplinary team execution \n \n• Leading process development, manufacturing optimization, and cross-functional operations across R&D, PD, QC, QA, manufacturing, logistics, and BD \n \n• Strengthening quality and regulatory readiness across U.S. and Taiwan operations, including U.S. FDA 21 CFR Part 820 / QMSR and ISO 9001 / ISO 13485 initiatives, product quality oversight, and serving as a key company representative during external customer and quality audits \n \n• Driving global business development and strategic partnerships across the U.S., China, Southeast Asia, India, and the Middle East, working with biotech companies, CDMOs, academic collaborators, suppliers, distributors, and other life-science partners \n \nI continue to bring my background in protein biochemistry, immunology, immuno-oncology, therapeutic design, and in vivo disease models into the creation of new biologics and advanced therapeutic opportunities.","skills":[]},{"title":"Scientist/Project Lead","company":"HanchorBio Inc. 漢康生技股份有限公司 · 全职","date_range":"2024年3月 - 2025年3月","duration":"1 年 1 个月","location":"台湾 台北市","description":"Led biologics programs across clinical, IND-stage, preclinical, and early discovery development in immuno-oncology and autoimmune diseases. \n \n• Advanced next-generation immunocytokine and conditionally activated cytokine therapeutics, integrating tumor-selective activation with translational immunology \n \n• Led and supported programs from preclinical and IND-enabling development through clinical-stage translation, including HCB101 and HCB301 \n \n• Developed an AI-enabled translational biomarker strategy to support clinical development \n \n• Created and initiated multiple new therapeutic concepts and early discovery programs, including innovative antibody-based and immune-modulatory strategies in oncology and autoimmune diseases \n \n• Built in vitro, ex vivo, and in vivo translational platforms supporting MoA, biomarker, PD, and preclinical studies while leading multidisciplinary scientific teams","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow (Immunology, Autoimmunity, Immuno-Oncology)","company":"UC San Diego · 全职","date_range":"2022年8月 - 2024年1月","duration":"1 年 6 个月","location":"San Diego","description":"1. Using several mouse models to explore the strategic role of particular regulatory T cells (Treg) in  \nthe regulation of autoimmune responses and anti-tumor immunity, and develop specific Treg-  \ntargeted cancer therapies. \n2. Studying Treg and B cells at molecular, cellular, and in vivo mouse model levels. \n3. Elucidating the functional interplay in a particular Treg, MDSCs, and T cell exhaustion in the  \ntumor microenvironment. \n4. To investigate the effect of NLRP3 inflammasome inhibitors on Th17 cell inhibition and  \nprogression of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) using SOD1 and TDP43 transgenic mouse  \nmodels. \n5. To study the role of a particular interleukin signaling in T cells in the control of Th17 cell-  \nmediated autoimmune diseases.","skills":[]},{"title":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow/Scholar (Protein Biochemistry, Cancer Immunology)","company":"Academia Sinica, Taiwan","date_range":"7 年 10 个月","duration":"2 年","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","description":"• Investigated ubiquitin signaling in innate immunity and cancer biology, focusing on regulatory mechanisms connecting protein homeostasis with tumor immune responses. \n• Studied tumor-infiltrating immune cells, cGAS–STING–IRF3 signaling, and resistance to immune checkpoint blockade using molecular, cellular, and in vivo tumor models. \n• Applied SILAC, BioID, mass spectrometry-based proteomics, molecular and cellular biology, and in vivo approaches to identify novel protein interactions, substrates, and regulatory mechanisms. \n• First-author work published in Nature Communications (2023).","skills":[]},{"title":"Doctoral Researcher (Protein Biochemistry, Molecular Cell Biology, Gene Therapy)","company":"Academia Sinica, Taiwan","date_range":"7 年 10 个月","duration":"2 年","location":"台湾 台北市 台北市","description":"• Investigated ubiquitin signaling in innate immunity and cancer biology, focusing on regulatory mechanisms connecting protein homeostasis with tumor immune responses. \n• Studied tumor-infiltrating immune cells, cGAS–STING–IRF3 signaling, and resistance to immune checkpoint blockade using molecular, cellular, and in vivo tumor models. \n• Applied SILAC, BioID, mass spectrometry-based proteomics, molecular and cellular biology, and in vivo approaches to identify novel protein interactions, substrates, and regulatory mechanisms. \n• First-author work published in Nature 